BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-107864@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:“Ken combines a gentle\, folksy spirit with toe-tapping\, tradi
 tional Appalachian fiddling\, and eventually gets all the children writing
  poetry before they even realize it.”\nKick off National Poetry Month with
  a performance and writing workshop for the whole family! Author and music
 ian\, Ken Waldman\, has designed a performance followed by a writing works
 hop for all ages. We’ll be writing a poem or two together and all attendee
 s will receive a few poems to take home! Waldman combines Appalachian-styl
 e string band music\, age-appropriate poetry\, and Alaska-set storytelling
  for a performance uniquely. His 20 books include 16 poetry collections\, 
 a memoir\, a novel\, a creative writing manual\, and a kids’ book. His 12 
 CDs include two for children.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230401T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230401T170000
LOCATION:FAR Center for Contemporary Arts\, 505 West 4th St. Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Kids Writing Workshop & Performance with Ken Waldman – Celebrate th
 e First Day of National Poetry Month with Alaska’s Fiddling Poet
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/kids-writing-workshop-performance-with-ken-waldm
 an-celebrate-the-first-day-of-national-poetry-month-with-alaskas-fiddling-
 poet/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>“Ken combines
  a gentle\, folksy spirit with toe-tapping\, traditional Appalachian fiddl
 ing\, and eventually gets all the children writing poetry before they even
  realize it.”</p>\n<p>Kick off National Poetry Month with a performance an
 d writing workshop for the whole family! Author and musician\, Ken Waldman
 \, has designed a performance followed by a writing workshop for all ages.
  We’ll be writing a poem or two together and all attendees will receive a 
 few poems to take home! Waldman combines Appalachian-style string band mus
 ic\, age-appropriate poetry\, and Alaska-set storytelling for a performanc
 e uniquely. His 20 books include 16 poetry collections\, a memoir\, a nove
 l\, a creative writing manual\, and a kids’ book. His 12 CDs include two f
 or children.<a href='https://kenwaldman.com/home' target='_blank' rel='nor
 eferrer noopener'><br />\n</a></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
