BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-107914@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Presented by the BCT & Neal-Marshall Black Culture Center  The 
 Buskirk-Chumley Theater and The Neal-Marshall Black Culture Center invite 
 you to a live-taping of “The Balcony” a Podcast looking at the intersectio
 ns of Race\, The movies\, Bloomington\, and the Buskirk-Chumley Theater. S
 o much of the theater and Bloomington’s past involving race is not written
  but told. This event will focus on conversations with established black v
 oices in our community to recover and document those stories\, creating a 
 more complete record. Interviewees include Gladys DeVane and Beverly Calen
 der-Anderson\, with more to come.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230403T183000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Balcony Podcast:  Kirkwood Past and Future
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-balcony-podcast-kirkwood-past-and-future/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Prese
 nted by the BCT & Neal-Marshall Black Culture Center</strong>  The Buskirk
 -Chumley Theater and The Neal-Marshall Black Culture Center invite you to 
 a live-taping of “The Balcony” a Podcast looking at the intersections of R
 ace\, The movies\, Bloomington\, and the Buskirk-Chumley Theater. So much 
 of the theater and Bloomington’s past involving race is not written but to
 ld. This event will focus on conversations with established black voices i
 n our community to recover and document those stories\, creating a more co
 mplete record. Interviewees include Gladys DeVane and Beverly Calender-And
 erson\, with more to come.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
