DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Dawn Brockett is the author of “Unrestricted: How I Stepped Off
  the Tightrope\, Learned to Say No\, and Silenced Anorexia.”\nIn her debut
  book\, she issues a call to action to change the way anorexia and anorect
 ics are viewed and treated. At once heart-wrenching\, heartwarming\, and h
 opeful\, Unrestricted is the story of how one woman stopped disappearing\,
  started listening to her own voice\, and finally claimed her rightful pla
 ce in the world.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230404T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230404T193000
LOCATION:Morgenstern's Books\, 849 Auto Mall Rd\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Author Talk — Dawn Brockett
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/author-talk-dawn-brockett/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='x11i
 5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xdj266r'>Dawn Brockett is the author of “Unr
 estricted: How I Stepped Off the Tightrope\, Learned to Say No\, and Silen
 ced Anorexia.”</div>\n<div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1
 s'>In her debut book\, she issues a call to action to change the way anore
 xia and anorectics are viewed and treated. At once heart-wrenching\, heart
 warming\, and hopeful\, Unrestricted is the story of how one woman stopped
  disappearing\, started listening to her own voice\, and finally claimed h
 er rightful place in the world.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
