CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday Celebration Commission pres
 ents:\nA community conversation about Dr. Martin Luther King\, Jr.’s book 
 “Why We Can’t Wait.” Facilitated by Ruth Aydt and Al Mann\, members of the
  Monroe County NAACP. Introduction by Lily Kleinlein\, MLK Commissioner.\n
 Plus for the children: a coloring corner with social justice coloring shee
 ts and crayons.\n“I am excited about Remembrance Week commemorating the 55
 th anniversary of Dr. King’s death. As we honor his life and legacy\, we h
 ave an opportunity to also celebrate Black history in Bloomington\, tell s
 ome beautiful stories alongside beautiful artwork\, and support our local 
 gems like Morgenstern ”\n– Gloria Howell\, Director\, Neal-Marshall Black 
 Culture Center at IU
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230405T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230405T200000
LOCATION:Morgenstern's Books\, 849 Auto Mall Rd\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
