BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-107690@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812-336-7110\; http://seeconstellation.org/
DESCRIPTION:As part of Constellation’s spring screening series\, we will be
  presenting the cult-favorite horror film: Midsommar. Originally released 
 in 2019\, this modern folk-horror film was written and directed by Ari Ast
 er (also known for his earlier film Hereditary). The film received high cr
 itical acclaim\, said to be “a savage yet evolved slice of Swedish folk-ho
 rror\, Ari Aster’s hallucinatory follow-up to Hereditary proves him a horr
 or director with no peer.”\n\nIt’s time for Summer\, or rather Midsommar t
 his April! The unsettling terror begins when a couple travels to Northern 
 Europe to visit a rural hometown’s fabled Swedish mid-summer festival. Wha
 t begins as an idyllic retreat quickly devolves into an increasingly viole
 nt and bizarre competition at the hands of a pagan cult.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230408T193000
LOCATION:Waldron Rose Firebay\, 122 S. Walnut Street Bloomington\, IN 47404
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A one-night-only screening of Midsommar (2019)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/a-one-night-only-screening-of-midsommar-2019/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>As part of 
 Constellation’s spring screening series\, we will be presenting the cult-f
 avorite horror film: <i>Midsommar</i>. Originally released in 2019\, this 
 modern folk-horror film was written and directed by Ari Aster (also known 
 for his earlier film <i>Hereditary</i>). The film received high critical a
 cclaim\, said to be “a savage yet evolved slice of Swedish folk-horror\, A
 ri Aster’s hallucinatory follow-up to Hereditary proves him a horror direc
 tor with no peer.”</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>It’s time for Summer\, or rath
 er <i>Midsommar</i> this April! The unsettling terror begins when a couple
  travels to Northern Europe to visit a rural hometown’s fabled Swedish mid
 -summer festival. What begins as an idyllic retreat quickly devolves into 
 an increasingly violent and bizarre competition at the hands of a pagan cu
 lt.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
