BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108002@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Two sets of great jazz music.  Enjoy the big band sound of the 
 Tom Walsh Jazz Ensemble for the first set.\nThe second set features the Pl
 ummer Jazz Sextet\, directed by Greg Ward\, with special guest\, guitarist
  Jeff Parker. Jeff Parker is recognized as one of contemporary music’s mos
 t versatile and innovative electric guitarists and composers. With a proli
 fic output characterized by musical ideas of angularity and logic\, he wor
 ks in a wide variety of mediums – from pop\, rock and jazz to new music – 
 using ideas informed by innovations and trends in both popular and experim
 ental forms. He creates works that explore and exploit the contrary relati
 onships between tradition and technology\, improvisation and composition\,
  and the familiar and the abstract.\nParker’s sonic palette may employ tec
 hniques from sample-based technologies\, analog and digital synthesis\, an
 d conventional and extended techniques from over 40 years of playing the g
 uitar.\nAn integral part of what has become known as “The Modern Chicago S
 ound”\, he is a longtime member of the influential indie band Tortoise\, a
 nd is also a founding member of Isotope 217˚ and Chicago Underground.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230410T193000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Tom Walsh Jazz Ens and Plummer Sextet – Special Guest Jeff Parker\,
  Guitar
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/tom-walsh-jazz-ens-and-plummer-sextet-special-gu
 est-jeff-parker-guitar/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='event_d
 escription'>\n<p>Two sets of great jazz music.  Enjoy the big band sound o
 f the Tom Walsh Jazz Ensemble for the first set.</p>\n<p>The second set fe
 atures the Plummer Jazz Sextet\, directed by Greg Ward\, with special gues
 t\, guitarist Jeff Parker. Jeff Parker is recognized as one of contemporar
 y music’s most versatile and innovative electric guitarists and composers.
  With a prolific output characterized by musical ideas of angularity and l
 ogic\, he works in a wide variety of mediums – from pop\, rock and jazz to
  new music – using ideas informed by innovations and trends in both popula
 r and experimental forms. He creates works that explore and exploit the co
 ntrary relationships between tradition and technology\, improvisation and 
 composition\, and the familiar and the abstract.</p>\n<p>Parker’s sonic pa
 lette may employ techniques from sample-based technologies\, analog and di
 gital synthesis\, and conventional and extended techniques from over 40 ye
 ars of playing the guitar.</p>\n<p>An integral part of what has become kno
 wn as “The Modern Chicago Sound”\, he is a longtime member of the influent
 ial indie band Tortoise\, and is also a founding member of Isotope 217˚ an
 d Chicago Underground.</p>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
