BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108113@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Holding onto hope when times are tough can take an awful lot of
  determination\, and sometimes\, an awful lot of determination comes in a 
 surprisingly small package. Little Orphan Annie has reminded generations o
 f theatergoers that sunshine is always right around the corner\, and now t
 he best-loved musical of all time is set to return to Bloomington in a new
  production—just as you remember it and just when we need it most.\nAnnie\
 , directed by Jenn Thompson\, features the iconic book and score\, written
  by Tony Award-winners Thomas Meehan\, Charles Strouse\, and Martin Charni
 n. This celebration of family\, optimism\, and the American spirit remains
  the ultimate cure for all the hard knocks life throws your way.\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230411T190000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230412T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Annie!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/annie/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Holding onto 
 hope when times are tough can take an awful lot of determination\, and som
 etimes\, an awful lot of determination comes in a surprisingly small packa
 ge. Little Orphan Annie has reminded generations of theatergoers that suns
 hine is always right around the corner\, and now the best-loved musical of
  all time is set to return to Bloomington in a new production—just as you 
 remember it and just when we need it most.</p>\n<p><em>Annie</em>\, direct
 ed by Jenn Thompson\, features the iconic book and score\, written by Tony
  Award-winners Thomas Meehan\, Charles Strouse\, and Martin Charnin. This 
 celebration of family\, optimism\, and the American spirit remains the ult
 imate cure for all the hard knocks life throws your way.</p>\n<p> </p>\n</
 BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
