BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108122@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Under the pretense of having a picnic\, a geologist (John Meill
 on) takes his teenage daughter (Jenny Agutter) and 6-year-old son (Luc Roe
 g) into the Australian Outback and attempts to shoot them. When he fails\,
  he turns the gun on himself\, and the two city-bred children must contend
  with harsh wilderness alone. They are saved by a chance encounter with an
  Indigenous Australian boy (David Gulpilil) on his “walkabout\,” a ritual 
 separation from his tribe. He shows them how to survive\, and in the proce
 ss underscores the disharmony between nature and modern life. [100 min\; d
 rama\, adventure\; English]  This screening will be preceded by an introdu
 ction from Chancellor Michael A. McRobbie.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230411T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. Seventh Street Bloomington\,(on the North side
  of the IU Auditorium\, across from Hoagy)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: WALKABOUT
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-walkabout/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Under the pre
 tense of having a picnic\, a geologist (John Meillon) takes his teenage da
 ughter (Jenny Agutter) and 6-year-old son (Luc Roeg) into the Australian O
 utback and attempts to shoot them. When he fails\, he turns the gun on him
 self\, and the two city-bred children must contend with harsh wilderness a
 lone. They are saved by a chance encounter with an Indigenous Australian b
 oy (David Gulpilil) on his “walkabout\,” a ritual separation from his trib
 e. He shows them how to survive\, and in the process underscores the disha
 rmony between nature and modern life. [100 min\; drama\, adventure\; Engli
 sh]  <i><strong>This screening will be preceded by an introduction from Ch
 ancellor Michael A. McRobbie.</strong></i></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
