BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108123@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Often called “the  mother of African cinema\,” Senegalese filmm
 aker Safi Faye was the first African woman to direct a commercial feature 
 film. Join visiting scholar Beti Ellerson for a conversation on Faye’s rev
 olutionary work and career\, and its lasting impact on African filmmaking.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230412T150000
LOCATION:\, Gayle Karch Cook Center Grand Hall\, Maxwell Hall\, 750 East Ki
 rkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Public Conversation: “I DARED TO MAKE A FILM”: A TRIBUTE TO THE LIF
 E AND WORK OF SAFI FAYE\, with Beti Ellerson\, the founder and director of
  the Centre for the Study of Research of African Women in Cinema
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/public-conversation-i-dared-to-make-a-film-a-tri
 bute-to-the-life-and-work-of-safi-faye-with-beti-ellerson-the-founder-and-
 director-of-the-centre-for-the-study-of-research-of-african-women-in-c/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Often called 
 “the  mother of African cinema\,” Senegalese filmmaker Safi Faye was the f
 irst African woman to direct a commercial feature film. Join visiting scho
 lar Beti Ellerson for a conversation on Faye’s revolutionary work and care
 er\, and its lasting impact on African filmmaking.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
