BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108066@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:(812) 333-7006
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, April 15 at 3 pm the Recorder Orchestra of the Mi
 d-west (ROMW) will give its first post-COVID concert at Trinity Episcopal 
 church\, downtown Bloomington\, entrance at 111 S Grant Street. The orches
 tra has members from 7 states and the program is called: ‘Bridges\, from J
 oyful to Sublime’. The program consists of music by Josquin des Prez\, Joh
 n Wilbye\, Samuel Scheidt\, several folk songs\, and a Basque carol. Music
  Director is Clea Galhano from Brazil. Admittance is free. The concert wil
 l last about 45 minutes.\nFree parking is available in the IU parking gara
 ge on 6th Street.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230415T150000
LOCATION:Trinity Episcopal church\, 111 S Grant St Bloomington\, IN 47408
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Recorder Orchestra of the Mid-west (ROMW)  Concert
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/recorder-orchestra-of-the-mid-west-romw-concert/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>On Saturday\,
  April 15 at 3 pm the Recorder Orchestra of the Mid-west (ROMW) will give 
 its first post-COVID concert at Trinity Episcopal church\, downtown Bloomi
 ngton\, entrance at 111 S Grant Street. The orchestra has members from 7 s
 tates and the program is called: ‘Bridges\, from Joyful to Sublime’. The p
 rogram consists of music by Josquin des Prez\, John Wilbye\, Samuel Scheid
 t\, several folk songs\, and a Basque carol. Music Director is Clea Galhan
 o from Brazil. Admittance is free. The concert will last about 45 minutes.
 </p>\n<div>Free parking is available in the IU parking garage on 6th Stree
 t.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
