UID:ai1ec-108242@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Independent\, alternative pop artists Tornsey and Verona Rose i
 nvite you to join in a musical experience where the two songwriters share 
 their common story with audiences – wrestling with identity\, loss\, heart
 break\, and a rediscovery of freedom.\nTheir separate\, but similar journe
 ys explore finding peace\, and community while working to heal their pain 
 and celebrate who they’ve become along the way. With lush electric guitar\
 , pop piano\, bold vocals\, energetic and yet emotional lyricism\, the two
 \nartists merge their sound to create a captivating live experience.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230415T170000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave Suite 001 (Underground)\, Bloom
 ington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:TORNSEY//VERONA ROSE//COPELAND JAMES
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/tornsey-verona-rose-copeland-james/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><span class='
 x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr
 53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzs
 f02u' dir='auto'>Independent\, alternative pop artists Tornsey and Verona 
 Rose invite you to join in a musical experience where the two songwriters 
 share their common story with audiences – wrestling with identity\, loss\,
  heartbreak\, and a rediscovery of freedom.<br />\nTheir separate\, but si
 milar journeys explore finding peace\, and community while working to heal
  their pain and celebrate who they’ve become along the way. With lush elec
 tric guitar\, pop piano\, bold vocals\, energetic and yet emotional lyrici
 sm\, the two<br />\nartists merge their sound to create a captivating live
  experience.</span></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108245@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6:30\, Concert at 7pm (donations are appreciated) danc
 e at 8pm  From the blazing hot bow of Sami Braman comes Riveter—the debut 
 solo record of original fiddle tunes\, inventively written and masterfully
  performed by the traditional roots wunderkind\, co-produced by Braman and
  legendary fiddler Brittany Haas. Known from her work with longtime Pacifi
 c Northwest string band\, The Onlies\, and as a member of Willie Watson’s 
 band\, here Braman celebrates the fiddle with a playful journey that\, ove
 r the course of ten tracks\, draws upon traditions from Appalachia to Irel
 and\, Cape Breton to Norway\, and beyond. Aptly named for the myriad fiddl
 ing styles Braman nimbly “rivets” together\, Riveter pulses with an old-ti
 me groove throughout and Braman’s sheer joy in playing her instrument roll
 s off it all in waves. Within a musical tradition where fully original wor
 ks are the exception\, Braman sets herself apart—and her compositional cho
 ps are undeniable. Supported by a stringband of fellow Nashville-based pal
 s (Emily Mann\, Jake Stargel\, and Frank Evans)\, she pushes us to imagine
  what traditionally inspired folk music can be.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230415T183000
LOCATION:The Pink Poodle\, 917 North Fairview St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sami Braman Album Release + Square Dance
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sami-braman-album-release-square-dance-at-the-pi
 nk-poodle/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 6:30\, Concert at 7pm (donations are appreciated) dance at 8pm</strong
 >  <span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928
 wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq
 8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u' dir='auto'>From the blazing hot bow of Sami Braman c
 omes Riveter—the debut solo record of original fiddle tunes\, inventively 
 written and masterfully performed by the traditional roots wunderkind\, co
 -produced by Braman and legendary fiddler Brittany Haas. Known from her wo
 rk with longtime Pacific Northwest string band\, The Onlies\, and as a mem
 ber of Willie Watson’s band\, here Braman celebrates the fiddle with a pla
 yful journey that\, over the course of ten tracks\, draws upon traditions 
 from Appalachia to Ireland\, Cape Breton to Norway\, and beyond. Aptly nam
 ed for the myriad fiddling styles Braman nimbly “rivets” together\, Rivete
 r pulses with an old-time groove throughout and Braman’s sheer joy in play
 ing her instrument rolls off it all in waves. Within a musical tradition w
 here fully original works are the exception\, Braman sets herself apart—an
 d her compositional chops are undeniable. Supported by a stringband of fel
 low Nashville-based pals (Emily Mann\, Jake Stargel\, and Frank Evans)\, s
 he pushes us to imagine what traditionally inspired folk music can be.</sp
 an></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
