BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108114@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The legendary African American Dance Company presents its Annua
 l Spring Concert on Saturday\, April 15\, 2023\, 7:30 p.m. at Buskirk-Chum
 ley Theater in Bloomington\, IN.\nDirected by Baba Stafford C. Berry Jr.\,
  the African American Dance Company shares movement traditions from Africa
 \, the diaspora\, and from African American culture. Since its founding in
  1974\, the African American Dance Company has performed throughout Indian
 a\, in New York City\, and internationally in China\, Jamaica\, and Cuba. 
 The company’s repertoire includes African dance styles\, contemporary\, mo
 dern\, jazz\, hip-hop\, and various cultural forms.\nThe African American 
 Dance Company is a course offered for credit through the Department of Afr
 ican American and African Diaspora Studies\, and is one of three performin
 g ensembles managed by African American Arts Institute at Indiana Universi
 ty Bloomington.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230415T193000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:African American Dance Company Spring Concert
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/african-american-dance-company-spring-concert-3/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='event_d
 escription'>\n<p>The legendary African American Dance Company presents its
  Annual Spring Concert on Saturday\, April 15\, 2023\, 7:30 p.m. at Buskir
 k-Chumley Theater in Bloomington\, IN.</p>\n<p>Directed by Baba Stafford C
 . Berry Jr.\, the African American Dance Company shares movement tradition
 s from Africa\, the diaspora\, and from African American culture. Since it
 s founding in 1974\, the African American Dance Company has performed thro
 ughout Indiana\, in New York City\, and internationally in China\, Jamaica
 \, and Cuba. The company’s repertoire includes African dance styles\, cont
 emporary\, modern\, jazz\, hip-hop\, and various cultural forms.</p>\n<p>T
 he African American Dance Company is a course offered for credit through t
 he Department of African American and African Diaspora Studies\, and is on
 e of three performing ensembles managed by African American Arts Institute
  at Indiana University Bloomington.</p>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
