UID:ai1ec-108115@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:t’s time for Trashion Refashion 2023 presented by Plato’s Close
 t!\nThis vibrant\, all‐ages event is a two‐part runway show featuring desi
 gns made from refashioned garments or unwanted materials including (but no
 t limited to!) paper and plastic bags\, pop tabs\, bicycle tires\, tablecl
 oths\, old clothes and even pet food containers!  Yael Ksander and Devta K
 idd will co-emcee.  Bloomington Trashion is proud to involve our community
  of creative designers\, performers\, businesses\, students and professors
  year after year.\nProceeds go to benefit the Center for Sustainable Livin
 g (CSL) and Discardia\, a CSL project whose mission is to help people reus
 e\, recycle and repurpose clothing & other textiles.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230416T190000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Trashion Refashion 2023 – A fundraiser for the Center for Sustainab
 le Living
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/trashion-refashion-2023-a-fundraiser-for-the-cen
 ter-for-sustainable-living/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>t’s time for 
 Trashion Refashion 2023 presented by Plato’s Closet!</p>\n<p>This vibrant\
 , all‐ages event is a two‐part runway show featuring designs made from ref
 ashioned garments or unwanted materials including (but not limited to!) pa
 per and plastic bags\, pop tabs\, bicycle tires\, tablecloths\, old clothe
 s and even pet food containers!  Yael Ksander and Devta Kidd will co-emcee
 .  Bloomington Trashion is proud to involve our community of creative desi
 gners\, performers\, businesses\, students and professors year after year.
 </p>\n<p>Proceeds go to benefit the Center for Sustainable Living (CSL) an
 d Discardia\, a CSL project whose mission is to help people reuse\, recycl
 e and repurpose clothing & other textiles.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
