BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108304@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Addict’s Wake delivers piercing and empathetic insight into
  one of the most serious health crises impacting our nation: the opioid ep
 idemic. Brown County is a charming\, tight-knit community but behind the s
 cenes it’s a community at war–battling an addiction crisis that is killing
  its best and brightest. The devastating fight happening in Brown County i
 s a reflection of the estimated 100\,000 overdose deaths in America just l
 ast year – each one sending families and loved ones drowning in its epic w
 ake. The film provides a revealing look at the second-by-second panic of o
 verdose and the slower burn of despair affecting nearly every family\, cla
 ssroom\, and workplace. Yet in powerful tones\, The Addict’s Wake finds ho
 pe growing to galvanize a community refusing to be defeated. Filmed over t
 wo years\, we see a community searching for answers\, and finding each oth
 er. A family’s grace\, an emerging leader\, a life saved. The Addict’s Wak
 e weaves an intimate story of hope\, redemption\, and a way forward.\nDue 
 to its content\, may not be suitable for children under 12.\nThere will be
  a panel discussion after the film. Each ticket holder can get a complimen
 tary popcorn\, soft drink/juice\, and candy!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230418T180000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:South Central Region Recovery & Hope Project: ‘Addict’s Wake\, A St
 ory of Addiction in Brown County’
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/south-central-region-recovery-hope-project-addic
 ts-wake-a-story-of-addiction-in-brown-county/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='primary
 ' class='content-area'><main id='main' class='site-main' role='main'></p>
 \n<div class='hentry'>\n<div class=' entry-content'>\n<div id='event_descr
 iption'>\n<p>The Addict’s Wake delivers piercing and empathetic insight in
 to one of the most serious health crises impacting our nation: the opioid 
 epidemic. Brown County is a charming\, tight-knit community but behind the
  scenes it’s a community at war–battling an addiction crisis that is killi
 ng its best and brightest. The devastating fight happening in Brown County
  is a reflection of the estimated 100\,000 overdose deaths in America just
  last year – each one sending families and loved ones drowning in its epic
  wake. The film provides a revealing look at the second-by-second panic of
  overdose and the slower burn of despair affecting nearly every family\, c
 lassroom\, and workplace. Yet in powerful tones\, The Addict’s Wake finds 
 hope growing to galvanize a community refusing to be defeated. Filmed over
  two years\, we see a community searching for answers\, and finding each o
 ther. A family’s grace\, an emerging leader\, a life saved. The Addict’s W
 ake weaves an intimate story of hope\, redemption\, and a way forward.</p>
 \n<p>Due to its content\, may not be suitable for children under 12.</p>\n
 <p>There will be a panel discussion after the film. Each ticket holder can
  get a complimentary popcorn\, soft drink/juice\, and candy!</p>\n</div>\n
 <div class='all_sponsors'></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p></main></div>\n</BODY
 ></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
