CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812-482-3070
DESCRIPTION:It’s only a little more than 6 weeks away! Jasper Community Art
 s’ 20th annual Chalk Walk Arts Festival\nwill once again be held at the Th
 yen-Clark Cultural Center (located at 100 3 rd Ave. Jasper\, IN 47546) on
 \nSaturday\, May 20th from 8:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m.\nChalk Walk 2023 will se
 e the return of crowd favorites\, such as tie-dye\, balloon art\, caricatu
 res\, eye-spy\nscavenger hunt\, and of course\, CHALKING!\nParticipants ar
 e encouraged to register now on Jasper Community Arts’ website\,\nwww.jasp
 erarts.org/chalkwalk. Every pre-registered participant will receive a free
  20 th Annual Chalk\nWalk tshirt among other goodies in a Chalk Walk cinch
  bag complete with a 24 count box of sidewalk\nchalk.\nRegistrants and the
 ir families are encouraged to park in the parking lot in the rear of the b
 uilding along\neast 4 th Street. Maps will be provided as activities will 
 span most of the building – indoors and outdoors.\nRegister online at jasp
 erarts.org/chalkwalk.\nIn the event of rain or inclimate weather\, many Ch
 alk Walk activities will be available inside the Thyen-\nClark Cultural Ce
 nter on May 20 th . In this instance\, bags will be available for pickup t
 hroughout the day\nso registrants can feel free to chalk at home since the
 re will be no rain date.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230420T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230420T120000
LOCATION:Thyen-Clark Cultural Center\, 100 3rd Ave. Jasper\, IN 47546
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Chalk Walk 2023 – 20th Anniversary !
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/chalk-walk-2023-20th-anniversary/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>It’s only a l
 ittle more than 6 weeks away! Jasper Community Arts’ 20th annual Chalk Wal
 k Arts Festival<br />\nwill once again be held at the Thyen-Clark Cultural
  Center (located at 100 3 rd Ave. Jasper\, IN 47546) on<br />\nSaturday\, 
 May 20th from 8:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m.<br />\nChalk Walk 2023 will see the r
 eturn of crowd favorites\, such as tie-dye\, balloon art\, caricatures\, e
 ye-spy<br />\nscavenger hunt\, and of course\, CHALKING!<br />\nParticipan
 ts are encouraged to register now on Jasper Community Arts’ website\,<br /
 >\nwww.jasperarts.org/chalkwalk. Every pre-registered participant will rec
 eive a free 20 th Annual Chalk<br />\nWalk tshirt among other goodies in a
  Chalk Walk cinch bag complete with a 24 count box of sidewalk<br />\nchal
 k.<br />\nRegistrants and their families are encouraged to park in the par
 king lot in the rear of the building along<br />\neast 4 th Street. Maps w
 ill be provided as activities will span most of the building – indoors and
  outdoors.<br />\nRegister online at jasperarts.org/chalkwalk.<br />\nIn t
 he event of rain or inclimate weather\, many Chalk Walk activities will be
  available inside the Thyen-<br />\nClark Cultural Center on May 20 th . I
 n this instance\, bags will be available for pickup throughout the day<br 
 />\nso registrants can feel free to chalk at home since there will be no r
 ain date.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108402@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Registration is open.\nJoin us on the third Thursday of the mon
 th to discuss a dynamic mix of fiction and nonfiction. This month’s select
 ion is The Seven Husbands of Evelyn Hugo by Taylor Jenkins Reid. \nSummary
 :\n“Aging and reclusive Hollywood movie icon Evelyn Hugo is finally ready 
 to tell the truth about her glamorous and scandalous life. But when she ch
 ooses unknown magazine reporter Monique Grant for the job\, no one is more
  astounded than Monique herself. Why her? Why now? Monique is not exactly 
 on top of the world. Her husband has left her\, and her professional life 
 is going nowhere. Regardless of why Evelyn has selected her to write her b
 iography\, Monique is determined to use this opportunity to jumpstart her 
 career.”\nAge 18 and up. Please register.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230420T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230420T140000
