BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108063@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:joybridy@yahoo.com
DESCRIPTION:Are the early blooming spring ephemerals catching your eye? Are
  you curious to see pawpaws budding and blooming? Are you craving a creati
 ve way to connect more with the natural world as a start to your Earth Day
 ? Come out to Nature Journaling on April 22\, 9am – Noon\, at Winslow Wood
 s Park.\nNature journaling is the process of spending time outside paying 
 attention to what we notice\, and recording these observations in a ‘natur
 e journal’ book. Techniques can include writing and drawing\, photography\
 , collage\, and any other process that appeals to you. With a goal of conn
 ecting deeply to our senses of wonder and curiosity\, our focus is less ab
 out making beautiful drawings and writings (although those sometimes happe
 n\, too)\, and more about reflecting our direct observations in nature. Jo
 in us as we gather each month to tap into our sense of awe.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230422T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230422T120000
LOCATION:Winslow Woods Park\, 2800 S Highland Ave Bloomington\, IN 47401
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Nature Journaling
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/nature-journaling/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Are the early
  blooming spring ephemerals catching your eye? Are you curious to see pawp
 aws budding and blooming? Are you craving a creative way to connect more w
 ith the natural world as a start to your Earth Day? Come out to Nature Jou
 rnaling on April 22\, 9am – Noon\, at Winslow Woods Park.</p>\n<p>Nature j
 ournaling is the process of spending time outside paying attention to what
  we notice\, and recording these observations in a ‘nature journal’ book. 
 Techniques can include writing and drawing\, photography\, collage\, and a
 ny other process that appeals to you. With a goal of connecting deeply to 
 our senses of wonder and curiosity\, our focus is less about making beauti
 ful drawings and writings (although those sometimes happen\, too)\, and mo
 re about reflecting our direct observations in nature. Join us as we gathe
 r each month to tap into our sense of awe.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
