BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108343@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A string band that produces songs spun from cautionary tales an
 d poignant remembrances punctuated with drums\, saw\, and trumpet\, Bigfoo
 t Yancey delivers action packed performances that are authentically Indian
 a. Songwriter Mike Angel\, of the historic Ford family of Brown County\, l
 eads the band while it pounds out hit after hit in a discography that date
 s back to the release of the EP “Welcome to the City” in 2015. Follow up r
 eleases including 2017’s “Hills” and 2019’s “Early Years” deliver sophisti
 cated productions that haven’t lost the raw energy of the multiple vocalis
 ts. Dig into their catalog on your favorite streaming platform and then ca
 tch Bigfoot Yancey live at the Historic Brown County Playhouse for a night
  of unforgettable music brought to you by Rainwater Studios and SERVPRO®.
 \nCrawfordsville\, Indiana’s own Bengebreakers are a three-piece indie-roc
 k dynamo led by songwriter and riff-monster Zach Benge. A self-described w
 eirdo that loves to spend time alone with his guitar\, Benge taps into a m
 usical flow that courses through his heart and out of his fingertips. His 
 enthusiasm and love for music and live performance has shown itself in pre
 vious appearances at the Historic Brown County Playhouse where he thrilled
  audiences opening for JD Simo and participating in Rainwater Studios show
 cases as a solo artist and with the Bengebreakers.\nKicking off the evenin
 g we will present the winner of the “Take the Stage” program performing a 
 brief solo acoustic set. Fans and judges will select this opening artist f
 rom 20 contestants participating in “Take the Stage” at Rainwater Studios 
 in the months of January\, February\, and March. Tune in to Rainwater Stud
 ios live on Facebook or YouTube February 24th and March 24th to participat
 e in choosing the opening act yourself!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230422T193000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 South Van Buren St\, Nashville\,
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Rainwater Studios Presents: Bigfoot Yancey\, with Bengebreakers
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/rainwater-studios-presents-bigfoot-yancey-with-b
 enchbreakers/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A string band
  that produces songs spun from cautionary tales and poignant remembrances 
 punctuated with drums\, saw\, and trumpet\, Bigfoot Yancey delivers action
  packed performances that are authentically Indiana. Songwriter Mike Angel
 \, of the historic Ford family of Brown County\, leads the band while it p
 ounds out hit after hit in a discography that dates back to the release of
  the EP “Welcome to the City” in 2015. Follow up releases including 2017’s
  “Hills” and 2019’s “Early Years” deliver sophisticated productions that h
 aven’t lost the raw energy of the multiple vocalists. Dig into their catal
 og on your favorite streaming platform and then catch Bigfoot Yancey live 
 at the Historic Brown County Playhouse for a night of unforgettable music 
 brought to you by Rainwater Studios and SERVPRO®.</p>\n<p>Crawfordsville\,
  Indiana’s own Bengebreakers are a three-piece indie-rock dynamo led by so
 ngwriter and riff-monster Zach Benge. A self-described weirdo that loves t
 o spend time alone with his guitar\, Benge taps into a musical flow that c
 ourses through his heart and out of his fingertips. His enthusiasm and lov
 e for music and live performance has shown itself in previous appearances 
 at the Historic Brown County Playhouse where he thrilled audiences opening
  for JD Simo and participating in Rainwater Studios showcases as a solo ar
 tist and with the Bengebreakers.</p>\n<p>Kicking off the evening we will p
 resent the winner of the “Take the Stage” program performing a brief solo 
 acoustic set. Fans and judges will select this opening artist from 20 cont
 estants participating in “Take the Stage” at Rainwater Studios in the mont
 hs of January\, February\, and March. Tune in to Rainwater Studios live on
  Facebook or YouTube February 24th and March 24th to participate in choosi
 ng the opening act yourself!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
