BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108523@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of the documentary The Working Hungry a
 nd a following Q&A with local community leaders. The Working Hungry is a 3
 0-minute film built around the stories of three families\, and through the
 m the stories of more than 700\,000 people across the state of Indiana. Mo
 st of these are working families\, and their hunger is hidden from those a
 round them.  \nThe compelling documentary asks why\, in a time of low unem
 ployment and food abundance\, is food insecurity and hunger so prevalent? 
 And what can be done? This film will dive deep into the reality of food in
 security in Indiana\, and what more could be done to destigmatize the conv
 ersation\, more clearly understand underlying causes\, and truly end hunge
 r. All ages.\nThis program is in partnership with Purdue Extension.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230425T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230425T200000
LOCATION:Auditorium\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 E Kirkwood Ave\, B
 loomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:‘The Working Hungry’ Film Screening and Q&A
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-working-hungry-film-screening-and-qa-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us for a
  screening of the documentary The Working Hungry and a following Q&A with 
 local community leaders. The Working Hungry is a 30-minute film built arou
 nd the stories of three families\, and through them the stories of more th
 an 700\,000 people across the state of Indiana. Most of these are working 
 families\, and their hunger is hidden from those around them.  </p>\n<p>Th
 e compelling documentary asks why\, in a time of low unemployment and food
  abundance\, is food insecurity and hunger so prevalent? And what can be d
 one? This film will dive deep into the reality of food insecurity in India
 na\, and what more could be done to destigmatize the conversation\, more c
 learly understand underlying causes\, and truly end hunger. All ages.</p>
 \n<p>This program is in partnership with Purdue Extension.</p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
END:VEVENT
