BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108541@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us as world-renowned pianist Emanuel Ax comes to Bloomingt
 on for an evening of magnificent music. His program at IU Auditorium will 
 include works by Schubert and Liszt.\nMr. Ax holds honorary doctorates of 
 music from Skidmore College\, New England Conservatory of Music\, Yale Uni
 versity\, and Columbia University\, is a Fellow of the American Academy of
  Arts and Sciences\, and has been a Sony Classical exclusive recording art
 ist since 1987. His most recent release\, Brahms Trios\, was with Yo-Yo Ma
  and Leonidas Kavakos.\nHe received Grammy Awards for the second and third
  volumes of his cycle of Haydn’s piano sonatas. He has also made a series 
 of Grammy-winning recordings of the Beethoven and Brahms sonatas for cello
  and piano with cellist Yo-Yo Ma. In 2005\, Mr. Ax contributed to an Inter
 national Emmy Award-Winning BBC documentary commemorating the Holocaust th
 at aired on the 60th anniversary of the liberation of Auschwitz. In 2013\,
  Mr. Ax’s recording Variations received the Echo Klassik Award for Solo Re
 cording of the Year.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230425T193000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Emanuel Ax
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/emanuel-ax/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us as wo
 rld-renowned pianist Emanuel Ax comes to Bloomington for an evening of mag
 nificent music. His program at IU Auditorium will include works by Schuber
 t and Liszt.</p>\n<p>Mr. Ax holds honorary doctorates of music from Skidmo
 re College\, New England Conservatory of Music\, Yale University\, and Col
 umbia University\, is a Fellow of the American Academy of Arts and Science
 s\, and has been a Sony Classical exclusive recording artist since 1987. H
 is most recent release\, Brahms Trios\, was with Yo-Yo Ma and Leonidas Kav
 akos.</p>\n<p>He received Grammy Awards for the second and third volumes o
 f his cycle of Haydn’s piano sonatas. He has also made a series of Grammy-
 winning recordings of the Beethoven and Brahms sonatas for cello and piano
  with cellist Yo-Yo Ma. In 2005\, Mr. Ax contributed to an International E
 mmy Award-Winning BBC documentary commemorating the Holocaust that aired o
 n the 60th anniversary of the liberation of Auschwitz. In 2013\, Mr. Ax’s 
 recording Variations received the Echo Klassik Award for Solo Recording of
  the Year.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
