BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-107682@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:cicadacinema@gmail.com\; cicadacinema.com
DESCRIPTION:Synopsis: This outrageously unique sci-fi headtrip was the debu
 t feature from genre film emperor John Carpenter. The film originally bega
 n as a 45-minute student film project by Carpenter and collaborator Dan O’
 Bannon (ALIEN\, THE RETURN OF THE LIVING DEAD) that was eventually expande
 d into a full length feature. The film takes place on the deep-space cruis
 er Dark Star\, where a crew of stoned astronauts (including O’Bannon himse
 lf) are assigned the task of blowing up planets with unsuitable life forms
  in order to make the universe safe for the human race. The leader is Comm
 ander Powell (Joe Sanders)\, who’s cryogenically frozen after being killed
  in a freak accident. Next in line is Doolittle (Brian Narelle) who tries 
 to keep the rest of the crew in check\, which—due to the onset of alien cr
 eatures and intergalactic existential hysteria—is a much tougher job than 
 expected.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230427T190000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave Suite 001 (Underground)\, Bloom
 ington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents Dark Star (18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-dark-star-18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Synopsis: Thi
 s outrageously unique sci-fi headtrip was the debut feature from genre fil
 m emperor John Carpenter. The film originally began as a 45-minute student
  film project by Carpenter and collaborator Dan O’Bannon (ALIEN\, THE RETU
 RN OF THE LIVING DEAD) that was eventually expanded into a full length fea
 ture. The film takes place on the deep-space cruiser Dark Star\, where a c
 rew of stoned astronauts (including O’Bannon himself) are assigned the tas
 k of blowing up planets with unsuitable life forms in order to make the un
 iverse safe for the human race. The leader is Commander Powell (Joe Sander
 s)\, who’s cryogenically frozen after being killed in a freak accident. Ne
 xt in line is Doolittle (Brian Narelle) who tries to keep the rest of the 
 crew in check\, which—due to the onset of alien creatures and intergalacti
 c existential hysteria—is a much tougher job than expected.</p>\n</BODY></
 HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
