UID:ai1ec-107689@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:info@bloomingtonwatercolor.org
DESCRIPTION:The Bloomington Watercolor Society presents an Encore Exhibit o
 f “We Paint…Historic Bloomington!”  In collaboration with the Monroe Count
 y History Center (MCHC)\, artists created watercolor paintings of Blooming
 ton’s historic buildings and homes\, early industry\, famous folks\, and m
 ore.   New paintings have been added to expand the show.\n\nThe opening re
 ception takes place Friday\, April 28 from 5:00 – 7:00 p.m. at MCHC.  In c
 onjunction with the show\, MCHC will host a paint-out on the lawn June 3 f
 rom 10-2.  All area artists are welcome to join in.\n\nThe exhibit runs Ap
 ril 25 through July 8 at the Monroe County History Center\, 212 6th Street
 \, Bloomington\, Indiana and may be viewed Tuesday through Saturday\, 10:0
 0 – 4:00.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230428T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230428T190000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E 6th St\, Bloomington\, IN 474
 08
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Bloomington Watercolor Society presents an Encore Exhibit of “W
 e Paint…Historic Bloomington!”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-bloomington-watercolor-society-presents-an-e
 ncore-exhibit-of-we-painthistoric-bloomington/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p style='font-w
 eight: 400\;'>The Bloomington Watercolor Society presents an Encore Exhibi
 t of “We Paint…Historic Bloomington!”  In collaboration with the Monroe Co
 unty History Center (MCHC)\, artists created watercolor paintings of Bloom
 ington’s historic buildings and homes\, early industry\, famous folks\, an
 d more.   New paintings have been added to expand the show.</p>\n<p style=
 'font-weight: 400\;'>\n<p style='font-weight: 400\;'>The opening reception
  takes place Friday\, April 28 from 5:00 – 7:00 p.m. at MCHC.  In conjunct
 ion with the show\, MCHC will host a paint-out on the lawn June 3 from 10-
 2.  All area artists are welcome to join in.</p>\n<p style='font-weight: 4
 00\;'>\n<p style='font-weight: 400\;'>The exhibit runs April 25 through Ju
 ly 8 at the Monroe County History Center\, 212 6<sup>th</sup> Street\, Blo
 omington\, Indiana and may be viewed Tuesday through Saturday\, 10:00 – 4:
 00.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
