BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108247@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Kiwanisbloomington.org
DESCRIPTION:Keith Klein Memorial Fund\nKlein\, a member of the MCCSC Board 
 of Directors\, was an active supporter of Kiwanis Club of Bloomington\, es
 pecially its annual fundraising pancake breakfast. Kiwanis has partnered w
 ith Foundation of MCCS to present the 2023 Kiwanis Pancake Breakfast & Ant
 ique Auto Show. At the FMCCS website\, one can find this post:\nTo honor K
 eith’s legacy a memorial fund has been created with the Foundation of Monr
 oe County Community Schools. The fund will support journalism and broadcas
 ting programs within the MCCSC.  Keith especially loved the Batchelor TV p
 rogram\; he believed it empowered young students to learn video\, editing\
 , and writing skills to tell a story.\nThe pancake breakfast proceeds will
  be divided between this exact fund and Kiwanis Youth Programs.\nKiwanis P
 ancake Breakfast & Antique Auto Show to benefit The Keith Klein Memorial F
 und and Kiwanis Youth Programs.\nThe menu is: Pancakes\, sausage\, cookie\
 , orange juice\, milk\, coffee and tea.  In Keith Klein’s honor\, Celebrit
 y Servers will plate the breakfasts.  They include Diane Daily of WGCL Rad
 io\; Monroe County Sheriff Reuben Marte\, Don Griffin\, Susan Sandberg and
  Kerry Thomson.\nThe Antique Auto Show features antique vehicles from the 
 30s and classic cars from the 40s to 60s.  Participants include members of
  The Model A Restorers Club of Columbus/Indiana Region and the Hoosier Hil
 ls Model A Restorers Club.  Attendees are encouraged to take pictures.\nTh
 e Monroe County Sheriff’s Office will display a squad car and a Polaris UT
 V\, depending upon availability\, for children to touch and tour.  A Sheri
 ff’s deputy will be on hand to meet kids and answer questions and to give 
 children 10 and under a free coloring book.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230429T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230429T110000
LOCATION:First United Church\, 2420 E 3rd St Bloomington\, IN 47401
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:2023 Kiwanis Pancake Breakfast & Antique Auto Show To Benefit Keith
  Klein Memorial Fund and Kiwanis Youth Programs
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/2023-kiwanis-pancake-breakfast-antique-auto-show
 -to-benefit-keith-klein-memorial-fund-and-kiwanis-youth-programs/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Keith Klein M
 emorial Fund<br />\nKlein\, a member of the MCCSC Board of Directors\, was
  an active supporter of Kiwanis Club of Bloomington\, especially its annua
 l fundraising pancake breakfast. Kiwanis has partnered with Foundation of 
 MCCS to present the 2023 Kiwanis Pancake Breakfast & Antique Auto Show. At
  the FMCCS website\, one can find this post:<br />\nTo honor Keith’s legac
 y a memorial fund has been created with the Foundation of Monroe County Co
 mmunity Schools. The fund will support journalism and broadcasting program
 s within the MCCSC.  Keith especially loved the Batchelor TV program\; he 
 believed it empowered young students to learn video\, editing\, and writin
 g skills to tell a story.<br />\nThe pancake breakfast proceeds will be di
 vided between this exact fund and Kiwanis Youth Programs.</p>\n<p>Kiwanis 
 Pancake Breakfast & Antique Auto Show to benefit The Keith Klein Memorial 
 Fund and Kiwanis Youth Programs.<br />\nThe menu is: Pancakes\, sausage\, 
 cookie\, orange juice\, milk\, coffee and tea.  In Keith Klein’s honor\, C
 elebrity Servers will plate the breakfasts.  They include Diane Daily of W
 GCL Radio\; Monroe County Sheriff Reuben Marte\, Don Griffin\, Susan Sandb
 erg and Kerry Thomson.<br />\nThe Antique Auto Show features antique vehic
 les from the 30s and classic cars from the 40s to 60s.  Participants inclu
 de members of The Model A Restorers Club of Columbus/Indiana Region and th
 e Hoosier Hills Model A Restorers Club.  Attendees are encouraged to take 
 pictures.<br />\nThe Monroe County Sheriff’s Office will display a squad c
 ar and a Polaris UTV\, depending upon availability\, for children to touch
  and tour.  A Sheriff’s deputy will be on hand to meet kids and answer que
 stions and to give children 10 and under a free coloring book.</p>\n</BODY
 ></HTML>
END:VEVENT
