DESCRIPTION:BRIAN! (Ithaca\, NY) https://linktr.ee/brianbassoon\nBassoon dr
 iven avant-garde trio BRIAN! return with their fifth studio album “The Cat
 aclysmic Engine”. Nine angular and heavy compositions blend whole-tone\, n
 on-western motifs with frenzied meter and tempo while taking inspiration f
 rom finding queer identity (“Rose”)\, the life blossoming from trauma (“In
 temperate to Death”)\, and embracing brevity when dealing with vulnerabili
 ty (“Smol”).\nDavid Brown + Ben Myers duo (Bloomington) https://dbinspace.
 com/ https://lather.bandcamp.com/\nImprovised sounds from two dudes with r
 egular names.\nSpiral (Bloomington) https://www.instagram.com/_spiral_band
 _/\nSaxophone-led Progressive-Metal Collective
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230429T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230429T230000
LOCATION:The I Fell Gallery\, 415 W. 4th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:BRIAN! w/ Spiral & David Brown+Ben Myers duo
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/brian-w-lather-spiral-at-i-fell/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>BRIAN! (Ithac
 a\, NY) https://linktr.ee/brianbassoon<br />\nBassoon driven avant-garde t
 rio BRIAN! return with their fifth studio album “The Cataclysmic Engine”. 
 Nine angular and heavy compositions blend whole-tone\, non-western motifs 
 with frenzied meter and tempo while taking inspiration from finding queer 
 identity (“Rose”)\, the life blossoming from trauma (“Intemperate to Death
 ”)\, and embracing brevity when dealing with vulnerability (“Smol”).</p>\n
 <p>David Brown + Ben Myers duo (Bloomington) https://dbinspace.com/ https:
 //lather.bandcamp.com/<br />\nImprovised sounds from two dudes with regula
 r names.</p>\n<p>Spiral (Bloomington) https://www.instagram.com/_spiral_ba
 nd_/<br />\nSaxophone-led Progressive-Metal Collective</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
