UID:ai1ec-108201@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:(812) 336-0909\; hgfvolunteers@gmail.com
DESCRIPTION:Bloomington Restorations\, Inc. invites you to the 2023 18th An
 nual Daisy Days Plant Sale and Museum Open Day on Saturday\, April 29\, fr
 om 11 a.m.-4 p.m. and Sunday\, April 30\, from 1-4 p.m. Plants are grown f
 rom seed\, harvested onsite\, or sourced from Spence Restoration Nursery\,
  since 1998 Indiana’s premier native plant supplier. Experts are on-hand d
 uring the sale to answer questions and guide selections. Tours of the main
  house will also be available from 1-4 p.m. on Saturday. The Farmstead is 
 listed on the National Register of Historic Places and is owned and mainta
 ined by Bloomington Restorations\, Inc.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230430T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230430T160000
LOCATION:Hinkle-Garton Farmstead\, 2920 E. 10th Street Bloomington\, IN 474
 08
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:18th Annual Daisy Days Plant Sale and Museum Open Day
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/18th-annual-daisy-days-plant-sale-and-museum-ope
 n-day-2/
