BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108848@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Come hear literature that has never been made available in Engl
 ish before! Seven translators will share their marvelous new projects. We’
 ll encounter some compelling poetry from Catalan\, Hindi\, and Japanese\; 
 witty and wise and creepy short stories from French\; and flowing Spanish 
 prose.\nThe presenters:\nRaquel Grove\, reading from The Theater of Animal
 s by Rachilde (French)\nNidhi Singh\, reading from the poetry of Kedarnath
  Singh (Hindi)\nAri Plymale\, reading from the prose of Rafael Sánchez Fer
 losio (Spanish)\nAmélie Lespilette\, reading from the fiction of Mélanie F
 azi (French)\nNuria Alishio-Caballero\, reading from the poetry of Maria-M
 ercè Marçal (Catalan)\nAvery Rist\, reading from the essays of Philippe De
 lerm (French)\nCynthia Shin\, reading from the poetry of Yoko Tawada (Japa
 nese)\nModerated by Bill Johnston\, Professor of Comparative Literature in
  the Department of Comparative Literature at IU\, and a passionate literar
 y translator.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230501T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230501T183000
LOCATION:Morgenstern's Books\, 849 Auto Mall Rd\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Read the World: An Evening of Literary Translation
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/read-the-world-an-evening-of-literary-translatio
 n/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Come hear lit
 erature that has never been made available in English before! Seven transl
 ators will share their marvelous new projects. We’ll encounter some compel
 ling poetry from Catalan\, Hindi\, and Japanese\; witty and wise and creep
 y short stories from French\; and flowing Spanish prose.<br />\nThe presen
 ters:<br />\nRaquel Grove\, reading from The Theater of Animals by Rachild
 e (French)<br />\nNidhi Singh\, reading from the poetry of Kedarnath Singh
  (Hindi)<br />\nAri Plymale\, reading from the prose of Rafael Sánchez Fer
 losio (Spanish)<br />\nAmélie Lespilette\, reading from the fiction of Mél
 anie Fazi (French)<br />\nNuria Alishio-Caballero\, reading from the poetr
 y of Maria-Mercè Marçal (Catalan)<br />\nAvery Rist\, reading from the ess
 ays of Philippe Delerm (French)<br />\nCynthia Shin\, reading from the poe
 try of Yoko Tawada (Japanese)<br />\nModerated by Bill Johnston\, Professo
 r of Comparative Literature in the Department of Comparative Literature at
  IU\, and a passionate literary translator.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
