BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-109044@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Synopsis: A struggling commercial actor camps for a month\, occ
 upying himself with historical research\, following the timeline/locations
  of Joseph Smith’s life. But as financial troubles seem to weigh heavily o
 n him (and his Domino’s Pizza commercial has still not aired yet)\, a dram
 atic detour is taken in order to get his life (and the film) back on track
 . Cash Cow was entirely self-funded and was shot alone over 30 days. “Cash
  Cow was shot alone (by me) over a month in October 2020 and plays like a 
 comedic essay/personal doc/diy diary film. I wanted it to feel sort of lik
 e a “PBS/BBC field correspondent” was left alone to make something and was
  slowly unraveling.” -Matt Barats
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230511T190000
LOCATION:Blockhouse Bar\, 205 South College Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema: CASH COW (a documentary by Matt Barats)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-cash-cow-a-documentary-by-matt-bar
 ats/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Synopsis: A s
 truggling commercial actor camps for a month\, occupying himself with hist
 orical research\, following the timeline/locations of Joseph Smith’s life.
  But as financial troubles seem to weigh heavily on him (and his Domino’s 
 Pizza commercial has still not aired yet)\, a dramatic detour is taken in 
 order to get his life (and the film) back on track. Cash Cow was entirely 
 self-funded and was shot alone over 30 days. <em>“Cash Cow was shot alone 
 (by me) over a month in October 2020 and plays like a comedic essay/person
 al doc/diy diary film. I wanted it to feel sort of like a “PBS/BBC field c
 orrespondent” was left alone to make something and was slowly unraveling.”
  -Matt Barats</em></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
