BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-109143@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A community-integrated environmental education concert program 
 celebrating the natural world through the commissioning and performance of
  new music is inspired by local environmental settings.\nIn February\, stu
 dent composers from the IU Jacobs School of Music and an environmentalist 
 from the IU Biology Department went for a hike at the IU Research and Teac
 hing Preserve. The composers wrote music based on what they heard\, saw an
 d felt on this hike. Meanwhile\, the ecologist developed curriculum based 
 on these pieces\, and student musicians were asked to perform the works at
  a final concert. The result? Half new music concert\, half ecology class\
 , all fun.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230512T180000
LOCATION:Bloomington Arts Alliance Center\, 2894 E 3rd St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Conserve Bloomington: Music for a Better Backyard
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/conserve-bloomington-music-for-a-better-backyard
 /
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> A community-
 integrated environmental education concert program celebrating the natural
  world through the commissioning and performance of new music is inspired 
 by local environmental settings.</p>\n<p>In February\, student composers f
 rom the IU Jacobs School of Music and an environmentalist from the IU Biol
 ogy Department went for a hike at the IU Research and Teaching Preserve. T
 he composers wrote music based on what they heard\, saw and felt on this h
 ike. Meanwhile\, the ecologist developed curriculum based on these pieces\
 , and student musicians were asked to perform the works at a final concert
 . The result? Half new music concert\, half ecology class\, all fun.</p>\n
 </BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
