BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108988@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.meditationinbloomington.org/may-13-kids-and-families-me
 ditation-class
DESCRIPTION:Join for the monthly kids and family meditation class on Saturd
 ays.\nIn April\, we are exploring “Growing Kindness”\nThe class is broken 
 down into bite-sized segments so kids [ages 6-12] and parents\nare engaged
  and feel inspired to integrate meditation into family life.\nEach class w
 ill follow the following format:\n> Lotus Circle of Kindness\n> Short Guid
 ed Meditation\n> Inspiration — A Short Talk\n> Activity & Snack\nYou don’t
  need to be Buddhist to benefit from this meditation class — no meditation
  experience is necessary.\nChildren must be accompanied by at least one ad
 ult\, either a parent or grandparent\, however\, families are welcome to c
 ome together! During the activity time\, Gen Chokyi will talk in more dept
 h with the parents about the teaching.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230513T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230513T160000
LOCATION:Kadampa Meditation Center Bloomington\, 234 N. Morton St. Blooming
 ton\, IN 47404
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:KIDS AND FAMILIES  MONTHLY MEDITATION CLASS
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/kids-and-families-monthly-meditation-class-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join for the 
 monthly kids and family meditation class on Saturdays.<br />\nIn April\, w
 e are exploring “Growing Kindness”</p>\n<p>The class is broken down into b
 ite-sized segments so kids [ages 6-12] and parents<br />\nare engaged and 
 feel inspired to integrate meditation into family life.</p>\n<p>Each class
  will follow the following format:<br />\n> Lotus Circle of Kindness<br />
 \n> Short Guided Meditation<br />\n> Inspiration — A Short Talk<br />\n> A
 ctivity & Snack</p>\n<p>You don’t need to be Buddhist to benefit from this
  meditation class — no meditation experience is necessary.<br />\nChildren
  must be accompanied by at least one adult\, either a parent or grandparen
 t\, however\, families are welcome to come together! During the activity t
 ime\, Gen Chokyi will talk in more depth with the parents about the teachi
 ng. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108912@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015804Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:IU Fine Arts Theater ♦ Purchase Tickets\nYou don’t have to be a
  pinball wizard to fall in love with this movie. Based on real life events
 \, Pinball is the story of Roger Sharpe\, a down-on-his-luck writer in 197
 0s New York City who has only one source of joy in life: pinball. When he 
 learns during a police raid that his passion is considered illegal gamblin
 g\, Roger sets out on a history-making mission: to overturn the ban by usi
 ng his own abilities to prove pinball is a game of skill rather than purel
 y one of chance. Mike Fasist (West Side Story) stars in this bouyant debut
  feature from filmmaking brothers Austin and Meredith Bragg captures the s
 pirit of a beloved American pastime with snappy humor and idiosyncratic ch
 aracters. (94 minutes)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230513T160000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Theater (upstairs)\, 1201 East 7th Street\, on the no
 rth side of Showalter Fountain\, next to the IU Auditorium
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: Pinball: The Man Who Saved the Game (Showings at
  4pm and 7pm)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-pinball-the-man-who-saved-the-
 game-showings-at-4pm-and-7pm/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>IU Fine Arts 
 Theater ♦ Purchase Tickets</p>\n<p>You don’t have to be a pinball wizard t
 o fall in love with this movie. Based on real life events\, Pinball is the
  story of Roger Sharpe\, a down-on-his-luck writer in 1970s New York City 
 who has only one source of joy in life: pinball. When he learns during a p
 olice raid that his passion is considered illegal gambling\, Roger sets ou
 t on a history-making mission: to overturn the ban by using his own abilit
 ies to prove pinball is a game of skill rather than purely one of chance. 
 Mike Fasist (West Side Story) stars in this bouyant debut feature from fil
 mmaking brothers Austin and Meredith Bragg captures the spirit of a belove
 d American pastime with snappy humor and idiosyncratic characters. (94 min
 utes)</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
