BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108986@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.meditationinbloomington.org/mothers-day-talk-tea-may-14
DESCRIPTION:It’s Mother’s Day — let’s celebrate together!\n“We should conte
 mplate the great kindness of all living beings. We can begin by rememberin
 g the kindness of our mother of this life”\n                              
                         — Venerable Geshe Kelsang Gyatso\nBring your mom\,
  or someone special like mom\, as a guest to this special Mother’s Day mor
 ning talk and guided meditations. The Sunday class will be followed by tea
  and scones\, please register so we can prepare for all our guests.\n10:00
  – 11:30am — Mother’s Day Talk\n11:30am – 12:30pm — Tea & Scones — please 
 register\nTEACHER\nGen Kelsang Chokyi has been practicing Kadampa Buddhism
  for 18 years and is an ordained American Buddhist nun. With joy\, wisdom\
 , and experience\, she shows how everyone can easily integrate Buddha’s te
 achings into daily life. \nEveryone is welcome\, no meditation experience 
 is necessary.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230514T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230514T130000
LOCATION:Kadampa Meditation Center Bloomington\, 234 N. Morton St. Blooming
 ton\, IN 47404
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:MOTHERS DAY TALK AND TEA
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mothers-day-talk-and-tea/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>It’s Mother’s
  Day — let’s celebrate together!</p>\n<p>“We should contemplate the great 
 kindness of all living beings. We can begin by remembering the kindness of
  our mother of this life”<br />\n                                         
              — Venerable Geshe Kelsang Gyatso</p>\n<p>Bring your mom\, or 
 someone special like mom\, as a guest to this special Mother’s Day morning
  talk and guided meditations. The Sunday class will be followed by tea and
  scones\, please register so we can prepare for all our guests.</p>\n<p>10
 :00 – 11:30am — Mother’s Day Talk<br />\n11:30am – 12:30pm — Tea & Scones 
 — please register</p>\n<p>TEACHER<br />\nGen Kelsang Chokyi has been pract
 icing Kadampa Buddhism for 18 years and is an ordained American Buddhist n
 un. With joy\, wisdom\, and experience\, she shows how everyone can easily
  integrate Buddha’s teachings into daily life. </p>\n<p>Everyone is welcom
 e\, no meditation experience is necessary.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
