BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-109021@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Midsummer Night’s Dream Overture\, by Felix Mendelssohn\nSelect
 ions from Scheherazade\, by Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov\nMar de recuerdos (Sea
  of Memories)\, by Antonio Medellín Fajardo (World Premiere)\nFirebird Sui
 te\, by Igor Stravinsky\nWhere do legends begin?\nThe BSO explores epic my
 thology as we end our 53rd season with Igor Stravinsky’s Firebird Suite. R
 imsky-Korsakov’s Scheherazade will add to the mystique\; Mendelssohn’s Mid
 summer Night’s Dream Overture introduces an element of high fantasy to the
  program. The premiere of Antonio Medellín Fajardo’s Mar de recuerdos (Sea
  of Memories) rounds out this evocative\, legendary performance. \nYour ti
 cket includes a 4:00 pre-concert conversation and Q&A with Drs. Alexis Wit
 t and Alejandro Gómez Guillén.\nLastly\, all good things must come to an e
 nd. Our conductor of the past 6 seasons\, Alejandro Gómez Guillén\, has ac
 cepted a position with the Omaha Symphony. Don’t miss this chance to watch
  him lead the BSO one last time\, and to wish him well in the next chapter
  of his career. A special Fanfare reception will be held on May 13th.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230514T170000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Symphony Orchestra presents: Imagine: Legends\, featuri
 ng Firebird and Scheherazade
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-symphony-orchestra-presents-imagine-
 legends-featuring-firebird-and-scheherazade/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Midsummer Nig
 ht’s Dream Overture\, by Felix Mendelssohn<br />\nSelections from Schehera
 zade\, by Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov<br />\nMar de recuerdos (Sea of Memories
 )\, by Antonio Medellín Fajardo (World Premiere)<br />\nFirebird Suite\, b
 y Igor Stravinsky</p>\n<p>Where do legends begin?<br />\nThe BSO explores 
 epic mythology as we end our 53rd season with Igor Stravinsky’s Firebird S
 uite. Rimsky-Korsakov’s Scheherazade will add to the mystique\; Mendelssoh
 n’s Midsummer Night’s Dream Overture introduces an element of high fantasy
  to the program. The premiere of Antonio Medellín Fajardo’s Mar de recuerd
 os (Sea of Memories) rounds out this evocative\, legendary performance. </
 p>\n<p>Your ticket includes a 4:00 pre-concert conversation and Q&A with D
 rs. Alexis Witt and Alejandro Gómez Guillén.</p>\n<p>Lastly\, all good thi
 ngs must come to an end. Our conductor of the past 6 seasons\, Alejandro G
 ómez Guillén\, has accepted a position with the Omaha Symphony. Don’t miss
  this chance to watch him lead the BSO one last time\, and to wish him wel
 l in the next chapter of his career. A special Fanfare reception will be h
 eld on May 13th.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
