CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Acclaimed writer-director Rebecca Zlotowski draws from her own 
 life to depict the emotional trajectory of Rachel (Virginie Efira)\, a sch
 oolteacher in Paris whose desire for a biological child seems increasingly
  unlikely to be fulfilled (as she’s informed by her gynecologist in a deli
 ghtful cameo from Frederick Wiseman). When Rachel enters into a relationsh
 ip with car designer Ali (Roschdy Zem)\, he’s slow to let her know that he
 ’s a single father\, but once she finds out she quickly grows to love his 
 precocious daughter\, Leila.\nFrance  104 min
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230519T193000
LOCATION:IU Radio & Television Theater (RTV 251)\, 1229 East 7th St\, Bloom
 ington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230526T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: OTHER PEOPLE’S CHILDREN
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-other-peoples-children/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Acclaimed wri
 ter-director Rebecca Zlotowski draws from her own life to depict the emoti
 onal trajectory of Rachel (Virginie Efira)\, a schoolteacher in Paris whos
 e desire for a biological child seems increasingly unlikely to be fulfille
 d (as she’s informed by her gynecologist in a delightful cameo from Freder
 ick Wiseman). When Rachel enters into a relationship with car designer Ali
  (Roschdy Zem)\, he’s slow to let her know that he’s a single father\, but
  once she finds out she quickly grows to love his precocious daughter\, Le
 ila.</p>\n<p>France  104 min</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-109229@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Carole King & James Taylor Story takes you on an incredible
  journey through the career of the six-time Grammy Award winner and 20-tim
 e platinum hit maker Carole King and five-time Grammy Award winner America
 n folk legend James Taylor. This new “show-umentary” format gives a fascin
 ating insight into the lives behind the music. Featuring passionate rendit
 ions of Fire and Rain\, Sweet Baby James\, I Feel the Earth Move\, Natural
  Woman\, You’ve Got a Friend and many more this astonishing back catalogue
  is realised with authenticity by Phoebe Katis and Dan Clews\, both well e
 stablished artists in their own right.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230519T193000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 South Van Buren St\, Nashville\,
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Carole King and James Taylor Story
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-carole-king-and-james-taylor-story/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The Carole Ki
 ng & James Taylor Story takes you on an incredible journey through the car
 eer of the six-time Grammy Award winner and 20-time platinum hit maker Car
 ole King and five-time Grammy Award winner American folk legend James Tayl
 or. This new “show-umentary” format gives a fascinating insight into the l
 ives behind the music. Featuring passionate renditions of Fire and Rain\, 
 Sweet Baby James\, I Feel the Earth Move\, Natural Woman\, You’ve Got a Fr
 iend and many more this astonishing back catalogue is realised with authen
 ticity by Phoebe Katis and Dan Clews\, both well established artists in th
 eir own right.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
