BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-108987@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.meditationinbloomington.org/apr-22-taming-the-wild-elep
 hant-mind-silent-meditation-retreat
DESCRIPTION:Unplug and enjoy a morning of silence guided by Gen Kelsang Cho
 kyi.\nWe all know that meditation is beneficial. Perhaps\, we started a pr
 actice and it’s off track as life commitments have taken over. Or\, maybe 
 we’ve wanted to started a daily meditation practice and aren’t sure where 
 to begin. \n“When the turbulence of distracting thoughts subsides and our 
 mind becomes still\, a deep happiness and contentment naturally arises fro
 m within. This feeling of contentment and well-being helps us to cope with
  the busyness and difficulties\nof daily life. So much of the stress and t
 ension we normally experience comes from our mind\, and many of the proble
 ms we experience\, including ill health\, are caused or aggravated by this
  stress.”\n— Venerable Geshe Kelsang Gyatso
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230520T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230520T130000
LOCATION:Kadampa Meditation Center Bloomington\, 234 N. Morton St. Blooming
 ton\, IN 47404
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:JUMP START YOUR MEDITATION PRACTICE
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/jump-start-your-meditation-practice/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Unplug and en
 joy a morning of silence guided by Gen Kelsang Chokyi.</p>\n<p>We all know
  that meditation is beneficial. Perhaps\, we started a practice and it’s o
 ff track as life commitments have taken over. Or\, maybe we’ve wanted to s
 tarted a daily meditation practice and aren’t sure where to begin. </p>\n<
 p>“When the turbulence of distracting thoughts subsides and our mind becom
 es still\, a deep happiness and contentment naturally arises from within. 
 This feeling of contentment and well-being helps us to cope with the busyn
 ess and difficulties<br />\nof daily life. So much of the stress and tensi
 on we normally experience comes from our mind\, and many of the problems w
 e experience\, including ill health\, are caused or aggravated by this str
 ess.”</p>\n<p>— Venerable Geshe Kelsang Gyatso</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
