BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-109587@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:During the 18th century\, Spain rebelled against the operatic b
 oom of France and Italy\, giving birth to Spanish music-theater\, embodyin
 g deep ties to folk and Gitano culture through entertainment and celebrati
 on without regard for social class. Old\, young\, rich\, and poor spilled 
 out into the streets\, ready to dance their beloved fandango. This vibrant
  performance brings Iberian Baroque decadently to life\, with a surprise e
 nding that will thrill even the most stoic of listeners.  (Melbourne\, Aus
 tralia)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230527T180000
LOCATION:Lotus Firebay\, 105 South Rogers St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mamás Bravas\, plus a Pre-Concert Discussion at: 5:45pm
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mamas-bravas-plus-a-pre-concert-discussion-at-54
 5pm/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>During the 18
 th century\, Spain rebelled against the operatic boom of France and Italy\
 , giving birth to Spanish music-theater\, embodying deep ties to folk and 
 Gitano culture through entertainment and celebration without regard for so
 cial class. Old\, young\, rich\, and poor spilled out into the streets\, r
 eady to dance their beloved fandango. This vibrant performance brings Iber
 ian Baroque decadently to life\, with a surprise ending that will thrill e
 ven the most stoic of listeners.  (Melbourne\, Australia)</p>\n</BODY></HT
 ML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-109521@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
