CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Registration is open This workshop focuses on Positive Approach
  to Care “care partnering” techniques\, including Positive Physical Approa
 ch™ (PPA) and Hand Under Hand™ (HUH). These newly learned skills enable ca
 re partners to shift from simply “dealing with the behaviors” to creating 
 a positive and caring environment. Learners develop observational skills n
 eeded to recognize signals of “unmet needs and growing distress” in the pe
 rson they care for and respond in a way that reduces anxiety and improves 
 quality of life. Age 18 and up. Please register.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230608T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230608T120000
LOCATION:Program Room 2B\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 E. Kirkwood A
 ve.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Caregiver University: A Positive Approach to Care (Age 18 and up)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/caregiver-university-a-positive-approach-to-care
 -age-18-and-up/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Regis
 tration is open</strong> This workshop focuses on Positive Approach to Car
 e “care partnering” techniques\, including Positive Physical Approach™ (PP
 A) and Hand Under Hand™ (HUH). These newly learned skills enable care part
 ners to shift from simply “dealing with the behaviors” to creating a posit
 ive and caring environment. Learners develop observational skills needed t
 o recognize signals of “unmet needs and growing distress” in the person th
 ey care for and respond in a way that reduces anxiety and improves quality
  of life. Age 18 and up. Please register.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
