BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-110062@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Juniper Art Gallery & Women Writing for (a) Change invite you t
 o a Community Read-Around\, lifting up voices from recent WWFC writing cir
 cles. Please join us for poetry\, prose\, stories\, and musings. Enjoy a l
 ate afternoon at Juniper Art Gallery with art\, writing and community. Fre
 e and open to the public.\n“Make up a story… For our sake and yours forget
  your name in the street\; tell us what the world has been to you in the d
 ark places and in the light. Don’t tell us what to believe\, what to fear.
  Show us belief’s wide skirt and the stitch that unravels fear’s caul.” – 
 Toni Morrison\, The Nobel Lecture in Literature\, 1993
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230614T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230614T180000
LOCATION:Juniper Art Gallery\, 615 W. Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Community Read Around
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/community-read-around/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Juniper Art G
 allery & Women Writing for (a) Change invite you to a Community Read-Aroun
 d\, lifting up voices from recent WWFC writing circles. Please join us for
  poetry\, prose\, stories\, and musings. Enjoy a late afternoon at Juniper
  Art Gallery with art\, writing and community. Free and open to the public
 .<br />\n“Make up a story… For our sake and yours forget your name in the 
 street\; tell us what the world has been to you in the dark places and in 
 the light. Don’t tell us what to believe\, what to fear. Show us belief’s 
 wide skirt and the stitch that unravels fear’s caul.” – Toni Morrison\, Th
 e Nobel Lecture in Literature\, 1993</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
