UID:ai1ec-109779@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:info@soulcraftbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The fire is in the sky and on the earth. The story begins. You 
 enter a different world\, a myth\, a time before time\, and the longest da
 ys of the year. Step into a world of soul stirring story meant to take hol
 d of your heart and bring it alive! Using an ancient story as our guide\, 
 we will surround the Summer Solstice with a new understanding of the unrav
 eling that happens before a new weaving and blossoming\, preparing our sou
 ls for the time of growth\, abundance\, and harvest. This is a two-part ou
 tdoor experience for adults only. Limited seats\, register on the website 
 at www.soulcraftbloomington.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230616T190000
LOCATION:Soulcraft Bloomington\, 3370 East Bethel Ln Bloomington\, IN
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230623T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mythic Evening: The Weaving
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mythic-evening-the-weaving/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> The fire is 
 in the sky and on the earth. The story begins. You enter a different world
 \, a myth\, a time before time\, and the longest days of the year. Step in
 to a world of soul stirring story meant to take hold of your heart and bri
 ng it alive! Using an ancient story as our guide\, we will surround the Su
 mmer Solstice with a new understanding of the unraveling that happens befo
 re a new weaving and blossoming\, preparing our souls for the time of grow
 th\, abundance\, and harvest. This is a two-part outdoor experience for ad
 ults only. Limited seats\, register on the website at www.soulcraftbloomin
 gton.com</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-110153@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Pietro\, a city boy\, and Bruno\, raised in the Alps\, meet as 
 11-year-olds one summer in Grana—a forgotten mountain village in northwest
 ern Italy. Their friendship grows through subsequent summer visits\, intro
 ducing them to love and loss\, reminding them of their origins\, letting t
 heir destinies unfold.\nAdapting Paolo Cognetti’s prize-winning 2016 novel
 \, directors Felix van Groeningen and Charlotte Vandermeersch craft an exq
 uisite\, rapturous epic of camaraderie and the physical spaces that define
  a relationship. Van Groeningen’s longtime cinematographer\, Ruben Impens\
 , imparts breathtaking\, meticulously composed visuals to this deeply affe
 cting epic of harmony and friction with the natural world. Winner of the J
 ury Prize at the 2022 Cannes Film Festival.\nItaly  subtitled  147 minute
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230616T190000
LOCATION:IU Radio & Television Theater (RTV 251)\, 1229 East 7th St\, Bloom
 ington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230623T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: THE EIGHT MOUNTAINS
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-the-eight-mountains/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Pietro\, a ci
 ty boy\, and Bruno\, raised in the Alps\, meet as 11-year-olds one summer 
 in Grana—a forgotten mountain village in northwestern Italy. Their friends
 hip grows through subsequent summer visits\, introducing them to love and 
 loss\, reminding them of their origins\, letting their destinies unfold.</
 p>\n<p>Adapting Paolo Cognetti’s prize-winning 2016 novel\, directors Feli
 x van Groeningen and Charlotte Vandermeersch craft an exquisite\, rapturou
 s epic of camaraderie and the physical spaces that define a relationship. 
 Van Groeningen’s longtime cinematographer\, Ruben Impens\, imparts breatht
 aking\, meticulously composed visuals to this deeply affecting epic of har
 mony and friction with the natural world. Winner of the Jury Prize at the 
 2022 Cannes Film Festival.</p>\n<p>Italy  subtitled  147 minute</p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
