BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-110442@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Shana Ritter and Barb Schwegman have shared writing together si
 nce the 1980’s. Although they come from different backgrounds\, their poem
 s share common themes: place\, family\, love\, loss\, and resilience. Barb
 ’s book\, Nightwalking\, explores familial relationships and human connect
 ion. Shana has published poetry\, short stories and a novel\, In the Time 
 of Leaving.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230623T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230623T150000
LOCATION:Juniper Art Gallery\, 615 W. Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Poetry in Conversation with Shana Ritter and Barb Schwegman
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/poetry-in-conversation-with-shana-ritter-and-bar
 b-schwegman/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Shana Ritter 
 and Barb Schwegman have shared writing together since the 1980’s. Although
  they come from different backgrounds\, their poems share common themes: p
 lace\, family\, love\, loss\, and resilience. Barb’s book\, Nightwalking\,
  explores familial relationships and human connection. Shana has published
  poetry\, short stories and a novel\, In the Time of Leaving.</p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
END:VEVENT
