BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-110405@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Tokyo Story is the crowning achievement of the unparalleled Yas
 ujirō Ozu. The film\, which follows an aging couple’s journey to visit the
 ir grown children in bustling postwar Tokyo\, surveys the rich and complex
  world of family life with the director’s customary delicacy and incisive 
 perspective on social mores. Featuring lovely performances from Ozu regula
 rs Chishu Ryu and Setsuko Hara\, Tokyo Story plumbs and deepens the direct
 or’s recurring theme of generational conflict\, creating what is without q
 uestion one of cinema’s mightiest masterpieces. [136 min\; drama\; Japanes
 e with English subtitles]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230624T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. Seventh Street Bloomington\,(on the North side
  of the IU Auditorium\, across from Hoagy)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: TOKYO STORY
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-tokyo-story/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Tokyo Story i
 s the crowning achievement of the unparalleled Yasujirō Ozu. The film\, wh
 ich follows an aging couple’s journey to visit their grown children in bus
 tling postwar Tokyo\, surveys the rich and complex world of family life wi
 th the director’s customary delicacy and incisive perspective on social mo
 res. Featuring lovely performances from Ozu regulars Chishu Ryu and Setsuk
 o Hara\, Tokyo Story plumbs and deepens the director’s recurring theme of 
 generational conflict\, creating what is without question one of cinema’s 
 mightiest masterpieces. [136 min\; drama\; Japanese with English subtitles
 ]</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
