CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Ben Myers\; 317-313-1501\; soundsfromtheblackhole@gmail.com\; https
 ://www.facebook.com/SoundsFromTheBlackHole/
DESCRIPTION:Sounds From the Black Hole\na concert series featuring experime
 ntal music and explorations of sound\, occurring every 4th Saturday of the
  month. This month features live video manipulations by Learn Not To.\n$7 
 /// ALL-AGES TICKETS AT ORBITBTOWN.COM\nAdeptive Radiation: Lineup #100 of
  Adeptive Radiation is the trio of John Hardwick\, Matt Rouge and John Kni
 ght. Formed in 2005 in tribute to Bloomington 80-90s (moved to Louisville 
 in 1995) freeform rock band The Belgian Waffles!\, they put their own twis
 t on the Midwest out-rock perspective–not playing outright covers but reco
 nceptualizing The Belgian Waffles! into a different band that could have b
 een–a horse of a different color. (Indianapolis\, etc.) https://adeptivera
 diation.bandcamp.com/\nLather: Psychedelic noise with your host\, performi
 ng a full set at home before embarking on a weeklong Midwest tour. (Bloomi
 ngton) https://lather.bandcamp.com/\ntwo bands from Canada: This odd duck 
 sent me a list of things they might do. You’ll just have to be there to se
 e what flies in. (Bloomington) https://twobandsfromcanada.bandcamp.com/\nT
 ickets: https://www.orbitbtown.com/events.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230624T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230624T230000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave Suite 001 (Underground)\, Bloom
 ington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds From the Black Hole: Adeptive Radiation / Lather / two bands
  from Canada
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-adeptive-radiation-la
 ther-two-bands-from-canada/
X-COST-TYPE:external
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Sounds From t
 he Black Hole<br />\na concert series featuring experimental music and exp
 lorations of sound\, occurring every 4th Saturday of the month. This month
  features live video manipulations by Learn Not To.<br />\n$7 /// ALL-AGES
  TICKETS AT ORBITBTOWN.COM<br />\nAdeptive Radiation: Lineup #100 of Adept
 ive Radiation is the trio of John Hardwick\, Matt Rouge and John Knight. F
 ormed in 2005 in tribute to Bloomington 80-90s (moved to Louisville in 199
 5) freeform rock band The Belgian Waffles!\, they put their own twist on t
 he Midwest out-rock perspective–not playing outright covers but reconceptu
 alizing The Belgian Waffles! into a different band that could have been–a 
 horse of a different color. (Indianapolis\, etc.) https://adeptiveradiatio
 n.bandcamp.com/</p>\n<p>Lather: Psychedelic noise with your host\, perform
 ing a full set at home before embarking on a weeklong Midwest tour. (Bloom
 ington) https://lather.bandcamp.com/</p>\n<p>two bands from Canada: This o
 dd duck sent me a list of things they might do. You’ll just have to be the
 re to see what flies in. (Bloomington) https://twobandsfromcanada.bandcamp
 .com/</p>\n<p>Tickets: <a class='ai1ec-ticket-url-exported' href='https://
 www.orbitbtown.com/events'>https://www.orbitbtown.com/events</a>.</p></BOD
 Y></HTML>
X-COST:$7
X-TICKETS-URL:https://www.orbitbtown.com/events
END:VEVENT
