CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://mediaschool.indiana.edu/news-events/events/event.html?p=250
 18
DESCRIPTION:Sound poetry\, performance art\, or just composing words to be 
 heard out loud\, call it what you will. The Electroacoustical Poetical Soc
 iety is offering a fun afternoon workshop to explore the sound in words an
 d the ideas in sound for performance. The workshop will begin with example
 s for discussion and then explore the joys of making words and sounds into
  equal partners.\nBring a short poem or just bring yourself with your voic
 e or instrument.\nThe workshop will be led by Marjorie Van Halteren\, Bria
 n Price\, and Tony Brewer. The event is sponsored by Writers Guild at Bloo
 mington\, Urban Deer Performance Series\, Indiana Arts Commission\, Bloomi
 ngton Arts Commission\, and The Media School.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230628T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230628T160000
LOCATION:Wells Library Moving Image Archive Screening room 048 1320 E 10th 
 St Bloomington IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Electroacoustical poetical society workshop
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/electroacoustical-poetical-society-workshop/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Sound poetry\
 , performance art\, or just composing words to be heard out loud\, call it
  what you will. The Electroacoustical Poetical Society is offering a fun a
 fternoon workshop to explore the sound in words and the ideas in sound for
  performance. The workshop will begin with examples for discussion and the
 n explore the joys of making words and sounds into equal partners.</p>\n<p
 >Bring a short poem or just bring yourself with your voice or instrument.<
 /p>\n<p>The workshop will be led by Marjorie Van Halteren\, Brian Price\, 
 and Tony Brewer. The event is sponsored by Writers Guild at Bloomington\, 
 Urban Deer Performance Series\, Indiana Arts Commission\, Bloomington Arts
  Commission\, and The Media School.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
