UID:ai1ec-110550@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:New English speakers will practice everyday language skills in 
 a relaxed\, informal atmosphere. Learners will enjoy friendly conversation
 \, learn about daily life in the U.S.\, gain confidence\, and meet new peo
 ple from around the world. \nIntermediate English skills are suggested. If
  you do not speak English\, please fill out the VITAL Services form to lea
 rn about programs for beginners. Conversation Groups are drop-in and no re
 gistration is needed.\nIf you have not attended a VITAL program before\, p
 lease stop by the office for more information (Downtown Library\, second f
 loor).
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230630T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230630T133000
LOCATION:VITAL Classroom\, 2nd floor\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 E
 ast Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:VITAL English Language Group: Conversation with Shane Tang
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/vital-english-language-group-conversation-with-s
 hane-tang-3/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>New English s
 peakers will practice everyday language skills in a relaxed\, informal atm
 osphere. Learners will enjoy friendly conversation\, learn about daily lif
 e in the U.S.\, gain confidence\, and meet new people from around the worl
 d. </p>\n<p>Intermediate English skills are suggested. If you do not speak
  English\, please fill out the VITAL Services form to learn about programs
  for beginners. Conversation Groups are drop-in and no registration is nee
 ded.</p>\n<p>If you have not attended a VITAL program before\, please stop
  by the office for more information (Downtown Library\, second floor).   <
 /p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
