DESCRIPTION:Come meet Potato the opossum\, Felix the American kestrel\, and
  learn about wildlife with WildCare Inc.! WildCare is a primarily voluntee
 r-led wildlife rehabilitation facility located in Bloomington. Annually\, 
 1\,400 ill\, injured\, or orphaned animals receive treatment under the car
 e protocols of volunteers and seven permitted wildlife rehabilitators\, wi
 th the goal of their eventual release back into the wild. All ages.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230715T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230715T153000
LOCATION:Meeting Room 1B & 1C Combo\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 Ea
 st Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:WildCare Inc. Animal Meet-and-Greet (All ages)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/wildcare-inc-animal-meet-and-greet-all-ages/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Come meet Pot
 ato the opossum\, Felix the American kestrel\, and learn about wildlife wi
 th WildCare Inc.! WildCare is a primarily volunteer-led wildlife rehabilit
 ation facility located in Bloomington. Annually\, 1\,400 ill\, injured\, o
 r orphaned animals receive treatment under the care protocols of volunteer
 s and seven permitted wildlife rehabilitators\, with the goal of their eve
 ntual release back into the wild. All ages.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-110919@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Terrace Concert | 3 – 9 p.m. | Join us on our terrace for live 
 music! We will be presenting alternative and jazz sounds from these local 
 artists:\n    THiN LiNES\n    JSoM Jazz Combo\n    Too Many Cooks\n    Pre
 mium Blend\nCurator Pop Up Talks | 4 & 5 p.m. | Interested in learning mor
 e about the intersection between art and music? Join our curators for a po
 p up talk in our galleries.\nArt-Making in Roehm Family Studio | 3 – 6 p.m
 . | Make some art of your own! Explore your creative process and take part
  in collaborative art making inspired by the work of McArthur Binion.
