BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-110259@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:amseader@gmail.com\; https://buskirkchumley.org/event/proof/
DESCRIPTION:“Description: As its inaugural production\, Off-Night Productio
 ns presents Proof by David Auburn. This Pulitzer Prize-winning play is ful
 l of humor and compassion\, even as it explores tragedy\, stigma\, and sex
 ism in one family and within the larger world of academia.\nDramatist’s Pl
 ay Service summarizes Proof: “On the eve of her twenty-fifth birthday\, Ca
 therine\, a troubled young woman\, has spent years caring for her brillian
 t but unstable father\, a famous mathematician. Now\, following his death\
 , she must deal with her own volatile emotions\; the arrival of her estran
 ged sister\, Claire\; and the attentions of Hal\, a former student of her 
 father’s who hopes to find valuable work in the 103 notebooks that her fat
 her left behind. Over the long weekend that follows\, a burgeoning romance
  and the discovery of a mysterious notebook draw Catherine into the most d
 ifficult problem of all: How much of her father’s madness or genius-will s
 he inherit?”\nOff Night Productions is a female-lead production company pr
 oducing contemporary theatre and music in Bloomington\, Indiana. Learn mor
 e at www.onptheatre.weebly.com.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230716T190000
LOCATION:Waldron Firebay Theatre\, in the John Waldron Arts Center\, (122 S
  Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN\, 47404)
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230717T190000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230718T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Off Night Productions presents “Proof”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/off-night-productions-presents-proof/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>“Description:
  As its inaugural production\, Off-Night Productions presents Proof by Dav
 id Auburn. This Pulitzer Prize-winning play is full of humor and compassio
 n\, even as it explores tragedy\, stigma\, and sexism in one family and wi
 thin the larger world of academia.</p>\n<p>Dramatist’s Play Service summar
 izes Proof: “On the eve of her twenty-fifth birthday\, Catherine\, a troub
 led young woman\, has spent years caring for her brilliant but unstable fa
 ther\, a famous mathematician. Now\, following his death\, she must deal w
 ith her own volatile emotions\; the arrival of her estranged sister\, Clai
 re\; and the attentions of Hal\, a former student of her father’s who hope
 s to find valuable work in the 103 notebooks that her father left behind. 
 Over the long weekend that follows\, a burgeoning romance and the discover
 y of a mysterious notebook draw Catherine into the most difficult problem 
 of all: How much of her father’s madness or genius-will she inherit?”</p>
 \n<p>Off Night Productions is a female-lead production company producing c
 ontemporary theatre and music in Bloomington\, Indiana. Learn more at www.
 onptheatre.weebly.com.” </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
