BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111142@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Duke is set in England in 1961 and is the true story of Kem
 pton Bunton\, a 60-year old taxi driver\, who stole Goya’s portrait of the
  Duke of Wellington from the National Gallery in London. It was the first 
 (and remains the only) theft in the Gallery’s history. Kempton sent ransom
  notes saying that he would return the painting on condition that the gove
 rnment agreed to provide television for free to the elderly. (This was lon
 g before the advent of Netflix and Hulu. If Kempton were planning his heis
 t today\, he’d have to steal a dozen Goyas to cover the cost of streaming 
 platforms.)\nWhat happened next became the stuff of legend. Only 50 years 
 later did the full story emerge – a startling revelation of how a good man
  set out to change the world and in so doing saved his son and his marriag
 e. Jim Broadbent and Helen Mirren star. The Duke is directed by Roger Mitc
 hell\, who died last year\, and has been compared to the classic British E
 aling comedies of the 1950s.\nCo-feature: The Thief Collector
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230721T193000
LOCATION:IU Radio & Television Theater (RTV 251)\, 1229 East 7th St\, Bloom
 ington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230728T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: THE DUKE
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-the-duke/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The Duke is s
 et in England in 1961 and is the true story of Kempton Bunton\, a 60-year 
 old taxi driver\, who stole Goya’s portrait of the Duke of Wellington from
  the National Gallery in London. It was the first (and remains the only) t
 heft in the Gallery’s history. Kempton sent ransom notes saying that he wo
 uld return the painting on condition that the government agreed to provide
  television for free to the elderly. (This was long before the advent of N
 etflix and Hulu. If Kempton were planning his heist today\, he’d have to s
 teal a dozen Goyas to cover the cost of streaming platforms.)</p>\n<p>What
  happened next became the stuff of legend. Only 50 years later did the ful
 l story emerge – a startling revelation of how a good man set out to chang
 e the world and in so doing saved his son and his marriage. Jim Broadbent 
 and Helen Mirren star. The Duke is directed by Roger Mitchell\, who died l
 ast year\, and has been compared to the classic British Ealing comedies of
  the 1950s.</p>\n<p>Co-feature: The Thief Collector</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111060@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Synopsis: Los Angeles painter Arthur Blue (Peter Coyote) and bu
 sinessman Eli Kahn (Nick Mancuso) are the best of friends\, commiserating 
 and competing always\, whether on the racquetball court or in the singles 
 bar. When Blue’s long-term girlfriend Cyd (Kathryn Harrold) leaves him for
  a more successful artist and Eli’s father passes away\, they each fall fo
 r a beguiling French art gallery manager\, and their fragmented bromance e
 nters crisis mode. The late Carol Wayne (The Tonight Show and Surf II) co-
 stars and leaves a lasting impression as Blue’s sad artistic muse and some
 time lover.\nTickets: https://cicadacinema.com/products/heartbreakers-july
 -21-backspace-gallery-8pm.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230721T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230721T220000
LOCATION:Backspace Gallery\, 112 W 6th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents “Heartbreakers” (1984)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-heartbreakers-1984/
X-COST-TYPE:external
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Synopsis: </s
 pan>Los Angeles painter Arthur Blue (Peter Coyote) and businessman Eli Kah
 n (Nick Mancuso) are the best of friends\, commiserating and competing alw
 ays\, whether on the racquetball court or in the singles bar. When Blue’s 
 long-term girlfriend Cyd (Kathryn Harrold) leaves him for a more successfu
 l artist and Eli’s father passes away\, they each fall for a beguiling Fre
 nch art gallery manager\, and their fragmented bromance enters crisis mode
 . The late Carol Wayne (The Tonight Show and Surf II) co-stars and leaves 
 a lasting impression as Blue’s sad artistic muse and sometime lover.</p>\n
 <p>Tickets: <a class='ai1ec-ticket-url-exported' href='https://cicadacinem
 a.com/products/heartbreakers-july-21-backspace-gallery-8pm'>https://cicada
 cinema.com/products/heartbreakers-july-21-backspace-gallery-8pm</a>.</p></
 BODY></HTML>
X-COST:$8
X-TICKETS-URL:https://cicadacinema.com/products/heartbreakers-july-21-backs
 pace-gallery-8pm
END:VEVENT
