BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111209@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Monroe County Health Equity Council (MCHEC) wants residents
  of Monroe County to be aware of an upcoming decision the City will make r
 egarding Cascades Park.  Specifically\, the Bloomington City Council will 
 discuss vehicular access within Lower Cascades Park. More information can 
 be found here: https://indianapublicmedia.org/…/hamilton-asks-city…. The d
 iscussion may involve access to the park and park use by all residents\, i
 ncluding vehicular and pedestrian use.\nMCHEC encourages all residents to 
 find out more on their own.  One opportunity for that is a Town Hall meeti
 ng at the park in the Waterfall Shelter on July 22 from 1:30 – 3:00 p.m. S
 ome City Council members will be present.  You can also attend City Counci
 l meetings addressing this decision.  The first reading will be on July 26
 \, and discussion and public comment will be on August 2 for the second re
 ading. City Council meetings start at 6:30 p.m.  You may attend in person 
 or virtually.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230722T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230722T150000
LOCATION:Waterfall Shelter\, Lower Cascades Park\, 2851 Old State Rd 37\, B
 loomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Town Hall Meeting to discuss possible Lower Cascades Park Road clos
 ure
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/town-hall-meeting-to-discuss-possible-lower-casc
 ades-park-road-closure/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The Monroe Co
 unty Health Equity Council (MCHEC) wants residents of Monroe County to be 
 aware of an upcoming decision the City will make regarding Cascades Park. 
  Specifically\, the Bloomington City Council will discuss vehicular access
  within Lower Cascades Park. More information can be found here: https://i
 ndianapublicmedia.org/…/hamilton-asks-city…. The discussion may involve ac
 cess to the park and park use by all residents\, including vehicular and p
 edestrian use.<br />\nMCHEC encourages all residents to find out more on t
 heir own.  One opportunity for that is a Town Hall meeting at the park in 
 the Waterfall Shelter on July 22 from 1:30 – 3:00 p.m. Some City Council m
 embers will be present.  You can also attend City Council meetings address
 ing this decision.  The first reading will be on July 26\, and discussion 
 and public comment will be on August 2 for the second reading. City Counci
 l meetings start at 6:30 p.m.  You may attend in person or virtually.</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
