BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111231@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in converting your old home movie recordings
 \, printed photographs\, or slides into a digital format you can share onl
 ine? Preserving your memories\, archiving\, and sharing them can be a powe
 rful way to connect with friends and family. In this open house\, we’ll te
 ach you how to create digital files using our Memory Preservation Station.
  You can use a cloud storage account like Google Drive\, Microsoft OneDriv
 e\, or Dropbox to save your content. Another option is to use a USB flash 
 drive––you can bring your own or check one out from the Library for tempor
 ary use. Age 18 and up.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230726T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230726T160000
LOCATION:Level Up\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 East Kirkwood Ave\, 
 Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Preserving Memories (18 and up)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/preserving-memories-18-and-up/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Are you inter
 ested in converting your old home movie recordings\, printed photographs\,
  or slides into a digital format you can share online? Preserving your mem
 ories\, archiving\, and sharing them can be a powerful way to connect with
  friends and family. In this open house\, we’ll teach you how to create di
 gital files using our Memory Preservation Station. You can use a cloud sto
 rage account like Google Drive\, Microsoft OneDrive\, or Dropbox to save y
 our content. Another option is to use a USB flash drive––you can bring you
 r own or check one out from the Library for temporary use. Age 18 and up. 
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
