BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111307@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Registration is open.\nJoin this book club to discuss nature-fo
 cused reads each month. You’ll also learn how to become more ecologically-
 minded through activities and speakers designed to enhance our reading. Jo
 in us at the Library for leaf pounding on fabric while we discuss Prodigal
  Summer by Barbara Kingsolver.\nSummary:\nProdigal Summer takes place over
  a sprawling\, humid summer in the Appalachian Mountains. Kingsolver write
 s three love stories that weave into the natural world into the lives of h
 umans living within it. A wildlife biologist\, an entomologist and an elde
 rly man working to restore the extinct American Chestnut tree swap perspec
 tives in this story of love amidst people having differing viewpoints on h
 ow to be in relation with the land and its creatures. It’s the perfect boo
 k for the high summer season. Age 18 and up. Please register.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230727T200000
LOCATION:Meeting Room 1B\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 East Kirkwood
  Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Green Peeps Book Club: ‘Prodigal Summer’ by Barbara Kingsolver (Age
  18 and up)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/green-peeps-book-club-prodigal-summer-by-barbara
 -kingsolver-age-18-and-up/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Regis
 tration is open.</strong><br />\nJoin this book club to discuss nature-foc
 used reads each month. You’ll also learn how to become more ecologically-m
 inded through activities and speakers designed to enhance our reading. Joi
 n us at the Library for leaf pounding on fabric while we discuss Prodigal 
 Summer by Barbara Kingsolver.</p>\n<p>Summary:<br />\nProdigal Summer take
 s place over a sprawling\, humid summer in the Appalachian Mountains. King
 solver writes three love stories that weave into the natural world into th
 e lives of humans living within it. A wildlife biologist\, an entomologist
  and an elderly man working to restore the extinct American Chestnut tree 
 swap perspectives in this story of love amidst people having differing vie
 wpoints on how to be in relation with the land and its creatures. It’s the
  perfect book for the high summer season. <strong>Age 18 and up. Please re
 gister.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111392@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:AN HONEST MAN opens with a yacht full of bodies\, a woman hidin
 g from killers on a nearby island\, and a man trying to prove his innocenc
 e and save his life–in a breathtaking new thriller from the New York Times
  bestselling author of Those Who Wish Me Dead.\nPublication Date: July 25t
 h\nLearn more: https://www.michaelkoryta.com/books/an-honest-man/\nMichael
  Koryta is the New York Times bestselling author of seventeen novels–inclu
 ding Those Who Wish Me Dead\, which has been adapted into a film starring 
 Angelina Jolie and directed by Taylor Sheridan. His previous novels were N
 ew York Times notable books\, national bestsellers\, and have won numerous
  awards\, including the Los Angeles Times Book Prize. Koryta is a former p
 rivate investigator and newspaper reporter. He lives in Bloomington\, Indi
 ana\, and Camden\, Maine
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230727T183000
LOCATION:Morgenstern's Books\, 849 Auto Mall Rd\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Michael Koryta: Book Signing
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/michael-koryta-book-signing/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>AN HONEST MAN
  opens with a yacht full of bodies\, a woman hiding from killers on a near
 by island\, and a man trying to prove his innocence and save his life–in a
  breathtaking new thriller from the New York Times bestselling author of T
 hose Who Wish Me Dead.<br />\nPublication Date: July 25th<br />\nLearn mor
 e: https://www.michaelkoryta.com/books/an-honest-man/<br />\nMichael Koryt
 a is the New York Times bestselling author of seventeen novels–including T
 hose Who Wish Me Dead\, which has been adapted into a film starring Angeli
 na Jolie and directed by Taylor Sheridan. His previous novels were New Yor
 k Times notable books\, national bestsellers\, and have won numerous award
 s\, including the Los Angeles Times Book Prize. Koryta is a former private
  investigator and newspaper reporter. He lives in Bloomington\, Indiana\, 
 and Camden\, Maine</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
