BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111360@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A budding childhood romance between Nora and Hae Sung\, classma
 tes at a primary school in Seoul\, ends abruptly when Nora’s family emigra
 tes to Canada. Two decades later\, they are reunited in New York for one f
 ateful week as they confront notions of destiny and love\, and the choices
  that make a life..\nAn deeply romantic debut feature from Korean-Canadian
  filmmaker and New York City playwright Celine Song (Endlings). Song’s art
 ful aesthetic and profound character writing explore love\, identity\, and
  “In Yun\,” a Korean notion of fate stemming from two people’s connection 
 in a past life. (106 minutes)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230728T190000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Theater (upstairs)\, 1201 East 7th Street\, on the no
 rth side of Showalter Fountain\, next to the IU Auditorium
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20230804T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: PAST LIVES
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-past-lives/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A budding chi
 ldhood romance between Nora and Hae Sung\, classmates at a primary school 
 in Seoul\, ends abruptly when Nora’s family emigrates to Canada. Two decad
 es later\, they are reunited in New York for one fateful week as they conf
 ront notions of destiny and love\, and the choices that make a life..</p>
 \n<p>An deeply romantic debut feature from Korean-Canadian filmmaker and N
 ew York City playwright Celine Song (Endlings). Song’s artful aesthetic an
 d profound character writing explore love\, identity\, and “In Yun\,” a Ko
 rean notion of fate stemming from two people’s connection in a past life. 
 (106 minutes)</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111355@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Stand Up for Disabilities is a fundraiser finally putting the F
 UN back into an event.  Join host\, Andrew Lambert\, along with the Down S
 yndrome Family Connection and Monroe County Autism Foundation\, as this on
 e-night event will have you laughing for a good cause.\nJoining Andrew are
  co-headliners Dwight Simmons and Brent Terhune.  These two Indianapolis b
 ased comics have been performing all over the U.S. and have been seen at t
 he Limestone Comedy Festival\, heard on multiple podcasts including No Acc
 ounting for Taste and Field Trip with Brent Terhune\, along with stand-up 
 performances at many well know comedy hotspots.\nThe money raised will be 
 shared between two worthy causes helping local Monroe County families supp
 orting loved ones living with disabilities.  While we love supporting thes
 e families\, this show is an 18 and over event.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230728T193000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Stand-Up for Disabilities\, Benefiting Down Syndrome Family Connect
 ion and Monroe County Autism Foundation (18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/stand-up-for-disabilities-benefiting-down-syndro
 me-family-connection-and-monroe-county-autism-foundation-18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Stand Up for 
 Disabilities is a fundraiser finally putting the FUN back into an event.  
 Join host\, Andrew Lambert\, along with the Down Syndrome Family Connectio
 n and Monroe County Autism Foundation\, as this one-night event will have 
 you laughing for a good cause.</p>\n<p>Joining Andrew are co-headliners Dw
 ight Simmons and Brent Terhune.  These two Indianapolis based comics have 
 been performing all over the U.S. and have been seen at the Limestone Come
 dy Festival\, heard on multiple podcasts including No Accounting for Taste
  and Field Trip with Brent Terhune\, along with stand-up performances at m
 any well know comedy hotspots.</p>\n<p>The money raised will be shared bet
 ween two worthy causes helping local Monroe County families supporting lov
 ed ones living with disabilities.  While we love supporting these families
 \, this show is an 18 and over event.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
