BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111362@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:11:00am Guitar Competition\nUp to 40 acoustic guitarists from a
 ll over the world will compete to win one of the prize guitars and move on
  to the International Competition in Winfield\, Kansas\, later this year. 
 The first round of competition will be followed by a Final Five Playoff\, 
 with winners announced immediately after.\n7:30PM Evening Concert\nThe Top
  Three players from the morning competition will open the show\, followed 
 by The Cruz Brothers and Michael Kelsey! The Cruz Brothers are Mark Cruz\,
  who won our competition in 2022\, and the award-winning Edgar Cruz.\nMich
 ael Kelsey joins the Cruz Brothers with his free-flowing improvisational s
 tyle that involves every inch of his instrument. From his funky\, percussi
 ve playing style that conjures an image of a one-man version of STOMP to l
 ush instrumentals reminiscent of Michael Hedges/Phil Keaggy\, his performa
 nce blends multiple musical genres and vocals along with some techno fun t
 o create a sound all his own. Throughout a performance\, Michael may make 
 use of technology\, his improv skills\, objects in the room\, and audience
  interaction to make music for the ears but more importantly a musical exp
 erience for the senses.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230729T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230729T220000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 South Van Buren St\, Nashville\,
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:12th Annual Indiana State Fingerstyle Guitar Festival – Guitar Comp
 etition (11am) and Evening Concert (7:30pm)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/12th-annual-indiana-state-fingerstyle-guitar-fes
 tival-guitar-competition-11am-and-evening-concert-730pm/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>11:00am Guita
 r Competition<br />\nUp to 40 acoustic guitarists from all over the world 
 will compete to win one of the prize guitars and move on to the Internatio
 nal Competition in Winfield\, Kansas\, later this year. The first round of
  competition will be followed by a Final Five Playoff\, with winners annou
 nced immediately after.</p>\n<p>7:30PM Evening Concert<br />\nThe Top Thre
 e players from the morning competition will open the show\, followed by Th
 e Cruz Brothers and Michael Kelsey! The Cruz Brothers are Mark Cruz\, who 
 won our competition in 2022\, and the award-winning Edgar Cruz.<br />\nMic
 hael Kelsey joins the Cruz Brothers with his free-flowing improvisational 
 style that involves every inch of his instrument. From his funky\, percuss
 ive playing style that conjures an image of a one-man version of STOMP to 
 lush instrumentals reminiscent of Michael Hedges/Phil Keaggy\, his perform
 ance blends multiple musical genres and vocals along with some techno fun 
 to create a sound all his own. Throughout a performance\, Michael may make
  use of technology\, his improv skills\, objects in the room\, and audienc
 e interaction to make music for the ears but more importantly a musical ex
 perience for the senses.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
