UID:ai1ec-110261@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812-325-1555\; http://www.autismrocksandrolls.com/
DESCRIPTION:My son is a superhero. He has autism and is making his mark. Sa
 m is the Executive Director of Autism Rocks and Rolls Corporation\, a podc
 aster\, an international speaker\, a TEDX speaker\, a blogger\, and a loca
 l event planner. His mission is to show the world that those on the spectr
 um are successful and he is living proof of this.\nOur Website is www.auti
 smrocksandrolls.com and you can find his podcast at https://www.listennote
 s.com/podcasts/autism-rocks-and-rolls-sam-mitchell-Eg759SekWvU/.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230805T093000
LOCATION:Harley Davidson of Bloomington\, 522 W Gourley Pike\, Bloomington\
 , IN 47404
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Autism Rocks and Rolls SummerFest Poker Run
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/autism-summerfest-and-poker-run-starts/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>My son is a s
 uperhero. He has autism and is making his mark. Sam is the Executive Direc
 tor of Autism Rocks and Rolls Corporation\, a podcaster\, an international
  speaker\, a TEDX speaker\, a blogger\, and a local event planner. His mis
 sion is to show the world that those on the spectrum are successful and he
  is living proof of this.<br />\nOur Website is www.autismrocksandrolls.co
 m and you can find his podcast at https://www.listennotes.com/podcasts/aut
 ism-rocks-and-rolls-sam-mitchell-Eg759SekWvU/.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-110256@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812-272-7001\; http://bike4thekids.com/
DESCRIPTION:3rd Annual Dr. Wrasse Memorial Bike 4 the Kids to be held the m
 orning of August 5th at Switchyard Park in Bloomington. Established in 202
 1\, this fun\, annual non-competitive bike ride (originally titled Bike 4 
 Fitness) for all ages honors the memory of Bloomington pediatrician and li
 felong cyclist Dr. John Wrasse. All registration fees go directly to Riley
  Kids Fund of Bloomington. Bike 4 the Kids features two ride options: a 2 
 mile loop around Switchyard Park and the B-Line Trail\, and an 11 mile loo
 p option that extends to the bridge at Clear Creek Trail.  We invite non-c
 yclists to walk or run with us on the park loop. Our event features live m
 usic\, food\, health and wellness booths\, helmet distribution and fitting
 s for kids\, and more. It’s fun for the whole family! We are excited to pa
 rtner this year with Kiwanis Club of South Central Indiana to host their K
 iwanis Idol auditions on the main stage after our ride\, as they raise fun
 ds for Riley. We invite you to stay and listen to the contestants\, or eve
 n audition for a spot in the Idol competition. For more information or to 
 register please visit bike4thekids.com.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230805T100000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 S Rogers St\, Bloomington\, IN 47403
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:3rd Annual Dr. Wrasse Memorial Bike 4 the Kids
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/3rd-annual-dr-wrasse-memorial-bike-4-the-kids/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>3rd Annual Dr
 . Wrasse Memorial Bike 4 the Kids to be held the morning of August 5th at 
 Switchyard Park in Bloomington. Established in 2021\, this fun\, annual no
 n-competitive bike ride (originally titled Bike 4 Fitness) for all ages ho
 nors the memory of Bloomington pediatrician and lifelong cyclist Dr. John 
 Wrasse. All registration fees go directly to Riley Kids Fund of Bloomingto
 n. Bike 4 the Kids features two ride options: a 2 mile loop around Switchy
 ard Park and the B-Line Trail\, and an 11 mile loop option that extends to
  the bridge at Clear Creek Trail.  We invite non-cyclists to walk or run w
 ith us on the park loop. Our event features live music\, food\, health and
  wellness booths\, helmet distribution and fittings for kids\, and more. I
 t’s fun for the whole family! We are excited to partner this year with Kiw
 anis Club of South Central Indiana to host their Kiwanis Idol auditions on
  the main stage after our ride\, as they raise funds for Riley. We invite 
 you to stay and listen to the contestants\, or even audition for a spot in
  the Idol competition. For more information or to register please visit bi
 ke4thekids.com.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111599@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:See you at Switchyard Brewing on August 5th\, 2023. Fun run sta
 rts from the taproom at 11am.\nWe’ve mapped out a 5k-ish course that start
 s and ends at Switchyard Brewing and weaves throughout Bloomington. Run\, 
 walk\, jog – whatever goes! All ages\, all levels are welcome.\nCross the 
 finish line and celebrate!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230805T110000
LOCATION:Switchyard Brewery\, 419 North Walnut Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:5K Beer Run\, to benefit the Monroe County Humane Association
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/5k-beer-run-to-benefit-the-monroe-county-humane-
 association/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>See you at Sw
 itchyard Brewing on August 5th\, 2023. Fun run starts from the taproom at 
 11am.<br />\nWe’ve mapped out a 5k-ish course that starts and ends at Swit
 chyard Brewing and weaves throughout Bloomington. Run\, walk\, jog – whate
 ver goes! All ages\, all levels are welcome.<br />\nCross the finish line 
 and celebrate! </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
