UID:ai1ec-111521@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Please register if interested  The Writing Circle is a safe and
  encouraging space that offers inspiration and connection for writers of a
 ll genders and abilities—and of any genre. Each circle will offer time to 
 write\, share our writing\, and receive feedback according to the writer’s
  needs. Sharing your writing aloud is always optional\, and all writing sh
 ared in the circle is kept confidential. This program is in partnership wi
 th Women Writing for (a) Change
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230805T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230805T170000
LOCATION:Program Room 2B\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 E. Kirkwood A
 ve.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Writer’s Circle (Age 18 and up\, recommended for ages 18–32)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-writers-circle-age-18-and-up-recommended-for
 -ages-18-32/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Pleas
 e register if interested</strong>  The Writing Circle is a safe and encour
 aging space that offers inspiration and connection for writers of all gend
 ers and abilities—and of any genre. Each circle will offer time to write\,
  share our writing\, and receive feedback according to the writer’s needs.
  Sharing your writing aloud is always optional\, and all writing shared in
  the circle is kept confidential. This program is in partnership with Wome
 n Writing for (a) Change</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
