BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111817@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Tipton\, Indiana native\, Janis Thornton\, is the author of nin
 e books\, including the award-winning\, No Place Like Murder—a modern rete
 lling of 20 sensational true crime stories that rocked Indiana from 1869 t
 hrough 1950. Thornton is also the author of another true crime book\, Too 
 Good a Girl. Her latest work is The 1965 Palm Sunday Tornadoes in Indiana.
  She has also authored three mystery novels: Love\, Lies & Azure Eyes\, Du
 st Bunnies & Dead Bodies\, and Dead Air & Double Dare. Janis is a member o
 f Sisters in Crime\, The Authors Guild\, Women Fiction Writers\, and the I
 ndianapolis Writers Center. Visit www.janis-thornton.com to learn more. Th
 ornton will have books for sale after the program. Age 18 and up.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230813T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230813T150000
LOCATION:Meeting Room 1B\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 East Kirkwood
  Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Coffee With Friends: Janis Thornton (Age 18 and up)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/coffee-with-friends-janis-thornton-age-18-and-up
 /
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Tipton\, Indi
 ana native\, Janis Thornton\, is the author of nine books\, including the 
 award-winning\, No Place Like Murder—a modern retelling of 20 sensational 
 true crime stories that rocked Indiana from 1869 through 1950. Thornton is
  also the author of another true crime book\, Too Good a Girl. Her latest 
 work is The 1965 Palm Sunday Tornadoes in Indiana. She has also authored t
 hree mystery novels: Love\, Lies & Azure Eyes\, Dust Bunnies & Dead Bodies
 \, and Dead Air & Double Dare. Janis is a member of Sisters in Crime\, The
  Authors Guild\, Women Fiction Writers\, and the Indianapolis Writers Cent
 er. Visit www.janis-thornton.com to learn more. Thornton will have books f
 or sale after the program. Age 18 and up.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
