BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-112004@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Cicada Cinema\; cicadacinema@gmail.com\; https://www.eventbrite.com
 /e/cicada-cinema-gala-registration-679481486417?aff=oddtdtcreator&syclid=c
 jd3u6qusviobib1e1ug&utm_campaign=emailmarketing_133646483500&utm_medium=em
 ail&utm_source=shopify_email
DESCRIPTION:Registration: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/cicada-cinema-gala-r
 egistration-679481486417\nThis event is a celebration of Cicada Cinema’s n
 early 7 year history! We are inviting the community to come and learn abou
 t what Cicada Cinema has contributed to Bloomington’s film\, arts and ente
 rtainment culture\, as well as letting people know how they can support us
  and help us grow in the coming years.\nFood and beverage will be provided
  by past and present community partners. There will also be a live DJ\, so
 me film related activities and finally a FREE screening of Joe Dante’s 199
 3 love letter to scrappy theatrical exhibition: Matinee. So\, please come 
 and hang with us and learn how you can help Cicada Cinema continue it’s jo
 urney to being Bloomington’s community movie theater.\nMatinee (1993)\nSyn
 opsis: Step back into a time of outrageous movie-theater gimmicks and larg
 er-than-life B-screen stars in this charming homage to the great sci-fi an
 d horror flicks of the 1950s and 1960s. John Goodman is at his uproarious 
 best as the William Castle-inspired movie promoter Lawrence Woolsey\, who 
 brings his unique brand of flashy showmanship to the unsuspecting resident
 s of Key West\, Florida. It’s 1962\, and fifteen-year-old fan Gene Loomis\
 , can’t wait for the arrival of Woolsey\, who is in town to promote his la
 test offering of atomic power gone berserk\, MANT!. But the absurd vision 
 of Woolsey’s tale takes on a sudden urgency as the Cuban Missile Crisis pl
 aces the real threat of atomic horror just 90 miles off the coast. With th
 e help of Gene and Woolsey’s leading lady\, Ruth(Cathy Moriarty)\, the mas
 ter showman gives Key West a premiere they’ll never forget. Anything can h
 appen in the movies\, and everything does in this hilarious tribute to a m
 ore and outrageous time in movie going.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230820T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230820T200000
LOCATION:FAR Center for Contemporary Arts\, 505 West 4th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema Gala featuring “Matinee” (1993)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-gala-featuring-matinee-1993/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Registration:
  https://www.eventbrite.com/e/cicada-cinema-gala-registration-679481486417
 </p>\n<p>This event is a celebration of Cicada Cinema’s nearly 7 year hist
 ory! We are inviting the community to come and learn about what Cicada Cin
 ema has contributed to Bloomington’s film\, arts and entertainment culture
 \, as well as letting people know how they can support us and help us grow
  in the coming years.</p>\n<p>Food and beverage will be provided by past a
 nd present community partners. There will also be a live DJ\, some film re
 lated activities and finally a FREE screening of Joe Dante’s 1993 love let
 ter to scrappy theatrical exhibition: Matinee. So\, please come and hang w
 ith us and learn how you can help Cicada Cinema continue it’s journey to b
 eing Bloomington’s community movie theater.</p>\n<p>Matinee (1993)</p>\n<d
 iv>Synopsis: Step back into a time of outrageous movie-theater gimmicks an
 d larger-than-life B-screen stars in this charming homage to the great sci
 -fi and horror flicks of the 1950s and 1960s. John Goodman is at his uproa
 rious best as the William Castle-inspired movie promoter Lawrence Woolsey\
 , who brings his unique brand of flashy showmanship to the unsuspecting re
 sidents of Key West\, Florida. It’s 1962\, and fifteen-year-old fan Gene L
 oomis\, can’t wait for the arrival of Woolsey\, who is in town to promote 
 his latest offering of atomic power gone berserk\, MANT!. But the absurd v
 ision of Woolsey’s tale takes on a sudden urgency as the Cuban Missile Cri
 sis places the real threat of atomic horror just 90 miles off the coast. W
 ith the help of Gene and Woolsey’s leading lady\, Ruth(Cathy Moriarty)\, t
 he master showman gives Key West a premiere they’ll never forget. Anything
  can happen in the movies\, and everything does in this hilarious tribute 
 to a more and outrageous time in movie going.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-112205@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:5:30pm\nDoors\n6pm\nDaniel Joseph Weddle\n7pm\nTravis Puntarell
 i with Eli Cherry\n8pm\nZiona Li Riley with Levi SaladFork
