BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-112221@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in converting your old home movie recordings
 \, printed photographs\, or slides into a digital format you can share onl
 ine? Preserving your memories\, archiving\, and sharing them can be a powe
 rful way to connect with friends and family. In this open house\, we’ll te
 ach you how to create digital files using our new Memory Preservation Stat
 ion. You can use a cloud storage account like Google Drive\, Microsoft One
 Drive\, or Dropbox to save your content. Another option is to use a USB fl
 ash drive––you can bring your own or check one out from the Library for te
 mporary use. Age 18 and up.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230823T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230823T150000
LOCATION:Level Up\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 East Kirkwood Ave\, 
 Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Preserving Memories (Age 18 and up)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/preserving-memories-age-18-and-up-5/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> Are you inte
 rested in converting your old home movie recordings\, printed photographs\
 , or slides into a digital format you can share online? Preserving your me
 mories\, archiving\, and sharing them can be a powerful way to connect wit
 h friends and family. In this open house\, we’ll teach you how to create d
 igital files using our new Memory Preservation Station. You can use a clou
 d storage account like Google Drive\, Microsoft OneDrive\, or Dropbox to s
 ave your content. Another option is to use a USB flash drive––you can brin
 g your own or check one out from the Library for temporary use. Age 18 and
  up. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
