BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-112613@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Registration is open\, please register if interested.\nOur nati
 ve plants and animals are losing their place in this world\, and one of th
 e best ways to help them is to grow your own native plants from seed. In t
 his class\, we’ll learn the steps of native seed propagation\, with a focu
 s on collecting and preparing your own seeds. Native seeds will be provide
 d for an opportunity for hands-on experience. If you’ve collected some of 
 your own\, you’re invited to bring them with you. Our instructor will be B
 ill Daniels\, Native Seed Communities Coordinator and Purdue Extension Adv
 anced Master Gardener. Attendees will leave with their own packet of nativ
 e seeds. Age 18 and up.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230902T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230902T113000
LOCATION:Program Room 2B and 2C Combo\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 
 East Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Native Seed Propagation  (Age 18 and up)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/native-seed-propagation-age-18-and-up/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Regis
 tration is open\, please register if interested.</strong></p>\n<p>Our nati
 ve plants and animals are losing their place in this world\, and one of th
 e best ways to help them is to grow your own native plants from seed. In t
 his class\, we’ll learn the steps of native seed propagation\, with a focu
 s on collecting and preparing your own seeds. Native seeds will be provide
 d for an opportunity for hands-on experience. If you’ve collected some of 
 your own\, you’re invited to bring them with you. Our instructor will be B
 ill Daniels\, Native Seed Communities Coordinator and Purdue Extension Adv
 anced Master Gardener. Attendees will leave with their own packet of nativ
 e seeds. Age 18 and up.<b><br />\n</b></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
