BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-111065@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Cicada Cinema\; cicadacinema@gmail.com\; https://cicadacinema.com/p
 roducts/jazz-on-a-summers-day-september-2-waldron-hill-and-buskirk-park-du
 sk-9pm
DESCRIPTION:JAZZ ON A SUMMER’S DAY\n\n1959 • USA • 88 minutes • 4k Restorat
 ion from camera negative\n\nSaturday\, September 2nd\nat Waldron\, Hill an
 d Buskirk Park (aka 3rd Street Park) – 331 S Washington St\n\nFREE\, no ti
 cket needed | All Ages \nShowtime: Dusk (~9pm)\n*OUTDOOR SCREENING in the 
 park*\n-Bring your own chair-\n\nTRAILER\nSynopsis: Filmed at the 1958 New
 port Jazz Festival in Rhode Island and directed by world-renowned photogra
 pher Bert Stern\, Jazz on a Summer’s Day features intimate performances by
  an all-star line-up of musical legends including Louis Armstrong\, Thelon
 ious Monk\, Gerry Mulligan\, Anita O’Day\, Chuck Berry\, Dinah Washington\
 , and closes with a beautiful rendition of The Lord’s Prayer by Mahalia Ja
 ckson at midnight to usher in Sunday morning.\n*In partnership with WFHB a
 nd City of Bloomington Park & Recreation.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230902T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230902T230000
LOCATION:Waldron\, Hill and Buskirk Park @ 331 S Washington S
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents “Jazz on a Summer’s Day” (1959)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-jazz-on-a-summers-day-195
 9-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><b>JAZZ ON A 
 SUMMER’S DAY<br />\n</b></p>\n<p><i><span style='font-weight: 400\;'>1959 
 • USA • 88 minutes • 4k Restoration from camera negative<br />\n</span></i
 ></p>\n<p><i><span style='font-weight: 400\;'>Saturday\, September 2nd</sp
 an></i><i><span style='font-weight: 400\;'><br />\n</span></i><i><span sty
 le='font-weight: 400\;'>at </span></i><i>Waldron\, Hill and Buskirk Park (
 aka 3rd Street Park) – </i><i><span class='LrzXr'>331 S Washington St<br /
 >\n</span></i></p>\n<p><i></i><b><i></i></b><i><span style='font-weight: 4
 00\;'>FREE\, no ticket needed | All Ages</span></i> <strong><br />\n</stro
 ng><i><span style='font-weight: 400\;'>Showtime: Dusk (~9pm)</span></i></p
 >\n<p><i><span style='font-weight: 400\;'><strong>*OUTDOOR SCREENING in th
 e park*<br />\n</strong></span></i><span style='font-weight: 400\;'><stron
 g>-Bring your own</strong></span><span style='font-weight: 400\;'><strong>
  chair-</strong></span><i><span style='font-weight: 400\;'><br />\n</span>
 </i></p>\n<p><a title='Jazz on a Summer's Day Trailer' href='https://www.y
 outube.com/watch?v=WWS1tt3ydV8' target='_blank' rel='noopener'><b>TRAILER<
 /b></a></p>\n<p><span style='font-weight: 400\;'>Synopsis: </span>Filmed a
 t the 1958 Newport Jazz Festival in Rhode Island and directed by world-ren
 owned photographer Bert Stern\, <em>Jazz on a Summer’s Day</em> features i
 ntimate performances by an all-star line-up of musical legends including L
 ouis Armstrong\, Thelonious Monk\, Gerry Mulligan\, Anita O’Day\, Chuck Be
 rry\, Dinah Washington\, and closes with a beautiful rendition of <em>The 
 Lord’s Prayer</em> by Mahalia Jackson at midnight to usher in Sunday morni
 ng.</p>\n<p>*In partnership with <strong><a href='https://wfhb.org/' targe
 t='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>WFHB</a></strong> and <strong><a href
 ='https://bloomington.in.gov/parks/parks'>City of Bloomington Park & Recre
 ation</a></strong>.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
