BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-112674@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The polyrhythmic heat of Evie Ladin’s clawhammer banjo\, resona
 nt voice\, real stories and rhythmic dance have been heard from A Prairie 
 Home Companion to Lincoln Center\, Celtic Connections to Hardly Strictly B
 luegrass\, Brazil to Bali. A prolific creator and gracious facilitator\, E
 vie grew up steeped in traditional folk music/dance up and down the East C
 oast\, bringing a syncretic vision to new work while holding fast to the r
 oots. A former Bloomington resident and DJ on WFHB\, Evie’s always keen to
  come back to her adopted home town. She writes clever lyrics with mature 
 arrangements\, calls rowdy square dances for urban crowds\, choreographs n
 ew body music/percussive dance for contemporary dance and film\, leads sem
 inars in movement anthropology\, rocks straight up old time clawhammer ban
 jo\, and gardens\, from the vibrant homebase of Oakland\, California. She’
 s won ribbons and arts fellowships\, performed in sold out concert halls a
 nd cozy living rooms\, and toured around the world\, to every state in the
  US except Florida. She’s never been to Florida.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230907T200000
LOCATION:The Pink Poodle\, 917 North Fairview St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Evie Ladin
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/evie-ladin/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><span class='
 x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr
 53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzs
 f02u' dir='auto'>The polyrhythmic heat of Evie Ladin’s clawhammer banjo\, 
 resonant voice\, real stories and rhythmic dance have been heard from A Pr
 airie Home Companion to Lincoln Center\, Celtic Connections to Hardly Stri
 ctly Bluegrass\, Brazil to Bali. A prolific creator and gracious facilitat
 or\, Evie grew up steeped in traditional folk music/dance up and down the 
 East Coast\, bringing a syncretic vision to new work while holding fast to
  the roots. A former Bloomington resident and DJ on WFHB\, Evie’s always k
 een to come back to her adopted home town. She writes clever lyrics with m
 ature arrangements\, calls rowdy square dances for urban crowds\, choreogr
 aphs new body music/percussive dance for contemporary dance and film\, lea
 ds seminars in movement anthropology\, rocks straight up old time clawhamm
 er banjo\, and gardens\, from the vibrant homebase of Oakland\, California
 . She’s won ribbons and arts fellowships\, performed in sold out concert h
 alls and cozy living rooms\, and toured around the world\, to every state 
 in the US except Florida. She’s never been to Florida. </span></p>\n</BODY
 ></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
