BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-113346@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Keri Miksza\; 303-746-8986\; contact@keepeducationpublic.org\; http
 s://www.icpe-monroecounty.org/cir2023.html
DESCRIPTION:Indiana Coalition for Public Education is hosting a roundtable 
 event covering local education issues. This informational event will be he
 ld on Sunday\, October 1 from 3pm to 4:30pm in the conference rooms of the
  NEW Monroe County Public Library Southwest at 890 W. Gordon Pike. Light s
 nacks and beverages will be served. \nThis event covers six topics – Findi
 ng common ground in the school culture wars\, MCCSC 2023 referendum\, spec
 ial education services\, preschool in public schools\, school choice\, and
  school funding. \nAttendees will be able to rotate to three different tab
 les where they will listen to an expert and ask questions.  \nThe roundtab
 le hosts: \nHal Turner\, Co-Chair\, Braver Angels of South Central Indiana
 \nJohn Kenny\, CFO\, Monroe County Community School Corporation\nWendy Mar
 encik\, Clinical Assistant Professor Emerita\, Indiana University\nSarah C
 assavaugh\, IN*SOURCE Team Leader & Special Education Liaison\nJennifer Bi
 ckel\, Assistant Special Education Director\, Monroe County Community Scho
 ol Corporation\nLaura Stickels\, Manager – Early Learning and Out of Schoo
 l Programs\, Monroe County Community School Corporation\nKeri Miksza\, Cha
 ir of Indiana Coalition for Public Education–Monroe County\nMatt Irwin\, A
 ssistant Superintendent\, Richland Bean Blossom Community Schools
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231001T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231001T163000
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library Southwest\, 890 W Gordon Pike
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Community Informational Roundtable: Local Education Topics
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/community-informational-roundtable-local-educati
 on-topics/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Indiana Coali
 tion for Public Education is hosting a roundtable event covering local edu
 cation issues. This informational event will be held on Sunday\, October 1
  from 3pm to 4:30pm in the conference rooms of the NEW Monroe County Publi
 c Library Southwest at 890 W. Gordon Pike. Light snacks and beverages will
  be served. </p>\n<p>This event covers six topics – Finding common ground 
 in the school culture wars\, MCCSC 2023 referendum\, special education ser
 vices\, preschool in public schools\, school choice\, and school funding. 
 </p>\n<p>Attendees will be able to rotate to three different tables where 
 they will listen to an expert and ask questions.  </p>\n<p>The roundtable 
 hosts: </p>\n<p>Hal Turner\, Co-Chair\, Braver Angels of South Central Ind
 iana<br />\nJohn Kenny\, CFO\, Monroe County Community School Corporation<
 br />\nWendy Marencik\, Clinical Assistant Professor Emerita\, Indiana Uni
 versity<br />\nSarah Cassavaugh\, IN*SOURCE Team Leader & Special Educatio
 n Liaison<br />\nJennifer Bickel\, Assistant Special Education Director\, 
 Monroe County Community School Corporation<br />\nLaura Stickels\, Manager
  – Early Learning and Out of School Programs\, Monroe County Community Sch
 ool Corporation<br />\nKeri Miksza\, Chair of Indiana Coalition for Public
  Education–Monroe County<br />\nMatt Irwin\, Assistant Superintendent\, Ri
 chland Bean Blossom Community Schools</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
