BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-113722@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Georgie is a resourceful 12-year-old girl. She secretly lives a
 lone in her flat in a working class suburb of London following the death o
 f her mother. She makes money stealing bikes with her best friend Ali and 
 keeps the social workers off her back by pretending to live with an uncle.
  Out of nowhere\, her estranged father\, Jason\, arrives. Uninterested in 
 this sudden new parental figure\, Georgie is stubbornly resistant to his a
 ttempts to connect to his daughter. As they adjust to their new circumstan
 ces\, Georgie and Jason find that they both still have a lot of growing up
  to do.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231006T190000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Theater (upstairs)\, 1201 East 7th Street\, on the no
 rth side of Showalter Fountain\, next to the IU Auditorium
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20231013T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: SCRAPPER
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-scrapper/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Georgie is a 
 resourceful 12-year-old girl. She secretly lives alone in her flat in a wo
 rking class suburb of London following the death of her mother. She makes 
 money stealing bikes with her best friend Ali and keeps the social workers
  off her back by pretending to live with an uncle. Out of nowhere\, her es
 tranged father\, Jason\, arrives. Uninterested in this sudden new parental
  figure\, Georgie is stubbornly resistant to his attempts to connect to hi
 s daughter. As they adjust to their new circumstances\, Georgie and Jason 
 find that they both still have a lot of growing up to do. </p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
