 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>From 10 am–3 
 pm. Art supplies provided.  All ages welcome! Artists’ demonstrations\, mu
 sic\, and storytelling throughout the day!</p>\n<p> All art completed for 
 judging must follow the guidelines below.</p>\n<p>·         NO REGISTRATIO
 N FEE:  Free event. No advance registration needed.</p>\n<p>·         Arti
 sts must check in at the pavilion between 9.30-11 am the day of the event.
  </p>\n<p>·         Original artwork eligible in any medium done in Bloomi
 ngton the day of the event.</p>\n<p>·         Open to professional and eme
 rging artists of all ages and skill levels.</p>\n<p>·         Canvasses or
  multi-media paper must be stamped before beginning.</p>\n<p>·         Sup
 plies are available to artists for painting on Bryant Park grounds. </p>\n
 <p>·         Completed artwork for judging must be delivered by 3 pm at Wo
 odlawn Pavilion. </p>\n<p>Artist’s name and contact info on the back. Do N
 OT sign artwork until after judging.<br />\nWet oil paintings should be in
  a frame for safe handling (or BYO easel.)</p>\n<p>Awards will be given fo
 r artists in the following categories in ALL media:</p>\n<p>Professional A
 rtists<br />\nAdult Artists<br />\nTeens (Ages 12-17)<br />\nYouth (Ages 7
 -11)<br />\nCollaborative Art</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
