BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-113685@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Bring your vegetable and flower seeds to exchange with other co
 mmunity members and help the gardens of Monroe County grow! During this pr
 ogram\, the Seed Library can accept seed donations\, so please come and he
 lp stock up this valuable community resource. The Library and Mother Hubba
 rd’s Cupboard will also have free seeds available. \nWhen donating seeds\,
  please make sure your seeds are not from invasive plants and note the fol
 lowing:\n    The type and variety of seed\n    The year the seeds are from
 \n    Whether the seeds are store-bought or self-saved\nWe ask that you pl
 ease package your seeds accordingly\; we will have tools and supplies on-h
 and. All ages.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231007T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231007T130000
LOCATION:Program Room 2B and 2C Combo\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 
 East Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Seed Swap
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/seed-swap-3/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Bring your ve
 getable and flower seeds to exchange with other community members and help
  the gardens of Monroe County grow! During this program\, the Seed Library
  can accept seed donations\, so please come and help stock up this valuabl
 e community resource. The Library and Mother Hubbard’s Cupboard will also 
 have free seeds available. </p>\n<p>When donating seeds\, please make sure
  your seeds are not from invasive plants and note the following:</p>\n<p> 
    The type and variety of seed<br />\n    The year the seeds are from<br 
 />\n    Whether the seeds are store-bought or self-saved</p>\n<p>We ask th
 at you please package your seeds accordingly\; we will have tools and supp
 lies on-hand. All ages.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
