BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114121@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Civil rights activist and independent archivist Marion Stokes v
 ideotaped 33 years of the 24-hour news cycle on 70\,000 VHS tapes. In an e
 ffort to protect the truth\, Stokes created an archive of U.S. history thr
 ough media\, starting with the Iranian Hostage Crisis and ending with Sand
 y Hook. In some cases\, Stokes’s recordings are the only ones in existence
  as networks disposed of their own copies and the collection is now being 
 digitized by the Internet Archive for future use.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231016T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. Seventh Street Bloomington\,(on the North side
  of the IU Auditorium\, across from Hoagy)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: RECORDER: THE MARION STOKES PROJECT
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-recorder-the-marion-stokes-project/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Civil rights 
 activist and independent archivist Marion Stokes videotaped 33 years of th
 e 24-hour news cycle on 70\,000 VHS tapes. In an effort to protect the tru
 th\, Stokes created an archive of U.S. history through media\, starting wi
 th the Iranian Hostage Crisis and ending with Sandy Hook. In some cases\, 
 Stokes’s recordings are the only ones in existence as networks disposed of
  their own copies and the collection is now being digitized by the Interne
 t Archive for future use. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
