BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114444@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A Compassionate Spy is a gripping real-life spy thriller about 
 Manhattan Project physicist Ted Hall\, who provided nuclear secrets to the
  Soviet Union\, told through the perspective of his loving wife Joan\, who
  protected his secret for decades. Recruited in 1944 as an 18-year-old Har
 vard undergraduate to help Robert Oppenheimer and his team create a bomb\,
  Hall was the youngest physicist on the Manhattan Project\, and didn’t sha
 re his colleagues’ elation after the successful detonation of the world’s 
 first atomic bomb. Concerned that a U.S. post-war monopoly on such a power
 ful weapon could lead to nuclear catastrophe\, Hall began passing key info
 rmation about the bomb’s construction to the Soviet Union. After the war\,
  he met\, fell in love with\, and married Joan\, a fellow student with who
 m he shared a passion for classical music and socialist causes — and the e
 xplosive secret of his espionage.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231027T190000
LOCATION:IU Radio & Television Theater (RTV 251)\, 1229 East 7th St\, Bloom
 ington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20231103T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: A COMPASSIONATE SPY
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-a-compassionate-spy/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A Compassiona
 te Spy is a gripping real-life spy thriller about Manhattan Project physic
 ist Ted Hall\, who provided nuclear secrets to the Soviet Union\, told thr
 ough the perspective of his loving wife Joan\, who protected his secret fo
 r decades. Recruited in 1944 as an 18-year-old Harvard undergraduate to he
 lp Robert Oppenheimer and his team create a bomb\, Hall was the youngest p
 hysicist on the Manhattan Project\, and didn’t share his colleagues’ elati
 on after the successful detonation of the world’s first atomic bomb. Conce
 rned that a U.S. post-war monopoly on such a powerful weapon could lead to
  nuclear catastrophe\, Hall began passing key information about the bomb’s
  construction to the Soviet Union. After the war\, he met\, fell in love w
 ith\, and married Joan\, a fellow student with whom he shared a passion fo
 r classical music and socialist causes — and the explosive secret of his e
 spionage. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114061@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Tony Mannia\; tonymannia@gmail.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Bloomington Community Band at the Buskirk-Chumley Theater 
 for an unforgettable evening of Spooky Beats and Theater Treats. As the cl
 ock strikes 7\, the Bloomington Community Band will cast a musical spell o
 ver the crowd.\n Brace yourself for a spine-tingling spectacle of creeptas
 tic\, yet entirely kid-friendly videos that will have you giggling with de
 light! It’s a Halloween movie marathon that will enchant and entertain the
  whole family!\n As you immerse yourself in the spooky atmosphere\, don’t 
 forget to venture out for a delightful trick-or-treat experience throughou
 t downtown! Collect candies and goodies from our friendly local businesses
  until the clock strikes 8 PM\, marking the end of this fantastic adventur
 e.\nWhether you’re dropping by for just a song or two or planning to stay 
 until the witching hour\, this event promises something for everyone. Come
  dressed in your most creative costumes\, ready to show off your spooky sp
 irit and mingle with fellow Halloween enthusiasts!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231027T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231027T220000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater 114 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Spooky Beats and Theater Treats Featuring the Bloomington Community
  Band
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/spooky-beats-and-theater-treats-featuring-the-bl
 oomington-community-band/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> Join Bloomin
 gton Community Band at the Buskirk-Chumley Theater for an unforgettable ev
 ening of Spooky Beats and Theater Treats. As the clock strikes 7\, the Blo
 omington Community Band will cast a musical spell over the crowd.</p>\n<p>
  Brace yourself for a spine-tingling spectacle of creeptastic\, yet entire
 ly kid-friendly videos that will have you giggling with delight! It’s a Ha
 lloween movie marathon that will enchant and entertain the whole family!</
 p>\n<p> As you immerse yourself in the spooky atmosphere\, don’t forget to
  venture out for a delightful trick-or-treat experience throughout downtow
 n! Collect candies and goodies from our friendly local businesses until th
 e clock strikes 8 PM\, marking the end of this fantastic adventure.</p>\n<
 p>Whether you’re dropping by for just a song or two or planning to stay un
 til the witching hour\, this event promises something for everyone. Come d
 ressed in your most creative costumes\, ready to show off your spooky spir
 it and mingle with fellow Halloween enthusiasts!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
