UID:ai1ec-114410@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Charlie Bird was a Bloomington treasure and icon. Let us come t
 ogether to celebrate his life and contribution to our community with a bik
 e ride up and down the B-Line.\nWe’ll begin near the Switchyard Park Pavil
 lion at about 12:15 p.m.\, ride to the Bloomington Community Farmer’s Mark
 et\, and return to Switchyard Park (3.4 miles total).\nThis event is open 
 to all ages\, and you may join or leave the ride at any point. Charlie Bir
 d-inspired attire is optional and encouraged!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231028T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231028T140000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park Pavillion\, 1601 S. Rogers Street.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Memorial Bike Ride: Remembering Charlie Bird
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/memorial-bike-ride-remembering-charlie-bird/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Charlie Bird 
 was a Bloomington treasure and icon. Let us come together to celebrate his
  life and contribution to our community with a bike ride up and down the B
 -Line.<br />\n<strong>We’ll begin near the Switchyard Park Pavillion at ab
 out 12:15 p.m.\, ride to the Bloomington Community Farmer’s Market\, and r
 eturn to Switchyard Park (3.4 miles total).</strong><br />\nThis event is 
 open to all ages\, and you may join or leave the ride at any point. Charli
 e Bird-inspired attire is optional and encouraged! </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
