BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114344@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This spoken-word event is the launch of Compost Diaries\, a cha
 pbook of poems and short prose by writer\, artist\, and die-hard composter
  LuAnne Holladay. She says the chapbook “is an example of celebrating and 
 embracing impermanence.”\nThe small edition of handbound pamphlets reflect
 s more than two decades’ experience with simple book-making that incorpora
 tes the use of found and – yes – compostable elements. “I hope people buy 
 copies\, enjoy them\, and perhaps find ideas that resonate with their own 
 experiences.”\nThe event includes readings by LuAnne and special guests th
 at reflect on our experiences with the beautiful and ordinary things that 
 pass through our hands and our lives\, the daily artifacts that we treasur
 e as talismans – or may treat as detritus for the compost bin. “There’s be
 auty all along the continuum\,” says LuAnne.\nAll proceeds from sales of C
 ompost Diaries will go to Friends of Juniper Art Gallery\, to support this
  community art resource.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231029T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231029T173000
LOCATION:Juniper Art Gallery\, 615 W. Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Compost Diaries – Reflections on Accumulation and Letting Go
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/compost-diaries-reflections-on-accumulation-and-
 letting-go/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>This spoken-w
 ord event is the launch of Compost Diaries\, a chapbook of poems and short
  prose by writer\, artist\, and die-hard composter LuAnne Holladay. She sa
 ys the chapbook “is an example of celebrating and embracing impermanence.”
 <br />\nThe small edition of handbound pamphlets reflects more than two de
 cades’ experience with simple book-making that incorporates the use of fou
 nd and – yes – compostable elements. “I hope people buy copies\, enjoy the
 m\, and perhaps find ideas that resonate with their own experiences.”<br /
 >\nThe event includes readings by LuAnne and special guests that reflect o
 n our experiences with the beautiful and ordinary things that pass through
  our hands and our lives\, the daily artifacts that we treasure as talisma
 ns – or may treat as detritus for the compost bin. “There’s beauty all alo
 ng the continuum\,” says LuAnne.<br />\nAll proceeds from sales of Compost
  Diaries will go to Friends of Juniper Art Gallery\, to support this commu
 nity art resource. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
