BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114686@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Taylor Swift: The Conference Era seeks to gather Swifties and S
 wifty-adjacent thinkers for a meeting of the (master)minds focused on exam
 ining pertinent topics through the lens of sold-out stadium star Taylor Sw
 ift.  This year\, Taylor Swift embarked on her record-breaking Eras Tour\,
  which sold over 2.4 million tickets in a single day. As the tour title si
 gnals\, this moment provides an opportunity to not only reflect on\, but a
 lso re-imagine Swift’s extensive impact. Scholars and fans alike see this 
 as a critical time to discuss and analyze Taylor Swift’s impact during yet
  another peak in her extensive and iconic career.\nThe conference will run
  from 9am-10pm Friday 11/3 and from 9am-6pm Saturday 11/4. You are welcome
  to attend all or some of the panels.\nA list of panels and times will be 
 available shortly. There will be a screening of CATS on Friday evening at 
 7:30pm.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231103T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231103T220000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Taylor Swift: The Conference Era (Recommended for age 12+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/taylor-swift-the-conference-era-recommended-for-
 age-12/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Taylo
 r Swift: The Conference Era</strong> seeks to gather Swifties and Swifty-a
 djacent thinkers for a meeting of the (master)minds focused on examining p
 ertinent topics through the lens of sold-out stadium star Taylor Swift.  T
 his year\, Taylor Swift embarked on her record-breaking Eras Tour\, which 
 sold over 2.4 million tickets in a single day. As the tour title signals\,
  this moment provides an opportunity to not only reflect on\, but also re-
 imagine Swift’s extensive impact. Scholars and fans alike see this as a cr
 itical time to discuss and analyze Taylor Swift’s impact during yet anothe
 r peak in her extensive and iconic career.</p>\n<p>The conference will run
  from 9am-10pm Friday 11/3 and from 9am-6pm Saturday 11/4. You are welcome
  to attend all or some of the panels.</p>\n<p>A list of panels and times w
 ill be available shortly. There will be a screening of<em> CATS</em> on Fr
 iday evening at 7:30pm.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
