BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114267@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Friends of Lake Monroe presents “Our Wondrous Watershed”\, a ph
 oto exhibit featuring work by fourteen members of the Bloomington Photogra
 phy Club. Photos in the exhibit were captured in the Lake Monroe watershed
 \, an area spanning more than 440 square miles\, reaching into five counti
 es. Most of the watershed is beautiful and rugged\, including Yellowwood S
 tate Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Charles C. Deam Wilderness
 . Attendees will be treated to stunning imagery ranging from macro-photogr
 aphy to sweeping landscapes!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231103T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231103T200000
LOCATION:Brick Room Gallery\, 107 N College Ave
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Friends of Lake Monroe present: Our Wonderous Watershed Opening Pho
 to Exhibit
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/our-wonderous-watershed-opening-photo-exhibit/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Friends of La
 ke Monroe presents “Our Wondrous Watershed”\, a photo exhibit featuring wo
 rk by fourteen members of the Bloomington Photography Club. Photos in the 
 exhibit were captured in the Lake Monroe watershed\, an area spanning more
  than 440 square miles\, reaching into five counties. Most of the watershe
 d is beautiful and rugged\, including Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown Coun
 ty State Park\, and the Charles C. Deam Wilderness. Attendees will be trea
 ted to stunning imagery ranging from macro-photography to sweeping landsca
 pes!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114618@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.bloomingfoods.coop/galleryb
DESCRIPTION:Photographer Patsy Rahn finds the magic in the mundane. In The 
 Alchemy Series\, she takes photographs of everyday objects and using the b
 asic editing tools on her Samsung Galaxy\, manipulates them to create enti
 rely new images. Through this alchemical journey\, the everyday photograph
  is used as basic material to create “the other.” The image emerges from t
 he old into the new like a sculpture emerging from a block of stone\, reve
 aling the inner imagination of the sculptor. The artist will be in the gal
 lery for Gallery Walk night.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231103T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231103T200000
LOCATION:Bloomingfoods Gallery B\, 316 West Sixth Street
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Alchemy Series: Photographs by Patsy Rahn
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-alchemy-series-photographs-by-patsy-rahn/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Photographer 
 Patsy Rahn finds the magic in the mundane. In The Alchemy Series\, she tak
 es photographs of everyday objects and using the basic editing tools on he
 r Samsung Galaxy\, manipulates them to create entirely new images. Through
  this alchemical journey\, the everyday photograph is used as basic materi
 al to create “the other.” The image emerges from the old into the new like
  a sculpture emerging from a block of stone\, revealing the inner imaginat
 ion of the sculptor. The artist will be in the gallery for Gallery Walk ni
 ght.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
