BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-114922@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In this interactive presentation\, Ken Keffer and Heather Ray\,
  owners of Wild Birds Unlimited\, will feature nature hotspots in Blooming
 ton and discuss phenology through the seasons. Learn about the endangered 
 whooping cranes that winter in Goose Pond Wildlife Area\, and why goldfinc
 hes are such late summer nesters. Ken and Heather will provide information
  on the best places to see and experience Bloomington’s beautiful nature s
 cene while discussing their books\, 100 Things to Do in Bloomington Before
  You Die and Knowing the Trees: Discovering the Forest from Seed to Snag. 
 Age 12 and up.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231112T150000
LOCATION:Meeting Room 1B\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 East Kirkwood
  Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Coffee with Friends: Heather Ray & Ken Keffer\, owners of Wild Bird
 s Unlimited
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/coffee-with-friends-heather-ray-ken-keffer-owner
 s-of-wild-birds-unlimited/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>In this inter
 active presentation\, Ken Keffer and<span class='Apple-converted-space'> <
 /span>Heather Ray\, owners of Wild Birds Unlimited\, will feature nature h
 otspots in Bloomington and discuss phenology through the seasons. Learn ab
 out the endangered whooping cranes that winter in Goose Pond Wildlife Area
 \, and why goldfinches are such late summer nesters. Ken and Heather<span 
 class='Apple-converted-space'> </span>will provide information on the best
  places to see and experience Bloomington’s beautiful nature scene while d
 iscussing their books\, <i>100 Things to Do in Bloomington Before You Die<
 /i> and <i>Knowing the Trees: Discovering the Forest from Seed to Snag</i>
 . Age 12 and up.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
