BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-115521@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Please register if interested.  Join this book club to discuss 
 nature-focused reads each month. You’ll also learn how to become more ecol
 ogically-minded through activities and speakers designed to enhance our re
 ading. This month\, we’ll be meeting at the Downtown Library and reading B
 irnam Wood by Booker Prize-winning author Eleanor Catton. Please join us t
 o read an eco-thriller that tests deeply held convictions and loyalties. W
 e’ll also be joined by the Community Gardening Program Manager of the City
  of Bloomington\, who will speak about Bloomington Community Gardens and h
 ow to create green space in urban environments.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231130T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231130T200000
LOCATION:Meeting Room 1B\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 East Kirkwood
  Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Green Peeps Book Club: Birnam Wood (Age 18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/green-peeps-book-club-birnam-wood/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Pleas
 e register if interested. </strong> Join this book club to discuss nature-
 focused reads each month. You’ll also learn how to become more ecologicall
 y-minded through activities and speakers designed to enhance our reading. 
 This month\, we’ll be meeting at the Downtown Library and reading <i>Birna
 m Wood</i> by Booker Prize-winning author Eleanor Catton. Please join us t
 o read an eco-thriller that tests deeply held convictions and loyalties. W
 e’ll also be joined by the Community Gardening Program Manager of the City
  of Bloomington\, who will speak about Bloomington Community Gardens and h
 ow to create green space in urban environments.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
