BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-115454@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A young boy named Ralphie Parker only wants one thing for Chris
 tmas: a Red Ryder BB gun. However\, he is not sure he will ever make it to
  Christmas\, between his brother Randy and the school bully Scut Farkus. W
 henever he tells someone how much he wants it\, he/she tells him that he w
 ill shoot his eye out and refuses to get it for him. Even a department sto
 re Santa Claus tells him the same thing. After Ralphie gets a C+\, he gets
  teased again by Scut. In response\, Ralphie beats him very badly while cu
 rsing loudly. However\, his parents do not get mad at him\, and on Christm
 as morning\, he gets the BB gun\, since his father had one at that age. Wh
 en he goes to try it out\, the BB ricochets and knocks off his glasses\, w
 hich he accidentally steps upon while looking for them. He makes up a stor
 y about an icicle\, and his parents believe him. In the end\, a horde of d
 ogs come in and steal the Christmas turkey\, so his family goes out for “C
 hinese turkey\,” or duck.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231201T193000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 South Van Buren St.\, Nashville
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20231202T193000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20231208T193000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20231209T193000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20231215T193000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20231216T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A Christmas Story
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/a-christmas-story/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A young boy n
 amed Ralphie Parker only wants one thing for Christmas: a Red Ryder BB gun
 . However\, he is not sure he will ever make it to Christmas\, between his
  brother Randy and the school bully Scut Farkus. Whenever he tells someone
  how much he wants it\, he/she tells him that he will shoot his eye out an
 d refuses to get it for him. Even a department store Santa Claus tells him
  the same thing. After Ralphie gets a C+\, he gets teased again by Scut. I
 n response\, Ralphie beats him very badly while cursing loudly. However\, 
 his parents do not get mad at him\, and on Christmas morning\, he gets the
  BB gun\, since his father had one at that age. When he goes to try it out
 \, the BB ricochets and knocks off his glasses\, which he accidentally ste
 ps upon while looking for them. He makes up a story about an icicle\, and 
 his parents believe him. In the end\, a horde of dogs come in and steal th
 e Christmas turkey\, so his family goes out for “Chinese turkey\,” or duck
 .</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-115431@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Screening begins at 8pm\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Community AIDS Action Gr
 oup is proud to partner with Visual AIDS (http://www.visualaids.org) and T
 he Back Door for Day With(out) Art 2023 by presenting Everyone I Know Is S
 ick\, a program of six videos generating connections between HIV and other
  forms of illness and disability.\n\nThe program features newly commission
 ed work by Dorothy Cheung (Hong Kong)\, Hiura Fernandes & Lili Nascimento 
 (Brazil)\, Beau Gomez (Canada/Philippines)\, Dolissa Medina & Ananias P. S
 oria (USA)\, Vasilos Papapitsios (USA)\, and Kurt Weston (USA).\nInspired 
 by a statement from Cyrée Jarelle Johnson in the book Black Futures\, Ever
 yone I Know Is Sick examines how our society excludes disabled and sick pe
 ople by upholding a false dichotomy of health and sickness. Inviting us to
  understand disability as a common experience rather than an exception to 
 the norm\, the program highlights a range of experiences spanning HIV\, CO
 VID\, mental health\, and aging. The commissioned artists foreground the k
 nowledge and expertise of disabled and sick people in a world still grappl
 ing with multiple ongoing pandemics.\n\nThis event is limited to those 21+
  years old.\n\nVisual AIDS is a New York-based non-profit that utilizes ar
 t to fight AIDS by provoking dialogue\, supporting HIV+ artists\, and pres
 erving a legacy\, because AIDS is not over.\nhttp://www.visualaids.org\n\n
 \n\n\n\ncalendar by Tockify
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231201T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231201T230000
LOCATION:The Back Door\, 207 South College Ave.\, in the alley behind the A
 tlas Ballroom
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Day With(out) Art\, includes a screening of ‘Everyone I Know is Sic
 k’
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/day-without-art-includes-a-screening-of-everyone
 -i-know-is-sick/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Scree
 ning begins at 8pm</strong></p>\n<div class='viewerArea__main ng-scope'>\n
 <div class='ng-scope ng-isolate-scope'>\n<div class='eventDetail'>\n<div c
 lass='eventDetail__what'>\n<div class='d-text eventDetail__what__descripti
 on ng-binding'>\n<div>The Community AIDS Action Group is proud to partner 
 with Visual AIDS (<a href='http://www.visualaids.org/?fbclid=IwAR2Ndt9qoq-
 Tx2GcpNyS9Ev_NA58UmHzQcZdxoOLcB2Rum7ikLqBdrIrUc4' target='_blank' rel='noo
 pener'>http://www.visualaids.org</a>) and The Back Door for Day With(out) 
 Art 2023 by presenting Everyone I Know Is Sick\, a program of six videos g
 enerating connections between HIV and other forms of illness and disabilit
 y.</p>\n</div>\n<div>The program features newly commissioned work by Dorot
 hy Cheung (Hong Kong)\, Hiura Fernandes & Lili Nascimento (Brazil)\, Beau 
 Gomez (Canada/Philippines)\, Dolissa Medina & Ananias P. Soria (USA)\, Vas
 ilos Papapitsios (USA)\, and Kurt Weston (USA).</p>\n<p>Inspired by a stat
 ement from Cyrée Jarelle Johnson in the book Black Futures\, Everyone I Kn
 ow Is Sick examines how our society excludes disabled and sick people by u
 pholding a false dichotomy of health and sickness. Inviting us to understa
 nd disability as a common experience rather than an exception to the norm\
 , the program highlights a range of experiences spanning HIV\, COVID\, men
 tal health\, and aging. The commissioned artists foreground the knowledge 
 and expertise of disabled and sick people in a world still grappling with 
 multiple ongoing pandemics.</p>\n</div>\n<div>This event is limited to tho
 se 21+ years old.</p>\n</div>\n<div>Visual AIDS is a New York-based non-pr
 ofit that utilizes art to fight AIDS by provoking dialogue\, supporting HI
 V+ artists\, and preserving a legacy\, because AIDS is not over.<br />\n<a
  href='http://www.visualaids.org/?fbclid=IwAR2DxQ2FrSYqGV3qgYusQyLvTESYwR5
 5SK9ZjIA1kRjwXLiOc9qMShxtVl0' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>http://www.vi
 sualaids.org</a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class
 ='viewerArea__brand ng-scope'><a class='ng-scope branding-subtle is-standa
 lone' translate='calendarByTockify' href='https://tockify.com' target='_bl
 ank' rel='noopener'>calendar by Tockify</a></div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
