BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-115547@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Past Lives is in the conversation as a BEST PICTURE candidate f
 or this year’s Academy Awards. A film about second chances\, if you missed
  Past Lives when we screened it this summer here’s your second chance….\nA
  budding childhood romance between Nora and Hae Sung\, classmates at a pri
 mary school in Seoul\, ends abruptly when Nora’s family emigrates to Canad
 a. Two decades later\, they are reunited in New York for one fateful week 
 as they confront notions of destiny and love\, and the choices that make a
  life.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231209T160000
LOCATION:IU Radio and Television Theater (RTV 251)\, 1229 East 7th St.\, Bl
 oomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: PAST LIVES (screenings at 4pm and 7pm)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-past-lives-screenings-at-4pm-a
 nd-7pm/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><em>Past Live
 s</em> is in the conversation as a BEST PICTURE candidate for this year’s 
 Academy Awards. A film about second chances\, if you missed <em>Past Lives
 </em> when we screened it this summer here’s your second chance….</p>\n<p>
 A budding childhood romance between Nora and Hae Sung\, classmates at a pr
 imary school in Seoul\, ends abruptly when Nora’s family emigrates to Cana
 da. Two decades later\, they are reunited in New York for one fateful week
  as they confront notions of destiny and love\, and the choices that make 
 a life.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
