BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-115762@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The finale will be the dance band class playing the dance Janua
 ry 24th.  \nEvery class will feature 1 to 2 new tunes taught slowly by ear
 \, along with the chords and other accompaniment ideas. In addition\, part
 icipants will practice next to each other\, finding the rhythmic sweet spo
 t of contra dance\, 110 BPM.\nLocal dancers and musicians know Sam\, but m
 ight not know:\nHe has played in virtually every old-time and contra dance
  community in the United States for the past 40 years\, and has played wit
 h a who’s who of touring dance bands including: Wild Asparagus\, the Clayf
 oot Strutters\, Notorious\, Rodney Miller and the Stringrays\, the Monks\,
  and of course Bloomington’s own Supertrad\, with Eric Schedler.   For que
 stions\, contact Sam at: sam@sambartlett.com.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231220T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231220T190000
LOCATION:Serendipity Martini Bar\, 201 S College Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sam Bartlett’s Contra Dance Band Class\, for players 55 and over (b
 ut anyone under that age too)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sam-bartletts-contra-dance-band-class-for-player
 s-55-and-over-but-anyone-under-that-age-too/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>The f
 inale will be the dance band class playing the dance January 24th.  </stro
 ng></p>\n<p>Every class will feature 1 to 2 new tunes taught slowly by ear
 \, along with the chords and other accompaniment ideas. In addition\, part
 icipants will practice next to each other\, finding the rhythmic sweet spo
 t of contra dance\, 110 BPM.</p>\n<p>Local dancers and musicians know Sam\
 , but might not know:</p>\n<p>He has played in virtually every old-time an
 d contra dance community in the United States for the past 40 years\, and 
 has played with a who’s who of touring dance bands including: Wild Asparag
 us\, the Clayfoot Strutters\, Notorious\, Rodney Miller and the Stringrays
 \, the Monks\, and of course Bloomington’s own Supertrad\, with Eric Sched
 ler.   For questions\, contact Sam at: <a href='mailto:sam@sambartlett.com
 ' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>sam@sambartlett.com</a>.</p>\n</BODY></HT
 ML>
