BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-116699@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Since 1989\, the slowest metal band on the planet has conjured 
 some of music’s most striking tectonic changes. Not only did the band Eart
 h create a glacially paced subgenre of metal and play a pivotal role in th
 e popularization of grunge\, but visionary leader Dylan Carlson also did i
 t while battling small-town boredom\, heroin addiction\, and the tragic de
 ath of his roommate and best friend\, Kurt Cobain.\nDespite the high volum
 e of its beloved and beautiful drone metal\, Earth has rarely had much to 
 say for itself. For the first time\, in a moving saga that respects the mu
 sic as much as the ragtag cast of eccentrics and surreal Pacific Northwest
  majesty that shaped it\, Clyde Petersen gets to the core of the could-hav
 e-been-tragic triumph of Earth\, the slow band that changed everything it 
 touched.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240118T200000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 South Walnut Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema Presents: Even Hell Has Its Heroes (18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-even-hell-has-its-heroes-
 18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='desc
 ription clearfix'>\n<div class='field field-name-field-alt-description fie
 ld-type-text-long field-label-hidden'>\n<div class='field-items'>\n<div cl
 ass='field-item even'>\n<p>Since 1989\, the slowest metal band on the plan
 et has conjured some of music’s most striking tectonic changes. Not only d
 id the band Earth create a glacially paced subgenre of metal and play a pi
 votal role in the popularization of grunge\, but visionary leader Dylan Ca
 rlson also did it while battling small-town boredom\, heroin addiction\, a
 nd the tragic death of his roommate and best friend\, Kurt Cobain.</p>\n<p
 >Despite the high volume of its beloved and beautiful drone metal\, Earth 
 has rarely had much to say for itself. For the first time\, in a moving sa
 ga that respects the music as much as the ragtag cast of eccentrics and su
 rreal Pacific Northwest majesty that shaped it\, Clyde Petersen gets to th
 e core of the could-have-been-tragic triumph of Earth\, the slow band that
  changed everything it touched.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
