BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-116292@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Andrea Hadsell\; 812-332-2517 Ext. 3\; http://www.monroehistory.org
 /
DESCRIPTION:Join local author Tristra Newyear for an exploration of her new
 est novel\, Starfall.\nStarfall is a sweeping tale told in the same place\
 , the utopian town of New Harmony\, Indiana\, but in two eras–1820s Americ
 a and the not-so-distant\, post-climate change future.\nIn each era\, a wo
 man stumbles into a community built to change humanity’s course\, founded 
 by eccentrics and scientists\, and finds a town filled with secrets. And o
 ut in the woods beyond the edge of town\, there are mysterious pools all f
 ear and avoid. There\, something strange is happening.\nExploring American
  history and our coming adaptation to climate change\, folklore and techno
 logy\, Starfall incorporates elements of romance and sci-fi\, horror\, and
  natural beauty. It leads readers through a forgotten but vital moment in 
 American progressive experimentation and suggests what might remain valuab
 le to us\, as we face one of humanity’s greatest challenges.\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240120T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240120T150000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E 6th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Tristra Newyear presents Starfall
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/tristra-newyear-presents-starfall/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p style='font-w
 eight: 400\;'>Join local author Tristra Newyear for an exploration of her 
 newest novel\, <em>Starfall</em>.</p>\n<p style='font-weight: 400\;'><em>S
 tarfall </em>is a sweeping tale told in the same place\, the utopian town 
 of New Harmony\, Indiana\, but in two eras–1820s America and the not-so-di
 stant\, post-climate change future.</p>\n<p style='font-weight: 400\;'>In 
 each era\, a woman stumbles into a community built to change humanity’s co
 urse\, founded by eccentrics and scientists\, and finds a town filled with
  secrets. And out in the woods beyond the edge of town\, there are mysteri
 ous pools all fear and avoid. There\, something strange is happening.</p>
 \n<p style='font-weight: 400\;'>Exploring American history and our coming 
 adaptation to climate change\, folklore and technology\, <em>Starfall</em>
  incorporates elements of romance and sci-fi\, horror\, and natural beauty
 . It leads readers through a forgotten but vital moment in American progre
 ssive experimentation and suggests what might remain valuable to us\, as w
 e face one of humanity’s greatest challenges.</p>\n<p> </p>\n</BODY></HTML
 >
END:VEVENT
