UID:ai1ec-116859@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This is an opportunity for everyone to get a sneak peek at 2024
  events and meet the WINGS organizers – and for women unfamiliar with WING
 S to learn more about our group and the programs we offer!\nWe’ll be offer
 ing “samples” of past and future WINGS activities: wild edibles foraging\,
  fishing & casting skills\, tent camping\, archery\, birding\, seed sowing
 \, and stand-up paddleboarding – along with themed snacks at each table.\n
 Drop by anytime between 11 a.m. and 1 p.m…. and maybe bring a friend with 
 you!\nThe goal of Women in Nature Gaining Skills (WINGS) is to encourage a
 nd empower women with the skills and confidence they need to partake in ou
 tdoor recreation activities in the south-central Indiana area. Each WINGS 
 event features women-led hands-on training\, with the goal of building a c
 ommunity of women interested in outdoor recreation. WINGS events take plac
 e on the 3rd Sunday of each month and are open to ages 16 and up.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240121T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240121T130000
LOCATION:Commons Building\, Karst Farm Park\, 2450 South Endwright Road\, B
 loomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:WINGS (Women In Nature Gaining Skills) Mini Expo
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/wings-women-in-nature-gaining-skills-mini-expo/
X-COST-TYPE:free
