BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117092@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:An intimate look at the war in Ukraine\, as seen through the ey
 es of artists who remained to make art as a defiant act in the face of agg
 ression.\nThe Rule of Two Walls has not yet opened in theaters (hence no r
 eviews to report) but we have this from the Tribecca Film Festival:\nWhile
  their lives are getting irreversibly altered\, the film beautifully docum
 ents how their work — as visual artists\, musicians\, street artists\, per
 formance artists\, and filmmakers — both processes the moment and offers h
 ope. Visceral\, poetic\, and urgent\, Rule of Two Walls illuminates the vi
 tal role of cultural and spiritual defiance in times of crisis.\n\npresent
 ed in part by the IU Dept of Slavic & East European Languages and the Russ
 ian and East European Institute
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240127T163000
LOCATION:IU Radio and Television Theater\, Radio & Television Theater (RTV 
 251) is at 1229 East 7th Street\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240203T163000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: RULE OF TWO WALLS (Screenings at 4:30pm and 7:30
 pm)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-rule-of-two-walls-screenings-a
 t-430pm-and-730pm/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>An intimate l
 ook at the war in Ukraine\, as seen through the eyes of artists who remain
 ed to make art as a defiant act in the face of aggression.</p>\n<p>The Rul
 e of Two Walls has not yet opened in theaters (hence no reviews to report)
  but we have this from the Tribecca Film Festival:</p>\n<p><strong><em>Whi
 le their lives are getting irreversibly altered\, the film beautifully doc
 uments how their work — as visual artists\, musicians\, street artists\, p
 erformance artists\, and filmmakers — both processes the moment and offers
  hope. Visceral\, poetic\, and urgent\, Rule of Two Walls illuminates the 
 vital role of cultural and spiritual defiance in times of crisis</em>.<br 
 />\n</strong></p>\n<p>presented in part by the IU Dept of Slavic & East Eu
 ropean Languages and the Russian and East European Institute</p>\n</BODY><
 /HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-116986@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Fifteen years ago\, a group of IU students founded Raas Royalty
 \, one of the most prestigious Indian dance competitions. Raas Royalty sho
 wcases eight collegiate Raas dance teams from across the country and allow
 s them to compete for the crown! For the 15th year running\, Raas Royalty 
 is free of charge and continues to be the only free collegiate garba-raas 
 competition in the United States. Raas Royalty invites you to learn more a
 bout Indian culture and to watch creative and energetic performances from 
 the best teams across the country.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240127T170000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Raas Royalty
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/raas-royalty-3/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Fifteen years
  ago\, a group of IU students founded Raas Royalty\, one of the most prest
 igious Indian dance competitions. Raas Royalty showcases eight collegiate 
 Raas dance teams from across the country and allows them to compete for th
 e crown! For the 15th year running\, Raas Royalty is free of charge and co
 ntinues to be the only free collegiate garba-raas competition in the Unite
 d States. Raas Royalty invites you to learn more about Indian culture and 
 to watch creative and energetic performances from the best teams across th
 e country.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
