BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117606@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A seemingly simple taxi ride across Paris evolves into a profou
 nd meditation on the realities of the driver\, whose personal life is in s
 hambles\, and his fare\, an elderly woman whose warmth belies her surprisi
 ng past.\nDriving Madeleine is highlighted by two wonderful performances: 
 actor/director Dany Boon as a taxi driver having a bad day and legendary 9
 2-year-old French chanteuse Line Renaud as a woman in need of a ride.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240204T160000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Theater\, 1201 East 7th St. (on the 2nd floor)\, Bloo
 mington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240211T160000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: DRIVING MADELEINE
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-driving-madeleine/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A seemingly s
 imple taxi ride across Paris evolves into a profound meditation on the rea
 lities of the driver\, whose personal life is in shambles\, and his fare\,
  an elderly woman whose warmth belies her surprising past.</p>\n<p>Driving
  Madeleine is highlighted by two wonderful performances: actor/director Da
 ny Boon as a taxi driver having a bad day and legendary 92-year-old French
  chanteuse Line Renaud as a woman in need of a ride.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117378@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Potluck at 5pm\, Music at 6pm\nHell Yes People Happy New Year\,
  we’re starting the year strong with another fantastic show. You know the 
 drill\, bring a dish if you wish\, some bucks for the bands(~$15) and a fr
 iend that likes great things. potluck at 5 music at 6\nThe Tillers- Cincin
 nati folk band that slays your heart and your ear bones. Last year we had 
 all but Aaron come through and play us a solo show now we got the full ban
 d altogether!\nHummingbird and the Beating Hearts- Bloomington – Bryn Crow
 song\, Jony Perron\, Tressa Martinie Eiler & Ross Martinie Eiler.\nEpic Ac
 oustic Harmonic Soul. HBBH was born at the Switchyard and then chemically 
 produced in a laboratory to put on a Switchyard House Venue show.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240204T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240204T213000
LOCATION:Switchyard House Venue\, 1417 South Monon Drive\, Blomington
SEQUENCE:0
