UID:ai1ec-117720@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Mark Lewis is a withdrawn young man who works as a focus puller
  in a film studio\, moonlighting as a “private” photographer of scantily-c
 lad women while obsessively working on his own “documentary” using the wor
 ld’s most lethal tripod. An uncharacteristic thriller/horror movie by the 
 co-director of The Red Shoes (whose prima ballerina\, Moira Shearer\, is a
 lso featured)\, Peeping Tom was savagely attacked by contemporary critics\
 , stalling Michael Powell’s career for years. In the ensuing decades\, the
  film’s reputation has skyrocketed\, and it’s now recognized as a provocat
 ive study of voyeurism\, a portrait of self-destruction\, and blackly play
 ful variations on “seeing” and identity. [101 min\; thriller\, horror\; En
 glish]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240206T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: Peeping Tom
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-peeping-tom/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Mark Lewis is
  a withdrawn young man who works as a focus puller in a film studio\, moon
 lighting as a “private” photographer of scantily-clad women while obsessiv
 ely working on his own “documentary” using the world’s most lethal tripod.
  An uncharacteristic thriller/horror movie by the co-director of <i>The Re
 d Shoes</i> (whose prima ballerina\, Moira Shearer\, is also featured)\, <
 i>Peeping Tom</i> was savagely attacked by contemporary critics\, stalling
  Michael Powell’s career for years. In the ensuing decades\, the film’s re
 putation has skyrocketed\, and it’s now recognized as a provocative study 
 of voyeurism\, a portrait of self-destruction\, and blackly playful variat
 ions on “seeing” and identity. [101 min\; thriller\, horror\; English]</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
