BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117687@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Thursday February 8 at 7:00 pm ET as we welco
 me Dr. Shemeka Thorpe for a conversation about Black women’s experiences o
 f sexual pleasure and pain.\nDr. Thorpe is an assistant professor at the U
 niversity of Kentucky and also co-founder of the Minority Sex Report. Host
 ed by Dr. Debby Herbenick – local sex researcher\, educator\, and author o
 f Yes Your Kid: What Parents Need to Know About Today’s Teens and Sex – th
 e Bloomington Sex Salon was created to foster campus-community conversatio
 ns about sexuality topics.\nOur format goes like this: for the first 30-40
  minutes\, Debby will ask Dr. Thorpe questions about her research and publ
 ic scholarship. The next 20-30 minutes will be Q&A with the audience.\nFre
 e for those ages 18+.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240208T190000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 South Walnut St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sex Salon\, hosted by Dr. Debby Herbenick: A conversation with Dr. 
 Shemeka Thorpe\, assistant professor at the University of Kentucky and als
 o co-founder of the Minority Sex Report. (18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sex-salon-hosted-by-dr-debby-herbenick-a-convers
 ation-with-dr-shemeka-thorpe-assistant-professor-at-the-university-of-kent
 ucky-and-also-co-founder-of-the-minority-sex-report-18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Please join u
 s on Thursday February 8 at 7:00 pm ET as we welcome Dr. Shemeka Thorpe fo
 r a conversation about Black women’s experiences of sexual pleasure and pa
 in.<br />\nDr. Thorpe is an assistant professor at the University of Kentu
 cky and also co-founder of the Minority Sex Report. Hosted by Dr. Debby He
 rbenick – local sex researcher\, educator\, and author of Yes Your Kid: Wh
 at Parents Need to Know About Today’s Teens and Sex – the Bloomington Sex 
 Salon was created to foster campus-community conversations about sexuality
  topics.<br />\nOur format goes like this: for the first 30-40 minutes\, D
 ebby will ask Dr. Thorpe questions about her research and public scholarsh
 ip. The next 20-30 minutes will be Q&A with the audience.<br />\nFree for 
 those ages 18+.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
