BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117930@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The first and best of the famous whodunnit The Thin Man series 
 which introduces the wisecracking\, martini-sipping husband-and-wife sleut
 hing team of Nick and Nora Charles\, who are investigating the disappearan
 ce of an inventor who later is implicated in the murder of his secretary. 
 An adaptation of a Dashiell Hammett private-eye classic\, The Thin Man was
  followed by five sequels\, with Powell and Loy appearing together in 14 f
 ilms total throughout their careers.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240210T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:90th Anniversary Screening of THE THIN MAN
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/90th-anniversary-screening-of-the-thin-man/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The first and
  best of the famous whodunnit <i>The Thin Man</i> series which introduces 
 the wisecracking\, martini-sipping husband-and-wife sleuthing team of Nick
  and Nora Charles\, who are investigating the disappearance of an inventor
  who later is implicated in the murder of his secretary. An adaptation of 
 a Dashiell Hammett private-eye classic\, <i>The Thin Man </i>was followed 
 by five sequels\, with Powell and Loy appearing together in 14 films total
  throughout their careers.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117932@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Winner of the Camera d’Or at the Cannes Film Festival and the p
 restigious André Bazin Prize from Cahiers du Cinema\, both celebrating out
 standing feature debuts\, this enthralling work from Vietnamese filmmaker 
 Pham Thien An is a reverie on faith\, loss\, and nature expressed with unc
 ommon invention and depth. The sudden death of his sister-in-law brings un
 expected responsibilities to Thien (Le Phong Vu)\, who is reluctantly task
 ed with bringing his five-year-old nephew Dao to their countryside hometow
 n. On the road\, Thien is drawn into a search for his long-missing older b
 rother\, haunted and spurred forward by a series of sublime dreams that re
 ignite suppressed memories\, forbidden desires\, and specters of his own y
 outh. What began as a journey home becomes a pilgrimage marked by visual s
 plendor and mystical overtones\, a quest for understanding and certainty i
 n a Vietnam that seems unable to provide any clear answers. As Thien battl
 es with the existential question of what is worth living for\, Inside the 
 Yellow Cocoon Shell interrogates the persistence and complexity of faith\,
  not only in the spiritual but in the delicate beauty of earthly existence
 .
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240210T163000
LOCATION:IU Radio and Television Theater\, Radio & Television Theater (RTV 
 251) is at 1229 East 7th Street\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240211T163000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240217T163000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240218T163000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: INSIDE THE YELLOW COCOON SHELL
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-inside-the-yellow-cocoon-shell
 /
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Winner of the
  Camera d’Or at the Cannes Film Festival and the prestigious André Bazin P
 rize from Cahiers du Cinema\, both celebrating outstanding feature debuts\
 , this enthralling work from Vietnamese filmmaker Pham Thien An is a rever
 ie on faith\, loss\, and nature expressed with uncommon invention and dept
 h. The sudden death of his sister-in-law brings unexpected responsibilitie
 s to Thien (Le Phong Vu)\, who is reluctantly tasked with bringing his fiv
 e-year-old nephew Dao to their countryside hometown. On the road\, Thien i
 s drawn into a search for his long-missing older brother\, haunted and spu
 rred forward by a series of sublime dreams that reignite suppressed memori
 es\, forbidden desires\, and specters of his own youth. What began as a jo
 urney home becomes a pilgrimage marked by visual splendor and mystical ove
 rtones\, a quest for understanding and certainty in a Vietnam that seems u
 nable to provide any clear answers. As Thien battles with the existential 
 question of what is worth living for\, <em>Inside the Yellow Cocoon Shell<
 /em> interrogates the persistence and complexity of faith\, not only in th
 e spiritual but in the delicate beauty of earthly existence.</p>\n</BODY><
 /HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
