BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117808@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join Mitchell Opera House for a meet & greet with the #1 Barney
  Fife Tribute AND a clean\, family-friendly comedy show!\nClean comedian R
 ik Roberts brings the big laughs without the bad words!!\nComedian and cre
 ative keynote speaker Rik Roberts grew up in Kentucky. He farmed tobacco a
 longside his father from an early age. Later\, as a teenager he worked for
  former Kentucky Wildcat and NBA Star Dan Issel on his Thoroughbred horse 
 farm “Courtland”. After earning a degree in communications from Bethany Co
 llege\, Rik worked for Simon & Schuster in Columbus\, OH. He joined a nati
 onally touring comedy troupe “Midwest Comedy Tool & Die” [MCTD] in 1992. S
 hortly thereafter\, he decided to jump head first into stand-up comedy. He
  now has nearly 30 years of headlining experience across the United States
  and abroad. He is the International spokesman for “Bin There\, Dump That”
 . He also was a writer and performer on “The Henry Cho Comedy Show” on Gre
 at American Country.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240210T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240210T210000
LOCATION:Mitchell Opera House\, 217 North 7th Street\, Mitchell
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Rik Roberts – Barney Fife Tribute Meet & Greet and Clean Comedy Nig
 ht!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/rik-roberts-barney-fife-tribute-meet-greet-and-c
 lean-comedy-night/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join Mitchell
  Opera House for a meet & greet with the #1 Barney Fife Tribute AND a clea
 n\, family-friendly comedy show!<br />\nClean comedian Rik Roberts brings 
 the big laughs without the bad words!!<br />\nComedian and creative keynot
 e speaker Rik Roberts grew up in Kentucky. He farmed tobacco alongside his
  father from an early age. Later\, as a teenager he worked for former Kent
 ucky Wildcat and NBA Star Dan Issel on his Thoroughbred horse farm “Courtl
 and”. After earning a degree in communications from Bethany College\, Rik 
 worked for Simon & Schuster in Columbus\, OH. He joined a nationally touri
 ng comedy troupe “Midwest Comedy Tool & Die” [MCTD] in 1992. Shortly there
 after\, he decided to jump head first into stand-up comedy. He now has nea
 rly 30 years of headlining experience across the United States and abroad.
  He is the International spokesman for “Bin There\, Dump That”. He also wa
 s a writer and performer on “The Henry Cho Comedy Show” on Great American 
 Country.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
