BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117918@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:As the Chinese New Year marks a significant cultural event in t
 he Chinese calendar\, the IU Chinese Students and Scholars Association (IU
 CSSA) is thrilled to host this celebration to share traditions and festivi
 ties with the wider Indiana University and Bloomington community. The them
 e for this year’s event\, “Dragon Brings Fortune\, Together We Paint the N
 ew Spring.” embodying the spirit of unity and prosperity that the Year of 
 the Dragon brings.\nThe evening promises a rich experience with a variety 
 of activities\, including:\n\nA buffet-style dinner featuring traditional 
 Chinese cuisine\nA series of performances showcasing Chinese cultural arts
 \nInteractive activities and games for attendees to engage in the festive 
 spirit\nA raffle draw with exciting prizes\nSpecial snack gift bags as a t
 oken of appreciation for our guests\n\nThe IUCSSA believes this event is a
  wonderful opportunity for cultural exchange and fostering a deeper unders
 tanding of Chinese traditions within the university community
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240211T190000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Chinese New Year Gala Hosted by IU’s Chinese Students and Scholar A
 ssociation
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/chinese-new-year-gala-hosted-by-ius-chinese-stud
 ents-and-scholar-association/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>As the Chines
 e New Year marks a significant cultural event in the Chinese calendar\, th
 e IU Chinese Students and Scholars Association (IUCSSA) is thrilled to hos
 t this celebration to share traditions and festivities with the wider Indi
 ana University and Bloomington community. The theme for this year’s event\
 , “Dragon Brings Fortune\, Together We Paint the New Spring.” embodying th
 e spirit of unity and prosperity that the Year of the Dragon brings.</p>\n
 <p>The evening promises a rich experience with a variety of activities\, i
 ncluding:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A buffet-style dinner featuring traditional Chine
 se cuisine</li>\n<li>A series of performances showcasing Chinese cultural 
 arts</li>\n<li>Interactive activities and games for attendees to engage in
  the festive spirit</li>\n<li>A raffle draw with exciting prizes</li>\n<li
 >Special snack gift bags as a token of appreciation for our guests</li>\n<
 /ul>\n<p>The IUCSSA believes this event is a wonderful opportunity for cul
 tural exchange and fostering a deeper understanding of Chinese traditions 
 within the university community</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
