BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118031@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A team of African-American climbers take on the challenge of su
 mmitting North America’s highest mountain in this enthralling documentary.
  Q&A to follow. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAbout An American Ascent\nAn American As
 cent is a documentary film about the first African-American expedition to 
 climb North America’s highest peak\, Denali. By taking on the grueling\, 2
 0\,310 foot peak of the continent’s biggest mountain\, nine African-Americ
 an climbers set out to build a legacy of inclusion in the outdoor/adventur
 e community. The film addresses often overlooked issues of race and the ou
 tdoors as it follows the team up the mountain\, chronicling  the many chal
 lenges of climbing one of the world’s most iconic peaks.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240213T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: AN AMERICAN ASCENT
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-an-american-ascent/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='content
 ' class='collapsed individual-film__intro collapsed bg-none section'>\n<di
 v class='row'>\n<div class='layout'>\n<div class='text'>\n<p class='text s
 creening-highlight'><strong> A team of African-American climbers take on t
 he challenge of summitting North America’s highest mountain in this enthra
 lling documentary. Q&A to follow. </strong></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<
 /div>\n<div class='section bg-none individual-film__intro'>\n<div class='r
 ow'>\n<div class='layout'>\n<div class='text'>\n<h3 class='visually-hidden
 '>About An American Ascent</h3>\n<p><i>An American Ascent</i> is a documen
 tary film about the first African-American expedition to climb North Ameri
 ca’s highest peak\, Denali. By taking on the grueling\, 20\,310 foot peak 
 of the continent’s biggest mountain\, nine African-American climbers set o
 ut to build a legacy of inclusion in the outdoor/adventure community. The 
 film addresses often overlooked issues of race and the outdoors as it foll
 ows the team up the mountain\, chronicling  the many challenges of climbin
 g one of the world’s most iconic peaks.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div
 >\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
