BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118033@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:David Cronenberg combines his trademark affinity for gore and h
 orror with strongly developed characters\, making The Fly a surprisingly a
 ffecting romantic tragedy. When scientist Seth Brundle (Jeff Goldblum) com
 pletes his teleportation device\, he decides to test its abilities on hims
 elf. Unbeknownst to him\, a housefly slips in during the process\, leading
  to a merger of man and insect. Initially\, Brundle appears to have underg
 one a successful teleportation\, but the fly’s cells begin to take over hi
 s body. As he becomes increasingly fly-like\, Brundle’s girlfriend (Geena 
 Davis) is horrified as the person she once loved deteriorates into a monst
 er. [95 min\; sci-fi\, horror\, romance\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240214T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: THE FLY
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-the-fly/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>David Cronenb
 erg combines his trademark affinity for gore and horror with strongly deve
 loped characters\, making <i>The Fly</i> a surprisingly affecting romantic
  tragedy. When scientist Seth Brundle (Jeff Goldblum) completes his telepo
 rtation device\, he decides to test its abilities on himself. Unbeknownst 
 to him\, a housefly slips in during the process\, leading to a merger of m
 an and insect. Initially\, Brundle appears to have undergone a successful 
 teleportation\, but the fly’s cells begin to take over his body. As he bec
 omes increasingly fly-like\, Brundle’s girlfriend (Geena Davis) is horrifi
 ed as the person she once loved deteriorates into a monster. [95 min\; sci
 -fi\, horror\, romance\; English]</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
