BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117995@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join the History Center for a fascinating presentation on the u
 nique dry stack stone walls seen across the county!\nIf you navigate the h
 ills and valleys of the western half of Monroe County\, you will pass many
  stands of dry stack stone walls. Wall stones have been repurposed near wh
 ere walls once marked a property line or other notable location. Join Susa
 n Snider Salmon as we look at the stories of what is known and examine wha
 t remains to be rediscovered.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240217T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240217T150000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E. 6th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:No Rolling Stones: a Landscape Perspective of the Dry Stack Stone W
 alls of Monroe County
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/no-rolling-stones-a-landscape-perspective-of-the
 -dry-stack-stone-walls-of-monroe-county-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='font
 -semibold mb-2'>Join the History Center for a fascinating presentation on 
 the unique dry stack stone walls seen across the county!</div>\n<div class
 ='mt-6 mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap text-gray-700'>If you navigate the hills a
 nd valleys of the western half of Monroe County\, you will pass many stand
 s of dry stack stone walls. Wall stones have been repurposed near where wa
 lls once marked a property line or other notable location. Join Susan Snid
 er Salmon as we look at the stories of what is known and examine what rema
 ins to be rediscovered.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118216@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:ANIMATED SHORTS – 80 minutes\nYou know your kids better than we
  do but this year’s animation shorts are probably not for children under 1
 3\n\nOur Uniform – a social satire about the clothing conventions imposed 
 on young children  Iran (in Farsi)\nLetter to a Pig – A Holocaust survivor
  reads a letter he wrote to the pig who saved his life.\, France/Israel (i
 n Hebrew)\nPachyderm– Louise spends time at her grandparent’s house\, Yet 
 this year\, the snow will fall in summer and a monster will die.\nNinety-F
 ive Senses – An ode to the body’s five senses\, delivered by a man with li
 ttle time left to enjoy them.\nWar is Over! Inspired by the Music of John 
 & Yoko Two soldiers on opposite sides play a game of chess.\nBONUS FILMS: 
 \nWild Summon – A natural history fantasy film\, following the dramatic li
 fecycle of the wild salmon in human form (narrated by Marianne Faithfull)
 \nI’m Hip – A self-absorbed cat\, in a jazzy song and dance\, proudly and 
 comically proclaims his “hipness” to the world. The world is less convince
 d than he is.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240217T140000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Theater\, 1201 East 7th St. (on the 2nd floor)\, Bloo
 mington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240218T140000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: OSCAR SHORTS–ANIMATION
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-oscar-shorts-animation-7/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>ANIMA
 TED SHORTS – 80 minutes</strong></p>\n<p><em>You know your kids better tha
 n we do but this year’s animation shorts are probably not for children und
 er 13<br />\n</em></p>\n<p><strong>Our Uniform</strong> – a social satire 
 about the <em>clothing</em> conventions imposed on young children  Iran (i
 n Farsi)</p>\n<p><strong>Letter to a Pig</strong> – A Holocaust survivor r
 eads a <em>letter</em> he wrote to the <em>pig</em> who saved his life.\, 
 France/Israel (in Hebrew)</p>\n<p><strong>Pachyderm</strong>– Louise spend
 s time at her grandparent’s house\, Yet this year\, the snow will fall in 
 summer and a monster will die.</p>\n<p><strong>Ninety-Five Senses</strong>
  – An ode to the body’s <em>five senses</em>\, delivered by a man with lit
 tle time left to enjoy them.</p>\n<p><strong>War is Over! Inspired by the 
 Music of John & Yoko</strong> Two soldiers on opposite sides play a game o
 f chess.</p>\n<p><strong>BONUS FILMS: </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Wild Summo
 n</strong> – A natural history fantasy film\, following the dramatic lifec
 ycle of the wild salmon in human form (narrated by Marianne Faithfull)</p>
 \n<p><strong>I’m Hip</strong> – A self-absorbed cat\, in a jazzy song and 
 dance\, proudly and comically proclaims his “hipness” to the world. The wo
 rld is less convinced than he is.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
