BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118039@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A favorite on the nationally syndicated Bob and Tom Radio Show\
 , Greg has also appeared on Late Night with Conan O’Brien\, Comedy Central
 \, CBS\, ABC\, FOX\, MTV and CMT.\nGreg Hahn has parlayed his absurdly ene
 rgetic\, all out style of physical humor\, one liners and crowd work into 
 a performance of immediate pandemonium and continuous laughs. His unique s
 tylings have led to numerous television\, corporate and theater appearance
 s throughout the US and Canada.\nDave “The King” Wilson\, a world renowned
  stand-up comedian of 11 years\, has been an Indianapolis radio listeners’
  companion for longer than that. First in 1983 to 1995 with Bob & Tom on Q
 -95 and then as the longtime host of the WIBC afternoon show\, Dave has be
 come part of the Indy landsape. A native of Speedway\, Wilson grew up less
  than a mile from the Brickyard and spent a great deal of time at the trac
 k during May as a youth\, just as he now does as an adult.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240217T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240217T220000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Greg Hahn\, with Dave “The King” Wilson
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/greg-hahn-with-dave-the-king-wilson/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A favorite on
  the nationally syndicated Bob and Tom Radio Show\, Greg has also appeared
  on Late Night with Conan O’Brien\, Comedy Central\, CBS\, ABC\, FOX\, MTV
  and CMT.<br />\nGreg Hahn has parlayed his absurdly energetic\, all out s
 tyle of physical humor\, one liners and crowd work into a performance of i
 mmediate pandemonium and continuous laughs. His unique stylings have led t
 o numerous television\, corporate and theater appearances throughout the U
 S and Canada.</p>\n<p>Dave “The King” Wilson\, a world renowned stand-up c
 omedian of 11 years\, has been an Indianapolis radio listeners’ companion 
 for longer than that. First in 1983 to 1995 with Bob & Tom on Q-95 and the
 n as the longtime host of the WIBC afternoon show\, Dave has become part o
 f the Indy landsape. A native of Speedway\, Wilson grew up less than a mil
 e from the Brickyard and spent a great deal of time at the track during Ma
 y as a youth\, just as he now does as an adult.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118217@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:ANIMATED SHORTS – 80 minutes\nYou know your kids better than we
  do but this year’s animation shorts are probably not for children under 1
 3\n\nOur Uniform – a social satire about the clothing conventions imposed 
 on young children  Iran (in Farsi)\nLetter to a Pig – A Holocaust survivor
  reads a letter he wrote to the pig who saved his life.\, France/Israel (i
 n Hebrew)\nPachyderm– Louise spends time at her grandparent’s house\, Yet 
 this year\, the snow will fall in summer and a monster will die.\nNinety-F
 ive Senses – An ode to the body’s five senses\, delivered by a man with li
 ttle time left to enjoy them.\nWar is Over! Inspired by the Music of John 
 & Yoko Two soldiers on opposite sides play a game of chess.\nBONUS FILMS: 
 \nWild Summon – A natural history fantasy film\, following the dramatic li
 fecycle of the wild salmon in human form (narrated by Marianne Faithfull)
 \nI’m Hip – A self-absorbed cat\, in a jazzy song and dance\, proudly and 
 comically proclaims his “hipness” to the world. The world is less convince
 d than he is.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240217T193000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Theater\, 1201 East 7th St. (on the 2nd floor)\, Bloo
 mington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240218T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryder Film Series: OSCAR SHORTS–ANIMATION
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryder-film-series-oscar-shorts-animation-8/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>ANIMA
 TED SHORTS – 80 minutes</strong></p>\n<p><em>You know your kids better tha
 n we do but this year’s animation shorts are probably not for children und
 er 13<br />\n</em></p>\n<p><strong>Our Uniform</strong> – a social satire 
 about the <em>clothing</em> conventions imposed on young children  Iran (i
 n Farsi)</p>\n<p><strong>Letter to a Pig</strong> – A Holocaust survivor r
 eads a <em>letter</em> he wrote to the <em>pig</em> who saved his life.\, 
 France/Israel (in Hebrew)</p>\n<p><strong>Pachyderm</strong>– Louise spend
 s time at her grandparent’s house\, Yet this year\, the snow will fall in 
 summer and a monster will die.</p>\n<p><strong>Ninety-Five Senses</strong>
  – An ode to the body’s <em>five senses</em>\, delivered by a man with lit
 tle time left to enjoy them.</p>\n<p><strong>War is Over! Inspired by the 
 Music of John & Yoko</strong> Two soldiers on opposite sides play a game o
 f chess.</p>\n<p><strong>BONUS FILMS: </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Wild Summo
 n</strong> – A natural history fantasy film\, following the dramatic lifec
 ycle of the wild salmon in human form (narrated by Marianne Faithfull)</p>
 \n<p><strong>I’m Hip</strong> – A self-absorbed cat\, in a jazzy song and 
 dance\, proudly and comically proclaims his “hipness” to the world. The wo
 rld is less convinced than he is.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
