BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118302@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:With lyrics and music by Emmy\, Grammy\, Oscar\, and Tony winne
 rs Tim Rice and Andrew Lloyd Webber\, Jesus Christ Superstar is set agains
 t the backdrop of an extraordinary series of events during the final weeks
  in the life of Jesus Christ as seen through the eyes of Judas. Reflecting
  the rock roots that defined a generation\, the legendary score includes “
 I Don’t Know How to Love Him\,” “Gethsemane\,” and “Superstar.”\n \nThis p
 roduction won the 2017 Olivier Award for Best Musical Revival\, garnering 
 unprecedented reviews and accolades. Appealing to both theater audiences a
 nd concert music fans\, this production pays tribute to the historic 1971 
 Billboard Album of the Year while creating a modern\, theatrical world tha
 t is uniquely fresh and inspiring.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240219T193000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240220T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Jesus Christ Superstar\, The 50th anniversary tour
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/jesus-christ-superstar-the-50th-anniversary-tour
 /
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>With lyrics a
 nd music by Emmy\, Grammy\, Oscar\, and Tony winners Tim Rice and Andrew L
 loyd Webber\,<i> Jesus Christ Superstar </i>is set against the backdrop of
  an extraordinary series of events during the final weeks in the life of J
 esus Christ as seen through the eyes of Judas. Reflecting the rock roots t
 hat defined a generation\, the legendary score includes “I Don’t Know How 
 to Love Him\,” “Gethsemane\,” and “Superstar.”</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>This prod
 uction won the 2017 Olivier Award for Best Musical Revival\, garnering unp
 recedented reviews and accolades. Appealing to both theater audiences and 
 concert music fans\, this production pays tribute to the historic 1971 Bil
 lboard Album of the Year while creating a modern\, theatrical world that i
 s uniquely fresh and inspiring.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
