BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118294@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:King Crimson is a band that people literally are dying to be in
 . In the Court of the Crimson King is a dark\, comic film for anyone who w
 onders whether it is worth sacrificing everything for just a single moment
  of transcendence. For over 50 years Robert Fripp\, also famous for his wo
 rk with David Bowie and Brian Eno\, has overseen a unique creative environ
 ment in which freedom and responsibility conspire to place extraordinary d
 emands on the band’s members – only alleviated by the applause of an audie
 nce whose adoration threatens to make their lives even harder. It’s a rewa
 rding and perilous space in which the extraordinary is possible\, nothing 
 is certain\, and not everyone survives intact.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240222T200000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 South Walnut St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema Film: In the Court of the Crimson King. King Crimson 
 at 50
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-film-in-the-court-of-the-crimson-k
 ing-king-crimson-at-50/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>King Crimson 
 is a band that people literally are dying to be in. In the Court of the Cr
 imson King is a dark\, comic film for anyone who wonders whether it is wor
 th sacrificing everything for just a single moment of transcendence. For o
 ver 50 years Robert Fripp\, also famous for his work with David Bowie and 
 Brian Eno\, has overseen a unique creative environment in which freedom an
 d responsibility conspire to place extraordinary demands on the band’s mem
 bers – only alleviated by the applause of an audience whose adoration thre
 atens to make their lives even harder. It’s a rewarding and perilous space
  in which the extraordinary is possible\, nothing is certain\, and not eve
 ryone survives intact.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
