BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118534@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:for writers who want to work with music and audio\nand musician
 s who want to work with spoken word\nand anyone in between!  \nImpressive 
 sources\, but what if we were to free ourselves from these categories? Wha
 t if we harness the beauty of words\, sounds\, and music as one\, without 
 depriving ourselves of one or the other?\nSound poetry\, performance art\,
  or just composing words to be heard out loud\, call it what you will. The
  Electroacoustical Poetical Society is offering a fun workshop during whic
 h we’ll throw genres to the winds and explore the sound in words and the i
 deas in sound\, for performance. We’ll start with some examples for discus
 sion and then explore the joys of making words and sounds into equal partn
 ers.\nBring a short poem or piece of writing you like to read\, or your in
 strument\, or just bring yourself with your voice.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240223T180000
LOCATION:Backspace Gallery\, inside Bonne Fête\, 112 West 6th Street\, on t
 he square in Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Electroacoustical Poetical Society Workshop
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/electroacoustical-poetical-society-workshop-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong><span
  class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkez
 so x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1
 l8bm xzsf02u' dir='auto'>for writers who want to work with music and audio
 <br />\nand musicians who want to work with spoken word<br />\nand anyone 
 in between!</span>  </strong></p>\n<div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x
 1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Impressive sources\, but what if we were to free ourselves
  from these categories? What if we harness the beauty of words\, sounds\, 
 and music as one\, without depriving ourselves of one or the other?</div>
 \n<div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Sound poetry\, pe
 rformance art\, or just composing words to be heard out loud\, call it wha
 t you will. The Electroacoustical Poetical Society is offering a fun works
 hop during which we’ll throw genres to the winds and explore the sound in 
 words and the ideas in sound\, for performance. We’ll start with some exam
 ples for discussion and then explore the joys of making words and sounds i
 nto equal partners.</div>\n<div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x
 tlvy1s'>Bring a short poem or piece of writing you like to read\, or your 
 instrument\, or just bring yourself with your voice.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117133@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Ready to press pause on what you already know? TEDxIndianaUnive
 rsity presents “Play or Pause\,” our seventh annual conference\, inviting 
 Bloomington and Indiana University communities for an exhilarating dive in
 to choice and transformation. Our curated lineup boasts six global speaker
 s\, driven by sharing impactful ideas. More than a conference\, it’s an im
 mersion into contemplating action and stillness\, momentum\, and reflectio
 n.\nLife oscillates between spirited playfulness and introspective pauses\
 , defining our existence. Some embrace “play” as life’s essence\; others s
 eek a blend. “Play or Pause” challenges the idea of a final endpoint to th
 is dynamic\, inviting us to reevaluate strategies and explore fresh perspe
 ctives on life’s choices.\nJoin us for a transformative journey\, redefini
 ng our narratives through choice at “Play or Pause.”\nThis event is recomm
 ended for ages 13 and older. It is possible that the content of our speake
 rs’ stories may be complex for younger audiences.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240223T180000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:TEDx Indiana University presents “Play or Pause”\, their Seventh An
 nual Conference
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/tedindiana-university-present-play-or-pause/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='prev
 iew-modal modal-body'>\n<p>Ready to press pause on what you already know? 
 TEDxIndianaUniversity presents “Play or Pause\,” our seventh annual confer
 ence\, inviting Bloomington and Indiana University communities for an exhi
 larating dive into choice and transformation. Our curated lineup boasts si
 x global speakers\, driven by sharing impactful ideas. More than a confere
 nce\, it’s an immersion into contemplating action and stillness\, momentum
 \, and reflection.</p>\n<p>Life oscillates between spirited playfulness an
 d introspective pauses\, defining our existence. Some embrace “play” as li
 fe’s essence\; others seek a blend. “Play or Pause” challenges the idea of
  a final endpoint to this dynamic\, inviting us to reevaluate strategies a
 nd explore fresh perspectives on life’s choices.</p>\n<p>Join us for a tra
 nsformative journey\, redefining our narratives through choice at “Play or
  Pause.”</p>\n<p>This event is recommended for ages 13 and older. It is po
 ssible that the content of our speakers’ stories may be complex for younge
 r audiences.</p>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
