BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-118303@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Les Ballets Trockadero de Monte Carlo\, the world’s foremost al
 l-male comic ballet company\, brings its internationally beloved troupe of
  dancers to Bloomington as part of its landmark 50th anniversary season\, 
 featuring gems from the company’s groundbreaking repertoire. Founded in Ne
 w York City in 1974\, the company\, affectionately known as The Trocks\, h
 as grown from its roots in late-late shows in off-off Broadway lofts to be
 come a global touring sensation\, performing from Tokyo to Toronto and eve
 rywhere in between.\n \nThe company dances with razor-sharp wit and breath
 taking pointe work\, performing polished parodies of works that span the c
 lassical ballet canon. Revered by ballet aficionados as well as by those w
 ho don’t know a plié from a jeté\, the Trocks are “a guaranteed hoot for p
 eople who know nothing of ballet and an absolute must for those who think 
 they know the originals.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240224T200000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Les Ballets Trockadero de Monte Carlo
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/les-ballets-trockadero-de-monte-carlo/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Les Ballets T
 rockadero de Monte Carlo\,<b> </b>the world’s foremost all-male comic ball
 et company\, brings its internationally beloved troupe of dancers to Bloom
 ington as part of its landmark 50th anniversary season\, featuring gems fr
 om the company’s groundbreaking repertoire. Founded in New York City in 19
 74\, the company\, affectionately known as The Trocks\, has grown from its
  roots in late-late shows in off-off Broadway lofts to become a global tou
 ring sensation\, performing from Tokyo to Toronto and everywhere in betwee
 n.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>The company dances with razor-sharp wit and breathtak
 ing pointe work\, performing polished parodies of works that span the clas
 sical ballet canon. Revered by ballet aficionados as well as by those who 
 don’t know a plié from a jeté\, the Trocks are “a guaranteed hoot for peop
 le who know nothing of ballet and an absolute must for those who think the
 y know the originals.”</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
