BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-117388@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Since June 2021\, Dr. Jeremy Wilson (Anthropology\, IU-Indianap
 olis) has been part of a multidisciplinary team working towards identifyin
 g\, exhuming\, and analyzing individuals murdered during the 1921 Tulsa Ra
 ce Massacre and destruction of Black Wall Street. In this talk\, he will s
 hare his path to the project\, summarize the field investigations and lab 
 work completed so far\, and highlight the valuable contributions that arch
 aeologists can make in restorative justice projects. Light refreshments wi
 ll be served.  
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240229T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240229T183000
LOCATION:IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology\, 416 N. Indiana Ave Blo
 omington\, IN 47408
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Archaeology for Restorative Justice
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/archaeology-for-restorative-justice/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><span class='
 m_-8678180562873164715m-6195452027064402902normaltextrun'>Since June 2021\
 , Dr. Jeremy Wilson (Anthropology\, IU-Indianapolis) has been part of a mu
 ltidisciplinary team working towards identifying\, exhuming\, and analyzin
 g individuals murdered during the 1921 Tulsa Race Massacre and destruction
  of Black Wall Street. In this talk\, he will share his path to the projec
 t\, summarize the field investigations and lab work completed so far\, and
  highlight the valuable contributions that archaeologists can make in rest
 orative justice projects. Light refreshments will be served. </span><span 
 class='m_-8678180562873164715m-6195452027064402902eop'> </span></p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
END:VEVENT
