CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In the wildly entertaining and refreshingly unfiltered document
 ary KOKOMO CITY\, filmmaker D. Smith passes the mic to four Black transgen
 der sex workers in Atlanta and New York City\n– Daniella Carter\, Koko Da 
 Doll\, Liyah Mitchell\, and Dominique Silver – who unapologetically break 
 down the walls of their profession. Holding nothing back\, the film vibrat
 es with energy\, sex\, challenge\, and hard – earned wisdom.\nThis vital p
 ortrait\, edited and shot by Smith in bold black and white\, is her featur
 e directorial debut. A two-time Grammy-nominated producer\, singer\, and s
 ongwriter\, Smith made history as the first trans woman cast on a primetim
 e unscripted TV show.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240229T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240229T230000
LOCATION:The Back Door\, 207 South College Ave.\, in the alley behind the A
 tlas Ballroom\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Kokomo City\, presented by Cicada Cinema
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-screening-kokomo-city-presented-by-cicada-c
 inema/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>In the wildly
  entertaining and refreshingly unfiltered documentary KOKOMO CITY\, filmma
 ker D. Smith passes the mic to four Black transgender sex workers in Atlan
 ta and New York City<br />\n– Daniella Carter\, Koko Da Doll\, Liyah Mitch
 ell\, and Dominique Silver – who unapologetically break down the walls of 
 their profession. Holding nothing back\, the film vibrates with energy\, s
 ex\, challenge\, and hard – earned wisdom.</p>\n<p>This vital portrait\, e
 dited and shot by Smith in bold black and white\, is her feature directori
 al debut. A two-time Grammy-nominated producer\, singer\, and songwriter\,
  Smith made history as the first trans woman cast on a primetime unscripte
 d TV show.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
