 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Our U
 niform</strong> – a social satire about the <em>clothing</em> conventions 
 imposed on young children  Iran (in Farsi)</p>\n<p><strong>Letter to a Pig
 </strong> – A Holocaust survivor reads a <em>letter</em> he wrote to the <
 em>pig</em> who saved his life.\, France/Israel (in Hebrew)</p>\n<p><stron
 g>Pachyderm</strong>– Louise spends time at her grandparent’s house\, Yet 
 this year\, the snow will fall in summer and a monster will die.</p>\n<p><
 strong>Ninety-Five Senses</strong> – An ode to the body’s <em>five senses<
 /em>\, delivered by a man with little time left to enjoy them.</p>\n<p><st
 rong>War is Over! Inspired by the Music of John & Yoko</strong> Two soldie
 rs on opposite sides play a game of chess.</p>\n<p><strong>BONUS FILMS: </
 strong></p>\n<p><strong>Wild Summon</strong> – A natural history fantasy f
 ilm\, following the dramatic lifecycle of the wild salmon in human form (n
 arrated by Marianne Faithfull)</p>\n<p><strong>I’m Hip</strong> – A self-a
 bsorbed cat\, in a jazzy song and dance\, proudly and comically proclaims 
 his “hipness” to the world. The world is less convinced than he is.</p>\n<
 /BODY></HTML>
