 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>DOCUM
 ENTARY SHORTS – 141 minutes </strong><strong><br />\n</strong></p>\n<p><em
 ><strong>Nǎi Nai</strong></em> <strong>and</strong> <em><strong>Wài Pó</st
 rong></em>– Sean Wang visits his maternal and paternal grandmothers who li
 ve as roommates. heir shared love for him is hilarious\, moving\, and full
  of the hard-won wisdom. USA (in Mandarin)</p>\n<p><strong>The Barber of L
 ittle Rock </strong>Arlo Washington\, a local barber whose visionary appro
 ach to a just economy can be found in the mission of People Trust\, the no
 nprofit community bank he founded.</p>\n<p><strong>The Local Repair Shop</
 strong> Four unassuming heroes who ensure no student is deprived of the jo
 y of music.</p>\n<p><b><span lang='EN-GB'>Island In Between </span></b><sp
 an lang='EN-GB'><span class='sc-466bb6c-1 dWufeH' role='presentation' data
 -testid='plot-l'>S. Leo Chiang reflects on his relationship with Taiwan\, 
 the United States a</span></span><span lang='EN-GB'><span class='sc-466bb6
 c-1 dWufeH' role='presentation' data-testid='plot-l'>nd China from the isl
 ands of Kinmen\, just a few miles from mainland China.</span></span></p>\n
 <p><strong>The ABCs of Book Banning </strong><span class='sc-466bb6c-1 dWu
 feH' role='presentation' data-testid='plot-l'>Reveals the voices of the im
 pacted parties of books banned from school districts\, inspiring hope for 
