UID:ai1ec-117870@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Map\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn Light Human Rights Documentary Film Fes
 tival 2024: Trauma and Healing\nIn Light 2024 invites you on an immersive 
 journey into the powerful intersection of human rights\, captivating narra
 tives\, and the art of documentary filmmaking. Experience eight thought-pr
 ovoking documentaries that explore the profound link between social and po
 litical trauma and mental health. From the heart of motherlands in Africa 
 to historic struggles worldwide to narratives of individual struggles\, ea
 ch film promises an intimate lens into compelling stories of resilience\, 
 empowerment\, and healing.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240328T130000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:In Light Human Rights Documentary Film Festival
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/in-light-human-rights-documentary-film-festival/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='desc
 ription-tabs-controller-container'>\n<div id='tabs_list' class='tabs-list'
 >\n<ul class='list-inline-float' data-tab=''>\n<li><a id='mapTab' href='ht
 tps://www.visitbloomington.com/event/in-lights-human-rights-documentary-fi
 lm-festival/52669/#tab-map' data-sv-maptabbutton='' data-seo-tab-map=''>Ma
 p</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class='description-tabs-content-co
 ntainer shared-detail'>\n<div class='detailPanes'>\n<div class='tabs-conte
 nt core-styles'>\n<div id='tab-details' class='content active' data-sv-map
 tabbuttoncontent=''>\n<div class='desc'>\n<p>In Light Human Rights Documen
 tary Film Festival 2024: Trauma and Healing</p>\n<p>In Light 2024 invites 
 you on an immersive journey into the powerful intersection of human rights
 \, captivating narratives\, and the art of documentary filmmaking. Experie
 nce eight thought-provoking documentaries that explore the profound link b
 etween social and political trauma and mental health. From the heart of mo
 therlands in Africa to historic struggles worldwide to narratives of indiv
 idual struggles\, each film promises an intimate lens into compelling stor
 ies of resilience\, empowerment\, and healing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>
 \n</div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
