BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120036@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Founded in 2012\, the Videri String Quartet is a revolutionary 
 ensemble dedicated to performing the music of video games. A pioneer in bo
 th the video game and classical music communities\, Videri is committed to
  reinventing the string quartet experience for the modern listener. Videri
  seeks to explore the ways in which video game music impacts its listeners
 \, discover the parallels between traditional classical music and video ga
 me music\, celebrate the dynamic link between music and storytelling\, and
  use video game music as a means of expression for children and young adul
 ts!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240328T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240328T180000
LOCATION:Room: MU011\, Merrill Hall\, 1201 East Third Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Introduction to the World of Video Game Music
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/introduction-to-the-world-of-video-game-music/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Founded in 20
 12\, the Videri String Quartet is a revolutionary ensemble dedicated to pe
 rforming the music of video games. A pioneer in both the video game and cl
 assical music communities\, Videri is committed to reinventing the string 
 quartet experience for the modern listener. Videri seeks to explore the wa
 ys in which video game music impacts its listeners\, discover the parallel
 s between traditional classical music and video game music\, celebrate the
  dynamic link between music and storytelling\, and use video game music as
  a means of expression for children and young adults!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120033@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Michael Koryta will be discussing his latest book\, Lost Man’s 
 Lane\, written under the pseudonym Scott Carson. Michael Koryta is a New Y
 ork Times bestselling author whose work has been translated into more than
  20 languages\, adapted into major motion pictures\, and won the Los Angel
 es Times Book Prize. A former private investigator and reporter\, his writ
 ing has been praised by Stephen King\, Michael Connelly\, and Dean Koontz\
 , among many others. Raised in Bloomington\, Indiana\, he now lives in Ind
 iana and Maine. Age 16 and up. This event is free and no tickets are requi
 red.
