CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Registration is requested. \nJoin us to learn about Brown Count
 y’s native flowers and the pollinator habitat that they create. Every plan
 t draws in their own specific and unique insect and forms a relationship. 
 Explore these different insects and their homes\, natural forming and man 
 made.\nPresented by Jordan Hart and Katie Starr of the Brown County Soil a
 nd Water Conservation District.\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240401T173000
LOCATION:Brown County Public Library\, 205 Locust Lane\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Native Flowers and their Insect Friends
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/native-flowers-and-their-insect-friends/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Regis
 tration is requested. </strong></p>\n<p>Join us to learn about Brown Count
 y’s native flowers and the pollinator habitat that they create. Every plan
 t draws in their own specific and unique insect and forms a relationship. 
 Explore these different insects and their homes\, natural forming and man 
 made.</p>\n<p>Presented by Jordan Hart and Katie Starr of the Brown County
  Soil and Water Conservation District.</p>\n<p> </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
