CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a performance geared towards art\, music\, and scie
 nce lovers alike. The Amity Trio will perform Illuminating Apologues\, a s
 ong cycle featuring anecdotal stories with animals: green frogs and firefl
 ies\, tussock moths\, scorpions\, Tiki geckos\, Brood X cicadas\, and hone
 y bees. The Amity Trio is a chamber ensemble that was founded in 2018 to p
 romote music by living composers through performing and teaching around th
 e globe.\n \n1–2 PM: Pre-concert musical activities for children\n2–3 PM: 
 Performance
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240406T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240406T150000
LOCATION:Auditorium\, 1B and 1C Combo\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 
 East Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Illuminating Apologues Featuring the Amity Trio
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/illuminating-apologues-featuring-the-amity-trio/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us for a
  performance geared towards art\, music\, and science lovers alike. The Am
 ity Trio will perform Illuminating Apologues\, a song cycle featuring anec
 dotal stories with animals: green frogs and fireflies\, tussock moths\, sc
 orpions\, Tiki geckos\, Brood X cicadas\, and honey bees. The Amity Trio i
 s a chamber ensemble that was founded in 2018 to promote music by living c
 omposers through performing and teaching around the globe.</p>\n<p> </p>\n
 <p>1–2 PM: Pre-concert musical activities for children<br />\n2–3 PM: Perf
 ormance</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
