UID:ai1ec-120173@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Heliphonie is informed by the science of helioseismology in the
  attempt to place the listeners inside the sun’s singing convection zone. 
 The cycle of twelve 4:48 minute cells correspond to the twelve solar hymns
  performed at Iunu\, the ancient city of Ra-Atum\, on solstices\, equinoxe
 s\, or eclipses.\nSeating is limited – prayer mats available\n$10 suggeste
 d donation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240407T150000
LOCATION:Tibetan Mongolian Buddhist Cultural Center\, 3655 S Snoddy Rd.\, B
 loomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Urban Deer Performance Series Presents Heliophonie
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/urban-deer-performance-series-presents-heliophon
 ie/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Heliphonie is
  informed by the science of helioseismology in the attempt to place the li
 steners inside the sun’s singing convection zone. The cycle of twelve 4:48
  minute cells correspond to the twelve solar hymns performed at Iunu\, the
  ancient city of Ra-Atum\, on solstices\, equinoxes\, or eclipses.</p>\n<p
 >Seating is limited – prayer mats available</p>\n<p>$10 suggested donation
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
