BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120614@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Dancing in the Dark\, the 50th Spring Concert of the legendary 
 IU African American Dance Company\, will take place at the Buskirk-Chumley
  Theater Saturday\, April 13!\nDancing in the Dark. Come dance with us and
  witness our latest works inspired by the 2024 Total Solar Eclipse. This c
 oncert will feature a collection of dances\, from meditative modern dance 
 honoring our shared ancestry to drum-infused contemporary masterpieces\, a
 ll performed in blackout! (just kidding). Dancing in the Dark\, the 50th S
 pring Concert of the legendary IU African American Dance Company will kick
  off a yearlong 50th Anniversary celebration next year.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240413T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240413T220000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:African American Dance Company Spring Concert
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/african-american-dance-company-spring-concert-5/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='font
 -semibold mb-2'>Dancing in the Dark\, the 50th Spring Concert of the legen
 dary IU African American Dance Company\, will take place at the Buskirk-Ch
 umley Theater Saturday\, April 13!</div>\n<div class='mt-6 mb-2 whitespace
 -pre-wrap text-gray-700'>Dancing in the Dark. Come dance with us and witne
 ss our latest works inspired by the 2024 Total Solar Eclipse. This concert
  will feature a collection of dances\, from meditative modern dance honori
 ng our shared ancestry to drum-infused contemporary masterpieces\, all per
 formed in blackout! (just kidding). Dancing in the Dark\, the 50th Spring 
 Concert of the legendary IU African American Dance Company will kick off a
  yearlong 50th Anniversary celebration next year.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120613@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Quarryland Men’s Chorus presents a snapshot of life in Indi
 ana\, featuring the titular rock anthem of John Mellencamp\, wistful and e
 vocative Indiana songs of Hoagy Carmichael and Jon McLaughlin\, and Hoosie
 r favorites like “On the Banks of the Wabash” and “Back Home Again in Indi
 ana.” The chorus is preparing this concert to be presented at its Blooming
 ton home\, First United Church\, 2420 E 3rd St. QMC sings proudly as the m
 usical voice of the LGBTQ+ community in south central Indiana\, and will r
 epresent our state at the international GALA Choruses Festival this summer
 .
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240413T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240413T210000
LOCATION:First United Church\, 2420 East Third St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Beyond Little Pink Houses – Ain’t THAT America – Quarryland Men’s C
 horus Spring Concert
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/beyond-little-pink-houses-aint-that-america-quar
 ryland-mens-chorus-spring-concert/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The Quarrylan
 d Men’s Chorus presents a snapshot of life in Indiana\, featuring the titu
 lar rock anthem of John Mellencamp\, wistful and evocative Indiana songs o
 f Hoagy Carmichael and Jon McLaughlin\, and Hoosier favorites like “On the
  Banks of the Wabash” and “Back Home Again in Indiana.” The chorus is prep
 aring this concert to be presented at its Bloomington home\, First United 
 Church\, 2420 E 3rd St. QMC sings proudly as the musical voice of the LGBT
 Q+ community in south central Indiana\, and will represent our state at th
 e international GALA Choruses Festival this summer.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
