BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120617@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:“Pieces of Me” is a catalyst for change\, an ode to resilience\
 , and a beacon of hope for a South Africa grappling with its tumultuous hi
 story.\nDiscover Bo Petersen’s family secrets in a riveting one-woman perf
 ormance. Unveiling her father’s hidden life during Apartheid\, this play d
 elves into identity complexities and the impact of historical injustices. 
 More than a play\, it’s a powerful exploration of transgenerational trauma
  and a call to break free from silence. Bo believes in theatre’s power to 
 heal across generations. Join us for an afternoon confronting shadows of t
 he past\, witnessing strength born from adversity.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240414T150000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E. 6th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Pieces of Me – One Family’s Story of Apartheid South Africa
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/pieces-of-me-one-familys-story-of-apartheid-sout
 h-africa/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='font
 -semibold mb-2'>“Pieces of Me” is a catalyst for change\, an ode to resili
 ence\, and a beacon of hope for a South Africa grappling with its tumultuo
 us history.</div>\n<div class='mt-6 mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap text-gray-700
 '>Discover Bo Petersen’s family secrets in a riveting one-woman performanc
 e. Unveiling her father’s hidden life during Apartheid\, this play delves 
 into identity complexities and the impact of historical injustices. More t
 han a play\, it’s a powerful exploration of transgenerational trauma and a
  call to break free from silence. Bo believes in theatre’s power to heal a
 cross generations. Join us for an afternoon confronting shadows of the pas
 t\, witnessing strength born from adversity.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
