BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120884@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Tony Brewer\, April Ridge\, Zilia Balkansky-Sellés\, Peter Kacz
 marczyk\, Ray Zdonek\, Lara Tokarski\, Walter Biskupski\, Jonathan S Baker
 \, and Arizona will perform climate conscious poems as spoken word with ex
 pressive dance accompaniment by Erin Strole\, Joanne Shank\, Maxime Werk\,
  Corinne Jones\, Kay Olges\, KaraLynn Hayes\, and Nonie Daniels. Percussio
 nist Julian Douglas will provide musical interludes.\nIn the forthcoming S
 tormwash: Environmental Poems anthology (The Grind Stone\, April 2024)\, 4
 0 poets address the climate crisis and its various effects. From the edito
 r’s Foreword:\n“Invariably\, these poems suggest an uncanny attunement wit
 h nature: Something in the air\, a shift in carbon molecules foreshadowing
  an ominous onslaught\, an accumulating avalanche\, some kind of storm—the
  stink of destruction. In either case\, these poems enable us to hope that
  the survival of future generations is not so tenuous after all.”\n–Hiromi
  Yoshida
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240419T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240419T200000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books\, 849 Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Stormwash: Climate Awareness –  climate conscious poems as spoken w
 ord with expressive dance accompaniment
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/stormwash-climate-awareness-climate-conscious-po
 ems-as-spoken-word-with-expressive-dance-accompaniment/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Tony Brewer\,
  April Ridge\, Zilia Balkansky-Sellés\, Peter Kaczmarczyk\, Ray Zdonek\, L
 ara Tokarski\, Walter Biskupski\, Jonathan S Baker\, and Arizona will perf
 orm climate conscious poems as spoken word with expressive dance accompani
 ment by Erin Strole\, Joanne Shank\, Maxime Werk\, Corinne Jones\, Kay Olg
 es\, KaraLynn Hayes\, and Nonie Daniels. Percussionist Julian Douglas will
  provide musical interludes.</p>\n<p>In the forthcoming Stormwash: Environ
 mental Poems anthology (The Grind Stone\, April 2024)\, 40 poets address t
 he climate crisis and its various effects. From the editor’s Foreword:</p>
 \n<p>“Invariably\, these poems suggest an uncanny attunement with nature: 
 Something in the air\, a shift in carbon molecules foreshadowing an ominou
 s onslaught\, an accumulating avalanche\, some kind of storm—the stink of 
 destruction. In either case\, these poems enable us to hope that the survi
 val of future generations is not so tenuous after all.”</p>\n<p>–Hiromi Yo
 shida</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
