BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120912@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A Question of Color weaves together interviews with Black Ameri
 cans of every complexion to explore colorism in the 1980s and early 1990s.
  Director Kathe Sandler also narrates the film\, providing historical cont
 ext\, personal anecdotes\, and sharing critical perspectives about coloris
 m. The documentary originally premiered at the 1993 Berlin International F
 ilm Festival\, and the new 4K restoration was created from the original ne
 gative\, which Sandler donated to the Black Film Center & Archive (BFCA) i
 n 2010 and 2018. IndieCollect completed the restoration with funding from 
 the HFPA Trust and donations contributed to the Jane Fonda Fund for Women 
 Directors. [58 min\; documentary\; English]\nA Q&A with filmmaker Kathe Sa
 ndler and Black Film Center & Archive Director Dr. Novotny Lawrence will f
 ollow the screening. 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240420T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: A QUESTION OF COLOR
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-a-question-of-color/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><i>A Question
  of Color </i>weaves together interviews with Black Americans of every com
 plexion to explore colorism in the 1980s and early 1990s. Director Kathe S
 andler also narrates the film\, providing historical context\, personal an
 ecdotes\, and sharing critical perspectives about colorism. The documentar
 y originally premiered at the 1993 Berlin International Film Festival\, an
 d the new 4K restoration was created from the original negative\, which Sa
 ndler donated to the Black Film Center & Archive (BFCA) in 2010 and 2018. 
 IndieCollect completed the restoration with funding from the HFPA Trust an
 d donations contributed to the Jane Fonda Fund for Women Directors. [58 mi
 n\; documentary\; English]</p>\n<p><i><strong>A Q&A with filmmaker Kathe S
 andler and Black Film Center & Archive Director Dr. Novotny Lawrence will 
 follow the screening. </strong></i></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
