BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121039@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:An Oscar-nominated documentary chronicling the web of racism\, 
 capitalism\, violence\, and civil rights that lie at the heart of one fami
 ly’s search for justice. Virtual Q&A with the filmmaker to follow. \n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\nAbout Who Killed Vincent Chin?\nExplore the circumstances of t
 he murder of Vincent Chin\, a Detroit resident who was the victim of a hat
 e crime in a climate of anti-Japanese sentiment among auto workers who wit
 nessed their factories being shut down\, and the lengths his family and co
 mmunity will go for justice. Restored by The Academy of Motion Picture Art
 s and Sciences Film Archive and The Film Foundation\, in association with 
 the Museum of Chinese in America. Restoration funding provided by the Hobs
 on/Lucas Family Foundation\, with additional support provided by Todd Phil
 lips. [87 min\; documentary\; English and Cantonese with English subtitles
 ]\nA virtual Q&A with director Christine Choy will follow the screening.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240424T200000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: WHO KILLED VINCENT CHIN?
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-who-killed-vincent-chin/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='content
 ' class='collapsed individual-film__intro collapsed bg-none section'>\n<di
 v class='row'>\n<div class='layout'>\n<div class='text'>\n<p class='text s
 creening-highlight'><strong> An Oscar-nominated documentary chronicling th
 e web of racism\, capitalism\, violence\, and civil rights that lie at the
  heart of one family’s search for justice. Virtual Q&A with the filmmaker 
 to follow. </strong></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class='sect
 ion bg-none individual-film__intro'>\n<div class='row'>\n<div class='layou
 t'>\n<div class='text'>\n<h3 class='visually-hidden'>About Who Killed Vinc
 ent Chin?</h3>\n<p>Explore the circumstances of the murder of Vincent Chin
 \, a Detroit resident who was the victim of a hate crime in a climate of a
 nti-Japanese sentiment among auto workers who witnessed their factories be
 ing shut down\, and the lengths his family and community will go for justi
 ce. Restored by The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences Film Archi
 ve and The Film Foundation\, in association with the Museum of Chinese in 
 America. Restoration funding provided by the Hobson/Lucas Family Foundatio
 n\, with additional support provided by Todd Phillips. [87 min\; documenta
 ry\; English and Cantonese with English subtitles]</p>\n<p><i><strong>A vi
 rtual Q&A with director Christine Choy will follow the screening.</strong>
 </i></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
