BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121040@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The legendary Hall of Fame drummer plays tribute to his friend 
 and former band mate\, Ronnie Van Zant. Artimus Pyle is now the only survi
 ving member left from the original Lynyrd Skynyrd band. The band plays all
  the favorites from the early years! Ronnie’s songs: Sweet Home Alabama\, 
 Gimme Back My Bullets\, That Smell and of course Free Bird! The Artimus Py
 le Band is a high energy\, true to the music\, and true to the era rock gr
 oup\, one of the few that is on the road today. The band featuring Artimus
  Pyle\, Brad Durden\, Jerry Lyda\, Dave Fowler and Scott Raines are not on
 ly a group of friends and contemporaries but also some of the most seasone
 d musicians in the country. For those who were fortunate enough to see the
  original band\, this show really captures the music in its purist form. F
 or those who never experienced Lynyrd Skynyrd from back in the day\, this 
 show is the next best thing!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240425T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240425T223000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Artimus Pyle Band with special guest Split Rail
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-artimus-pyle-band-with-special-guest-split-r
 ail/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The legendary
  Hall of Fame drummer plays tribute to his friend and former band mate\, R
 onnie Van Zant. Artimus Pyle is now the only surviving member left from th
 e original Lynyrd Skynyrd band. The band plays all the favorites from the 
 early years! Ronnie’s songs: Sweet Home Alabama\, Gimme Back My Bullets\, 
 That Smell and of course Free Bird! The Artimus Pyle Band is a high energy
 \, true to the music\, and true to the era rock group\, one of the few tha
 t is on the road today. The band featuring Artimus Pyle\, Brad Durden\, Je
 rry Lyda\, Dave Fowler and Scott Raines are not only a group of friends an
 d contemporaries but also some of the most seasoned musicians in the count
 ry. For those who were fortunate enough to see the original band\, this sh
 ow really captures the music in its purist form. For those who never exper
 ienced Lynyrd Skynyrd from back in the day\, this show is the next best th
 ing!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121025@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The internationally acclaimed hit theatre show The Simon & Garf
 unkel Story will make its Bloomington debut next spring. This immersive co
 ncert-style production chronicles the amazing journey shared by the folk-r
 ock duo\, Paul Simon and Art Garfunkel. It tells the story from their humb
 le beginnings as Tom and Jerry\, to their incredible success as one of the
  best-selling music groups of the 1960s and their dramatic split in 1970. 
 The show culminates with the pair’s famous “The Concert in Central Park” r
 eunion in 1981 which had more than half a million fans in attendance.\nUsi
 ng state-of-the-art video projection\, incredible lighting\, and a full li
 ve band\, the show is a moving and powerful concert featuring all the hits
  including “Mrs. Robinson\,” “Cecilia\,” “Bridge Over Troubled Water\,” “H
 omeward Bound\,” and many more.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240425T193000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Simon and Garfunkel Story
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-simon-and-garfunkel-story/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The internati
 onally acclaimed hit theatre show <i>The Simon & Garfunkel Story<b> </b></
 i>will make its Bloomington debut next spring. This immersive concert-styl
 e production chronicles the amazing journey shared by the folk-rock duo\, 
 Paul Simon and Art Garfunkel. It tells the story from their humble beginni
 ngs as Tom and Jerry\, to their incredible success as one of the best-sell
 ing music groups of the 1960s and their dramatic split in 1970. The show c
 ulminates with the pair’s famous “The Concert in Central Park” reunion in 
 1981 which had more than half a million fans in attendance.</p>\n<p>Using 
 state-of-the-art video projection\, incredible lighting\, and a full live 
 band\, the show is a moving and powerful concert featuring all the hits in
 cluding “Mrs. Robinson\,” “Cecilia\,” “Bridge Over Troubled Water\,” “Home
 ward Bound\,” and many more.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
