BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121027@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Dubbed by Jerry Seinfeld as the “best young up and coming comic
 \,” Mark Normand is quickly becoming one of the most talked about touring 
 comedians on the scene.  Normand’s recent one-hour Netflix special\, SOUP 
 TO NUTS\, has been a staple in the streamers’ Top Ten since its July 25th 
 premiere.  This follows Normand’s self-released special\, 2020’s “Out to L
 unch” which amassed over 12 million views on YouTube.  He also starred on 
 Netflix’s Season 3 of The Stand Ups.\nAn extremely prolific stand-up\, he 
 previously had two Comedy Central special and has made an unparalleled sev
 en appearances on “Conan\,” four appearances on “The Tonight Show with Jim
 my Fallon\,” and has also appeared on “The Late Show with Stephen Colbert.
 ” Mark is a frequent guest on “The Joe Rogan Experience\,” and hosts his o
 wn podcasts “Tuesdays with Stories” and “We Might Be Drunk.”\nRecommended 
 for mature audiences.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240426T190000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Outback presents MARK NORMAND
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mark-normand/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='prev
 iew-modal modal-body'>\n<p>Dubbed by Jerry Seinfeld as the “best young up 
 and coming comic\,” Mark Normand is quickly becoming one of the most talke
 d about touring comedians on the scene.  Normand’s recent one-hour Netflix
  special\, SOUP TO NUTS\, has been a staple in the streamers’ Top Ten sinc
 e its July 25th premiere.  This follows Normand’s self-released special\, 
 2020’s “Out to Lunch” which amassed over 12 million views on YouTube.  He 
 also starred on Netflix’s Season 3 of The Stand Ups.</p>\n<p>An extremely 
 prolific stand-up\, he previously had two Comedy Central special and has m
 ade an unparalleled seven appearances on “Conan\,” four appearances on “Th
 e Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon\,” and has also appeared on “The Late Sho
 w with Stephen Colbert.” Mark is a frequent guest on “The Joe Rogan Experi
 ence\,” and hosts his own podcasts “Tuesdays with Stories” and “We Might B
 e Drunk.”</p>\n<p>Recommended for mature audiences.</p>\n</div>\n</BODY></
 HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
