 rowling ‘round your back door and howling in a low\, sexy way\, swinging w
 ith the angels dancin’ around their heads and leaving blood on the floorbo
 ards. Folks enamored of Mick Taylor-era Stones\, early Hendrix\, and The B
 lack Keys will eat up this up with impolite gusto. It’s a great pleasure t
 o see a band fully realize their potential as they ride into their second 
 decade together\, and Clava presents these Chicago survivors at their eart
 hy\, appealing finest.
