BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-120057@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In anticipation of Granfalloon Festival Performance by the Youn
 g@Heart Chorus June 7th at Buskirk Chumley Theater! Granfalloon – What a t
 ime to be alive\nThis 2007 documentary follows Young@Heart – a chorus of t
 wenty-four senior citizens with an average age of eighty – as they prepare
  for a concert in their hometown of Northampton\, Massachusetts and a Euro
 pean tour learning new songs by the likes of Sonic Youth\, James Brown\, A
 llen Toussaint\, Coldplay\, Jimi Hendrix\, Talking Heads\, and Prince.\nYo
 ung @ Heart’s Mission:\nTo eliminate ageism and shatter stereotypes of gro
 wing old through innovative musical performances that inspire and unite di
 verse communities. https://youngatheartchorus.com/home\nRated PG.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240430T193000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Granfalloon Presents a Film: “Young at Heart Chorus–Rock’n Roll Wil
 l Never Die”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bct-presents-young-heart/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><b><u>In anti
 cipation of Granfalloon Festival Performance by the Young@Heart Chorus Jun
 e 7<sup>th</sup> at Buskirk Chumley Theater! </u></b><b><u><a href='https:
 //granfalloon.indiana.edu/index.html' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-
 saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?q=https://granfalloon.indiana.
 edu/index.html&source=gmail&ust=1711771473627000&usg=AOvVaw16mixnCt9M07S7u
 mgdDqY0'>Granfalloon – What a time to be alive</a></u></b></p>\n<p>This 20
 07 documentary follows Young@Heart – a chorus of twenty-four senior citize
 ns with an average age of eighty – as they prepare for a concert in their 
 hometown of Northampton\, Massachusetts and a European tour learning new s
 ongs by the likes of Sonic Youth\, James Brown\, Allen Toussaint\, Coldpla
 y\, Jimi Hendrix\, Talking Heads\, and Prince.</p>\n<p><b>Young @ Heart’s 
 Mission:<br />\n</b>To eliminate ageism and shatter stereotypes of growing
  old through innovative musical performances that inspire and unite divers
 e communities. <u><a href='https://youngatheartchorus.com/home'><b>https:/
 /youngatheartchorus.com/home</b></a></u></p>\n<p>Rated PG.</p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
