BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121713@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In his follow-up to the Oscar-winning The English Patient\, wri
 ter/director Anthony Minghella tried his hand at another tricky literary a
 daptation with The Talented Mr. Ripley\, featuring ’90s heartthrob Matt Da
 mon cast against type as a bisexual murderer. A bright and charismatic soc
 iopath making his way in mid-1950s NYC through menial work and petty scams
 \, Tom Ripley is hired through a case of mistaken identity by a shipping m
 agnate to bring back his loafing son\, Dickie (Jude Law)\, from a too-long
  extended Italian vacation with his girlfriend\, Marge (Gwyneth Paltrow). 
 Tom soon finds that he’d rather be Dickie than bring him home and makes an
  impulsive decision with no return. The three enigmatic leads are buoyed b
 y indelible supporting performances from Cate Blanchett and Philip Seymour
  Hoffman. [
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240516T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: THE TALENTED MR. RIPLEY
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-the-talented-mr-ripley/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>In his follow
 -up to the Oscar-winning The English Patient\, writer/director Anthony Min
 ghella tried his hand at another tricky literary adaptation with The Talen
 ted Mr. Ripley\, featuring ’90s heartthrob Matt Damon cast against type as
  a bisexual murderer. A bright and charismatic sociopath making his way in
  mid-1950s NYC through menial work and petty scams\, Tom Ripley is hired t
 hrough a case of mistaken identity by a shipping magnate to bring back his
  loafing son\, Dickie (Jude Law)\, from a too-long extended Italian vacati
 on with his girlfriend\, Marge (Gwyneth Paltrow). Tom soon finds that he’d
  rather be Dickie than bring him home and makes an impulsive decision with
  no return. The three enigmatic leads are buoyed by indelible supporting p
 erformances from Cate Blanchett and Philip Seymour Hoffman. [</p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
