BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121707@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The mission of the National Coalition for Drug Legalization (50
 1(c)3) is to advance the conversation about legalization of all drugs thro
 ugh research and community service. The current drug war has had devastati
 ng effects on communities of color\, the working poor\, and those who suff
 er from medical illness in search of alternative medicine. Through meaning
 ful and impactful research\, the National Coalition for Drug Legalization 
 can push for policies and laws that will save lives from drug overdoses an
 d reduce incarcerations.\nPlease join the National Coalition for Drug Lega
 lization on May 17\, 2023.\nThis event will provide an opportunity for com
 munity engagement\, education\, and a chance to discuss the benefits of a 
 public health approach to drug use.\nThe forum will be a moderated panel d
 iscussion followed by Q&A. The panel will be led by experts in the field o
 f drug policy.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240517T183000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A Conversation About Drug Legalization
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/a-conversation-about-drug-legalization-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY>\n<p>The mission
  of the National Coalition for Drug Legalization (501(c)3) is to advance t
 he conversation about legalization of all drugs through research and commu
 nity service. The current drug war has had devastating effects on communit
 ies of color\, the working poor\, and those who suffer from medical illnes
 s in search of alternative medicine. Through meaningful and impactful rese
 arch\, the National Coalition for Drug Legalization can push for policies 
 and laws that will save lives from drug overdoses and reduce incarceration
 s.</p>\n<p>Please join the National Coalition for Drug Legalization on May
  17\, 2023.</p>\n<p>This event will provide an opportunity for community e
 ngagement\, education\, and a chance to discuss the benefits of a public h
 ealth approach to drug use.</p>\n<p>The forum will be a moderated panel di
 scussion followed by Q&A. The panel will be led by experts in the field of
  drug policy.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
