BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121772@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Learn more about how barns tell the story of their creators and
  how the designs have changed over time.\nDuncan Campbell served on Bloomi
 ngton’s Historic Preservation Commission from 1992 to 2008\, and co-author
 ed the city’s Historic Preservation Ordinance.  He has been active as a bo
 ard member of Bloomington Restorations\, Inc.\, a local preservation non-p
 rofit\, has served as their affordable housing construction manager and ch
 airman of their Revolving Loan Fund Committee. In retirement\, Duncan serv
 es on the Bloomington Historic Preservation Commission as an advisory memb
 er\, the Monroe Co. Historic Preservation Board of Review\, and is an acti
 ve board member of the Indiana Barn Foundation.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240518T133000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E. 6th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Talk: Indiana Barns: Settlement Imprint & Evolution with Duncan Cam
 pbell
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/talk-indiana-barns-settlement-imprint-evolution-
 with-duncan-campbell/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Learn more ab
 out how barns tell the story of their creators and how the designs have ch
 anged over time.<br />\nDuncan Campbell served on Bloomington’s Historic P
 reservation Commission from 1992 to 2008\, and co-authored the city’s Hist
 oric Preservation Ordinance.  He has been active as a board member of Bloo
 mington Restorations\, Inc.\, a local preservation non-profit\, has served
  as their affordable housing construction manager and chairman of their Re
 volving Loan Fund Committee. In retirement\, Duncan serves on the Blooming
 ton Historic Preservation Commission as an advisory member\, the Monroe Co
 . Historic Preservation Board of Review\, and is an active board member of
  the Indiana Barn Foundation.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
