BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121715@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Considered one of the greatest films ever made\, The Rules of t
 he Game (La règle du jeu) by Jean Renoir is a scathing critique of corrupt
  French society cloaked in a comedy of manners in which a weekend at a mar
 quis’ country château lays bare some ugly truths about a group of haut bou
 rgeois acquaintances. The film has had a tumultuous history: it was subjec
 ted to cuts after the violent response of the premiere audience in 1939\, 
 and the original negative was destroyed during World War II and wasn’t rec
 onstructed until 1959. That version\, which has stunned viewers for decade
 s\, is presented here in a gorgeous new 4K restoration.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240518T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: THE RULES OF THE GAME
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-the-rules-of-the-game/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Considered on
 e of the greatest films ever made\, The Rules of the Game (La règle du jeu
 ) by Jean Renoir is a scathing critique of corrupt French society cloaked 
 in a comedy of manners in which a weekend at a marquis’ country château la
 ys bare some ugly truths about a group of haut bourgeois acquaintances. Th
 e film has had a tumultuous history: it was subjected to cuts after the vi
 olent response of the premiere audience in 1939\, and the original negativ
 e was destroyed during World War II and wasn’t reconstructed until 1959. T
 hat version\, which has stunned viewers for decades\, is presented here in
  a gorgeous new 4K restoration. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
