BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-121934@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Green Drinks Bloomington is a lively\, informal social networki
 ng event for people from all\nwalks of life who are interested in making a
  greener world. The organization gathers monthly to share\nlibations and d
 ialogue\, explore ideas and make new friends and business connections.\nTh
 is month’s gathering will hear from Dr. Ben Kravitz\, Assistant Professor 
 in the\nDepartment of Earth and Atmospheric Sciences at Indiana University
 \, for a\npresentation entitled “Geoengineering: Can we do it? Should we d
 o it?”. As people get\nmore desperate about climate change\, they may turn
  to technologies to deliberately cool the\nplanet. Dr. Kravitz will explor
 e some of the benefits and risks in this talk.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240522T180000
LOCATION:Upland Brewing Wood SHop\, 354 W 11th St\, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Green Drinks presents Dr. Ben Kravitz\, “Geoengineering: Can we do 
 it? Should we do it?”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/green-drinks-presents-dr-ben-kravitz-geoengineer
 ing-can-we-do-it-should-we-do-it/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Green Drinks 
 Bloomington is a lively\, informal social networking event for people from
  all<br />\nwalks of life who are interested in making a greener world. Th
 e organization gathers monthly to share<br />\nlibations and dialogue\, ex
 plore ideas and make new friends and business connections.</p>\n<p>This mo
 nth’s gathering will hear from Dr. Ben Kravitz\, Assistant Professor in th
 e<br />\nDepartment of Earth and Atmospheric Sciences at Indiana Universit
 y\, for a<br />\npresentation entitled “Geoengineering: Can we do it? Shou
 ld we do it?”. As people get<br />\nmore desperate about climate change\, 
 they may turn to technologies to deliberately cool the<br />\nplanet. Dr. 
 Kravitz will explore some of the benefits and risks in this talk.</p>\n</B
 ODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
