BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-122127@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Eat cake. Drink Tea. Talk about Death.\nA Death Cafe is a group
 -directed discussion of death with no agenda\, objectives or themes. It is
  a discussion group rather than a grief support or counseling session.\nDe
 ath Cafes have spread quickly around the world. Over 16\,500 Death Cafes a
 re held in 85 countries. It is all volunteer-run.\nThe Bloomington chapter
  is hosted by Rick Clayton\, a hospice chaplain and musician who enjoys pl
 aying harp and cello for his clients. It meets monthly at Morgenstern’s.\n
 “The Death Cafe is a safe place for people who are dealing with the loss o
 f loved ones\, without ideology.” – Rick
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240625T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240625T210000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books\, 849 S Auto Mall Rd\, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Death Cafe
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/death-cafe-3/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Eat cake. Dri
 nk Tea. Talk about Death.</p>\n<p>A Death Cafe is a group-directed discuss
 ion of death with no agenda\, objectives or themes. It is a discussion gro
 up rather than a grief support or counseling session.</p>\n<p>Death Cafes 
 have spread quickly around the world. Over 16\,500 Death Cafes are held in
  85 countries. It is all volunteer-run.</p>\n<p>The Bloomington chapter is
  hosted by Rick Clayton\, a hospice chaplain and musician who enjoys playi
 ng harp and cello for his clients. It meets monthly at Morgenstern’s.</p>
 \n<p>“The Death Cafe is a safe place for people who are dealing with the l
 oss of loved ones\, without ideology.” – Rick</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
