BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-122938@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015805Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Fronted by Shaun Hague\, JOURNEYMAN has become the #1 tribute t
 o Clapton in a short amount of time. With over 50 years of music to choose
  from\, JOURNEYMAN covers it all – “Layla”\, “Badge”\, “The Core”\, “White
  Room”\, “Lay Down Sally”\, “Tulsa Time”\, “Cocaine” and many more!\nThis 
 gifted group of musicians channels Clapton’s spirit\, passion\, and musici
 anship. The guitar playing is spot on recreating the Clapton catalog in al
 l its splendid glory!\nShaun Hague has built quite the resume in the ten y
 ears. At just 17\, he was named “The Best Young Blues Guitarist” by The Ho
 use of Blues\, and by 21\, the young guitarist was playing guitar for Blue
 s phenom Kenny Wayne Shepherd. In his career\, he has shared the stage wit
 h Amos Lee\, John Waite\, and Terra Naomi\, as well as performing on Jay L
 eno and sitting in with John Fogerty! Together\, Hague and the band provid
 e a powerful performance of all aspects of Clapton’s career from Bluesbrea
 kers to From The Cradle!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240627T193000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Journeyman: A Tribute to Eric Clapton
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/journeyman-a-tribute-to-eric-clapton/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Fronted by Sh
 aun Hague\, JOURNEYMAN has become the #1 tribute to Clapton in a short amo
 unt of time. With over 50 years of music to choose from\, JOURNEYMAN cover
 s it all – “Layla”\, “Badge”\, “The Core”\, “White Room”\, “Lay Down Sally
 ”\, “Tulsa Time”\, “Cocaine” and many more!</p>\n<p>This gifted group of m
 usicians channels Clapton’s spirit\, passion\, and musicianship. The guita
 r playing is spot on recreating the Clapton catalog in all its splendid gl
 ory!</p>\n<p>Shaun Hague has built quite the resume in the ten years. At j
 ust 17\, he was named “The Best Young Blues Guitarist” by The House of Blu
 es\, and by 21\, the young guitarist was playing guitar for Blues phenom K
 enny Wayne Shepherd. In his career\, he has shared the stage with Amos Lee
 \, John Waite\, and Terra Naomi\, as well as performing on Jay Leno and si
 tting in with John Fogerty! Together\, Hague and the band provide a powerf
 ul performance of all aspects of Clapton’s career from Bluesbreakers to Fr
 om The Cradle!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
