BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-123302@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Duke Tumatoe is an American blues guitarist\, vocalist and song
 writer who fuses gritty R&B\, rock\, blues\, and funk injected with equal 
 parts humor and gut-level sincerity.\nHe has gigged with Muddy Waters\, Bo
  Diddley\, B.B. King\, Willie Dixon\, Buddy Guy\, John Fogerty and George 
 Thorogood. He was a founding member of arena-rock giants REO Speedwagon.\n
 He has released fifteen albums as the bandleader of Duke Tumatoe & The All
 -Star Frogs and Duke Tumatoe & The Power Trio. His 1988 live album I Like 
 My Job was produced by John Fogerty. He typically plays more than 100 date
 s per year. duketumatoe.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240629T193000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Duke Tumatoe W/ special guests Mike Milligan and Steam Shovel
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/duke-tumatoe-w-special-guests-mike-milligan-and-
 steam-shovel/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Duke Tumatoe 
 is an American blues guitarist\, vocalist and songwriter who fuses gritty 
 R&B\, rock\, blues\, and funk injected with equal parts humor and gut-leve
 l sincerity.</p>\n<p>He has gigged with Muddy Waters\, Bo Diddley\, B.B. K
 ing\, Willie Dixon\, Buddy Guy\, John Fogerty and George Thorogood. He was
  a founding member of arena-rock giants REO Speedwagon.</p>\n<p>He has rel
 eased fifteen albums as the bandleader of Duke Tumatoe & The All-Star Frog
 s and Duke Tumatoe & The Power Trio. His 1988 live album I Like My Job was
  produced by John Fogerty. He typically plays more than 100 dates per year
 . duketumatoe.com </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-122694@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A stunning stage show that replicates the songs\, stories\, sty
 les\, and moods of the Canadian singer-songwriter’s BEST\, performed by Mi
 ke Fornes! His portrayal of Gordon Lightfoot is simply an honest effort to
  entertain with an accurate representation of a Gordon Lightfoot concert. 
 Fornes tireless research and personal interaction with Lightfoot have led 
 to accurate mannerisms\, speaking patterns\, clothing\, and identical guit
 ars used by the Canadian icon on stage.\nOn stage\, he demonstrates his lo
 ve of the timeless music that captured millions during the 1960s\, 1970s\,
  and 1980s. His catalog of Lightfoot’s music includes 77 songs that he cho
 oses from in concert! Rarely does he break character\, usually only to int
 roduce the band or give a personal message before the show’s conclusion. M
 ike is backed by four talented musicians who play the roles of Gordon Ligh
 tfoot’s stage band\, replicating parts heard on recordings and in live per
 formances. So get ready for a visual\, acoustic trip from the Great Lakes 
 to the Canadian Rockies\; through the pains of lost loves and haunting mel
 odies.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240629T193000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Gordon Lightfoot Tribute
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-gordon-lightfoot-tribute/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A stunning st
 age show that replicates the songs\, stories\, styles\, and moods of the C
 anadian singer-songwriter’s BEST\, performed by Mike Fornes! His portrayal
  of Gordon Lightfoot is simply an honest effort to entertain with an accur
 ate representation of a Gordon Lightfoot concert. Fornes tireless research
  and personal interaction with Lightfoot have led to accurate mannerisms\,
  speaking patterns\, clothing\, and identical guitars used by the Canadian
  icon on stage.</p>\n<p>On stage\, he demonstrates his love of the timeles
 s music that captured millions during the 1960s\, 1970s\, and 1980s. His c
 atalog of Lightfoot’s music includes 77 songs that he chooses from in conc
 ert! Rarely does he break character\, usually only to introduce the band o
 r give a personal message before the show’s conclusion. Mike is backed by 
 four talented musicians who play the roles of Gordon Lightfoot’s stage ban
 d\, replicating parts heard on recordings and in live performances. So get
  ready for a visual\, acoustic trip from the Great Lakes to the Canadian R
 ockies\; through the pains of lost loves and haunting melodies.</p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
