BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-124068@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Peyton Womock – R&B\, soul\, smooth jazz\, and funk\nPeyton Wom
 ock\, a renowned artist\, showcases his exceptional saxophone skills\, sea
 mlessly blending genres such as Smooth Jazz\, Funk\, R&B\, Hip-Hop/Rap\, a
 nd Pop. With a repertoire including beloved covers and compelling original
  compositions\, Womock’s live performances promise a luxury experience cha
 racterized by unmatched energy that electrifies the stage.\nFind out more 
 about Peyton Womock at https://peytonwomock.com/.\nOpener: Ehaesi – blend 
 of Pop\, R&B and Afro-pop\nEhaesi is a 22-year-old singer-songwriter who h
 as recently embraced her true passion for music. Growing up in a Nigerian-
 Zambian household in America\, Ehaesi’s musical influences are a unique bl
 end of her rich African heritage and the diverse sounds of American pop\, 
 Afro-pop\, and R&B. This fusion of cultures has shaped her distinctive mus
 ical style\, blending soulful Afrobeat rhythms with contemporary melodies 
 and heartfelt lyrics. Despite balancing societal expectations and academic
  pursuits\, Ehaesi’s love for music has always been a guiding force. Now\,
  fully committed to her musical journey\, she crafts songs that resonate d
 eeply with listeners\, establishing herself as a promising new voice and s
 tory in the music industry.\nThis concert will feature a beer garden in ma
 in stage lawn with Bloomington Brewing Company and Cardinal Spirits.\nThes
 e concerts are held in conjunction with Bloomington Food Truck Fridays.\nF
 or more information about upcoming Performing Arts Series’ concerts\, plea
 se visit: https://bloomington.in.gov/parks/events/concerts
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240719T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240719T204500
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 S. Rogers Street Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Performing Arts Series presents Peyton Womock
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/performing-arts-series-presents-peyton-womock/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p class='LC20lb
  MBeuO DKV0Md'>Peyton Womock – R&B\, soul\, smooth jazz\, and funk</p>\n<p
 >Peyton Womock\, a renowned artist\, showcases his exceptional saxophone s
 kills\, seamlessly blending genres such as Smooth Jazz\, Funk\, R&B\, Hip-
 Hop/Rap\, and Pop. With a repertoire including beloved covers and compelli
 ng original compositions\, Womock’s live performances promise a luxury exp
 erience characterized by unmatched energy that electrifies the stage.</p>
 \n<p>Find out more about Peyton Womock at <a class='extl track' href='http
 s://peytonwomock.com/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow noopener noreferrer' 
 data-track='EventPage|clicks-external|200026692829644'>https://peytonwomoc
 k.com/</a>.</p>\n<p>Opener: Ehaesi – blend of Pop\, R&B and Afro-pop</p>\n
 <p>Ehaesi is a 22-year-old singer-songwriter who has recently embraced her
  true passion for music. Growing up in a Nigerian-Zambian household in Ame
 rica\, Ehaesi’s musical influences are a unique blend of her rich African 
 heritage and the diverse sounds of American pop\, Afro-pop\, and R&B. This
  fusion of cultures has shaped her distinctive musical style\, blending so
 ulful Afrobeat rhythms with contemporary melodies and heartfelt lyrics. De
 spite balancing societal expectations and academic pursuits\, Ehaesi’s lov
 e for music has always been a guiding force. Now\, fully committed to her 
 musical journey\, she crafts songs that resonate deeply with listeners\, e
 stablishing herself as a promising new voice and story in the music indust
 ry.</p>\n<p>This concert will feature a beer garden in main stage lawn wit
 h Bloomington Brewing Company and Cardinal Spirits.</p>\n<p>These concerts
  are held in conjunction with Bloomington Food Truck Fridays.</p>\n<p>For 
 more information about upcoming Performing Arts Series’ concerts\, please 
 visit: <a class='extl track' href='https://bloomington.in.gov/parks/events
 /concerts' target='_blank' rel='nofollow noopener noreferrer' data-track='
 EventPage|clicks-external|200026692829644'>https://bloomington.in.gov/park
 s/events/concerts</a></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
