BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-122669@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Brazil’s official selection for the 2024 Academy Awards\, PICTU
 RES OF GHOSTS\, from acclaimed director Kleber Mendonça Filho (BACURAU\, A
 QUARIUS and NEIGHBORING SOUNDS)\, is a multidimensional journey through ti
 me\, sound\, architecture and filmmaking\, set in the urban landscape of R
 ecife\, Brazilian coastal capital of Pernambuco: a historical and human te
 rritory\, examined through the great movie theatres that served as spaces 
 of conviviality during the 20th century. Having hosted dreams and progress
 \, these places have also embodied a major transformation on social practi
 ces. Combining archive documentary\, mystery\, film clips and personal mem
 ories\, PICTURES OF GHOSTS is a map of a city through the lens of cinema.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240721T190000
LOCATION:Redbud Books\, 408 W. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents: Pictures of Ghosts
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-pictures-of-ghosts/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>\n<p><b> </
 b><b>Brazil’s official selection for the 2024 Academy Awards\, PICTURES OF
  GHOSTS\, from acclaimed director Kleber Mendonça Filho (BACURAU\, AQUARIU
 S and NEIGHBORING SOUNDS)\, is a multidimensional journey through time\, s
 ound\, architecture and filmmaking\, set in the urban landscape of Recife\
 , Brazilian coastal capital of Pernambuco: a historical and human territor
 y\, examined through the great movie theatres that served as spaces of con
 viviality during the 20th century. Having hosted dreams and progress\, the
 se places have also embodied a major transformation on social practices. C
 ombining archive documentary\, mystery\, film clips and personal memories\
 , PICTURES OF GHOSTS is a map of a city through the lens of cinema.</b></p
 >\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
