BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-124317@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Experience the timeless charm and sophisticated wit of “The Phi
 ladelphia Story\,” a sparkling comedy that has captivated audiences for de
 cades. Set in the glamorous world of Philadelphia’s high society\, the pla
 y follows the spirited Tracy Lord as she navigates a whirlwind of romantic
  entanglements on the eve of her second marriage. With ex-husbands\, repor
 ters\, and fiancés vying for her attention\, Tracy must confront her past 
 and rediscover what truly matters. Filled with sharp dialogue\, vibrant ch
 aracters\, and heartwarming moments\, “The Philadelphia Story” is a deligh
 tful exploration of love\, class\, and personal growth that promises an ev
 ening of elegance and laughter.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240802T193000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St\, Nashville
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240803T193000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240809T193000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240810T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Philidelphia Story\, by Phillip Barry
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-philidelphia-story-by-phillip-barry/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Experience th
 e timeless charm and sophisticated wit of “The Philadelphia Story\,” a spa
 rkling comedy that has captivated audiences for decades. Set in the glamor
 ous world of Philadelphia’s high society\, the play follows the spirited T
 racy Lord as she navigates a whirlwind of romantic entanglements on the ev
 e of her second marriage. With ex-husbands\, reporters\, and fiancés vying
  for her attention\, Tracy must confront her past and rediscover what trul
 y matters. Filled with sharp dialogue\, vibrant characters\, and heartwarm
 ing moments\, “The Philadelphia Story” is a delightful exploration of love
 \, class\, and personal growth that promises an evening of elegance and la
 ughter.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-123820@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In rural Western Massachusetts\, 11-year-old Lacy spends the su
 mmer of 1991 at home\, enthralled by her own imagination and the attention
  of her mother\, Janet. As the months pass\, three visitors enter their or
 bit\, all captivated by Janet and her spellbinding nature. In her solitary
  moments\, Lacy inhabits an inner world so extraordinarily detailed that i
 t begins to seep into the outside world. Pulitzer Prize-winning playwright
  Annie Baker captures a child’s experience of time passing\, and the ineff
 ability of a daughter falling out of love with her mother\, in this singul
 arly sublime film debut.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240802T200000
LOCATION:Hopscotch Coffee + Kitchen\, 235 W Dodds St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents: Janet Planet (2024)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-janet-planet-2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><b> </b><b>In
  rural Western Massachusetts\, 11-year-old Lacy spends the summer of 1991 
 at home\, enthralled by her own imagination and the attention of her mothe
 r\, Janet. As the months pass\, three visitors enter their orbit\, all cap
 tivated by Janet and her spellbinding nature. In her solitary moments\, La
 cy inhabits an inner world so extraordinarily detailed that it begins to s
 eep into the outside world. Pulitzer Prize-winning playwright Annie Baker 
 captures a child’s experience of time passing\, and the ineffability of a 
 daughter falling out of love with her mother\, in this singularly sublime 
 film debut.</b></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
