BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-124904@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:From organizer Teri Klassen:\nPlease bring stories\, memories\,
  instruments\, songs and tunes to share\, a dish for the pitch-in if you c
 an (our contract specifies no alcohol)\, and flowers (if you have them 🙂 )
 . We will have a wide array of photographs\, all three of Hawk’s fiddles\,
  and his ashes in a beautiful ceramic urn made by his sister Shawn and car
 ried from Florida to Indiana by his brother Ed\, following Hawk’s request 
 to go “home to Bloomington.”\nWe will bury his ashes at Rose Hill cemetery
  (the plot is close to the maintenance shed at the southwest corner) at 11
  Monday\, and perhaps go to lunch afterwards.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240811T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240811T190000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E. 6th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Celebration of Life for Brian “Hawk” Hubbard
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/celebration-of-life-for-brian-hawk-hubbard/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>From organize
 r Teri Klassen:<br />\nPlease bring stories\, memories\, instruments\, son
 gs and tunes to share\, a dish for the pitch-in if you can (our contract s
 pecifies no alcohol)\, and flowers (if you have them 🙂 ). We will have a w
 ide array of photographs\, all three of Hawk’s fiddles\, and his ashes in 
 a beautiful ceramic urn made by his sister Shawn and carried from Florida 
 to Indiana by his brother Ed\, following Hawk’s request to go “home to Blo
 omington.”<br />\nWe will bury his ashes at Rose Hill cemetery (the plot i
 s close to the maintenance shed at the southwest corner) at 11 Monday\, an
 d perhaps go to lunch afterwards.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
