BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-124917@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to use Foundation Directory to search for grantmakers
  who have funded organizations working on causes and with communities simi
 lar to those you serve. Following a presentation\, you will have the oppor
 tunity to conduct your own searches and ask questions. Please bring a lapt
 op or other device that connects to the internet if you wish to participat
 e in this research lab portion. Note: This workshop is for nonprofit organ
 izations looking for funding. It is not geared to individuals seeking gran
 ts.\nThis Nonprofit Central class is brought to you in partnership with Ca
 ndid\, a nonprofit that helps other nonprofits serve their communities. As
  a Candid community member\, we offer Candid’s key tools including GuideSt
 ar and Foundation Directory. Library patrons can access GuideStar to resea
 rch local nonprofits to support and to find services. Nonprofits seeking f
 unding can also access Foundation Directory to find and connect with funde
 rs. Please contact Jack Kovaleski at jkovaleski@mcpl.info if you have any 
 questions about this program.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240814T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240814T120000
LOCATION:Meeting Room 2A\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 East Kirkwood
  Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Searching for Grants with Foundation Directory  (age 18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/searching-for-grants-with-foundation-directory-a
 ge-18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Learn how to 
 use Foundation Directory to search for grantmakers who have funded organiz
 ations working on causes and with communities similar to those you serve. 
 Following a presentation\, you will have the opportunity to conduct your o
 wn searches and ask questions. Please bring a laptop or other device that 
 connects to the internet if you wish to participate in this research lab p
 ortion. Note: This workshop is for nonprofit organizations looking for fun
 ding. It is not geared to individuals seeking grants.</p>\n<p>This Nonprof
 it Central class is brought to you in partnership with Candid\, a nonprofi
 t that helps other nonprofits serve their communities. As a Candid communi
 ty member\, we offer Candid’s key tools including GuideStar and Foundation
  Directory. Library patrons can access GuideStar to research local nonprof
 its to support and to find services. Nonprofits seeking funding can also a
 ccess Foundation Directory to find and connect with funders. Please contac
 t Jack Kovaleski at jkovaleski@mcpl.info if you have any questions about t
 his program.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
