UID:ai1ec-125075@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:linktr.ee/jakebraunecker\nJake Braunecker is a singer/songwrite
 r historically a multi-genre musician drawing inspiration from country\, r
 eggae\, funk\, etc… though recently deeply inspired by traditional Bluegra
 ss. Motivated by creating meaningful connections and social evolution thro
 ugh everything he does\, music included but also through community organiz
 ing and general good-heartedness 😉\nHe is a Southern Indiana native who ha
 s been living in France for the last 10 years. Back in town for just a few
  days so don’t miss the moment to come by\, have listen and say hi.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240817T180000
LOCATION:The Pink Poodle House Venue\, 917 North Fairview St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Jake Braunecker
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/jake-braunecker/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>linktr.ee/jak
 ebraunecker<br />\nJake Braunecker is a singer/songwriter historically a m
 ulti-genre musician drawing inspiration from country\, reggae\, funk\, etc
 … though recently deeply inspired by traditional Bluegrass. Motivated by c
 reating meaningful connections and social evolution through everything he 
 does\, music included but also through community organizing and general go
 od-heartedness 😉<br />\nHe is a Southern Indiana native who has been livin
 g in France for the last 10 years. Back in town for just a few days so don
 ’t miss the moment to come by\, have listen and say hi.</p>\n</BODY></HTML
 >
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
