BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-124945@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a powerful and thought-provoking free presentation 
 of “The Addict’s Wake\,” in conjunction with the Nashville United Methodis
 t Church. This compelling film delves deep into the lives affected by addi
 ction\, offering a raw and honest portrayal of the struggles and triumphs 
 faced by individuals and their families. Through intimate storytelling and
  heartfelt interviews\, “The Addict’s Wake” sheds light on the path to rec
 overy and the importance of community support. Don’t miss this opportunity
  to witness a moving narrative that inspires hope and fosters understandin
 g. Come and be a part of a community conversation that could change lives.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240818T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240818T160000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: The Addict’s Wake – Educational Edit
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-addicts-wake-educational-edit/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us for a
  powerful and thought-provoking free presentation of “The Addict’s Wake\,”
  in conjunction with the Nashville United Methodist Church. This compellin
 g film delves deep into the lives affected by addiction\, offering a raw a
 nd honest portrayal of the struggles and triumphs faced by individuals and
  their families. Through intimate storytelling and heartfelt interviews\, 
 “The Addict’s Wake” sheds light on the path to recovery and the importance
  of community support. Don’t miss this opportunity to witness a moving nar
 rative that inspires hope and fosters understanding. Come and be a part of
  a community conversation that could change lives.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
