BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-125433@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Get Ready for 5th Annual WFHB Block Rocker!\nThis is a FREE and
  ALL AGES outdoor event\, located on 4th street between College and Walnut
  avenues\, right outside the WFHB studios. The Block Rocker is a community
 -centered event highlighting local musicians\, local non-profit booths\, l
 ocal small business sponsors\, and local food and drink vendors. We hope t
 o see you there!\nLINEUP CHANGE! Unfortunately\, due to a death in a band 
 mates family\, Negative Glow will not be performing during this Saturday’s
  Block Rocker. However\, beloved Bloomington band\, Busman’s Holiday\, is 
 coming to rescue us with very short notice!\nSpecial thanks to our sponsor
 s the Bloomington Arts Commission\, Indiana Arts Commission\, Visit Bloomi
 ngton\, Secretly Canadian\, and Russian Recording.\nWHAT: WFHB Block Rocke
 r\nWHERE: On 4th street between College and Walnut avenues\, downtown Bloo
 mington\nWHEN: Saturday\, August 24th\, 5pm until 11pm\nLINEUP (Starting w
 ith the Headliner): LowDown Brass Band (from Chicago)\, Busman’s Holiday (
 Bloomington)\, The Namby Pamby (Fort Wayne\, IN)\, Low Landers (Nashville\
 , IN)\, Reggae Union (Bloomington)\nYou can count on beverages from Bloomi
 ngton Brewing Company and Cardinal Spirits. With Food from The Orbit Room\
 , Pili’s Taco Truck\, Planted\, Popkorn with a Twist\, and Rasta Pops! Pop
 ups by Badknees Tees\, Secretly Canadian’s Paved Paradise and informationa
 l booths by nonprofits Redbud Books and Tandem.\nHUGE THANKS to our sponso
 rs! Secretly Group\, City of Bloomington Arts Commission\, Russian Recordi
 ng\, Visit Bloomington\, and the Indiana Arts Commission.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240824T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240824T230000
LOCATION:WFHB\, 108 W. 4th St.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:2024 WFHB Block Rocker
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/2024-wfhb-block-rocker/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><h4 style='text-
 align: center\;'><strong>Get Ready for 5th Annual WFHB Block Rocker!</stro
 ng></h4>\n<p><strong>This is a FREE and ALL AGES outdoor event</strong>\, 
 located on 4th street between College and Walnut avenues\, right outside t
 he WFHB studios. The Block Rocker is a community-centered event highlighti
 ng local musicians\, local non-profit booths\, local small business sponso
 rs\, and local food and drink vendors. We hope to see you there!</p>\n<p>L
 INEUP CHANGE! Unfortunately\, due to a death in a band mates family\, Nega
 tive Glow will not be performing during this Saturday’s Block Rocker. Howe
 ver\, beloved Bloomington band\, Busman’s Holiday\, is coming to rescue us
  with very short notice!</p>\n<p><strong>Special thanks to our sponsors th
 e Bloomington Arts Commission\, Indiana Arts Commission\, Visit Bloomingto
 n\, Secretly Canadian\, and Russian Recording.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>WH
 AT: WFHB Block Rocker</strong><br />\n<strong>WHERE: On 4th street between
  College and Walnut avenues\, downtown Bloomington</strong><br />\n<strong
 >WHEN: Saturday\, August 24th\, 5pm until 11pm</strong><br />\n<strong>LIN
 EUP (Starting with the Headliner): LowDown Brass Band (from Chicago)\, Bus
 man’s Holiday (Bloomington)\, The Namby Pamby (Fort Wayne\, IN)\, Low Land
 ers (Nashville\, IN)\, Reggae Union (Bloomington)</strong></p>\n<p>You can
  count on beverages from Bloomington Brewing Company and Cardinal Spirits.
  With Food from The Orbit Room\, Pili’s Taco Truck\, Planted\, Popkorn wit
 h a Twist\, and Rasta Pops! Popups by Badknees Tees\, Secretly Canadian’s 
 Paved Paradise and informational booths by nonprofits Redbud Books and Tan
 dem.</p>\n<p><strong>HUGE THANKS to our sponsors! Secretly Group\, City of
  Bloomington Arts Commission\, Russian Recording\, Visit Bloomington\, and
  the Indiana Arts Commission.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
