BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-125463@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:RSVP Requested. Sit back and relax as Portia Sholar Jackson tel
 ls stories of Black history\, intertwined with original stories exploring 
 themes from this year’s Brown County Reads selection\, “All That She Carri
 ed” by author Tiya Miles.\nPortia Sholar Jackson is a professional storyte
 ller and teaching artist with Arts for Learning. The power of her voice an
 d her dramatic interpretations leaves listeners spellbound as she makes th
 e words of legendary black women like Harriet Tubman and Mary McLeod Bethu
 ne take on new meaning.\nIdeal for adults and kids grade 4 and up\, but al
 l ages welcome.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240827T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240827T190000
LOCATION:Brown County Public Library\, 205 Locust Lane\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Stories of Strength: Storytelling with Portia Sholar Jackson
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/stories-of-strength-storytelling-with-portia-sho
 lar-jackson/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>RSVP 
 Requested. Sit back and relax as Portia Sholar Jackson tells stories of Bl
 ack history\, intertwined with original stories exploring themes from this
  year’s Brown County Reads selection\, “All That She Carried” by author Ti
 ya Miles.</p>\n<p>Portia Sholar Jackson is a professional storyteller and 
 teaching artist with Arts for Learning. The power of her voice and her dra
 matic interpretations leaves listeners spellbound as she makes the words o
 f legendary black women like Harriet Tubman and Mary McLeod Bethune take o
 n new meaning.</p>\n<p>Ideal for adults and kids grade 4 and up\, but all 
 ages welcome.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
