BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-125683@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Monroe County Humane Association veterinary team and Monroe
  Fire Station 24 are hosting a pop-up mobile vaccine clinic! No appointmen
 t needed\; all are welcome!\n\nA range of services are available\, includi
 ng legally mandated rabies vaccines for pets aged 12 weeks and older. Clin
 ics also provide nail trims\, microchips\, and preventive measures for fle
 a\, tick\, and heartworm.\n\nSubsidized rates are available to residents e
 xperiencing financial hardship if they provide documentation. Cats must be
  in carriers\, and dogs must be leashed (no retractable leashes). Pets sho
 wing signs of illness or aggression might be turned away.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240901T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240901T150000
LOCATION:Monroe Fire Station 24\, 7606 E State Road 45\, Unionville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Pop-Up Vaccine Clinic for Dogs and Cats
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/pop-up-vaccine-clinic-for-dogs-and-cats/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>The <a href
 ='http://monroehumane.org'>Monroe County Humane Association</a> veterinary
  team and Monroe Fire Station 24 are hosting a pop-up mobile vaccine clini
 c! No appointment needed\; all are welcome!</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>A ran
 ge of services are available\, including legally mandated rabies vaccines 
 for pets aged 12 weeks and older. Clinics also provide nail trims\, microc
 hips\, and preventive measures for flea\, tick\, and heartworm.</div>\n<di
 v></div>\n<div>Subsidized rates are available to residents experiencing fi
 nancial hardship if they provide documentation. Cats must be in carriers\,
  and dogs must be leashed (no retractable leashes). Pets showing signs of 
 illness or aggression might be turned away.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
