BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-125909@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In Exposed\, noted historian Wendy Kline uncovers the procedure
 ’s fascinating—and often disturbing—history. From gynecological research o
 n enslaved women’s bodies to nonconsensual practice on anesthetized patien
 ts\, the pelvic exam as we know it today carries the burden of its sordid 
 past. Its story is one of pain and pleasure\, life-saving discoveries and 
 heartbreaking encounters\, questionable procedures and triumphant breakthr
 oughs. Drawing on previously unpublished archival sources\, along with int
 erviews with patients\, providers\, and activists\, Kline traces key momen
 ts and movements in gynecological history\, from the surgeons of the ninet
 eenth century to the OB/GYNs of today.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240905T193000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books\, 849 Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Non-Fiction Author Event with Wendy Kline: ‘Exposed\, the Hidden Hi
 story of the Pelvic Exam’
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/non-fiction-author-event-with-wendy-kline-expose
 d-the-hidden-history-of-the-pelvic-exam/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>In Ex
 posed\, noted historian Wendy Kline uncovers the procedure’s fascinating—a
 nd often disturbing—history. From gynecological research on enslaved women
 ’s bodies to nonconsensual practice on anesthetized patients\, the pelvic 
 exam as we know it today carries the burden of its sordid past. Its story 
 is one of pain and pleasure\, life-saving discoveries and heartbreaking en
 counters\, questionable procedures and triumphant breakthroughs. Drawing o
 n previously unpublished archival sources\, along with interviews with pat
 ients\, providers\, and activists\, Kline traces key moments and movements
  in gynecological history\, from the surgeons of the nineteenth century to
  the OB/GYNs of today.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
