BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-124986@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Founded in 1969 and 1974 respectively\, the Neal-Marshall Black
  Culture Center (NMBCC) and African American Arts Institute (AAAI) have be
 come invaluable sources of community for Black students\, staff\, and facu
 lty at Indiana University. In celebration of 50-plus years of community\, 
 scholarship\, artistic excellence\, and service\, this exhibition shares t
 he history of each organization and highlights the legacy and efforts of H
 erman Hudson and other supportive IU faculty\, staff\, alumni\, and commun
 ity members over the last five decades.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240906T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240906T180000
LOCATION:University Collections at McCalla\, 525 E. 9th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Exhibition Opening: “Lasting Legacies: Honoring the Neal-Marshall B
 lack Culture Center and African American Arts Institute”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/exhibition-opening-lasting-legacies-honoring-the
 -neal-marshall-black-culture-center-and-african-american-arts-institute/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Founded in 19
 69 and 1974 respectively\, the Neal-Marshall Black Culture Center (NMBCC) 
 and African American Arts Institute (AAAI) have become invaluable sources 
 of community for Black students\, staff\, and faculty at Indiana Universit
 y. In celebration of 50-plus years of community\, scholarship\, artistic e
 xcellence\, and service\, this exhibition shares the history of each organ
 ization and highlights the legacy and efforts of Herman Hudson and other s
 upportive IU faculty\, staff\, alumni\, and community members over the las
 t five decades.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
