BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-125867@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Watch the best cat videos the internet has to offer and support
  the Monroe County Humane Association Each CatVideoFest screening helps ra
 ise money for cats in need through partnerships with local cat charities\,
  animal welfare organizations\, and shelters to best serve cats in local a
 reas. Since 2019\, over $150\,000 has been raised for local shelters in ad
 dition to adoptions\, fostering\, volunteer sign-ups\, and much more throu
 gh CatVideoFest screenings. In 2024 so far\, $30\,000 has been raised to b
 enefit local shelters and animal welfare organizations.\nIU Cinema’s CatVi
 deoFest 2024 screening supports the Monroe County Humane Association (MCHA
 ). Since 1956\, MCHA has embodied hope and compassion for animals and thei
 r human companions throughout Monroe County and its surrounding regions. W
 ith a legacy rich in heartfelt service and impactful change spanning more 
 than six decades\, MCHA steadfastly remains a sanctuary of support\, kindn
 ess\, and proactive care for animals in their most vulnerable times.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240908T130000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:CATVIDEOFEST 2024
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/catvideofest-2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Watch
  the best cat videos the internet has to offer and support the Monroe Coun
 ty Humane Association</strong> Each CatVideoFest screening helps raise mon
 ey for cats in need through partnerships with local cat charities\, animal
  welfare organizations\, and shelters to best serve cats in local areas. S
 ince 2019\, over $150\,000 has been raised for local shelters in addition 
 to adoptions\, fostering\, volunteer sign-ups\, and much more through CatV
 ideoFest screenings. In 2024 so far\, $30\,000 has been raised to benefit 
 local shelters and animal welfare organizations.</p>\n<p>IU Cinema’s CatVi
 deoFest 2024 screening supports the Monroe County Humane Association (MCHA
 ). Since 1956\, MCHA has embodied hope and compassion for animals and thei
 r human companions throughout Monroe County and its surrounding regions. W
 ith a legacy rich in heartfelt service and impactful change spanning more 
 than six decades\, MCHA steadfastly remains a sanctuary of support\, kindn
 ess\, and proactive care for animals in their most vulnerable times.</p>\n
 </BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
