 ndex.html
DESCRIPTION:Join the next Food for Thought livestream\, which will feature 
 a presentation and Q&A with Professor and Chair of Political Science Aurel
 ian Craiutu\, who will discuss moderation as a crucial but overlooked virt
 ue and its potential to serve as a powerful tool for navigating and bridgi
 ng divides in our increasingly polarized political landscape.\nThe College
  of Arts and Sciences’ Food for Thought series of lifelong-learning events
  enables IU alumni and friends to hear from faculty experts\, explore inte
 llectually engaging topics\, and stay connected with Indiana University an
 d the College of Arts and Sciences.\nAll past Food for Thought livestreams
  are available on the College’s YouTube channel.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240910T190000
LOCATION:Zoom
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:In Praise of a Forgotten Virtue: Moderation in the Twenty-First Cen
 tury
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/in-praise-of-a-forgotten-virtue-moderation-in-th
 e-twenty-first-century/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join the next
  Food for Thought <strong><a href='https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_
 cYhuzDNrTye_pmRfseQ5Kw?j=1862986&sfmc_sub=144944421&l=83668_HTML&u=5341669
 5&mid=518003125&jb=7#/registration'>livestream</a></strong>\, which will f
 eature a presentation and Q&A with Professor and Chair of Political Scienc
 e Aurelian Craiutu\, who will discuss moderation as a crucial but overlook
 ed virtue and its potential to serve as a powerful tool for navigating and
  bridging divides in our increasingly polarized political landscape.</p>\n
 <p>The College of Arts and Sciences’ <b><a title='Food for Thought' href='
 https://click.e.iu.edu/?qs=3a0bc107a6980bc94155c792fc55b54278ab3c2210322d5
 a96eb8451efe6076d7105c605a60abb35d9baf73a48a8ab723998ac4340a66cd3' target=
 '_blank' rel='noopener' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?q
 =https://click.e.iu.edu/?qs%3D3a0bc107a6980bc94155c792fc55b54278ab3c221032
 2d5a96eb8451efe6076d7105c605a60abb35d9baf73a48a8ab723998ac4340a66cd3&sourc
 e=gmail&ust=1725489165780000&usg=AOvVaw0ccgeQL8Pgh20i609wAWQq'>Food for Th
 ought</a> </b>series of lifelong-learning events enables IU alumni and fri
 ends to hear from faculty experts\, explore intellectually engaging topics
 \, and stay connected with Indiana University and the College of Arts and 
 Sciences.</p>\n<p>All past Food for Thought livestreams are available on <
 a class='external' href='https://www.youtube.com/@iucollegeofartssciences6
 084/playlists'>the College’s YouTube channel.</a></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
