UID:ai1ec-126306@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Maggie Hutt\; mhutt@mcpl.info\; https://calendar.mcpl.info/event/11
 150330
DESCRIPTION:Join to learn the basics of backyard composting\, including\n\n
 What foods you can compost\nDifferent setups and methods\, from worm bins 
 to tumblers to the ol’ fashioned compost pile\nHot composting versus cold 
 composting methods\n“Greens” versus “browns” and how to have a well balanc
 ed\, healthy compost nutrition ratio\nComposting throughout the year\; you
 r methods should adapt to the seasons based on heat\, cold\, and moisture
 \nMethods for maintaining an odorless pest free composting process\nFinish
 ing compost and how to use it in your garden\n\nThe program is in partners
 hip between the MCPL and the City of Bloomington Parks and Recreation.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240912T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240912T193000
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library\, 303 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington (D
 owntown Library\, Meeting Room 2B)
SEQUENCE:0
