X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Join 
 to learn the basics of backyard composting\,</strong> including</p>\n<ul>
 \n<li>What foods you can compost</li>\n<li>Different setups and methods\, 
 from worm bins to tumblers to the ol’ fashioned compost pile</li>\n<li>Hot
  composting versus cold composting methods</li>\n<li>“Greens” versus “brow
 ns” and how to have a well balanced\, healthy compost nutrition ratio</li>
 \n<li>Composting throughout the year\; your methods should adapt to the se
 asons based on heat\, cold\, and moisture</li>\n<li>Methods for maintainin
 g an odorless pest free composting process</li>\n<li>Finishing compost and
  how to use it in your garden</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The program is in partnershi
 p between the MCPL and the City of Bloomington Parks and Recreation.</p>\n
 </BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
