BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126109@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://indianapublicmedia.org/swinginseptember/
DESCRIPTION:WFIU Public Radio and the Department of Jazz Studies at the Ind
 iana University Jacobs School of Music are partnering to co-host Swing in 
 September\, a free outdoor concert series featuring a variety of musical a
 cts from swing bands to jazz vocalists and more. WFIU hosts David Brent Jo
 hnson and William Morris will emcee the concerts.\nAbout the Swing in Sept
 ember artists:\nPalonegro’s music spans from South American Andean styles 
 to Afro-Caribbean rhythms and Latin jazz and features the original composi
 tions and arrangements of the band’s director Sergio Ospina Romero. Palone
 gro’s journey began in Bogotá\, Colombia\, in 2009. Between 2014 and 2019 
 Palonegro was based in Ithaca\, New York\, where they recorded their first
  album Two Minutes Apart. After another season in Colombia\, Sergio reloca
 ted to Bloomington and Palonegro became a Latin jazz quartet with Sergio O
 spina Romero on piano\, Jacob Smith on bass\, Michael Wimer on congas\, an
 d John Maruri on drums.\nThe Big Push is a quintet based in Bloomington th
 at performs a mix of original music and arrangements of jazz standards. Th
 e band is named after Wayne Shorter’s composition “The Big Push” from his 
 album The Soothsayer. In addition to Shorter\, influences include Joshua R
 edman\, Brian Blade\, Joe Henderson\, and Art Blakey. This band loves to s
 wing! The group is comprised of Caleb Robinson on tenor saxophone\, Nadia 
 Reist on trumpet\, Dan Ventura on piano\, Alex Hoberty on bass\, and Tate 
 Sherman on drums and cymbals.\nThe Postmodern Jazz Quartet has played regu
 larly at venues around Bloomington since its formation in 2004\, including
  Tutto Bene Wine Bar\, Player’s Pub\, Café Django\, Topos\, Bear’s Place\,
  C3\, and Morgenstern’s Books and Café\, where the band currently holds a 
 monthly jazz salon. The group’s set list features jazz standards and hard 
 bop classics. The band includes Jeff Isaac on piano\, Pat Harbison on trum
 pet\, Jonathan Elmer on trombone\, Dave Bruker on bass\, and Dan Deckard o
 n drums.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240913T183000
LOCATION:Indiana University\, Northwest Quad\, Bloomington (If rain\, Recit
 al Hall)
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240920T183000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20240927T183000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Swing in September: Palonegro (9/13)\, The Big Push (9/20) and The 
 Postmodern Jazz Quartet (9/27)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/swing-in-september-palonegro-9-13-the-big-push-9
 -20-and-the-postmodern-jazz-quartet-9-27/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>WFIU Public R
 adio and the Department of Jazz Studies at the Indiana University Jacobs S
 chool of Music are partnering to co-host <strong>Swing in September</stron
 g>\, a free outdoor concert series featuring a variety of musical acts fro
 m swing bands to jazz vocalists and more. WFIU hosts David Brent Johnson a
 nd William Morris will emcee the concerts.</p>\n<p>About the <strong>Swing
  in September</strong> artists:<br />\n<strong>Palonegro</strong>’s music 
 spans from South American Andean styles to Afro-Caribbean rhythms and Lati
 n jazz and features the original compositions and arrangements of the band
 ’s director Sergio Ospina Romero. Palonegro’s journey began in Bogotá\, Co
 lombia\, in 2009. Between 2014 and 2019 Palonegro was based in Ithaca\, Ne
 w York\, where they recorded their first album Two Minutes Apart. After an
 other season in Colombia\, Sergio relocated to Bloomington and Palonegro b
 ecame a Latin jazz quartet with Sergio Ospina Romero on piano\, Jacob Smit
 h on bass\, Michael Wimer on congas\, and John Maruri on drums.</p>\n<p><s
 trong>The Big Push</strong> is a quintet based in Bloomington that perform
 s a mix of original music and arrangements of jazz standards. The band is 
 named after Wayne Shorter’s composition “The Big Push” from his album The 
 Soothsayer. In addition to Shorter\, influences include Joshua Redman\, Br
 ian Blade\, Joe Henderson\, and Art Blakey. This band loves to swing! The 
 group is comprised of Caleb Robinson on tenor saxophone\, Nadia Reist on t
 rumpet\, Dan Ventura on piano\, Alex Hoberty on bass\, and Tate Sherman on
  drums and cymbals.</p>\n<p><strong>The Postmodern Jazz Quartet</strong> h
 as played regularly at venues around Bloomington since its formation in 20
 04\, including Tutto Bene Wine Bar\, Player’s Pub\, Café Django\, Topos\, 
 Bear’s Place\, C3\, and Morgenstern’s Books and Café\, where the band curr
 ently holds a monthly jazz salon. The group’s set list features jazz stand
 ards and hard bop classics. The band includes Jeff Isaac on piano\, Pat Ha
 rbison on trumpet\, Jonathan Elmer on trombone\, Dave Bruker on bass\, and
  Dan Deckard on drums.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
