BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126954@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:sites.google.com/bloomington.in.gov/cobbyb
DESCRIPTION:The City of Bloomington will hosting\nThe event\, organized by 
 the city’s Safe and Civil City Programs and the Commission on Hispanic and
  Latino Affairs\, aims to celebrate and showcase the contributions of arti
 sts of color through visual and performing arts.\nThe festival will begin 
 at 10 a.m. with an arts market in the Switchyard Park Pavilion\, featuring
  a variety of works by local artists\, including paintings\, sculptures\, 
 ceramics\, and jewelry. Starting at 12:30 p.m.\, performances will take pl
 ace on the Grand Stage\, with a lineup that includes the African American 
 Dance Company\, Matixando\, and Peyton Womock & Friends.\nIn addition to t
 he art and performances\, attendees can expect food vendors\, interactive 
 art activities\, and booths offering community information. The festival i
 s free and open to the public\, creating a family-friendly environment whe
 re people of all backgrounds can engage with and appreciate the artistic c
 ontributions of Black and Brown artists in the community.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T160000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park Pavilion and Grand Stage\, 1601 S Rogers St\, Bloo
 mington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:6th Annual Black y Brown Arts Festival
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/black-y-brown-arts-festival-2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>The C
 ity of Bloomington will hosting</strong><br />\nThe event\, organized by t
 he city’s Safe and Civil City Programs and the Commission on Hispanic and 
 Latino Affairs\, aims to celebrate and showcase the contributions of artis
 ts of color through visual and performing arts.</p>\n<p>The festival will 
 begin at 10 a.m. with an arts market in the Switchyard Park Pavilion\, fea
 turing a variety of works by local artists\, including paintings\, sculptu
 res\, ceramics\, and jewelry. Starting at 12:30 p.m.\, performances will t
 ake place on the Grand Stage\, with a lineup that includes the African Ame
 rican Dance Company\, Matixando\, and Peyton Womock & Friends.</p>\n<p>In 
 addition to the art and performances\, attendees can expect food vendors\,
  interactive art activities\, and booths offering community information. T
 he festival is free and open to the public\, creating a family-friendly en
 vironment where people of all backgrounds can engage with and appreciate t
 he artistic contributions of Black and Brown artists in the community.</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
