BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126094@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812.318.1236\; https://www.meditationinbloomington.org/taming
DESCRIPTION:Do you ever feel like your mind is like a wild elephant? How ca
 n you train or tame your mind to pacify the distracting and destructive th
 oughts that hold you captive? We can improve the quality of our minds thro
 ugh training in mindfulness and alertness with joy. From improving the qua
 lity of our mind and clearly understanding how to guard the mind\, our hap
 piness will increase and we will experience a deep inner peace and supplen
 ess of mind.\nIn this retreat\, we will explore:\n> Guarding the mind vers
 us suppression through mindfulness\n> Protecting our mind when it’s upset 
 and feeling uncontrolled\n> Becoming familiar with how to pacify negativit
 y through a daily practice\nThe retreat is suitable for all meditation lev
 els\, including beginners. It includes guided meditations\, short teaching
 s as well as Q&A in the last session. Everyone can benefit from this retre
 at — you don’t have to be Buddhist to participate.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T130000
LOCATION:Kadampa Meditation Center Bloomington\, 234 N. Morton St\, Bloomin
 gton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Taming the Wild Elephant Mind Retreat (In Person)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/taming-the-wild-elephant-mind-retreat/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Do you ever f
 eel like your mind is like a wild elephant? How can you train or tame your
  mind to pacify the distracting and destructive thoughts that hold you cap
 tive? We can improve the quality of our minds through training in mindfuln
 ess and alertness with joy. From improving the quality of our mind and cle
 arly understanding how to guard the mind\, our happiness will increase and
  we will experience a deep inner peace and suppleness of mind.</p>\n<p>In 
 this retreat\, we will explore:<br />\n> Guarding the mind versus suppress
 ion through mindfulness<br />\n> Protecting our mind when it’s upset and f
 eeling uncontrolled<br />\n> Becoming familiar with how to pacify negativi
 ty through a daily practice</p>\n<p>The retreat is suitable for all medita
 tion levels\, including beginners. It includes guided meditations\, short 
 teachings as well as Q&A in the last session. Everyone can benefit from th
 is retreat — you don’t have to be Buddhist to participate.</p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
END:VEVENT
