BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126079@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:DOOR TIME 6 pm\nJoin us for a night of celebration and empowerm
 ent at the 43th Freedom Fund Award Dinner. Get ready to be inspired by our
  guest speakers\, enjoy delicious food\, and connect with community member
 s who share your passion for social justice.\nThe “Freedom Fund” represent
 s the resources the branch uses to support its mission to ensure the polit
 ical\, educational\, social\, and economic equality of rights of all perso
 ns and to eliminate race-based discrimination.\nThe National Association f
 or the Advancement of Colored People presents an annual NAACP President’s 
 Award. Winners are selected by the NAACP president in recognition of speci
 al achievement and distinguished public service. This year’s winner for th
 e President’s Award goes to Bloomington Historian Elizabeth Mitchell!\nDon
 ’t miss out on this opportunity to support the NAACP’s important work in a
 dvancing civil rights and equality for all. See you there!\nPartner with u
 s as we raise funds for scholarships\, public forums on civil rights issue
 s & community programs. Become a sponsor HERE.\nTicket prices will increas
 e to $65 for both youth and adults beginning Monday\, September 9th – Satu
 rday\, September 14th. Online and box office sales will end at 4pm on Frid
 ay September 13th. After that tickets can be purchased at the door of Shre
 ve Hall- Ivy Tech Community College (200 Daniels Way\, Bloomington\, IN 47
 404) at 6pm. Cash and Check will be accepted at the door of the event.\nTh
 ere will be no physical tickets your name and quantity of tickets will be 
 on a list at the door at the venue Shreve Hall- Ivy Tech Community College
  (200 Daniels Way\, Bloomington\, IN 47404) starting at 6pm. Have your ID 
 or Confirmation email ready at entry.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T210000
LOCATION:Ivy Tech Community College - Shreve Hall\, 200 Daniels Way\, Bloom
 ington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Monroe County National Association for the Advancement of Color
 ed People Branch #3062 presents: The 2024 NAACP Freedom Fund Awards Dinner
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-monroe-county-national-association-for-the-a
 dvancement-of-colored-people-branch-3062-presents-the-2024-naacp-freedom-f
 und-awards-dinner/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>DOOR 
 TIME 6 pm</strong><br />\nJoin us for a night of celebration and empowerme
 nt at the 43th Freedom Fund Award Dinner. Get ready to be inspired by our 
 guest speakers\, enjoy delicious food\, and connect with community members
  who share your passion for social justice.</p>\n<p>The “Freedom Fund” rep
 resents the resources the branch uses to support its mission to ensure the
  political\, educational\, social\, and economic equality of rights of all
  persons and to eliminate race-based discrimination.</p>\n<p>The National 
 Association for the Advancement of Colored People presents an annual NAACP
  President’s Award. Winners are selected by the NAACP president in recogni
 tion of special achievement and distinguished public service. This year’s 
 winner for the President’s Award goes to Bloomington Historian Elizabeth M
 itchell!</p>\n<p>Don’t miss out on this opportunity to support the NAACP’s
  important work in advancing civil rights and equality for all. See you th
 ere!</p>\n<p>Partner with us as we raise funds for scholarships\, public f
 orums on civil rights issues & community programs. Become a sponsor HERE.<
 /p>\n<p>Ticket prices will increase to $65 for both youth and adults begin
 ning Monday\, September 9th – Saturday\, September 14th. Online and box of
 fice sales will end at 4pm on Friday September 13th. After that tickets ca
 n be purchased at the door of Shreve Hall- Ivy Tech Community College (200
  Daniels Way\, Bloomington\, IN 47404) at 6pm. Cash and Check will be acce
 pted at the door of the event.</p>\n<p>There will be no physical tickets y
 our name and quantity of tickets will be on a list at the door at the venu
 e Shreve Hall- Ivy Tech Community College (200 Daniels Way\, Bloomington\,
  IN 47404) starting at 6pm. Have your ID or Confirmation email ready at en
 try.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
