BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126153@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.mitchelloperahouse.com/event/mark-wills/
DESCRIPTION:Doors Open 6:15 p.m.\nIt was “19(90) Somethin’” when Grand Ole 
 Opry member Mark Wills went from singing at Atlanta’s infamous Buckboard t
 o releasing his first of 19 Billboard-charting singles across seven albums
  including “Wish You Were Here\,” “Jacob’s Ladder”\, “I Do (Cherish You)”\
 , “Places I’ve Never Been\,” “Don’t Laugh at Me\,” and No. 1 single “Wish 
 You Were Here”. While climbing his musical ‘ladder\,’ he has recorded Gold
  and Platinum albums and released some of the most enduring and recognizab
 le Country Music hits of the last 25 Years. One of his biggest hits to dat
 e is the RIAA Gold-certified “19 Somethin’” – a six-week No. 1 on the Bill
 board Hot Country Songs chart . He also has taken more than a dozen trips 
 to entertain U.S. troops in Iraq\, Kuwait\, Afghanistan\, Korea\, and Ital
 y. Wills continues to hit the road with his high-energy show full of hits 
 that were the soundtrack to so many people’s lives.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T210000
LOCATION:Mitchell Opera House\, N 7th & Brook St\, Mitchell
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mark Wills
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mark-wills-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  Open 6:15 p.m.</strong><br />\nIt was “19(90) Somethin’” when <strong>Gra
 nd Ole Opry</strong> member <strong>Mark Wills</strong> went from singing 
 at <strong>Atlanta’s infamous Buckboard</strong> to releasing his first of
  19 Billboard-charting singles across seven albums including “Wish You Wer
 e Here\,” “Jacob’s Ladder”\, “I Do (Cherish You)”\, “Places I’ve Never Bee
 n\,” “Don’t Laugh at Me\,” and No. 1 single “Wish You Were Here”. While cl
 imbing his musical ‘ladder\,’ he has recorded Gold and Platinum albums and
  released some of the most enduring and recognizable Country Music hits of
  the last 25 Years. One of his biggest hits to date is the RIAA Gold-certi
 fied “19 Somethin’” – a six-week No. 1 on the Billboard Hot Country Songs 
 chart . He also has taken more than a dozen trips to entertain U.S. troops
  in Iraq\, Kuwait\, Afghanistan\, Korea\, and Italy. Wills continues to hi
 t the road with his high-energy show full of hits that were the soundtrack
  to so many people’s lives.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
