BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126026@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\; 812.323.3020\; boxoffice@buskirkchumley.o
 rg\; https://buskirkchumley.org/
DESCRIPTION:DOORS 7 pm\nA portion of profits from this event will be donate
 d to Social Justice Work of UU Church of Bloomington.\nJoin Carrie Newcome
 r with pianist Gary Walters and The Gathering of Spirits String Quartet fo
 r an intimate and uplifting evening of musical storytelling\, humor\, poet
 ry and award-winning songwriting. Newcomer’s performances explore themes o
 f connection\, spirituality\, the natural world and the human possibility.
  Her concerts are warm and folk-inspired\, always leaving her audiences fe
 eling encouraged and reminded of what is both gritty and beautiful in huma
 nity.\nSpecial guest musician and opener will be Jason Wilber\, songwriter
 \, recording artist\, and 24-year music director/guitarist for the legenda
 ry singer-songwriter John Prine.\nWe hope you join for this evening of hea
 rt opening music\, A Gathering of Spirits: Hope in Hard Times.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240914T213000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Roots presents: A Gathering of Spirits – Hope in Hard T
 imes\, with Carrie Newcomer\, pianist Gary Walters and The Gathering of Sp
 irits String Quartet (also opener Jason Wilbur)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/a-gathering-of-spirits-hope-in-hard-times/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>DOORS
  7 pm</strong><br />\n<i>A portion of profits from this event will be dona
 ted to Social Justice Work of UU Church of Bloomington.</i></p>\n<p>Join <
 strong>Carrie Newcomer</strong> with pianist <strong>Gary Walters</strong>
  and <strong>The Gathering of Spirits String Quartet</strong> for an intim
 ate and uplifting evening of musical storytelling\, humor\, poetry and awa
 rd-winning songwriting. Newcomer’s performances explore themes of connecti
 on\, spirituality\, the natural world and the human possibility. Her conce
 rts are warm and folk-inspired\, always leaving her audiences feeling enco
 uraged and reminded of what is both gritty and beautiful in humanity.</p>
 \n<p>Special guest musician and opener will be <strong>Jason Wilber</stron
 g>\, songwriter\, recording artist\, and 24-year music director/guitarist 
 for the legendary singer-songwriter John Prine.</p>\n<p>We hope you join f
 or this evening of heart opening music\, A Gathering of Spirits: Hope in H
 ard Times.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
