DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Double down with Claire Arbogast and Shana Ritter in the multim
 edia release of two remarkable novels.\nCoupled with powerful music and im
 ages\, hear Arbogast and Ritter read from novels that are centuries apart 
 but sisters in their resilient women standing firm in turbulent times.\nAr
 bogast’s “If Not the Whole Truth\,” called “historically rich with . . .se
 aring contemporary relevance” by Kirkus Reviews\, is releasing in bookstor
 es and on Amazon on September 10.\nRitter’s new edition of “In the Time of
  Leaving\,” called “A captivating meditation on home\, leaving\, and longi
 ng full of beautiful writing\,” by readers\, will be available on Amazon i
 n September.\nQ&A\, Burning Convictions open mic\, book signing.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240915T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240915T170000
LOCATION:Backspace Gallery\, inside Bonne Fête\, 112 West 6th Street\, on t
 he square in Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
