BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126027@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\; 812.323.3020\; boxoffice@buskirkchumley.o
 rg\; https://buskirkchumley.org/
DESCRIPTION:Presented by The Buskirk-Chumley Theater | DOOR TIME 6:30 pm\n
 \nSaving the planet\, one acre at a time…..\nCommon Ground is a hopeful an
 d uplifting story of the pioneers of the “Regenerative Movement” who produ
 ce tremendous quantities of nutritionally dense food and are working to ba
 lance the climate – all while bringing our entire ecosystem back to life.
 \nThe documentary film explores how Americans from different walks of life
 \, different political backgrounds\, and different parts of the country sh
 are one thing in common –the very soil beneath their feet. The film invest
 igates the power of “regenerative” farming systems –from large to small-sc
 ale farmers who are the champions of soil health as the key to unlocking m
 ore (and healthier) food to feed America and the world.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240917T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240917T210000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:BCT presents: Common Ground (2023)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bct-presents-common-ground-2023/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>\n<p class=
 'details_center'><strong>Presented by The Buskirk-Chumley Theater | DOOR T
 IME 6:30 pm</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p>Saving the planet\, one acre at a tim
 e…..</p>\n<p><a href='https://commongroundfilm.org/'>Common Ground</a> is 
 a hopeful and uplifting story of the pioneers of the “Regenerative Movemen
 t” who produce tremendous quantities of nutritionally dense food and are w
 orking to balance the climate – all while bringing our entire ecosystem ba
 ck to life.</p>\n<p>The documentary film explores how Americans from diffe
 rent walks of life\, different political backgrounds\, and different parts
  of the country share one thing in common –the very soil beneath their fee
 t. The film investigates the power of “regenerative” farming systems –from
  large to small-scale farmers who are the champions of soil health as the 
 key to unlocking more (and healthier) food to feed America and the world.<
 /p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126565@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.thebishopbar.com/events/sex-salon-27
DESCRIPTION:Bloomington Sex Salon #42 will include a conversation with Dr D
 r. Hannah Javidi\, a postdoctoral fellow at the Indiana University School 
 of Public Health. Dr. Javidi is an adolescent sexual health researcher and
  will be in conversation with us on the topic of “Teens\, Technology\, and
  Sexuality.”\nWhether you’re a parent\, grandparent\, teacher\, researcher
 \, youth-engaged professional\, or just someone who cares deeply about tee
 n sexual health and wellness\, you’ll find this to be an engaging event.\n
 If you’re new to the Bloomington Sex Salon\, here is how it works:\n\nArri
 ve early to grab a seat and a drink. We will start promptly at 7pm.\nFor t
 he first 30-40 minutes\, our host (local sex researcher/educator Dr. Debby
  Herbenick) will ask questions of Dr. Javidi about her career and adolesce
 nt sexuality and technology.\nFor the remaining 20-30 minutes\, Dr. Javidi
  will take questions from the audience.\n\nThe Bloomington Sex Salon is me
 ant to bridge campus-conversations about sexuality topics. It’s fun and ca
 sual – please join us and bring your friends!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240917T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240917T200000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Sex Salon (21+)\, hosted by Dr. Debby Herbenick
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-sex-salon-hosted-by-dr-debby-herbeni
 ck/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong><a hr
 ef='https://sexualhealth.indiana.edu/community/sexsalon.html'>Bloomington 
 Sex Salon</a> #42</strong> will include a conversation with Dr Dr. Hannah 
 Javidi\, a postdoctoral fellow at the Indiana University School of Public 
 Health. Dr. Javidi is an adolescent sexual health researcher and will be i
 n conversation with us on the topic of “Teens\, Technology\, and Sexuality
 .”</p>\n<p>Whether you’re a parent\, grandparent\, teacher\, researcher\, 
 youth-engaged professional\, or just someone who cares deeply about teen s
 exual health and wellness\, you’ll find this to be an engaging event.</p>
 \n<p>If you’re new to the Bloomington Sex Salon\, here is how it works:</p
 >\n<ol>\n<li>Arrive early to grab a seat and a drink. We will start prompt
 ly at 7pm.</li>\n<li>For the first 30-40 minutes\, our host (local sex res
 earcher/educator Dr. Debby Herbenick) will ask questions of Dr. Javidi abo
 ut her career and adolescent sexuality and technology.</li>\n<li>For the r
 emaining 20-30 minutes\, Dr. Javidi will take questions from the audience.
 </li>\n</ol>\n<p>The Bloomington Sex Salon is meant to bridge campus-conve
 rsations about sexuality topics. It’s fun and casual – please join us and 
 bring your friends!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
