DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Waldron Arts Center presents the OSOGBO: Art & Heritage Exh
 ibition\, a retrospective of Nigerian contemporary art from the world-reno
 wned Osogbo School of Art. The exhibition will feature a talk with Indiana
  University College Professor Emeritus of Folklore\, Henry Glassie\, on We
 dnesday\, September 18. The event will run from 5-8pm\, with the talk begi
 nning at 6pm. Glassie will speak about his relationship and work with Twin
 s Seven-Seven\, and his book Prince Twins Seven-Seven: His Art\, His Life 
 in Nigeria\, His Exile in America.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240918T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240918T200000
LOCATION:Rosemary P. Miller Gallery\, Waldron Arts Center\, 122 S Walnut St
 \, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:“OSOGBO: Art and Heritage Exhibition” Folklore Talk
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/osogbo-art-and-heritage-exhibition-folklore-talk
 /
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The Waldron A
 rts Center presents the OSOGBO: Art & Heritage Exhibition\, a retrospectiv
 e of Nigerian contemporary art from the world-renowned Osogbo School of Ar
 t. The exhibition will feature a talk with Indiana University College Prof
 essor Emeritus of Folklore\, Henry Glassie\, on Wednesday\, September 18. 
 The event will run from 5-8pm\, with the talk beginning at 6pm. Glassie wi
 ll speak about his relationship and work with Twins Seven-Seven\, and his 
 book Prince Twins Seven-Seven: His Art\, His Life in Nigeria\, His Exile i
 n America.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
