BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126825@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The theme for this year’s Fiesta is “Your Contributions Matter:
  Shaping the Future Together” or “Tus Contribuciones Importan: Formando el
  Futuro Juntos.” La Fiesta del Otoño offers educational and informative bo
 oths\, cultural activities from a variety of Spanish-speaking countries\, 
 and opportunities to interact with our community partners.\nDuring the eve
 nt\, attendees have the chance to experience traditional ethnic performanc
 es such as Flamenco dancer Sofia Crespo and Mariachi Internacional de Bloo
 mington\, listen to live regional music from nomás and the Vick Luna Quart
 et and purchase Latine food from our food trucks. The afternoon also featu
 res arts and crafts for children and a dance competition with several priz
 es.\nNational Hispanic Heritage Month\, which runs from September 15th thr
 ough October 15th\, is dedicated to celebrating the history\, culture\, an
 d contributions of Hispanics in the United States.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240921T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240921T160000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park - Pavilion\, 1601 S Rogers St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:La Fiesta del Otoño\, featuring performances by Flamenco dancer\, S
 ofia Crespo / Mariachi Internacional de Bloomington / nomás / Vick Luna Qu
 arte
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/la-fiesta-del-otono-2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The theme for
  this year’s Fiesta is “<strong>Your Contributions Matter: Shaping the Fut
 ure Together</strong>” or “<strong>Tus Contribuciones Importan: Formando e
 l Futuro Juntos.</strong>” La Fiesta del Otoño offers educational and info
 rmative booths\, cultural activities from a variety of Spanish-speaking co
 untries\, and opportunities to interact with our community partners.</p>\n
 <p>During the event\, attendees have the chance to experience traditional 
 ethnic performances such as <strong>Flamenco dancer Sofia Crespo</strong> 
 and <strong>Mariachi Internacional de Bloomington</strong>\, listen to liv
 e regional music from <strong>nomás</strong> and the <strong>Vick Luna Qua
 rtet</strong> and purchase Latine food from our food trucks. The afternoon
  also features arts and crafts for children and a dance competition with s
 everal prizes.</p>\n<p>National Hispanic Heritage Month\, which runs from 
 September 15th through October 15th\, is dedicated to celebrating the hist
 ory\, culture\, and contributions of Hispanics in the United States.</p>\n
 </BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
