BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-123098@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.thefar.org/events/event/81211/
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6:30pm\nHawktail is the instrumental acoustic group co
 mprised of fiddler Brittany Haas (Crooked Still\, Dave Rawlings Machine)\,
  bassist Paul Kowert (Punch Brothers\, Dave Rawlings Machine)\, and guitar
 ist Jordan Tice. Though at first glance Hawktail looks like a superpicker 
 side-project\, their all-original music is cohesive and unique\, distingui
 shing them as an ensemble with a sound built from the ground up. Flush wit
 h orchestral sweeps and sparse vigils\, with strains of the American South
  and the North Atlantic\, this cosmopolitan sound is not what you’d expect
  from a string band.\nVäsen hails from Uppsala\, Sweden and is a perennial
  favorite at the Lotus World Music Festival\, leading Bloomington to name 
 a street after the group and the band to name an album after the street: V
 äsen Street. Olov Johansson (nyckelharpa) and Mikael Marin (viola) will pe
 rform on this tour as a duo and together in collaboration with Hawktail fo
 r a set not to be missed.\nThe Hand Picked music series is a series of con
 certs located at the FAR Center for Contemporary Arts. Located in the Four
 th and Rogers neighborhood\, this historic building offers beautiful acous
 tics and a truly intimate experience seating up to 160. The 505 Theater at
  FAR has been carefully restored and designed with live performance in min
 d\, the large vaulted ceilings and 12-foot glass garage doors provide a ve
 nue unlike any other you will find in Bloomington.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240922T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240922T213000
LOCATION:FAR Center for the Performing Arts - 505 Theater\, 202 S Rogers St
 \, Bloomington (Fourth And Rogers)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Roots Foundation\, Inc. presents – Hand Picked: Hawktai
 l + Väsen
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-roots-foundation-inc-presents-hawkta
 il-and-vasen/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 6:30pm</strong><br />\n<strong>Hawktail</strong> is the instrumental a
 coustic group comprised of fiddler Brittany Haas (Crooked Still\, Dave Raw
 lings Machine)\, bassist Paul Kowert (Punch Brothers\, Dave Rawlings Machi
 ne)\, and guitarist Jordan Tice. Though at first glance Hawktail looks lik
 e a superpicker side-project\, their all-original music is cohesive and un
 ique\, distinguishing them as an ensemble with a sound built from the grou
 nd up. Flush with orchestral sweeps and sparse vigils\, with strains of th
 e American South and the North Atlantic\, this cosmopolitan sound is not w
 hat you’d expect from a string band.</p>\n<p><strong>Väsen</strong> hails 
 from Uppsala\, Sweden and is a perennial favorite at the Lotus World Music
  Festival\, leading Bloomington to name a street after the group and the b
 and to name an album after the street: Väsen Street. Olov Johansson (nycke
 lharpa) and Mikael Marin (viola) will perform on this tour as a duo and to
 gether in collaboration with Hawktail for a set not to be missed.</p>\n<p>
 The <strong>Hand Picked music series</strong> is a series of concerts loca
 ted at the FAR Center for Contemporary Arts. Located in the Fourth and Rog
 ers neighborhood\, this historic building offers beautiful acoustics and a
  truly intimate experience seating up to 160. The 505 Theater at FAR has b
 een carefully restored and designed with live performance in mind\, the la
 rge vaulted ceilings and 12-foot glass garage doors provide a venue unlike
  any other you will find in Bloomington.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
