DESCRIPTION:Eat cake. Drink tea. Talk about Death. The Death Café is a grou
 p-directed discussion of death with no agenda\, objectives\, or themes. It
  is a discussion group rather than grief support or counseling session. Bl
 oomington’s Death Café chapter is led by musician and hospice chaplain\, R
 ick Clayton\, and it meets monthly at Morgenstern Books.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240924T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240924T210000
