BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-125822@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Vanessa Cloe\, Director of Alumni Relations\; 812.855.8891\; vcloe@
 indiana.edu\; https://college.indiana.edu/alumni-giving/food-for-thought/i
 ndex.html
DESCRIPTION:This livestream will feature a presentation and Q&A with Distin
 guished Professor of Sociology Bernice Pescosolido\, who will discuss how 
 Indiana University has become a national trailblazer in addressing mental 
 health stigma\, a critical impediment to identifying and addressing mental
  health challenges. Following her presentation\, Professor Pescosolido wil
 l participate in a moderated Q&A session. \n\n\nThe College of Arts and Sc
 iences’ Food for Thought livestreaming series serves as an opportunity for
  alumni and friends to hear from faculty and fellow alumni\, explore topic
 s of interest\, and stay connected with IU and the College of Arts and Sci
 ences.\n\nAll past Food for Thought livestreams are available on the Colle
 ge’s YouTube channel.\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240924T190000
LOCATION:Zoom
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Students\, Scientists\, a Presidential Initiative and the Indianapo
 lis Colts: How a Unique Partnership Aims to End the Stigma of Mental Illne
 ss
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/students-scientists-a-presidential-initiative-an
 d-the-indianapolis-colts-how-a-unique-partnership-aims-to-end-the-stigma-o
 f-mental-illness/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='lw_cal_
 event_detail_intro' class='lw_cal_event_detail_block'>\n<p>This <span data
 -contrast='auto'><a href='https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_n7Po590VT
 We8eVy0htoYxg#/registration'><strong>livestream</strong></a> will feature 
 a presentation and Q&A with Distinguished Professor of Sociology Bernice P
 escosolido\, who will discuss how Indiana University has become a national
  trailblazer in addressing mental health stigma\, a critical impediment to
  identifying and addressing mental health challenges. Following her presen
 tation\, Professor Pescosolido will participate in a moderated Q&A session
 . </span></p>\n</div>\n<div id='lw_cal_event_detail_description' class='lw
 _cal_event_detail_block'>\n<p><span data-contrast='auto'>The College of Ar
 ts and Sciences’ <strong><a href='https://college.indiana.edu/alumni-givin
 g/food-for-thought/index.html'>Food for Thought</a></strong> livestreaming
  series serves as an opportunity for alumni and friends to hear from facul
 ty and fellow alumni\, explore topics of interest\, and stay connected wit
 h IU and the College of Arts and Sciences.<br />\n</span></p>\n<p>All past
  Food for Thought livestreams are available on <a class='external' href='h
 ttps://www.youtube.com/@iucollegeofartssciences6084/playlists'>the College
 ’s YouTube channel.</a></p>\n<p><span data-contrast='auto'> </span></p>\n<
 /div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
