BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126080@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Marcia Veldman\, Green Drinks Bloomington\; 812.325.2446\; marciave
 ldman@gmail.com\; www.greendrinks.org
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Ellen Ketterson\, Distinguished Professor of Biology at Ind
 iana University\, will present a talk entitled\, “3 Billion Missing Birds”
 . Ketterson will share her deep concern about the decline in biodiversity 
 that is happening all around us\, but can be hard to notice until\, she fe
 ars\, it will be too late to turn things around. She will present the dire
  situation with birds in America\, and some of the research done on a bird
  in decline that also shows signs of adapting. From there Ketterson will t
 urn to things that are happening at Indiana University to try and address 
 the issue.\nGreen Drinks Bloomington is a lively\, informal social network
 ing event for people from all walks of life who are interested in making a
  greener world. We gather monthly to share libations and dialogue\, explor
 e ideas and make new friends and business connections. Events are held the
  4th Wednesday of the month through October from 5:30 – 7:30 pm at the Upl
 and Brewing Company’s Wood Shop venue.\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240925T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240925T193000
LOCATION:Upland Brewing Wood Shop\, 354 W 11th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Green Drinks Bloomington presents: Dr. Ellen Ketterson\, “3 Billion
  Missing Birds”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/green-drinks-sep2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Dr. E
 llen Ketterson\, Distinguished Professor of Biology at Indiana University<
 /strong>\, will present a talk entitled\, “3 Billion Missing Birds”. Kette
 rson will share her deep concern about the decline in biodiversity that is
  happening all around us\, but can be hard to notice until\, she fears\, i
 t will be too late to turn things around. She will present the dire situat
 ion with birds in America\, and some of the research done on a bird in dec
 line that also shows signs of adapting. From there Ketterson will turn to 
 things that are happening at Indiana University to try and address the iss
 ue.</p>\n<p>Green Drinks Bloomington is a lively\, informal social network
 ing event for people from all walks of life who are interested in making a
  greener world. We gather monthly to share libations and dialogue\, explor
 e ideas and make new friends and business connections. Events are held the
  4th Wednesday of the month through October from 5:30 – 7:30 pm at the Upl
 and Brewing Company’s Wood Shop venue.</p>\n<p> </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
