BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126041@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Martina Celerin is the Arts Alliance of Greater Bloomington fea
 tured artist for the month of October. This is an amazing opportunity to v
 iew her talented work and connect with her and fellow patrons of the arts 
 in our community.\nMartina’s description of her work: “In the past I focus
 ed on oil pastels and acrylic painting. Independently\, experimentation wi
 th each of these has been useful for my current medium of choice\, fiber. 
 Work with oil pastels forced me to focus on visual mixing of color\, and t
 he powerful interplay of colors when they are applied proximally compared 
 to when they are physically distant. Acrylic painting allowed for quick mi
 xing of colors both before and after applying it to the canvas\, but\, as 
 with oil pastels\, I became dissatisfied with the flatness of the art. I b
 egan gluing found objects onto the canvas and then painting over them. Thi
 s was better\, but still not enough. Eventually I realized that I needed t
 o create my canvas. Weaving allows me to incorporate objects\, textures an
 d shapes\, as well as colors and coarsenesses into the canvas. By combinin
 g this with needle felting\, I have been able to push the dimensional limi
 ts of wall art and to create weaving-felting fusions that are 3D tapestrie
 s.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240928T180000
LOCATION:Arts Alliance Center\, 2894 E 3rd St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Open Reception: Martina Celerin “On the Cusp of Autumn”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/open-reception-martina-celerin-on-the-cusp-of-au
 tumn/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Martina Celer
 in is the Arts Alliance of Greater Bloomington featured artist for the mon
 th of October. This is an amazing opportunity to view her talented work an
 d connect with her and fellow patrons of the arts in our community.</p>\n<
 p>Martina’s description of her work: “In the past I focused on oil pastels
  and acrylic painting. Independently\, experimentation with each of these 
 has been useful for my current medium of choice\, fiber. Work with oil pas
 tels forced me to focus on visual mixing of color\, and the powerful inter
 play of colors when they are applied proximally compared to when they are 
 physically distant. Acrylic painting allowed for quick mixing of colors bo
 th before and after applying it to the canvas\, but\, as with oil pastels\
 , I became dissatisfied with the flatness of the art. I began gluing found
  objects onto the canvas and then painting over them. This was better\, bu
 t still not enough. Eventually I realized that I needed to create my canva
 s. Weaving allows me to incorporate objects\, textures and shapes\, as wel
 l as colors and coarsenesses into the canvas. By combining this with needl
 e felting\, I have been able to push the dimensional limits of wall art an
 d to create weaving-felting fusions that are 3D tapestries.”</p>\n</BODY><
 /HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
