BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126262@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Alain Barker\, Sibling Cities Bloomington program director\; abarke
 r@iu.edu
DESCRIPTION:UPDATE: Please note that this event will be held online only. W
 e’ve decided to shift from the in-person hybrid meeting format to make thi
 s conversation available to as many people as possible.\n\nListen to Dr. S
 cott Shackelford\, Professor of Business Law and Ethics\, Indiana Universi
 ty\, and Affiliated Scholar at Stanford\, on how the national voter access
  landscape has changed since the last Presidential election.\nLearn from L
 eague of Women Voters’ representatives Rachel Kellerman (Palo Alto) and Dr
 . Debora (Ralf) Jane Shaw (Bloomington)\, along with Mark Fraley\, of the 
 IU Political and Civic Engagement (PACE) program about voter access & turn
 out data and efforts to increase them.\nEngage in meaningful\, facilitated
  dialog and share your views in a safe and respectful setting.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240929T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240929T173000
LOCATION:https://bit.ly/3TvSVsA
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Town Hall: Democracy – Voter Access and Turnout
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/town-hall-democracy-voter-access-and-turnout/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>UPDAT
 E: Please note that this event will be held online only. We’ve decided to 
 shift from the in-person hybrid meeting format to make this conversation a
 vailable to as many people as possible.</strong></p>\n<ul style='font-weig
 ht: 400'>\n<li>Listen to <strong>Dr. Scott Shackelford</strong>\, Professo
 r of Business Law and Ethics\, Indiana University\, and Affiliated Scholar
  at Stanford\, on how the national voter access landscape has changed sinc
 e the last Presidential election.</li>\n<li>Learn from <strong>League of W
 omen Voters</strong>’ representatives Rachel Kellerman (Palo Alto) and Dr.
  Debora (Ralf) Jane Shaw (Bloomington)\, along with Mark Fraley\, of the I
 U <strong>Political and Civic Engagement </strong>(PACE) program about vot
 er access & turnout data and efforts to increase them.</li>\n<li>Engage in
  meaningful\, facilitated dialog and share your views in a safe and respec
 tful setting.</li>\n</ul>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
