UID:ai1ec-125833@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812.336.6599\; media@lotusfest.org\; https://www.lotusfest.org/
DESCRIPTION:Doors open at 4:30 pm\nBread and Puppet Theater is a politicall
 y radical puppet theater company founded in 1963 by Peter Schumann on New 
 York City’s Lower East Side. In 1974 Bread and Puppet moved to a farm in G
 lover in the Northeast Kingdom of Vermont\, where it has made a home. The 
 puppets are larger than life\, and each show’s content reflects themes fro
 m present-day political news.\nArrive early and bring a picnic dinner and 
 blankets (lawn chairs will be allowed for the back rows). RSVP to ensure c
 ommunication about rain location. Bread and Puppet requests that you bring
  a cash donation to the show. All are welcome. No one will be turned away 
 due to lack of funds.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241001T174500
LOCATION:Loesch Farm\, 2687 N Loesch Rd\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:‘Bread and Puppet Theater’ Presented by Lotus
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bread-and-puppet-presented-by-lotus/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  open at 4:30 pm</strong></p>\n<p><a href='https://breadandpuppet.org/'><s
 trong>Bread and Puppet Theater</strong></a> is a politically radical puppe
 t theater company founded in 1963 by Peter Schumann on New York City’s Low
 er East Side. In 1974 Bread and Puppet moved to a farm in Glover in the No
 rtheast Kingdom of Vermont\, where it has made a home. The puppets are lar
 ger than life\, and each show’s content reflects themes from present-day p
 olitical news.</p>\n<p>Arrive early and bring a picnic dinner and blankets
  (lawn chairs will be allowed for the back rows). <strong><a href='https:/
 /www.lotusfest.org/event/bread-and-puppet-presented-by-lotus/'>RSVP</a> to
  ensure communication about rain location.</strong> Bread and Puppet reque
 sts that you bring a <strong>cash</strong> donation to the show. All are w
 elcome. No one will be turned away due to lack of funds.</p>\n</BODY></HTM
 L>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126084@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Amy Kendall\, Beacon Development Director\; amykendall@beaconinc.or
 g\; https://beaconinc.org/
DESCRIPTION:Park at 1201 W 3rd St between 6 and 6:30 pm and catch a shuttle
  to the Walk check-in and starting location at Loren Wood Design Build\, 9
 00 S Walnut St\, Bloomington. The event will conclude at 9pm at 1201 W. 3r
 d Street\, Bloomington.\n\nTo kick off the Light the Way capital campaign\
 , supporters of Beacon Inc. will walk from Loren Wood Design Build (near t
 he current Shalom Center) to the future home of Beacon Inc. at 1201 W. 3rd
  Street. The approximately 50-minute/1.5 mile walk will venture up Walnut 
 Street\, past the Shalom Center\, to the courthouse square\, and then on t
 o the new location while enjoying some live music along the way. The new f
 acility will bring together Beacon’s programs of temporary shelter\, resou
 rce center\, and housing\, with a special emphasis on community partnershi
 ps and improving the quality of care available to people experiencing extr
 eme poverty in our community.\n\nFollowing the walk\, we will celebrate at
  the new location with music\, refreshments\, and brief remarks. Shuttle s
 ervice and parking will be available between Loren Wood Builders (LWB) and
  the new location but please note parking is more limited near LWB.\n\nTho
 se who are unable to participate in the walk are encouraged to attend the 
 celebration at the new location\, starting at 7:45pm.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241001T210000
LOCATION:The future home of Beacon Inc.\, 1201 W 3rd St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Beacon’s “Light the Way” Procession & Celebration
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/beacon-light-the-way-procession-celebration/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div dir='ltr'>
 \n<div id='m_-8996343539128321169gmail-x_mail-editor-reference-message-con
 tainer'>Park at 1201 W 3<sup>rd</sup> St between 6 and 6:30 pm and catch a
  shuttle to the Walk check-in and starting location at Loren Wood Design B
 uild\, 900 S Walnut St\, Bloomington. The event will conclude at 9pm at 12
 01 W. 3rd Street\, Bloomington.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>To kick off the <
 strong>Light the Way</strong> capital campaign\, supporters of Beacon Inc.
  will walk from Loren Wood Design Build (near the current Shalom Center) t
 o the future home of Beacon Inc. at 1201 W. 3rd Street. The approximately 
 50-minute/1.5 mile walk will venture up Walnut Street\, past the Shalom Ce
 nter\, to the courthouse square\, and then on to the new location while en
 joying some live music along the way. The new facility will bring together
  Beacon’s programs of temporary shelter\, resource center\, and housing\, 
 with a special emphasis on community partnerships and improving the qualit
 y of care available to people experiencing extreme poverty in our communit
 y.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Following the walk\, we will celebrate at the 
 new location with music\, refreshments\, and brief remarks. Shuttle servic
 e and parking will be available between Loren Wood Builders (LWB) and the 
 new location but please note parking is more limited near LWB.</div>\n<div
 ></div>\n<div>Those who are unable to participate in the walk are encourag
 ed to attend the celebration at the new location\, starting at 7:45pm.</di
 v>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
