BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126751@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Thursdays in October\nThis month in Discovery Time we are going
  to explore the natural world! Many studies show that early environmental 
 education benefits children’s emotional\, social\, cognitive\, and physica
 l development. Through a blend of hands-on activities\, engaging experimen
 ts\, and captivating storytelling\, children embark on a journey to discov
 er the wonders of the natural world around them. The program curriculum is
  carefully crafted to align with early childhood development principles wh
 ile instilling key concepts of environmental science. Tailored for childre
 n aged 3 to 6\, this program ignites curiosity\, fosters a love for nature
 \, and cultivates a sense of responsibility towards the environment.\nHand
 s-on activities include:\n\nSinging songs about recycling and conservation
 \nTaking a guided nature walk through the WonderGarden\nParticipating in a
 n experiment that demonstrates the concept of water filtration
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241003T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241003T173000
LOCATION:WonderLab\, 308 W 4th St\, Bloomington
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20241031T235959Z;BYDAY=TH;WKST=MO
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Discovery Time – Environmental Science (ages 3-6)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/discovery-time-environmental-science/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><b>Thursdays 
 in October</b></p>\n<p>This month in Discovery Time we are going to explor
 e the natural world! Many studies show that early environmental education 
 benefits children’s emotional\, social\, cognitive\, and physical developm
 ent. Through a blend of hands-on activities\, engaging experiments\, and c
 aptivating storytelling\, children embark on a journey to discover the won
 ders of the natural world around them. The program curriculum is carefully
  crafted to align with early childhood development principles while instil
 ling key concepts of environmental science. Tailored for children aged 3 t
 o 6\, this program ignites curiosity\, fosters a love for nature\, and cul
 tivates a sense of responsibility towards the environment.</p>\n<p><b>Hand
 s-on activities include:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Singing songs about recycling 
 and conservation</li>\n<li>Taking a guided nature walk through the WonderG
 arden</li>\n<li>Participating in an experiment that demonstrates the conce
 pt of water filtration</li>\n</ul>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
