BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126467@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.comedyattic.com/events/100255
DESCRIPTION:Door Time: 9:00 PM\nOver the past several months\, Bobcat Goldt
 hwait has been on the creative fast track. As one of the most recognizable
  comedians in show business\, Goldthwait unleashed his one of a kind brand
  of comedy in his new Showtime one hour special entitled “You Don’t Look t
 he Same Either.”\nSince his first appearance on David Letterman at the age
  of 20\, Bobcat has expanded his resume\, directing movies and sharing his
  behind the camera talents on shows such as\; “Jimmy Kimmel Live\,” “The D
 emetri Martin show\,” “The Chappelle Show\,” “The Man Show\,” and “Crank Y
 ankers.” Best known for his unforgettable movies that were huge in the 80’
 s\, Bobcat has also starred in several HBO specials and a slew of televisi
 on appearances to numerous to mention. Bob continues to push the envelope 
 with his unique brand of humor headlining major comedy clubs across the co
 untry.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241004T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241004T231500
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, upstairs at 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington (4th 
 and Walnut)
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;UNTIL=20241005T235959Z
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Legendary Bobcat Goldthwait Returns to The Comedy Attic!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-legendary-bobcat-goldthwait-returns-to-the-c
 omedy-attic-lateshow/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Door 
 Time: 9:00 PM</strong><br />\nOver the past several months\, Bobcat Goldth
 wait has been on the creative fast track. As one of the most recognizable 
 comedians in show business\, Goldthwait unleashed his one of a kind brand 
 of comedy in his new Showtime one hour special entitled “You Don’t Look th
 e Same Either.”</p>\n<p>Since his first appearance on David Letterman at t
 he age of 20\, Bobcat has expanded his resume\, directing movies and shari
 ng his behind the camera talents on shows such as\; “Jimmy Kimmel Live\,” 
 “The Demetri Martin show\,” “The Chappelle Show\,” “The Man Show\,” and “C
 rank Yankers.” Best known for his unforgettable movies that were huge in t
 he 80’s\, Bobcat has also starred in several HBO specials and a slew of te
 levision appearances to numerous to mention. Bob continues to push the env
 elope with his unique brand of humor headlining major comedy clubs across 
 the country.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
