UID:ai1ec-127178@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://bloomington.in.gov/parks/events/trick-or-treat-trail
DESCRIPTION:Dress up the family in your favorite costumes and play themed g
 ames and win prizes while waiting for your turn to tour the trail of our f
 avorite childhood storybook characters\, played by the theater students at
  Bloomington High School North. We’re looking forward to it!\nThe paved tr
 ail through the woods comes to life with your child’s favorite movie\, sto
 rybook\, and fairy-tale characters!\nParticipate in games and strike a pos
 e at a photo booth while you wait to go on the trail.\nDue to the populari
 ty of this event there may be a wait to enter the trail. We appreciate you
 r patience!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241005T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241005T160000
LOCATION:RCA Community Park\, 1400 W RCA Park Dr\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Trick or Treat Trail
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/trick-or-treat-trail-4/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Dress up the 
 family in your favorite costumes and play themed games and win prizes whil
 e waiting for your turn to tour the trail of our favorite childhood storyb
 ook characters\, played by the theater students at Bloomington High School
  North. We’re looking forward to it!</p>\n<p>The paved trail through the w
 oods comes to life with your child’s favorite movie\, storybook\, and fair
 y-tale characters!<br />\nParticipate in games and strike a pose at a phot
 o booth while you wait to go on the trail.<br />\nDue to the popularity of
  this event there may be a wait to enter the trail. We appreciate your pat
 ience!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126755@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://wonderlab.org/events/category/stem-saturday/
DESCRIPTION:The program is typically located in Lab A\, but may also be in 
 the garden if the weather is nice.\nSTEM Saturday is a weekly program that
  gets visitors to engage in STEM. STEM (Science\, Technology\, Engineering
 \, and Mathematics) Saturdays are designed to provide engaging hands-on ST
 EM activities aimed at inspiring interest in STEM subjects and to make lea
 rning both hands-on and fun. STEM Saturday is meant for ages 5 and up. Eac
 h week the Education Team and volunteers develop different hands-on activi
 ties meant for the entire family. STEM Saturday is designed for ages 5-17\
 , but we encourage adults and children to work together so that they can l
 earn together! STEM Saturday is partially sponsored by Cook Medical and CF
 C Properties.\nKey features of STEM Saturdays include:\n\nA variety of han
 ds-on activities that encourage exploration of STEM concepts.\nAge-appropr
 iate Curriculum: STEM Saturday content is tailored to different age groups
 \, ensuring that the activities are suitable for a wide range of developme
 ntal levels.\nExpert Guidance: WonderLab Educators and Volunteers lead the
 se sessions. They guide and answer questions helping guests gain a deeper 
 understanding of the concepts.\nCollaborative Learning: STEM Saturdays enc
 ourages collaboration among participants\, fostering teamwork and communic
 ation.\nParent Involvement: Parents and caregivers are encouraged to parti
 cipate\, creating an experience for everyone in your group to take part in
 .
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241005T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241005T160000
LOCATION:WonderLab\, 308 W 4th St\, Bloomington (Lab A and/or garden)
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20241031T235959Z;BYDAY=TH,SA;WKST=MO
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:STEM Saturday – Science of the World
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/stem-saturday-science-of-the-world/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><b>The progra
 m is typically located in Lab A\, but may also be in the garden if the wea
 ther is nice.</b></p>\n<p>STEM Saturday is a weekly program that gets visi
 tors to engage in STEM. STEM (Science\, Technology\, Engineering\, and Mat
 hematics) Saturdays are designed to provide engaging hands-on STEM activit
 ies aimed at inspiring interest in STEM subjects and to make learning both
  hands-on and fun. STEM Saturday is meant for ages 5 and up. Each week the
  Education Team and volunteers develop different hands-on activities meant
  for the entire family. <strong>STEM Saturday is designed for ages 5-17\, 
 but we encourage adults and children to work together so that they can lea
 rn together!</strong> STEM Saturday is partially sponsored by Cook Medical
  and CFC Properties.</p>\n<p><b>Key features of STEM Saturdays include:</b
 ></p>\n<ul>\n<li>A variety of hands-on activities that encourage explorati
 on of STEM concepts.</li>\n<li>Age-appropriate Curriculum: STEM Saturday c
 ontent is tailored to different age groups\, ensuring that the activities 
 are suitable for a wide range of developmental levels.</li>\n<li>Expert Gu
 idance: WonderLab Educators and Volunteers lead these sessions. They guide
  and answer questions helping guests gain a deeper understanding of the co
 ncepts.</li>\n<li>Collaborative Learning: STEM Saturdays encourages collab
 oration among participants\, fostering teamwork and communication.</li>\n<
 li>Parent Involvement: Parents and caregivers are encouraged to participat
 e\, creating an experience for everyone in your group to take part in.</li
 >\n</ul>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
