UID:ai1ec-127479@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening of music and storytelling to support com
 munities in Western North Carolina and East Tennessee affected by the rece
 nt disasters of Hurricane Helene. Enjoy performances from artists and tale
 s from the mountains as we show our support for those still dealing with t
 he wake of devastation and mourn those who have passed. All donations will
  directly support non-profit projects and programs dedicated to recovery e
 fforts in the region. Bring your friends and family for a night in the hol
 ler away from the hills.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241007T183000
LOCATION:Runcible Spoon\, 412 E 6th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Runcible Spoon fundraiser for Hurricane Helene
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/runcible-spoon-fundraiser-for-hurricane-helene/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us for a
 n evening of music and storytelling to support communities in Western Nort
 h Carolina and East Tennessee affected by the recent disasters of Hurrican
 e Helene. Enjoy performances from artists and tales from the mountains as 
 we show our support for those still dealing with the wake of devastation a
 nd mourn those who have passed. All donations will directly support non-pr
 ofit projects and programs dedicated to recovery efforts in the region. Br
 ing your friends and family for a night in the holler away from the hills.
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126989@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://diversity.iu.edu/news-events/news/2024/iu-presents-byron-pe
 rkins.html.
DESCRIPTION:In honor of LGBTQ+ History Month\nNalini Krishnan\, President o
 f the Queer Student Union\, will have a fireside chat with Byron followed 
 by a Q&A session.\nByron is a former collegiate football player\, with pro
 fessional athlete impact and engagement. A man of God\, Byron is determine
 d to use his platform to amplify good will throughout the world. Last year
 \, Byron came out to the world and inspired millions. Byron recently appea
 red in front of millions on the Tamron Hall show\, which garnered him thou
 sands of responses of people lauding his courage. That same courage led to
  him being honored last year by the Better Brothers of LA\, Truth Awards\,
  where he received the Courage Award. An event that featured the likes of 
 Sheryl Lee Ralph\, Raven Simone\, Judge Greg Mathis\, Jason Lee and more. 
 As Byron grows forward\, he is determined not to let his orientation defin
 e him\, as he leans into his other passions and purpose. Whether it’s acti
 ng\, comedy\, music or public speaking\, Byron is poised to elevate the co
 nversations that are near and dear to him.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241007T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241007T203000
LOCATION:Indiana University - Ballantine Hall - Room 013\, 1020 E Kirkwood 
 Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:LGBTQ+ Culture Center’s Speaking of Excellence hosts\, A Conversati
 on with Byron Perkins.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/lgbtq-culture-centers-speaking-of-excellence-hos
 ts-a-conversation-with-byron-perkins/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>In honor of L
 GBTQ+ History Month<br />\nNalini Krishnan\, President of the Queer Studen
 t Union\, will have a fireside chat with Byron followed by a Q&A session.<
 /p>\n<p>Byron is a former collegiate football player\, with professional a
 thlete impact and engagement. A man of God\, Byron is determined to use hi
 s platform to amplify good will throughout the world. Last year\, Byron ca
 me out to the world and inspired millions. Byron recently appeared in fron
 t of millions on the Tamron Hall show\, which garnered him thousands of re
 sponses of people lauding his courage. That same courage led to him being 
 honored last year by the Better Brothers of LA\, Truth Awards\, where he r
 eceived the Courage Award. An event that featured the likes of Sheryl Lee 
 Ralph\, Raven Simone\, Judge Greg Mathis\, Jason Lee and more. As Byron gr
 ows forward\, he is determined not to let his orientation define him\, as 
 he leans into his other passions and purpose. Whether it’s acting\, comedy
 \, music or public speaking\, Byron is poised to elevate the conversations
  that are near and dear to him.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
