BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126078@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:http://www.amethysthouse.org/concert-2024.html
DESCRIPTION:Support from Hannah Frances | DOOR TIME 6:30 pm\nDon’t miss a s
 pecial solo set from Hiss Golden Messenger\, performing the 2010 record “B
 ad Debt” in its entirety\, along with other favorites. Coming to Buskirk C
 humley Theater on October 9th. Tickets on sale now.\nIn 2010\, M.C. Taylor
 —leader\, songwriter and singer of Hiss GoldenMessenger—sat down at his ki
 tchen table and started writing and recording the songs that would eventua
 lly become his beloved album Bad Debt. At the time\, the songwriter was li
 ving in a drafty cedar cabin in the woods outside of Pittsboro\, North Car
 olina with his wife and three-month old son Elijah\, having recently moved
  across the country from California. Taylor was\, for all intents and purp
 oses\, out of the music game.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241009T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241009T220000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Amethyst House presents: Hiss Golden Messenger Solo Plays “Bad Debt
 ” and Other Favorites
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/amethyst-house-presents-hiss-golden-messenger-so
 lo-plays-bad-debt-and-other-favorites/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p class='previe
 w-modal'><span style='text-decoration: underline'>Support from Hannah Fran
 ces | DOOR TIME 6:30 pm</span></p>\n<p><strong>Don’t miss a special solo s
 et from Hiss Golden Messenger\, performing the 2010 record “Bad Debt” in i
 ts entirety\, along with other favorites. Coming to Buskirk Chumley Theate
 r on October 9th. Tickets on sale now.</strong></p>\n<p>In 2010\, <strong>
 M.C. Taylor</strong>—leader\, songwriter and singer of Hiss GoldenMessenge
 r—sat down at his kitchen table and started writing and recording the song
 s that would eventually become his beloved album <em>Bad Debt.</em> At the
  time\, the songwriter was living in a drafty cedar cabin in the woods out
 side of Pittsboro\, North Carolina with his wife and three-month old son E
 lijah\, having recently moved across the country from California. Taylor w
 as\, for all intents and purposes\, out of the music game.</p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
END:VEVENT
