BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126323@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This event is sold out and the wait list is closed.\nEver dream
  of all your favorite Bloomington bands reuniting\, and reliving a weekend
  that could have happened somewhere in the 90’s? Well\, we have and are ma
 king it happen!\nTo celebrate Musical Family Tree’s 20 anniversary\, and t
 he Japonize Elephants 30th anniversary\, we’ve teamed up to have a big ol 
 90’s throw down. This is your chance to call up your old college or townie
  buddies\, and party like it’s 1999.\nCurrently 14 bands/acts are confirme
 d:\n(lineup subject to change and specific schedule to be released closer 
 to event date):\n– United States Three\n– Japonize Elephants (celebrating 
 their 30th anniversary!)\n– Stranded at the Drive In\n– Tribute to Lon Pau
 l Ellrich\n– Cadmium Orange\n– John P Strohm and friends\n– El Nino\n– Ars
 on Garden\n– Uvula\n– Shine\n– The Academy\n– Speed Luxury\n– Intro To Air
 lift\n– Neenah Foundry\nMusical Family Tree has been preserving and promot
 ing Indiana music since 2004.\nThe MFT archive was started in 2004 when re
 cordings from the 1990s were digitized and shared via the MFT website. The
 se 90s bands got MFT started and many of them are going to reunite to cele
 brate all times we had in the 90s and MFT’s 20 years of archiving and pres
 erving original Indiana music.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241011T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241011T235900
LOCATION:Blockhouse Bar + Backdoor\, 205 S College Ave\, Bloomington
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;UNTIL=20241012T235959Z
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:MFT 90’s Fest: Bloomington’s Musical Family Reunion shows [SOLD OUT
 ]
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mft-90s-fest/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>This 
 event is sold out and the wait list is closed.</strong></p>\n<p>Ever dream
  of all your favorite Bloomington bands reuniting\, and reliving a weekend
  that could have happened somewhere in the 90’s? Well\, we have and are ma
 king it happen!<br />\nTo celebrate <a href='https://www.musicalfamilytree
 .org/'>Musical Family Tree</a>’s 20 anniversary\, and the Japonize Elephan
 ts 30th anniversary\, we’ve teamed up to have a big ol 90’s throw down. Th
 is is your chance to call up your old college or townie buddies\, and part
 y like it’s 1999.</p>\n<p><b>Currently 14 bands/acts are confirmed:</b><br
  />\n(lineup subject to change and specific schedule to be released closer
  to event date):<br />\n– United States Three<br />\n– Japonize Elephants 
 (celebrating their 30th anniversary!)<br />\n– Stranded at the Drive In<br
  />\n– Tribute to Lon Paul Ellrich<br />\n– Cadmium Orange<br />\n– John P
  Strohm and friends<br />\n– El Nino<br />\n– Arson Garden<br />\n– Uvula<
 br />\n– Shine<br />\n– The Academy<br />\n– Speed Luxury<br />\n– Intro T
 o Airlift<br />\n– Neenah Foundry</p>\n<p>Musical Family Tree has been pre
 serving and promoting Indiana music since 2004.</p>\n<p>The MFT archive wa
 s started in 2004 when recordings from the 1990s were digitized and shared
  via the MFT website. These 90s bands got MFT started and many of them are
  going to reunite to celebrate all times we had in the 90s and MFT’s 20 ye
 ars of archiving and preserving original Indiana music.</p>\n</BODY></HTML
 >
END:VEVENT
