BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126726@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:http://www.thebishopbar.com/events/maeve-quinn-matriarch
DESCRIPTION:Ages 21+\nDescribed as “anything but ordinary” by the Chicago T
 ribune\, MAEVE & QUINN is the duo of Alaskan twin sisters Maris and Bryce 
 O’Tierney\, multi-instrumentalists\, songwriters\, and composers. Maeve & 
 Quinn’s music fuses alt rock\, pop\, and folk influences\, distinguished b
 y lyrical vocal harmonies and dynamic instrumental interplay. Classically 
 trained (voice\, guitar\, violin\, piano)\, the duo also draws on improvis
 ation in their practice.\nMaeve & Quinn’s collaboration as twin sisters is
  conversational and fluid between past and present. They bring together ly
 rics and melodies from their respective experiences for songs of layered p
 erspective\, addressing themes of memory\, truth\, and relationship. Maeve
  & Quinn’s music has a feeling of landscape\, and draws from multiple poin
 ts of origin: where the sisters grew up (Alaska)\, their country of herita
 ge (Ireland)\, and present home (Chicago).\nMaeve & Quinn have performed t
 heir music and poetry in concert with the Museum of Contemporary Art Chica
 go and the Poetry Foundation\; premiered their symphonic compositions with
  the Chicago Composers Orchestra and Anchorage Symphony Orchestra\; and co
 llaborated with dancers for film works\, most recently with Alvin Ailey Am
 erican Dance Theater.\nFollowing their 2018 release something overheard\, 
 something overhead\, their EP star-crossed (August 2021) was featured on B
 andcamp’s ‘New & Notable’ releases. Their first full-length LP\, Another D
 oor\, released September 2023.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241012T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241012T233000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Maeve & Quinn // The Matriarch / Claire Pendreigh
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/maeve-quinn-the-matriarch-claire-pendreigh/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Ages 
 21+</strong><br />\nDescribed as “anything but ordinary” by the Chicago Tr
 ibune\, <a href='https://maeveandquinn.com/'>MAEVE & QUINN</a> is the duo 
 of Alaskan twin sisters Maris and Bryce O’Tierney\, multi-instrumentalists
 \, songwriters\, and composers. Maeve & Quinn’s music fuses alt rock\, pop
 \, and folk influences\, distinguished by lyrical vocal harmonies and dyna
 mic instrumental interplay. Classically trained (voice\, guitar\, violin\,
  piano)\, the duo also draws on improvisation in their practice.</p>\n<p>M
 aeve & Quinn’s collaboration as twin sisters is conversational and fluid b
 etween past and present. They bring together lyrics and melodies from thei
 r respective experiences for songs of layered perspective\, addressing the
 mes of memory\, truth\, and relationship. Maeve & Quinn’s music has a feel
 ing of landscape\, and draws from multiple points of origin: where the sis
 ters grew up (Alaska)\, their country of heritage (Ireland)\, and present 
 home (Chicago).</p>\n<p>Maeve & Quinn have performed their music and poetr
 y in concert with the Museum of Contemporary Art Chicago and the Poetry Fo
 undation\; premiered their symphonic compositions with the Chicago Compose
 rs Orchestra and Anchorage Symphony Orchestra\; and collaborated with danc
 ers for film works\, most recently with Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater
 .</p>\n<p>Following their 2018 release something overheard\, something ove
 rhead\, their EP star-crossed (August 2021) was featured on Bandcamp’s ‘Ne
 w & Notable’ releases. Their first full-length LP\, Another Door\, release
 d September 2023.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
