BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126829@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://sites.google.com/site/mcbnaacp/announcements/70-years-post-
 brown-looking-to-the-past-transforming-the-future
DESCRIPTION:We are excited to announce an upcoming event\, 70 Years Post-Br
 own: Looking to the Past\, Transforming the Future\, in commemoration of t
 he 70th anniversary of the landmark Supreme Court decision\, Brown v. Boar
 d of Education. On October 13th\, the Monroe County NAACP invites you to j
 oin us for an afternoon of engaging\, action-oriented dialogue focused on 
 improving the educational experiences of youth in our local community.\nTh
 is event aims to move beyond simply honoring this historic moment and towa
 rd a renewed commitment to equitable\, quality education for all youth. To
 gether\, we will explore how we can continue to work toward the vision of 
 equal opportunity in education for all.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241013T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241013T170000
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library\, 303 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:70 Years Post-Brown: Looking to the Past\, Transforming the Future
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/70-years-post-brown-looking-to-the-past-transfor
 ming-the-future/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>We are excite
 d to announce an upcoming event\, 70 Years Post-Brown: Looking to the Past
 \, Transforming the Future\, in commemoration of the 70th anniversary of t
 he landmark Supreme Court decision\, Brown v. Board of Education. On Octob
 er 13th\, the <strong>Monroe County NAACP</strong> invites you to join us 
 for an afternoon of engaging\, action-oriented dialogue focused on improvi
 ng the educational experiences of youth in our local community.</p>\n<p>Th
 is event aims to move beyond simply honoring this historic moment and towa
 rd a renewed commitment to equitable\, quality education for all youth. To
 gether\, we will explore how we can continue to work toward the vision of 
 equal opportunity in education for all.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126579@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:DOOR TIME 3:30 pm\n“Cruces de Caminos/Intersections: Celebratin
 g Movements of the Diaspora” tells stories of migration and lived experien
 ces from Latinx and African diasporic perspectives. The concert will inclu
 de an opening performance by the Indiana University African American Dance
  Company directed by Baba Stafford C Berry Jr.\, followed by a full-length
  performance by Indianapolis-based Seda Negra/Black Silk Dance Company dir
 ected by Iris Rosa. Through a fusion of contemporary and traditional dance
  forms\, poetry\, and music\, the concert presents a creative and innovati
 ve relationship between Latinx and Black diasporic dance\, spirituality\, 
 and culture. The event will also include a post-performance dialogue with 
 audiences and performers.\nThere will be a post-show conversation and Q&A.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241013T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241013T173000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Seda Negra/Black Silk Dance Company presents: Cruces de Caminos/Int
 ersections
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/seda-negra-black-silk-dance-company-presents-cru
 ces-de-caminos-intersections/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>DOOR 
 TIME 3:30 pm</strong><br />\n“Cruces de Caminos/Intersections: Celebrating
  Movements of the Diaspora” tells stories of migration and lived experienc
 es from Latinx and African diasporic perspectives. The concert will includ
 e an opening performance by the Indiana University African American Dance 
 Company directed by Baba Stafford C Berry Jr.\, followed by a full-length 
 performance by Indianapolis-based Seda Negra/Black Silk Dance Company dire
 cted by Iris Rosa. Through a fusion of contemporary and traditional dance 
 forms\, poetry\, and music\, the concert presents a creative and innovativ
 e relationship between Latinx and Black diasporic dance\, spirituality\, a
 nd culture. The event will also include a post-performance dialogue with a
 udiences and performers.</p>\n<p>There will be a post-show conversation an
 d Q&A.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
