BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126760@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/through-our-eyes
DESCRIPTION:Drop in on a conversation between the three Indigenous curators
  of IUMAA’s Through Our Eyes: A Reclamation.\nDebra Yepa-Pappan (Jemez Pue
 blo/Korean)\, Molina Two Bulls-Parker (Oglala Lakota/Northern Cheyenne)\, 
 and Yatika Starr Fields (Osage/Muscogee Creek/Cherokee) will discuss their
  experience collaborating with the IUMAA team\, describe how they engaged 
 with harmful colonial narratives within the collections\, and reflect on t
 he significance of telling their own stories.\n\n10:30 – 11:00 a.m.: A dig
 ital exhibition and hospitality will be available in the Scholars’ Commons
  (East Tower\, first floor). .\n11:00 – 11:45 a.m.: Panel conversation in 
 Hazelbaker Hall (Wells Library E159).\n\nTo attend in person\, please regi
 ster. To attend the panel conversation virtually via Zoom\, use the “atten
 d virtual event” button.\nThis exhibition event is a result of the “Connec
 ting Collections: Indigenous Identities in Edward Curtis and Joseph Dixon 
 Materials” project\, made possible in part by funding from the Library of 
 Congress. The exhibition is supported by the IU Libraries\, Archives of Tr
 aditional Music\, First Nations Educational and Cultural Center\, and UITS
  Advanced Visualization Lab.\nThe Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology i
 s thrilled to open its doors to the public this fall. On October 19\, 2024
 \, the Museum will host a Community Grand Opening Celebration from 12:30 –
  5:30 p.m.\, complete with food\, festivities\, and behind-the-scenes tour
 s. Join us and see Debra\, Molina\, and Yatika’s creative projects inside 
 the reimagined museum alongside the other newly unveiled exhibitions.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241015T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241015T114500
LOCATION:Herman B Wells Library\, Scholars Commons (East Tower\, first floo
 r)\, 1320 E 10th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Through Our Eyes: A Conversation with Indigenous Curators
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/through-our-eyes-a-conversation-with-indigenous-
 curators/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Drop in on a 
 conversation between the three Indigenous curators of IUMAA’s Through Our 
 Eyes: A Reclamation.</p>\n<p>Debra Yepa-Pappan (Jemez Pueblo/Korean)\, Mol
 ina Two Bulls-Parker (Oglala Lakota/Northern Cheyenne)\, and Yatika Starr 
 Fields (Osage/Muscogee Creek/Cherokee) will discuss their experience colla
 borating with the IUMAA team\, describe how they engaged with harmful colo
 nial narratives within the collections\, and reflect on the significance o
 f telling their own stories.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>10:30 – 11:00 a.m.: A digital 
 exhibition and hospitality will be available in the Scholars’ Commons (Eas
 t Tower\, first floor). .</li>\n<li>11:00 – 11:45 a.m.: Panel conversation
  in Hazelbaker Hall (Wells Library E159).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To attend in per
 son\, please register. To attend the panel conversation virtually via Zoom
 \, use the “attend virtual event” button.</p>\n<p>This exhibition event is
  a result of the “Connecting Collections: Indigenous Identities in Edward 
 Curtis and Joseph Dixon Materials” project\, made possible in part by fund
 ing from the Library of Congress. The exhibition is supported by the IU Li
 braries\, Archives of Traditional Music\, First Nations Educational and Cu
 ltural Center\, and UITS Advanced Visualization Lab.</p>\n<p>The Museum of
  Archaeology and Anthropology is thrilled to open its doors to the public 
 this fall. On October 19\, 2024\, the Museum will host a Community Grand O
 pening Celebration from 12:30 – 5:30 p.m.\, complete with food\, festiviti
 es\, and behind-the-scenes tours. Join us and see Debra\, Molina\, and Yat
 ika’s creative projects inside the reimagined museum alongside the other n
 ewly unveiled exhibitions.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
