CONTACT:Sarah Nichols\, Gallery Manager\; gallery@seeconstellation.org
DESCRIPTION:The exhibits are all timely reflections of power\, identity\, a
 nd democracy. There will be interactive opportunities for participation\, 
 including making your own buttons inspired by the “I Voted” sticker. The s
 hows will also be featured in November’s First Friday Gallery Walk on Nove
 mber 1\, from 5-8pm.\nIn the Miller Gallery\, Joseph Ovalle presents Devil
 s of Dispatch\, A Ballot of Postal Conflicts. In the Educational Gallery\,
  Caleb Poer presents his show\, Inflection\, and in the Treasury Gallery i
 s The State of Democracy\, a group show curated by Nicole Jacquard.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241018T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241018T200000
LOCATION:Waldron Arts Center\, 122 S Walnut St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:[Opening Reception] Reflections of Power: Identity and Democracy
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/opening-reception-reflections-of-power-identity-
 and-democracy/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The exhibits 
 are all timely reflections of power\, identity\, and democracy. There will
  be interactive opportunities for participation\, including making your ow
 n buttons inspired by the “I Voted” sticker. The shows will also be featur
 ed in November’s First Friday Gallery Walk on November 1\, from 5-8pm.</p>
 \n<p>In the <strong>Miller Gallery</strong>\, <strong>Joseph Ovalle</stron
 g> presents Devils of Dispatch\, A Ballot of Postal Conflicts. In the <str
 ong>Educational Gallery</strong>\, <strong>Caleb Poer</strong> presents hi
 s show\, Inflection\, and in the <strong>Treasury Gallery</strong> is The 
 State of Democracy\, a group show curated by <strong>Nicole Jacquard</stro
 ng>.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
