BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126601@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812.323.3020\; boxoffice@buskirkchumley.org\; buskirkchumley.org
DESCRIPTION:There is only one consensus pick of peers and predecessors\, of
  the traditionalists\, the rebels\, and the next gen devotees. Music’s ult
 imate inside outsider. Or is it outside insider? There is only one Sam Bus
 h.  Sam Bush is an American mandolinist who is considered an originator of
  progressive bluegrass music. In 2020\, he was inducted into the Internati
 onal Bluegrass Music Hall of Fame as a member of New Grass Revival. He was
  inducted into the Hall of Fame a second time in 2023 as a solo artist.\nG
 uitarist Jason Wilber and bassist Dave Jacques (both members of the John P
 rine Band) will lead the John Prine Tribute along with Emily Scott Robinso
 n\, Oh Boy Records recording artist\, and other featured vocalists to high
 light the legacy of the legendary folk artist in his birthday month.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241018T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241018T220000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Roots presents: BloominGrass with Friday’s Line Up: Sam
  Bush Band\, John Prine Tribute feat. Emily Scott Robinson and members of 
 the John Prine Band Jason Wilber and Dave Jacques
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomingrass/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>There is only
  one consensus pick of peers and predecessors\, of the traditionalists\, t
 he rebels\, and the next gen devotees. Music’s ultimate inside outsider. O
 r is it outside insider? There is only one Sam Bush.  Sam Bush is an Ameri
 can mandolinist who is considered an originator of progressive bluegrass m
 usic. In 2020\, he was inducted into the International Bluegrass Music Hal
 l of Fame as a member of New Grass Revival. He was inducted into the Hall 
 of Fame a second time in 2023 as a solo artist.</p>\n<p>Guitarist <strong>
 Jason Wilber</strong> and bassist <strong>Dave Jacques</strong> (both memb
 ers of the John Prine Band) will lead the John Prine Tribute along with Em
 ily Scott Robinson\, Oh Boy Records recording artist\, and other featured 
 vocalists to highlight the legacy of the legendary folk artist in his birt
 hday month.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
