UID:ai1ec-126929@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.bloomingtonwinterfarmersmarket.com/woolery-farmers-mark
 et
DESCRIPTION:A Dixieland band performing in and around Bloomington\, the Her
 itage Hall Ramblers play traditional songs from the 1920’s up to the prese
 nt. Favorite artists\, whose music they are known to perform\, include Lou
 is Armstrong\, Pete Fountain\, Fats Waller\, Bing Crosby\, and the Shotgun
  Jazz Band. They are an affiliate band of the Bloomington Community Band a
 s well. Come check out the Heritage Hall Ramblers at market this Saturday 
 morning.\nThe Bloomington Flute Choir is an all volunteer group of flutist
 s who enjoy playing for the community whose members include players of all
  ages. They perform a variety of music at indoor events like weddings or c
 hurch events\, and outdoor events like festivals and farmers’ markets.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241019T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241019T120000
LOCATION:Woolery Mill front lot\, 2250 W Sunstone Dr\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Woolery Farmers’ Market\, with music from Heritage Hall Ramblers (8
 :30-10AM) / Bloomington Flute Choir (10:30-Noon)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/woolery-farmers-market-2024-10-19/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A Dixieland b
 and performing in and around Bloomington\, the <strong>Heritage Hall Rambl
 ers</strong> play traditional songs from the 1920’s up to the present. Fav
 orite artists\, whose music they are known to perform\, include Louis Arms
 trong\, Pete Fountain\, Fats Waller\, Bing Crosby\, and the Shotgun Jazz B
 and. They are an affiliate band of the Bloomington Community Band as well.
  Come check out the Heritage Hall Ramblers at market this Saturday morning
 .</p>\n<p>The <strong>Bloomington Flute Choir</strong> is an all volunteer
  group of flutists who enjoy playing for the community whose members inclu
 de players of all ages. They perform a variety of music at indoor events l
 ike weddings or church events\, and outdoor events like festivals and farm
 ers’ markets.  </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127994@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812-318-1236\; https://www.meditationinbloomington.org/unplug
DESCRIPTION:We all have negative narratives that drag us and others down. H
 ow is it possible to not get caught in the iron net of negative narratives
 ? Perhaps\, you or family members have been harmed? Perhaps\, coworkers ot
  others are critical towards you? Maybe\, you are critical of yourself?\n“
 Just as there is room in the sky for a thunderstorm\, so there is room in 
 the vast space of our mind for a few painful feelings\; and just as a stor
 m has no power to destroy the sky\, so unpleasant feelings have no power t
 o destroy our mind.” — Geshe Kelsang Gyatso Rinpoche\nIn this retreat\, we
  will explore:\n\nHow to recognize and reduce negative narratives\nNegativ
 e vs positive perspectives to shift narrative\nMeditation techniques to fo
 cus letting go authentically from negative narratives of ourself and other
 s\n\nThe retreat is suitable for all meditation levels\, including beginne
 rs. It includes guided meditations\, short teachings as well as Q&A in the
  last session. Everyone can benefit from this retreat — you don’t have to 
 be Buddhist to participate.\nWhat to Expect\n\n2 sessions with 15-min brea
 k\ncalming guided meditations\nshort talks to inspire\nguided meditations 
 to transform
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241019T130000
LOCATION:Kadampa Meditation Center Bloomington\, 234 N Morton St\, Blooming
 ton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Unplug Negative Narratives – Meditation Retreat
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/unplug-negative-narratives-meditation-retreat/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>We all have n
 egative narratives that drag us and others down. How is it possible to not
  get caught in the iron net of negative narratives? Perhaps\, you or famil
 y members have been harmed? Perhaps\, coworkers ot others are critical tow
 ards you? Maybe\, you are critical of yourself?</p>\n<p>“Just as there is 
 room in the sky for a thunderstorm\, so there is room in the vast space of
  our mind for a few painful feelings\; and just as a storm has no power to
  destroy the sky\, so unpleasant feelings have no power to destroy our min
 d.” — Geshe Kelsang Gyatso Rinpoche</p>\n<p>In this retreat\, we will expl
 ore:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>How to recognize and reduce negative narratives</li>\n
 <li>Negative vs positive perspectives to shift narrative</li>\n<li>Meditat
 ion techniques to focus letting go authentically from negative narratives 
 of ourself and others</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The retreat is suitable for all medi
 tation levels\, including beginners. It includes guided meditations\, shor
 t teachings as well as Q&A in the last session. Everyone can benefit from 
 this retreat — you don’t have to be Buddhist to participate.</p>\n<p>What 
 to Expect</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2 sessions with 15-min break</li>\n<li>calming gu
 ided meditations</li>\n<li>short talks to inspire</li>\n<li>guided meditat
 ions to transform</li>\n</ul>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
