 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Prese
 nted by Resilience Productions and Monroe County History Center</strong><b
 r />\nThis original play exposes the contentious relationship between Blac
 k and White suffrage movement leaders. It shows how two groups fighting fo
 r a common good but whose differing worldviews created a yawning chasm res
 ulting in irreparable damage.<br />\nWritten by Gladys DeVane (In Collabor
 ation with Danielle Bruce) | Directed by Danielle Bruce<br />\nWith Post-S
 how TalkBack and Reception</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
