BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-128003@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Blooming Zone Initiative\; BloomingtonBlueZone@gmail.com
DESCRIPTION:A group of local professionals will be present to answer questi
 ons posed by Blooming Zone Initiative volunteers and audience members. Fou
 nders Bridgett DiVohl and Cynthia Schultz will host and moderate the discu
 ssion\, focusing on this question:\nHow might the greater Bloomington Comm
 unity improve its health and wellness programs and services to become elig
 ible for Blue Zones Project certification?\nPanelists\n\nMary Hoedeman Con
 iaris: Professional Dance Instructor\; Movement Expert\; Blue Zones Princi
 ples & Healthy Living Advocate\nLandry Culp: Cook Medical\, Studio Manager
 \; COB’s Commission on the Status of Women and Blooming Zone Initiative\, 
 Director of Strategy & Development\nJulie Hill: Indiana Arts Commission Fe
 llow\, Dementia Friendly Bloomington\, Founder\; and Creative Aging Profes
 sional\nPhil Stafford\, Co-Design Commons LLC\, Co-Founder\; IU Adjunct Pr
 ofessor\, Dept. of Anthropology and Retired Director of IU’s Center on Agi
 ng & Disabilities\n\n——–\nThe Blue Zones Project© aims to make healthy lif
 estyle choices readily available to individuals and communities. The Bloom
 ing Zone Initiative (BZI) is a local\, all-volunteer team working toward a
  Blue Zones Project certification for Bloomington.\nFounded in January 202
 4\, BZI has offered programs and services to familiarize the community wit
 h the Blue Zones lifestyle principles. One of the most popular programs is
  the Health & Wellness program\, which has been meeting monthly on the thi
 rd Monday to read and discuss the book\, The Blue Zones: 9 Lessons for Liv
 ing Longer from the People Who’ve Lived the Longest by Dan Buettner\, auth
 or and founder of the Blue Zones Project. Now that the book is finished\, 
 we are changing the meeting format to a panel discussion with a Q&A sessio
 n and everyone is invited.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241021T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241021T200000
LOCATION:Morgensterns Cafe and Bookstore\, 849 S Auto Mall Rd. Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Blooming Zone Initiative – Panel Discussion
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/blooming-zone-initiative-panel-discussion/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A group of lo
 cal professionals will be present to answer questions posed by <strong><a 
 href='https://www.bloomingtonbluezone.com/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'
 >Blooming Zone Initiative</a></strong> volunteers and audience members. Fo
 unders Bridgett DiVohl and Cynthia Schultz will host and moderate the disc
 ussion\, focusing on this question:</p>\n<p><strong>How might the greater 
 Bloomington Community improve its health and wellness programs and service
 s to become eligible for Blue Zones Project certification?</strong></p>\n<
 p>Panelists</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mary Hoedeman Coniaris: Professional Dance Inst
 ructor\; Movement Expert\; Blue Zones Principles & Healthy Living Advocate
 </li>\n<li>Landry Culp: Cook Medical\, Studio Manager\; COB’s Commission o
 n the Status of Women and Blooming Zone Initiative\, Director of Strategy 
 & Development</li>\n<li>Julie Hill: Indiana Arts Commission Fellow\, Demen
 tia Friendly Bloomington\, Founder\; and Creative Aging Professional</li>
 \n<li>Phil Stafford\, Co-Design Commons LLC\, Co-Founder\; IU Adjunct Prof
 essor\, Dept. of Anthropology and Retired Director of IU’s Center on Aging
  & Disabilities</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>——–</em></p>\n<p><em>The Blue Zones Pr
 oject©</em> aims to make healthy lifestyle choices readily available to in
 dividuals and communities. The Blooming Zone Initiative (BZI) is a local\,
  all-volunteer team working toward a Blue Zones Project certification for 
 Bloomington.</p>\n<p>Founded in January 2024\, BZI has offered programs an
 d services to familiarize the community with the Blue Zones lifestyle prin
 ciples. One of the most popular programs is the Health & Wellness program\
 , which has been meeting monthly on the third Monday to read and discuss t
 he book\, <strong>The Blue Zones: 9 Lessons for Living Longer from the Peo
 ple Who’ve Lived the Longest</strong> by <a href='https://morgensternbooks
 .com/search/Buettner%2C%20Dan?type=author'>Dan Buettner</a>\, author and f
 ounder of the Blue Zones Project. Now that the book is finished\, we are c
 hanging the meeting format to a panel discussion with a Q&A session and ev
 eryone is invited.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
