BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127480@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Jill Vance\, Paynetown Activity Center\; 812-837-9967\; jvance@dnr.
 in.gov\; tinyurl.com/60monroe
DESCRIPTION:Monroe Lake to celebrate 60 years with reception beneath dam\, 
 Oct. 24\nOn October 24\, 1964\, representatives from the U.S. Army Corps o
 f Engineers officially dedicated the newly constructed Monroe Reservoir. 6
 0 years later\, Monroe Lake will commemorate that occasion with an anniver
 sary reception on October 24 from 2 to 3:30 p.m.\nThe reception will take 
 place in the tailwater\, directly beneath the reservoir dam\, at 1620 E. M
 onroe Dam Court\, Bloomington. The public is invited and encouraged to att
 end.\nBeginning at 2 p.m.\, there will be displays of historical items and
  photos from the reservoir’s history\, a self-guided tour of the dam\, and
  info tables from organizations tied to the lake. The first 100 people in 
 attendance will receive a 60th anniversary souvenir.\nDaniel Bortner\, Dir
 ector of the Indiana Department of Natural Resources\, Michael Chaveas\, H
 oosier National Forest Supervisor\, and Tyler Blakenship\, U.S. Army Corps
  of Engineers Natural Resource Specialist\, will speak on the history and 
 significance of the reservoir at 2:30 p.m.\nFollowing the remarks\, attend
 ees can enjoy refreshments\, sponsored by Visit Bloomington\, and all atte
 ndees can enter to win a 2025 Indiana State Parks Annual Entrance Pass.\nI
 f you plan to attend the reception\, an RSVP by noon on Oct. 23 is greatly
  appreciated to assist with planning. However\, walk-up attendees are also
  welcome.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241024T153000
LOCATION:1620 E. Monroe Dam Court\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Monroe Lake: 60th Anniversary Reception
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/monroe-lake-anniversary-reception-2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Monroe Lake t
 o celebrate 60 years with reception beneath dam\, Oct. 24</p>\n<p>On Octob
 er 24\, 1964\, representatives from the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers offic
 ially dedicated the newly constructed Monroe Reservoir. 60 years later\, M
 onroe Lake will commemorate that occasion with an anniversary reception on
  October 24 from 2 to 3:30 p.m.</p>\n<p>The reception will take place in t
 he tailwater\, directly beneath the reservoir dam\, at 1620 E. Monroe Dam 
 Court\, Bloomington. The public is invited and encouraged to attend.</p>\n
 <p>Beginning at 2 p.m.\, there will be displays of historical items and ph
 otos from the reservoir’s history\, a self-guided tour of the dam\, and in
 fo tables from organizations tied to the lake. The first 100 people in att
 endance will receive a 60th anniversary souvenir.</p>\n<p>Daniel Bortner\,
  Director of the Indiana Department of Natural Resources\, Michael Chaveas
 \, Hoosier National Forest Supervisor\, and Tyler Blakenship\, U.S. Army C
 orps of Engineers Natural Resource Specialist\, will speak on the history 
 and significance of the reservoir at 2:30 p.m.</p>\n<p>Following the remar
 ks\, attendees can enjoy refreshments\, sponsored by Visit Bloomington\, a
 nd all attendees can enter to win a 2025 Indiana State Parks Annual Entran
 ce Pass.</p>\n<p>If you plan to attend the reception\, an <a href='http://
 tinyurl.com/60monroe'>RSVP</a> by noon on Oct. 23 is greatly appreciated t
 o assist with planning. However\, walk-up attendees are also welcome.</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
