BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-122246@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A musical “tail” that will bring the house down\n\n\nThere are 
 two sides to every story\, and when the Big Bad Wolf takes the stand in Pi
 ggsylvania’s Trial of the Century\, he finally gets his say. But whether h
 e’ll get a fair trial in a corrupt piggy court is anyone’s guess. Will the
  pigs’ splashy show make a puppet out of justice\, or is the wolf’s song a
 nd dance about a sneeze gone wrong all razzle-dazzle? Enter the jury box a
 nd help decide the fate of Big ‘n’ Bad in this musical adaptation of the h
 it children’s book. Fun for all ages! 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241025T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241025T193000
LOCATION:Constellation Stage & Screen (Waldron Auditorium)\, 122 S Walnut S
 treet\, Bloomington\, IN
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20241025T183000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20241101T183000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20241108T183000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The True Story of the Three Little Pigs!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-true-story-of-the-three-little-pigs/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><i><span styl
 e='font-family: arial\, sans-serif\;'>A musical “tail” that will bring the
  house down</span></i></p>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><span style='font-family: ari
 al\, sans-serif\;'>There are two sides to every story\, and when the Big B
 ad Wolf takes the stand in Piggsylvania’s Trial of the Century\, he finall
 y gets his say. But whether he’ll get a fair trial in a corrupt piggy cour
 t is anyone’s guess. Will the pigs’ splashy show make a puppet out of just
 ice\, or is the wolf’s song and dance about a sneeze gone wrong all razzle
 -dazzle? Enter the jury box and help decide the fate of Big ‘n’ Bad in thi
 s musical adaptation of the hit children’s book. <em>Fun for all ages! </e
 m></span></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126147@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://cicadacinema.com/products/ms-45-october-25-orbit-room-7pm
DESCRIPTION:Synopsis: Eerie and unforgettable\, MS. 45 is an essential snap
 shot of New York City in the early 1980s from Abel Ferrara (DRILLER KILLER
 \, THE ADDICTION)—one of the greatest and most unique living filmmakers on
  the planet. Thana (Zoë Tamerlis) is a garment worker who’s had the ultima
 te bad day\, as she’s assaulted twice in visceral fashion. Shocked to her 
 core\, Thana’s nights become consumed by vengeful prowls through the city\
 , which result in men winding up on the wrong end of a bullet. Knocking th
 e DEATH WISH rip-off subgenre into a new stratosphere\, MS. 45 showcases a
  haunting performance from Tamerlis and Ferrara’s knack for transforming l
 imited resources into genre revolutions.\n*In partnership with The Orbit R
 oom\, The American Genre Film Archive and Vulture Video\, our Cicada Under
 ground series comes from the ethos that while as imperfect as the people w
 ho made them\, genre films deserved to be screened to both enrich our live
 s and have a good time doing it!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241025T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241025T201500
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, downstairs at 107 N College Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents: Ms. 45 (1981)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-ms-45/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Synop
 sis</strong>: Eerie and unforgettable\, MS. 45 is an essential snapshot of
  New York City in the early 1980s from Abel Ferrara (DRILLER KILLER\, THE 
 ADDICTION)—one of the greatest and most unique living filmmakers on the pl
 anet. Thana (Zoë Tamerlis) is a garment worker who’s had the ultimate bad 
 day\, as she’s assaulted twice in visceral fashion. Shocked to her core\, 
 Thana’s nights become consumed by vengeful prowls through the city\, which
  result in men winding up on the wrong end of a bullet. Knocking the DEATH
  WISH rip-off subgenre into a new stratosphere\, MS. 45 showcases a haunti
 ng performance from Tamerlis and Ferrara’s knack for transforming limited 
 resources into genre revolutions.</p>\n<p><em>*In partnership with <strong
 ><a href='https://www.facebook.com/orbitroombtown/'>The Orbit Room</a></st
 rong>\, <strong><a href='https://www.americangenrefilm.com/'>The American 
 Genre Film Archive</a></strong> and <strong><a href='https://instagram.com
 /vulturevideo'>Vulture Video</a></strong>\, our <strong>Cicada Underground
 </strong> series comes from the ethos that while as imperfect as the peopl
 e who made them\, genre films deserved to be screened to both enrich our l
 ives and have a good time doing it!</em></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127175@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.bloomington.in.gov/recreation/programs/12414
DESCRIPTION:Under a dark sky and a rising moon\, nothing seems so scary as 
 tales of ghosts\, ghouls and terrifying situations. It is the annual Festi
 val of Ghost Stories and we invite you to let your imagination run wild as
  tellers from the Bloomington Storytellers Guild weave stories that will k
 eep you on the edge of your blanket! You can bring a lawn chair\, and dres
 s warmly to soothe your frayed nerves. Stories are best suited for adults\
 , teens and older school-age children and may not be appropriate for young
 er children. \nThe program is presented by Bloomington Parks and Recreatio
 n and sponsored by the Monroe County Public Library.\nFor weather-related 
 updates\, call the Community Events Hotline at 349-3754. Rain location is 
 the Monroe County Public Library Auditorium\, 303 E. Kirkwood Ave.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241025T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241025T203000
LOCATION:Bryan Park\, 1001 S Henderson St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Festival of Ghost Stories (ages 10+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/festival-of-ghost-stories-2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Under a dark 
 sky and a rising moon\, nothing seems so scary as tales of ghosts\, ghouls
  and terrifying situations. It is the annual Festival of Ghost Stories and
  we invite you to let your imagination run wild as tellers from the Bloomi
 ngton Storytellers Guild weave stories that will keep you on the edge of y
 our blanket! You can bring a lawn chair\, and dress warmly to soothe your 
 frayed nerves. Stories are best suited for adults\, teens and older school
 -age children and may not be appropriate for younger children. </p>\n<p>Th
 e program is presented by Bloomington Parks and Recreation and sponsored b
 y the Monroe County Public Library.<br />\nFor weather-related updates\, c
 all the Community Events Hotline at 349-3754. Rain location is the Monroe 
 County Public Library Auditorium\, 303 E. Kirkwood Ave.</p>\n</BODY></HTML
 >
END:VEVENT
