BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-123723@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://bloomington.in.gov/farmers-market
DESCRIPTION:Nestled in picturesque downtown charm and\, in 2024\, celebrati
 ng its 50th anniversary\, the Bloomington Community Farmers’ Market is a v
 ital part of the local food culture.\nMarket goers can expect to find a wi
 de assortment of goods from the farm and field\, including fruits and vege
 tables\, eggs\, meats and cheeses\, honey\, seasonal flowers\, and annual 
 and perennial plants. Food and beverage artisans provide a tasteful variet
 y of satisfying breads\, drinks\, pastries\, and savory dishes. This weekl
 y gathering provides individuals the opportunity to connect with their com
 munity in meaningful ways while supporting small farmers and businesses.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T130000
LOCATION:Showers Common next to City Hall\, 401 N Morton St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Community Farmers’ Market with entertainment from the M
 CCSC Elementary Sing at 10:15 am and Ken & Debbie Wilson at 11 am
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-community-farmers-market-9/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Nestled in pi
 cturesque downtown charm and\, in 2024\, celebrating its 50th anniversary\
 , the Bloomington Community Farmers’ Market is a vital part of the local f
 ood culture.</p>\n<p>Market goers can expect to find a wide assortment of 
 goods from the farm and field\, including fruits and vegetables\, eggs\, m
 eats and cheeses\, honey\, seasonal flowers\, and annual and perennial pla
 nts. Food and beverage artisans provide a tasteful variety of satisfying b
 reads\, drinks\, pastries\, and savory dishes. This weekly gathering provi
 des individuals the opportunity to connect with their community in meaning
 ful ways while supporting small farmers and businesses.</p>\n</BODY></HTML
 >
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126641@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.bloomingtonwinterfarmersmarket.com/woolery-farmers-mark
 et
DESCRIPTION:For the last day of our 5th season at the Woolery Farmers’ Mark
 et\, we’ll be going out with a bang – or should I say\, a boo! Come trick 
 or treat your way around the market booths and stock up on some sweet trea
 ts. Enjoy the music of Destin Wernicke as he provides the proper Halloween
  ambiance with some seriously spooky organ music. Deck out your doggy in t
 heir best duds and dazzle the other dogs (No\, Fluffy\, a collar does not 
 count as a costume!).  Keep an eye out for our last Woolery Market Newslet
 ter of the season next week for more spooky surprises. Hope to see you sca
 re! I mean\, there!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T120000
LOCATION:Woolery Mill front lot\, 2250 W Sunstone Dr\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Woolery Farmers’ Market – Spooky Season\, with music from Destin We
 rnicke (8:30-10AM) / Bloomington Brass Band (10:30-Noon)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/woolery-farmers-market-2024-10-26/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>For the last 
 day of our 5th season at the Woolery Farmers’ Market\, we’ll be going out 
 with a bang – or should I say\, a boo! Come trick or treat your way around
  the market booths and stock up on some sweet treats. Enjoy the music of D
 estin Wernicke as he provides the proper Halloween ambiance with some seri
 ously spooky organ music. Deck out your doggy in their best duds and dazzl
 e the other dogs (No\, Fluffy\, a collar does not count as a costume!).  K
 eep an eye out for our last Woolery Market Newsletter of the season next w
 eek for more spooky surprises. Hope to see you scare! I mean\, there!</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126715@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:There will be singing from both the 1991 revision The Sacred Ha
 rp and The Shenandoah Harmony. Loaner song books will be available. Feel f
 ree to drop by to observe if you have limited time!\nDoors will be open ar
 ound 9am and are asking everyone to register even if not leading a song.\n
 There will be breakfast snacks and drinks.\nA traditional potluck dinner o
 n the grounds at noon.\nSocial with a spaghetti supper at Barb’s house (52
 0 W 6th St) in the evening.
