BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127555@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Jessica Filer\; (812) 829-2235 ext. 2\; Jfiler@dnr.in.gov\; https:/
 /events.in.gov/event/fall-o-ween-mccormicks-creek-state-park
DESCRIPTION:10am-12pm: Spooky Crafts- (Craft) Drop by the Nature Center to 
 create a fangtastic craft that will make you want to sink your fangs into 
 reading. Come create a cute snake bookmark and meet a few our snakes.\n1-3
 pm: Pumpkin Carving- (Event) Carve a pumpkin\, $3 cost per pumpkin. Please
  bring cash. Meet at Nature Center Amphitheater. Supplies is limited to th
 e first 50 guest\n4-5:30pm: Trick or Treat Trail- (Event) Put on a costume
  and meet the Friends of McCormick’s Creek at the Nature Center to go Tric
 k or Treating. We will be walking the habitat trail and trail 8 to get be 
 spooked by a trick or a sweet treat on the way. The trail is accessible fo
 r all.\n6:30-8pm: Spooky Story Telling- (Event) Join the Bloomington Story
 teller Guild at the Canyon Inn in front of the fireplace. They will be tel
 ling family friendly spooky stories.\n8:30 pm: Spider Spoofing Hike- (Hike
 ) Join Park Naturalist Jessie at the Nature Center to look for spider’s ey
 e shine at night. Bring a flashlight! This is a family friendly event. The
  trail is accessible for all.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T220000
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, 250 McCormick's Creek Park Rd\, Spe
 ncer
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Fall-O-Ween
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/fall-o-ween-2024-10-26/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>10am-
 12pm: Spooky Crafts- (Craft) </strong>Drop by the Nature Center to create 
 a fangtastic craft that will make you want to sink your fangs into reading
 . Come create a cute snake bookmark and meet a few our snakes.<br />\n<str
 ong>1-3pm: Pumpkin Carving- (Event)</strong> Carve a pumpkin\, $3 cost per
  pumpkin. Please bring cash. Meet at Nature Center Amphitheater. Supplies 
 is limited to the first 50 guest<br />\n<strong>4-5:30pm: Trick or Treat T
 rail- (Event)</strong> Put on a costume and meet the Friends of McCormick’
 s Creek at the Nature Center to go Trick or Treating. We will be walking t
 he habitat trail and trail 8 to get be spooked by a trick or a sweet treat
  on the way. The trail is accessible for all.<br />\n<strong>6:30-8pm: Spo
 oky Story Telling- (Event)</strong> Join the Bloomington Storyteller Guild
  at the Canyon Inn in front of the fireplace. They will be telling family 
 friendly spooky stories.<br />\n<strong>8:30 pm: Spider Spoofing Hike- (Hi
 ke)</strong> Join Park Naturalist Jessie at the Nature Center to look for 
 spider’s eye shine at night. Bring a flashlight! This is a family friendly
  event. The trail is accessible for all.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
