BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126723@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:http://www.thebishopbar.com/events/daniel-nunnelee-june-baby-fall-t
 our
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Spirit of ’68 | Ages 18+\nWith the arrival of his 
 self-released breakout single “Pick and Choose” in 2022\, Memphis-born sin
 ger/songwriter Daniel Nunnelee introduced the world to his sweetly offbeat
  and soul-baring form of folk/indie-rock. An instant viral sensation that 
 amassed over a million streams in just ten days\, “Pick and Choose” soon l
 ed to the making of June\, Baby: a strangely enchanting debut album reveal
 ing both his old-soul sensibilities and wide-eyed perspective on finding y
 our way in the world. With its title nodding to his birthday month and to 
 the duality he embodies as a quintessential Gemini\, June\, Baby explores 
 such emotionally heavy matters as anxiety and anticipatory grief\, endless
 ly showcasing the graceful musicality he first developed by playing guitar
  in church as a kid. \nA lifelong nature lover who wrote much of June\, Ba
 by at his favorite park and at remote cabins in Mississippi and Colorado\,
  the Nashville-based artist also sets his self-reflection to a one-of-a-ki
 nd sound matching its homespun charm with the unbridled energy he’s brough
 t to the stage opening for artists like Madi Diaz and Shakey Graves (in ad
 dition to headlining his own tours). A truly gifted vocalist who brings an
  undeniably playful spirit to his existential questioning\, Nunnelee ultim
 ately hopes that listeners might take whatever they need from his songs — 
 whether it’s a deeper communion with the natural world that incessantly in
 spires his music\, or a monumental shift in their own outlook on life.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241026T230000
LOCATION:The Bishop\, 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Daniel Nunnelee “June\, Baby” Fall Tour // Hana Eid
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/daniel-nunnelee-june-baby-fall-tour-hana-eid/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Prese
 nted by Spirit of ’68</strong> | Ages 18+<br />\nWith the arrival of his s
 elf-released breakout single “Pick and Choose” in 2022\, Memphis-born sing
 er/songwriter <strong>Daniel Nunnelee</strong> introduced the world to his
  sweetly offbeat and soul-baring form of folk/indie-rock. An instant viral
  sensation that amassed over a million streams in just ten days\, “Pick an
 d Choose” soon led to the making of June\, Baby: a strangely enchanting de
 but album revealing both his old-soul sensibilities and wide-eyed perspect
 ive on finding your way in the world. With its title nodding to his birthd
 ay month and to the duality he embodies as a quintessential Gemini\, June\
 , Baby explores such emotionally heavy matters as anxiety and anticipatory
  grief\, endlessly showcasing the graceful musicality he first developed b
 y playing guitar in church as a kid. </p>\n<p>A lifelong nature lover who 
 wrote much of <em>June\, Baby</em> at his favorite park and at remote cabi
 ns in Mississippi and Colorado\, the Nashville-based artist also sets his 
 self-reflection to a one-of-a-kind sound matching its homespun charm with 
 the unbridled energy he’s brought to the stage opening for artists like Ma
 di Diaz and Shakey Graves (in addition to headlining his own tours). A tru
 ly gifted vocalist who brings an undeniably playful spirit to his existent
 ial questioning\, Nunnelee ultimately hopes that listeners might take what
 ever they need from his songs — whether it’s a deeper communion with the n
 atural world that incessantly inspires his music\, or a monumental shift i
 n their own outlook on life.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
