BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-122092@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION: Mark your calendars and join in on the 9th annual Monroe Count
 y Childhood Conditions Summit!  This event allows for opportunities to exp
 lore what it takes to make Monroe County a community where all youth & fam
 ilies can thrive\, through the lens of Power & Possibility.\n\nDig into id
 entifying your own power\, and opportunities to build and share power with
  young people. Explore ways to collaborate that don’t overburden individua
 ls. Come together to build systems of collective care\, so that no one bur
 ns out while we work to improve community conditions. Hear directly from y
 outh\, parents\, and youth workers about what a safe\, stable\, and nurtur
 ing community means to them. And connect with others around both increment
 al but meaningful\, and system-wide opportunities for change.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241030T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241030T160000
LOCATION:Monroe Convention Center\, 302 S College Ave\, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:2024 Monroe County Childhood Conditions Summit (MC3)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/2024-monroe-county-childhood-conditions-summit-m
 c3/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div><b> </b>Mar
 k your calendars and join in on the 9th annual Monroe County Childhood Con
 ditions Summit!  This event allows for opportunities to explore what it ta
 kes to make Monroe County a community where all youth & families can thriv
 e\, through the lens of Power & Possibility.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Dig 
 into identifying your own power\, and opportunities to build and share pow
 er with young people. Explore ways to collaborate that don’t overburden in
 dividuals. Come together to build systems of collective care\, so that no 
 one burns out while we work to improve community conditions. Hear directly
  from youth\, parents\, and youth workers about what a safe\, stable\, and
  nurturing community means to them. And connect with others around both in
 cremental but meaningful\, and system-wide opportunities for change.</div>
 \n<div>\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
