BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127258@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Rating: R | Series: Friday Night Frights\nIt’s a Found Footage 
 Freakout Double Feature with one of this year’s best new horror films and 
 a classic that helped start it all.\nLate Night with the Devil (Colin Cair
 nes and Cameron Cairnes\, Australia and USA\, 2024): October 31\, 1977. Ja
 ck Delroy’s syndicated talk show Night Owls has long been a trusted compan
 ion to insomniacs around the country\, but a year on from the tragic death
  of Jack’s wife\, ratings have plummeted. Desperate to turn his fortunes a
 round\, Jack plans a Halloween special like no other\, unaware he is about
  to unleash evil into the living rooms of America. [93 min\; horror\; Engl
 ish]\nThe Blair Witch Project (Daniel Myrick and Eduardo Sánchez\, USA\, 1
 999): The micro-indie film that took over the world 25 years ago is back o
 n the big screen and just as unsettling as ever. When three film students 
 travel deep into the Maryland woods to search for local legend the Blair W
 itch\, they have no idea their student film is about to take a frightening
  and horrific turn—and that they will never be seen again. [81 min\; docum
 entary\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241031T190000
LOCATION:Indiana University Cinema\, 1213 E 7th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Found Footage Freakout Double Feature: Late Night with the Devil (2
 024) + The Blair Witch Project (1999)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/found-footage-freakout-double-feature-late-night
 -with-the-devil-2024-the-blair-witch-project-1999/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Ratin
 g: R | Series: Friday Night Frights</strong><br />\nIt’s a Found Footage F
 reakout Double Feature with one of this year’s best new horror films and a
  classic that helped start it all.</p>\n<p><strong>Late Night with the Dev
 il</strong> (Colin Cairnes and Cameron Cairnes\, Australia and USA\, 2024)
 : October 31\, 1977. Jack Delroy’s syndicated talk show Night Owls has lon
 g been a trusted companion to insomniacs around the country\, but a year o
 n from the tragic death of Jack’s wife\, ratings have plummeted. Desperate
  to turn his fortunes around\, Jack plans a Halloween special like no othe
 r\, unaware he is about to unleash evil into the living rooms of America. 
 [93 min\; horror\; English]</p>\n<p><strong>The Blair Witch Project</stron
 g> (Daniel Myrick and Eduardo Sánchez\, USA\, 1999): The micro-indie film 
 that took over the world 25 years ago is back on the big screen and just a
 s unsettling as ever. When three film students travel deep into the Maryla
 nd woods to search for local legend the Blair Witch\, they have no idea th
 eir student film is about to take a frightening and horrific turn—and that
  they will never be seen again. [81 min\; documentary\; English]</p>\n</BO
 DY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
