X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><ul>\n<li>10:00a
 m – 11:00am: Children’s Hour – KIM HOWARD</li>\n<li>11:30am – 12:00pm: Mus
 ic Event – (Girls Rock Bloomington)</li>\n<li>12:00pm – 1:30pm: Writing Cl
 ass – Worldbuilding with C.L. CLARK</li>\n<li>1:30pm – 3:00pm: Writing Cla
 ss – Magical Worlds\, Imaginative Realities & Invisible Cities with ALEXAN
 DER WEINSTEIN</li>\n<li>3:00pm – 5:00pm (Indoors) : Music Event – Jeff Isa
 ac/Dave Bruker Duo</li>\n<li>3:00pm – 4:30pm: Speculative Fiction Author P
 anel (C.L. CLARK\, ALEXANDER WEINSTEIN\, MAURICE BROADUS) Moderated by LAR
 ISSA LAI</li>\n<li>5:00pm – 7:00pm: Keynote Author Event – MICHAEL KORYTA 
 in conversation with RICHARD CHIZMAR</li>\n<li>7:00pm – 9:00pm: Music Even
 t – DON’T CALL ME BETTY</li>\n</ul>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127549@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Writers Guild at Bloomington presents\nJoin the Writers Gui
 ld for a fun-filled day at the Local Author Book Fair! This event will fea
 ture 32 local authors selling their books\, including notable writers Nate
  Powell\, Rob Harrell\, Keiko Kasza\, Teresa Robeson\, and Tanya Konerman.
  Fifteen literary genres represented (including 10 children’s authors)! Mu
 sic all day\, plus tamales\, cake\, cookies and coffee. FREE raffle. What 
 else do you need on a beautiful fall day?\nLive Music All Day!\nFood vendo
 rs\, including Tamales by Biviana Torres
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241102T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241102T150000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E 6th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
