BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-128381@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Bring your vegetable and flower seeds to exchange with other co
 mmunity members and help the gardens of Monroe County grow! All ages.\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n \nThe Downtown Library and Mother Hubbard’s Cupboard will also 
 have free seeds available. Any seeds left over from the Swap will be donat
 ed to the participating seed libraries so that they’re still available for
  the community.\nWhen donating seeds\, please make sure your seeds are not
  from invasive plants and note the following:\n\nThe type and variety of s
 eed\nThe year the seeds are from\nWhether the seeds are store-bought or se
 lf-saved\n\nWe ask that you please package your seeds accordingly\; we wil
 l have tools and supplies on-hand.\nPlease contact Maggie Hutt at mhutt@mc
 pl.info if you have any questions about this program.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241102T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241102T130000
LOCATION:Meeting Room 2B and 2C Combo\, Monroe County Public Library\, 303 
 East Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Seed Swap
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/seed-swap-4/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='idlw5ZC
 ' class='amh-row row'>\n<div id='idjLXfv' class='amh-block amh-text col-md
 -12' data-block-type='text'>\n<div class='amh-content'>\n<p class='custom1
 '>Bring your vegetable and flower seeds to exchange with other community m
 embers and help the gardens of Monroe County grow! All ages.</p>\n</div>\n
 </div>\n</div>\n<div id='idQ9R9H' class='amh-row row'>\n<div id='idiga4D' 
 class='amh-block amh-text col-md-12' data-block-type='text'>\n<div class='
 amh-content'>\n<p> </p>\n<p>The Downtown Library and Mother Hubbard’s Cupb
 oard will also have free seeds available. Any seeds left over from the Swa
 p will be donated to the participating seed libraries so that they’re stil
 l available for the community.</p>\n<p>When donating seeds\, please make s
 ure your seeds are <strong>not from invasive plants</strong> and note the 
 following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The type and variety of seed</li>\n<li>The year 
 the seeds are from</li>\n<li>Whether the seeds are store-bought or self-sa
 ved</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We ask that you please package your seeds accordingly\
 ; we will have tools and supplies on-hand.</p>\n<p>Please contact Maggie H
 utt at mhutt@mcpl.info if you have any questions about this program.</p>\n
 </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
