UID:ai1ec-125685@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Monroe County Humane Association veterinary team and the Ba
 nneker Community Center are hosting a pop-up mobile vaccine clinic! No app
 ointment needed\; all are welcome!\n\nA range of services are available\, 
 including legally mandated rabies vaccines for pets aged 12 weeks and olde
 r. Clinics also provide nail trims\, microchips\, and preventive measures 
 for flea\, tick\, and heartworm.\n\nSubsidized rates are available to resi
 dents experiencing financial hardship if they provide documentation. Cats 
 must be in carriers\, and dogs must be leashed (no retractable leashes). P
 ets showing signs of illness or aggression might be turned away.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241103T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241103T150000
LOCATION:Banneker Community Center\, 930 W 7th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Pop-Up Vaccine Clinic for Cats and Dogs
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/pop-up-vaccine-clinic-for-cats-and-dogs-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>The <a href
 ='http://monroehumane.org'>Monroe County Humane Association</a> veterinary
  team and the Banneker Community Center are hosting a pop-up mobile vaccin
 e clinic! No appointment needed\; all are welcome!</div>\n<div></div>\n<di
 v>A range of services are available\, including legally mandated rabies va
 ccines for pets aged 12 weeks and older. Clinics also provide nail trims\,
  microchips\, and preventive measures for flea\, tick\, and heartworm.</di
 v>\n<div></div>\n<div>Subsidized rates are available to residents experien
 cing financial hardship if they provide documentation. Cats must be in car
 riers\, and dogs must be leashed (no retractable leashes). Pets showing si
 gns of illness or aggression might be turned away.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
