BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127547@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Door Time: 6:00 PM\nIf you aren’t familiar with Ben Roy\, he’s 
 been taking comedy audiences by storm since 2004\, bringing an unparallele
 d energy and unique voice to the stage. Often compared to Lewis Black or B
 ill Hicks due to his passionate\, ranting approach\, Roy has a style that 
 is definitively his own.\nRoy cut his comedic teeth in Denver at the world
 -famous Comedy Works. Since then\, he has been selected to perform at the 
 Montreal Just for Laughs Comedy Festival\, Just For Laughs Toronto\, Just 
 For Laughs Chicago\, The New York Comedy Festival\, Austin’s South by Sout
 hwest festival\, San Francisco SketchFest\, and many more. Roy has been fe
 atured on HBO’s Funny as Hell series\; as well as on the Comedy Central sh
 ows Adam DeVine’s House Party\, Corporate\, @midnight\, and This Is Not Ha
 ppening. Ben has also released four stand-up comedy albums and was listed 
 as one of Variety’s Top 10 Comics to Watch.\nAlong with fellow Denver Come
 dians Adam Cayton-Holland and Andrew Orvedahl (who collectively perform as
  The Grawlix)\, Ben created\, wrote\, and starred in TruTV’s original come
 dy series Those Who Can’t\, which now has all three seasons available for 
 streaming on HBOMax. In addition to stand-up comedy\, Roy is a prolific mu
 sician\, currently the lead singer of pop punk outfit SPELLS.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241107T204500
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ben Roy Returns To Bloomington – One Night Only!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ben-roy-returns-to-bloomington-one-night-only/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Door 
 Time: 6:00 PM</strong><br />\nIf you aren’t familiar with Ben Roy\, he’s b
 een taking comedy audiences by storm since 2004\, bringing an unparalleled
  energy and unique voice to the stage. Often compared to Lewis Black or Bi
 ll Hicks due to his passionate\, ranting approach\, Roy has a style that i
 s definitively his own.</p>\n<p>Roy cut his comedic teeth in Denver at the
  world-famous Comedy Works. Since then\, he has been selected to perform a
 t the Montreal Just for Laughs Comedy Festival\, Just For Laughs Toronto\,
  Just For Laughs Chicago\, The New York Comedy Festival\, Austin’s South b
 y Southwest festival\, San Francisco SketchFest\, and many more. Roy has b
 een featured on HBO’s Funny as Hell series\; as well as on the Comedy Cent
 ral shows Adam DeVine’s House Party\, Corporate\, @midnight\, and This Is 
 Not Happening. Ben has also released four stand-up comedy albums and was l
 isted as one of Variety’s Top 10 Comics to Watch.</p>\n<p>Along with fello
 w Denver Comedians Adam Cayton-Holland and Andrew Orvedahl (who collective
 ly perform as The Grawlix)\, Ben created\, wrote\, and starred in TruTV’s 
 original comedy series Those Who Can’t\, which now has all three seasons a
 vailable for streaming on HBOMax. In addition to stand-up comedy\, Roy is 
 a prolific musician\, currently the lead singer of pop punk outfit SPELLS.
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
