BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126473@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://mcpl.info/friends/power-words-ashley-hope-perez-and-jacinda
 -townsend
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an inspiring program dedicated to amplifying authen
 tic voices and celebrating the richness of diversity in literature\, featu
 ring acclaimed authors Ashley Hope Pérez and Jacinda Townsend in conversat
 ion with Yael Ksander as they explore the transformative power of storytel
 ling.\nThe Power of Words: Changing Our World\, One Story at a Time is a b
 iennial partnership between The Friends of the Library and Monroe County P
 ublic Library to create a visible community of readers by hosting an autho
 r writing on important topics of our time—and more specifically\, topics t
 hat speak to the average citizen’s ability to positively change the world 
 in which we live. Join in the community of Monroe County readers sharing a
 nd discussing award-winning authors Ashley Hope Peréz\, author of Out of D
 arkness\, and Jacinda Townsend\, author of Mother Country. \nOut of Darkne
 ss received the American Library Association’s Michael L. Printz Award for
  Literacy and Mother Country received the Ernest J. Gaines Award for Liter
 ary Excellence.\nAshley Hope Pérez\, an author of young adult fiction with
  a passion for representation\, brings her background as an educator and h
 er deep connections with her students to her writing. Her critically accla
 imed works\, including Out of Darkness and The Knife and the Butterfly\, o
 ffers an honest look into the lives of young people in the margins of soci
 ety. Pérez’s stories steer clear of stereotypes and generalizations\, pres
 enting complex characters and nuanced narratives that reflect real-life ex
 periences.\nJacinda Townsend\, an author of adult fiction\, brings a rich 
 tapestry of lived experiences from her upbringing in Kentucky and travels 
 throughout the world. Her novel Mother Country offers a compelling explora
 tion into motherhood and survival\, inspired by real-life encounters with 
 modern-day slavery and human trafficking in Côte d’Ivoire\, Morocco\, and 
 Mali. Her award-winning Saint Monkey\, a vibrant coming-of-age story set i
 n 1950s Eastern Kentucky and the Harlem Jazz scene provides a powerful exp
 loration of personal and cultural histories. \nThese programs are supporte
 d by the Paula B. Anderson Endowment for The Power of Words.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241109T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241109T201500
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Power of Words: Changing Our World\, One Story at a Time\, feat
 uring Ashley Hope Peréz and Jacinda Townsend
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-power-of-words/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us for a
 n inspiring program dedicated to amplifying authentic voices and celebrati
 ng the richness of diversity in literature\, featuring acclaimed authors A
 shley Hope Pérez and Jacinda Townsend in conversation with Yael Ksander as
  they explore the transformative power of storytelling.</p>\n<p><strong>Th
 e Power of Words: Changing Our World\, One Story at a Time</strong> is a b
 iennial partnership between The Friends of the Library and Monroe County P
 ublic Library to create a visible community of readers by hosting an autho
 r writing on important topics of our time—and more specifically\, topics t
 hat speak to the average citizen’s ability to positively change the world 
 in which we live. Join in the community of Monroe County readers sharing a
 nd discussing award-winning authors <strong>Ashley Hope Peréz</strong>\, a
 uthor of Out of Darkness\, and <strong>Jacinda Townsend</strong>\, author 
 of Mother Country. </p>\n<p>Out of Darkness received the American Library 
 Association’s Michael L. Printz Award for Literacy and Mother Country rece
 ived the Ernest J. Gaines Award for Literary Excellence.</p>\n<p><strong>A
 shley Hope Pérez</strong>\, an author of young adult fiction with a passio
 n for representation\, brings her background as an educator and her deep c
 onnections with her students to her writing. Her critically acclaimed work
 s\, including Out of Darkness and The Knife and the Butterfly\, offers an 
 honest look into the lives of young people in the margins of society. Pére
 z’s stories steer clear of stereotypes and generalizations\, presenting co
 mplex characters and nuanced narratives that reflect real-life experiences
 .</p>\n<p><strong>Jacinda Townsend</strong>\, an author of adult fiction\,
  brings a rich tapestry of lived experiences from her upbringing in Kentuc
 ky and travels throughout the world. Her novel Mother Country offers a com
 pelling exploration into motherhood and survival\, inspired by real-life e
 ncounters with modern-day slavery and human trafficking in Côte d’Ivoire\,
  Morocco\, and Mali. Her award-winning Saint Monkey\, a vibrant coming-of-
 age story set in 1950s Eastern Kentucky and the Harlem Jazz scene provides
  a powerful exploration of personal and cultural histories. </p>\n<p>These
  programs are supported by the Paula B. Anderson Endowment for The Power o
 f Words.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
