BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-128839@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Amped at IU features unique guitars and other instruments from 
 The Jim Irsay Collection\, IU Jacobs School of Music\, and Traditional Art
 s Indiana.\n\n\nAmped at IU highlights the history of the modern guitar an
 d allows patrons to survey some of the most important and iconic instrumen
 ts of the last 70 years. It reflects on how guitars and similar stringed i
 nstruments have impacted popular music genres including jazz\, country\, f
 olk\, and especially rock and roll.\nThe year-long exhibition will feature
  guitars not normally seen on The Jim Irsay Collection tour\, including an
  1850s CF Martin guitar\, 1910 Gibson Model U Harp Guitar\, 1939 Rickenbac
 ker Silver Hawaiian Lap Steel\, 1950 Epiphone Electar Lap Steel\, 1954 Gib
 son #B-1 electric bass\, 1959 Fender Stratocaster Sunburst\, 1959 Gibson L
 es Paul Standard\, 1964 Firebird V\, and 1971 Fender Telecaster Rosewood. 
 It also highlights instruments held by the IU Jacobs School of Music and I
 U’s Traditional Arts Indiana\, including an armadillo guitar\, banjo\, cav
 aquinho guitar\, cuarto\, dulcimer\, guitarron\, kora\, lute\, and oud.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241112T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241112T163000
LOCATION:McCalla School\, 525 E. 9th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Amped at IU: The Jim Irsay Guitar Collection
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/amped-at-iu-the-jim-irsay-guitar-collection/
X-COST-TYPE:free
