 > <span data-contrast='auto'>IU</span> <span data-contrast='auto'>Jacobs S
 chool of Music\, and Traditional Arts Indiana.</span></p>\n</div>\n<div id
 ='lw_cal_event_detail_description' class='lw_cal_event_detail_block'>\n<p>
 <span data-contrast='auto'><em>Amped at IU</em> highlights the history of 
 the moder</span><span data-contrast='auto'>n</span> <span data-contrast='a
 uto'>guitar and allows patrons to survey some of the most important and ic
 onic instruments of the last 70 years. It reflects on how guitars and simi
 lar stringed instruments have impacted popular music genres including jazz
 \, country\, folk\, and especially rock and roll.</span></p>\n<p><span dat
 a-contrast='auto'>The year-long exhibition will feature guitars not normal
 ly seen on The Jim Irsay Collection tour\, including an 1850s CF Martin gu
 itar\, 1910 Gibson Model U Harp Guitar\, 1939 Rickenbacker Silver Hawaiian
  Lap Steel\, 1950 Epiphone Electar Lap Steel\, 1954 Gibson #B-1 electric b
 ass\, 1959 Fender Stratocaster Sunburst\, 1959 Gibson Les Paul Standard\, 
 1964 Firebird V\, and 1971 Fender Telecaster Rosewood. It also highlights 
 instruments held by the IU Jacobs School of Music and IU’s Traditional Art
 s Indiana\, including an armadillo guitar\, banjo\, cavaquinho guitar\, cu
 arto\, dulcimer\, guitarron\, kora\, lute\, and oud.</span></p>\n</div>\n<
 /BODY></HTML>
