BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126980@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.comedyattic.com/events/97826
DESCRIPTION:Door Time: 6:00 PM\nJay Jurden is a New York based comedian\, w
 riter and actor. Originally from Mississippi\, Jay regularly performs come
 dy all over the country. He was recently a Staff Writer for Apple TV+’s  E
 mmy-nominated show\, The Problem With Jon Stewart. \nJay has performed on 
 The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon three times and has also been seen 
 on The Late Late Show with James Corden\, Comedy Central Featuring\, The L
 ate Show with Stephen Colbert\, and HBO’s High Maintenance. \nJay was name
 d one of Variety’s 10 Comics to Watch in 2022. His album\, Jay Jurden Y’al
 l\, debuted #1 on iTunes. Jay has written for numerous publications includ
 ing: Vulture\, Teen Vogue\, McSweeney’s\, and The New Yorker. He has also 
 written for Marvel’s Voices: X-Men #1. He was listed on Vulture’s  Comedia
 ns You Should and Will Know in 2020 and was selected to be featured in Jus
 t for Laughs Festival’s New Faces in 2019.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241115T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241115T204500
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, upstairs at 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington (4th 
 and Walnut)
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;UNTIL=20241116T235959Z
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Jay Jurden: Back at The Comedy Attic!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/jay-jurden-back-at-the-comedy-attic-earlyshow/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Door 
 Time: 6:00 PM</strong><br />\nJay Jurden is a New York based comedian\, wr
 iter and actor. Originally from Mississippi\, Jay regularly performs comed
 y all over the country. He was recently a Staff Writer for Apple TV+’s  Em
 my-nominated show\, The Problem With Jon Stewart. </p>\n<p>Jay has perform
 ed on The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon three times and has also been
  seen on The Late Late Show with James Corden\, Comedy Central Featuring\,
  The Late Show with Stephen Colbert\, and HBO’s High Maintenance. </p>\n<p
 >Jay was named one of Variety’s 10 Comics to Watch in 2022. His album\, Ja
 y Jurden Y’all\, debuted #1 on iTunes. Jay has written for numerous public
 ations including: Vulture\, Teen Vogue\, McSweeney’s\, and The New Yorker.
  He has also written for Marvel’s Voices: X-Men #1. He was listed on Vultu
 re’s  Comedians You Should and Will Know in 2020 and was selected to be fe
 atured in Just for Laughs Festival’s New Faces in 2019. </p>\n</BODY></HTM
 L>
END:VEVENT
