BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-128902@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Orson Welles\, Joseph Cotten\, Carol Reed\, Robert Krasker\, an
 d Graham Greene combine talents to create one of the finest films ever mad
 e\, back in theaters as a 4K restoration in honor of its 75th anniversary.
  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAbout The Third Man\nPulp writer Holly Martins (Joseph 
 Cotten) arrives in a bombed-out\, post-war Vienna only to find his childho
 od friend Harry Lime (Orson Welles) dead\, perhaps by the hand of a myster
 ious “third man” present at the time of Harry’s death. Armed with his cons
 piracy theory\, he quickly stumbles headfirst into Harry’s shadowy underwo
 rld\, butting up against interference from British police officer Major Ca
 lloway (Trevor Howard) and falling head-over-heels for Harry’s grief-stric
 ken lover Anna (Alida Valli).
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241116T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:IU Cinema International Art House Series: THE THIRD MAN (1949)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/iu-cinema-international-art-house-series-the-thi
 rd-man-1949/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id='content
 ' class='collapsed individual-film__intro collapsed bg-none section'>\n<di
 v class='row'>\n<div class='layout'>\n<div class='text'>\n<p class='text s
 creening-highlight'><strong> Orson Welles\, Joseph Cotten\, Carol Reed\, R
 obert Krasker\, and Graham Greene combine talents to create one of the fin
 est films ever made\, back in theaters as a 4K restoration in honor of its
  75th anniversary. </strong></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div cla
 ss='section bg-none individual-film__intro'>\n<div class='row'>\n<div clas
 s='layout'>\n<div class='text'>\n<h3 class='visually-hidden'>About The Thi
 rd Man</h3>\n<p>Pulp writer Holly Martins (Joseph Cotten) arrives in a bom
 bed-out\, post-war Vienna only to find his childhood friend Harry Lime (Or
 son Welles) dead\, perhaps by the hand of a mysterious “third man” present
  at the time of Harry’s death. Armed with his conspiracy theory\, he quick
 ly stumbles headfirst into Harry’s shadowy underworld\, butting up against
  interference from British police officer Major Calloway (Trevor Howard) a
 nd falling head-over-heels for Harry’s grief-stricken lover Anna (Alida Va
 lli).</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
