BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-128901@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This program of black-and-white 16mm films explores different m
 eans of searching for purpose and a sense of belonging by queer individual
 s.\nDamned If You Don’t (Su Friedrich\, 1987\, digital) and First Comes Lo
 ve (Su Friedrich\, 1991\, 16mm): The characters in Su Friedrich’s Damned I
 f You Don’t and First Comes Love attempt to find solace and order by assim
 ilating themselves within traditional institutions that don’t quite fit th
 em\, such as religion and marriage\, only to find that these are catechist
 ically flawed. [Damned If You Don’t: 42 min\; drama\; English and German |
  First Comes Love: 22 min\; experimental\; English]\nWhich Is Scary (Paula
  Gauthier\, 1991\, 16mm): Which Is Scary takes the opposite approach of Fr
 iedrich’s films\, seeking to explore the similar feelings of alienation an
 d rejection shared across seven different LGBTQI+ portraits and determine 
 whether\, despite vastly differing circumstances\, these might have cause-
 and-effect relationships on how queer culture is formed. [15 min\; experim
 ental\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241116T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:IU Cinema Underground Film Series: CATECHISM-ICALLY FLAWED
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/iu-cinema-underground-film-series-catechism-ical
 ly-flawed/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>This program 
 of black-and-white 16mm films explores different means of searching for pu
 rpose and a sense of belonging by queer individuals.</p>\n<p><i><strong>Da
 mned If You Don’t </strong></i><strong>(Su Friedrich\, 1987\, digital) and
  </strong><i><strong>First Comes Love</strong></i><strong> (Su Friedrich\,
  1991\, 16mm):</strong> The characters in Su Friedrich’s<i> Damned If You 
 Don’t</i> and <i>First Comes Love</i> attempt to find solace and order by 
 assimilating themselves within traditional institutions that don’t quite f
 it them\, such as religion and marriage\, only to find that these are cate
 chistically flawed. [<i>Damned If You Don’t</i>: 42 min\; drama\; English 
 and German | <i>First Comes Love</i>: 22 min\; experimental\; English]</p>
 \n<p><i><strong>Which Is Scary</strong></i><strong> (Paula Gauthier\, 1991
 \, 16mm):</strong> <i>Which Is Scary</i> takes the opposite approach of Fr
 iedrich’s films\, seeking to explore the similar feelings of alienation an
 d rejection shared across seven different LGBTQI+ portraits and determine 
 whether\, despite vastly differing circumstances\, these might have cause-
 and-effect relationships on how queer culture is formed. [15 min\; experim
 ental\; English]</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-128979@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Moving Canvas: An Experimental Dance Jam Hosted by Utam Moses\n
 Move. Connect. Create.\nEnter the unknown together! Experience the magic o
 f spontaneous expression in a space of reciprocity as we explore the impul
 ses of the body\, sound and silence. An Experimental Jam is a space to com
 e together and explore presence and move into innate creativity beyond wha
 t we may think is possible.\nBegin your journey with a intentional warm-up
  to awaken your senses\, practices to open deepened listening\, deepened s
 eeing and collaborative potential. Then the space is yours to move freely 
 inspired by the live\, innovative sounds of Fractured. This new improvisat
 ional ensemble features Kyle Quass on trumpet\, Julian Douglas on percussi
 on\, and Brendan Keller-Tuberg on bass\, pushing the boundaries of contemp
 orary music. We will weave the improvised space together.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241116T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241116T213000
LOCATION:Windfall Dancers\, 1101 N Dunn St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Moving Canvas: An Experimental Dance Jam Hosted by Utam Moses
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/moving-canvas-an-experimental-dance-jam-hosted-b
 y-utam-moses/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='xdj2
 66r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs'>Moving Canvas: An Experimental Danc
 e Jam Hosted by Utam Moses</div>\n<div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1
 vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Move. Connect. Create.</div>\n<div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr 
 x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Enter the unknown together! Experience the magic
  of spontaneous expression in a space of reciprocity as we explore the imp
 ulses of the body\, sound and silence. An Experimental Jam is a space to c
 ome together and explore presence and move into innate creativity beyond w
 hat we may think is possible.</div>\n<div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r
  x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Begin your journey with a intentional warm-up to awaken 
 your senses\, practices to open deepened listening\, deepened seeing and c
 ollaborative potential. Then the space is yours to move freely inspired by
  the live\, innovative sounds of Fractured. This new improvisational ensem
 ble features Kyle Quass on trumpet\, Julian Douglas on percussion\, and Br
 endan Keller-Tuberg on bass\, pushing the boundaries of contemporary music
 . We will weave the improvised space together.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127972@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.mitchelloperahouse.com/event/nightflyer/
DESCRIPTION:Doors will open at 6:15 p.m.\nFounded in 2016\, NIGHTFLYER is c
 omposed of veteran central Kentucky area members. The music is performed t
 o exacting standards of the universally loved band\, The Eagles.\nOur core
  audience includes both country and rock fans due to the iconic songs from
  the number one selling album of all time\, The Eagles Greatest Hits (1971
 -1975). We play every song from that album plus several other hits that ar
 e familiar to all ages and genres\, sure to please a wide spectrum of atte
 ndees to your events.\nWe believe in the power of music to bring people to
 gether and inspire joy through music. Our core values include meticulous r
 eproduction of the classic Eagles sound\, commitment to provide our highes
 t standards of performance and the reliability that our reputation has pro
 vided since 2016.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241116T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241116T210000
LOCATION:Mitchell Opera House\, 217 N 7th St\, Mitchell
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Nightflyer
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/nightflyer/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  will open at 6:15 p.m.</strong><br />\nFounded in 2016\, NIGHTFLYER is co
 mposed of veteran central Kentucky area members. The music is performed to
  exacting standards of the universally loved band\, The Eagles.</p>\n<p>Ou
 r core audience includes both country and rock fans due to the iconic song
 s from the number one selling album of all time\, The Eagles Greatest Hits
  (1971-1975). We play every song from that album plus several other hits t
 hat are familiar to all ages and genres\, sure to please a wide spectrum o
 f attendees to your events.</p>\n<p>We believe in the power of music to br
 ing people together and inspire joy through music. Our core values include
  meticulous reproduction of the classic Eagles sound\, commitment to provi
 de our highest standards of performance and the reliability that our reput
 ation has provided since 2016.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
