UID:ai1ec-127068@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:follies@wfhb.org\; https://wfhb.org/category/arts-entertainment/fol
 lies/
DESCRIPTION:Doors open at 1 PM\nThe Firehouse Follies is a worldwide showca
 se for the amazing talent we have in Bloomington and South Central Indiana
 . A live broadcast performance features audio theatre plays and comedy ske
 tches by the Mighty Firehouse Art Players\, music from Kid Kazooey and the
  Four-Alarm Orchestra\, special musical guest Krista Detor\, and poetry cr
 eated by Indiana’s Literary Champion\, Tony Brewer. \nWe’ll have a lot of 
 fun taking a sideways look at our community — and the audience becomes par
 t of the show! Come join us at the Waldron Auditorium\, November 17 – door
 s open at 1 p.m. and the Waldron now features a full bar. Starting at 2\, 
 the show will be sponsored by\, and broadcast and streamed live over WFHB\
 , 91.3 FM and http://www.wfhb.org\nTickets available at the door or in adv
 ance from the Buskirk-Chumley Box Office https://buskirkchumley.org/events
 / (phone 812-323-3020)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241117T160000
LOCATION:The Waldron Auditorium\, 122 S Walnut St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Firehouse Follies: Keep Bloomington Weird!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-firehouse-follies-keep-bloomington-weird/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  open at 1 PM</strong><br />\nThe Firehouse Follies is a worldwide showcas
 e for the amazing talent we have in Bloomington and South Central Indiana.
  A live broadcast performance features audio theatre plays and comedy sket
 ches by the Mighty Firehouse Art Players\, music from Kid Kazooey and the 
 Four-Alarm Orchestra\, special musical guest Krista Detor\, and poetry cre
 ated by Indiana’s Literary Champion\, Tony Brewer. </p>\n<p>We’ll have a l
 ot of fun taking a sideways look at our community — and the audience becom
 es part of the show! Come join us at the Waldron Auditorium\, November 17 
 – doors open at 1 p.m. and the Waldron now features a full bar. Starting a
 t 2\, the show will be sponsored by\, and broadcast and streamed live over
  WFHB\, 91.3 FM and http://www.wfhb.org</p>\n<p>Tickets available at the d
 oor or in advance from the Buskirk-Chumley Box Office https://buskirkchuml
 ey.org/events/ (phone 812-323-3020)</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
