BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-129063@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The enthralling true story of how journalists Carl Bernstein an
 d Bob Woodward exposed one of the biggest political scandals in American h
 istory.  \nWatergate looms large in both American political consciousness 
 and in the mythos surrounding the practice of investigative reporting. Bas
 ed on the bestselling book by Bob Woodward and Carl Bernstein\, whose repo
 rting on Watergate won a Pulitzer Prize for the Washington Post\, Robert R
 edford and Dustin Hoffman portray the journalists as they work to unravel 
 the scandal that ultimately led to the resignation of President Nixon. [13
 8 min\; drama\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241120T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: ALL THE PRESIDENT’S MEN (Q and A with Carl Bernstein to follo
 w screening)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-all-the-presidents-men-q-and-a-with-carl-be
 rnstein-to-follow-screening/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>The e
 nthralling true story of how journalists Carl Bernstein and Bob Woodward e
 xposed one of the biggest political scandals in American history.  </stron
 g></p>\n<p>Watergate looms large in both American political consciousness 
 and in the mythos surrounding the practice of investigative reporting. Bas
 ed on the bestselling book by Bob Woodward and Carl Bernstein\, whose repo
 rting on Watergate won a Pulitzer Prize for the <i>Washington Post\, </i>R
 obert Redford and Dustin Hoffman portray the journalists as they work to u
 nravel the scandal that ultimately led to the resignation of President Nix
 on. [138 min\; drama\; English]</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
