BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-129469@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we welcome the Poetry Potluck Tour to Morgenstern Bo
 oks!\nFeatured poets: Kelsey Bigelow\, Caleb “The Negro Artist” Rainey\, a
 nd Naomi G. Lau.\nMidwestern poets Kelsey Bigelow and Caleb “The Negro Art
 ist” Rainey host the Instagram project called “Poetry Potluck.” Every firs
 t Monday of the month\, their audiences send in random words and then they
  write a poem using those words. Audiences are invited to join in the fun 
 by writing their own and sending them in to be published in the annual Poe
 try Potluck Anthology. This showcase event is part of the 2023 Poetry Potl
 uck Anthology Tour\, and we will highlight local poet\, Naomi G. Lau\, who
  has published poems in the anthology. Following the showcase\, the public
  is invited to share their poetry on the open mic! Come join the potluck!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241205T180000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books\, 849 Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Poetry Potluck Tour and Open Mic
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/poetry-potluck-tour-and-open-mic/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us as we
  welcome the Poetry Potluck Tour to Morgenstern Books!<br />\nFeatured poe
 ts: Kelsey Bigelow\, Caleb “The Negro Artist” Rainey\, and Naomi G. Lau.<b
 r />\nMidwestern poets Kelsey Bigelow and Caleb “The Negro Artist” Rainey 
 host the Instagram project called “Poetry Potluck.” Every first Monday of 
 the month\, their audiences send in random words and then they write a poe
 m using those words. Audiences are invited to join in the fun by writing t
 heir own and sending them in to be published in the annual Poetry Potluck 
 Anthology. This showcase event is part of the 2023 Poetry Potluck Antholog
 y Tour\, and we will highlight local poet\, Naomi G. Lau\, who has publish
 ed poems in the anthology. Following the showcase\, the public is invited 
 to share their poetry on the open mic! Come join the potluck!</p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
