BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-129554@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Andrew Scott stuns in this one-man retelling of Chekhov’s class
 ic black comedy Uncle Vanya.\nAbout Vanya\nAndrew Scott (Fleabag\, All of 
 Us Strangers) brings multiple characters to life in Simon Stephens’ (The C
 urious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time) radical new version of Chekh
 ov’s Uncle Vanya. Hopes\, dreams\, and regrets are thrust into sharp focus
  in this one-man adaptation which explores the complexities of human emoti
 ons. Ivan (Uncle Vanya) has spent his life managing the estate and busines
 s affairs of his family with little regard for his efforts. Scott plays th
 e titular character\, retired professor Alexander and his daughter Sonia\,
  Alexander’s second wife Helena\, Vanya’s widowed mother Maureen\, his rom
 antic rival the country doctor Michael\, and more. Filmed live during the 
 play’s sold-out run in London’s West End. [100 min\; drama\; English with 
 open captions]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241208T130000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:IU Cinema presents National Theater Live: VANYA
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/iu-cinema-presents-national-theater-live-vanya/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> Andrew Scott
  stuns in this one-man retelling of Chekhov’s classic black comedy Uncle V
 anya.<br />\nAbout Vanya<br />\nAndrew Scott (Fleabag\, All of Us Stranger
 s) brings multiple characters to life in Simon Stephens’ (The Curious Inci
 dent of the Dog in the Night-Time) radical new version of Chekhov’s Uncle 
 Vanya. Hopes\, dreams\, and regrets are thrust into sharp focus in this on
 e-man adaptation which explores the complexities of human emotions. Ivan (
 Uncle Vanya) has spent his life managing the estate and business affairs o
 f his family with little regard for his efforts. Scott plays the titular c
 haracter\, retired professor Alexander and his daughter Sonia\, Alexander’
 s second wife Helena\, Vanya’s widowed mother Maureen\, his romantic rival
  the country doctor Michael\, and more. Filmed live during the play’s sold
 -out run in London’s West End. [100 min\; drama\; English with open captio
 ns]</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
