BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-129652@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:All Static & Noise is an award-winning documentary on the Uyghu
 r crisis by American director David Novack. The film\, which exposes both 
 the enormity of state-sponsored oppression and the individual struggles un
 der horrific conditions\, is the result of a five-year collaboration with 
 Uyghur diaspora communities and 21 partner organizations across seven coun
 tries. An original score\, animation\, and the use of illustrations from t
 he Uyghur Transitional Justice Database’s virtual reality camp project off
 er a chilling and emotional complement to the first-hand testimony from ca
 mp survivors and family members enduring this tragedy\, including Jewher I
 lham and Abduweli Ayup\, among others. Filmed partially at IU. [102 min\; 
 documentary\; English\, Uyghur\, Kazakh\, and Mandarin with English subtit
 les]\nA Q&A with Gardner Bovingdon (IU Central Eurasian Studies)\, associa
 te producer Jewher Ilham\, and co-writer/co-producer Janice Englehart will
  follow the screening.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241210T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film – a Human Rights Day Screening: ALL STATIC AND NOISE
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-human-rights-day-screening-all-static-and-n
 oise/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>All Static & 
 Noise is an award-winning documentary on the Uyghur crisis by American dir
 ector David Novack. The film\, which exposes both the enormity of state-sp
 onsored oppression and the individual struggles under horrific conditions\
 , is the result of a five-year collaboration with Uyghur diaspora communit
 ies and 21 partner organizations across seven countries. An original score
 \, animation\, and the use of illustrations from the Uyghur Transitional J
 ustice Database’s virtual reality camp project offer a chilling and emotio
 nal complement to the first-hand testimony from camp survivors and family 
 members enduring this tragedy\, including Jewher Ilham and Abduweli Ayup\,
  among others. Filmed partially at IU. [102 min\; documentary\; English\, 
 Uyghur\, Kazakh\, and Mandarin with English subtitles]</p>\n<p>A Q&A with 
 Gardner Bovingdon (IU Central Eurasian Studies)\, associate producer Jewhe
 r Ilham\, and co-writer/co-producer Janice Englehart will follow the scree
 ning.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
