BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-129915@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Synopsis: While out looking for a Christmas tree one winter day
 \, siblings François and Katou encounter a bizarrely dressed entity who em
 anates bubbles and shoplifts from a convenience store. With Katou convince
 d this “man” is really a Martian\, the children follow his green trail all
  the way to a flying saucer. After confirming his alien identity\, they fo
 rm an instant bond and pool their efforts to fix the Martian’s damaged spa
 ceship\, so he can return to his home planet. Meanwhile\, the police join 
 forces with a vigilante mob to track down this mysterious visitor and put 
 his antics to an end.\nA viable contender for weirdest Canadian movie of a
 ll time\, The Christmas Martian takes family-friendly holiday entertainmen
 t to imaginatively inspired new places. With a uniquely carefree and child
 -like approach\, director Bernard Gosselin (making his one and only fictio
 n feature) paved the way for producer Rock Demers’ celebrated Tales for Al
 l series and arguably even E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial. The Christmas Marti
 an is a misunderstood (and underseen) holiday gift that keeps on giving.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241219T190000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema: The Christmas Martian (1971) ALL AGES
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-the-christmas-martin-1971-all-ages
 /
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Synopsis: Whi
 le out looking for a Christmas tree one winter day\, siblings François and
  Katou encounter a bizarrely dressed entity who emanates bubbles and shopl
 ifts from a convenience store. With Katou convinced this “man” is really a
  Martian\, the children follow his green trail all the way to a flying sau
 cer. After confirming his alien identity\, they form an instant bond and p
 ool their efforts to fix the Martian’s damaged spaceship\, so he can retur
 n to his home planet. Meanwhile\, the police join forces with a vigilante 
 mob to track down this mysterious visitor and put his antics to an end.<br
  />\nA viable contender for weirdest Canadian movie of all time\, The Chri
 stmas Martian takes family-friendly holiday entertainment to imaginatively
  inspired new places. With a uniquely carefree and child-like approach\, d
 irector Bernard Gosselin (making his one and only fiction feature) paved t
 he way for producer Rock Demers’ celebrated Tales for All series and argua
 bly even E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial. The Christmas Martian is a misunderst
 ood (and underseen) holiday gift that keeps on giving.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
