BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130010@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Shanda Sung is a comedian from Bloomington\, Indiana. Her stand
  up has been seen by audiences throughout the Midwest. Shanda was featured
  on the album On Tour Live from Bloomington and the premiere episode of th
 e Vice network show Hunters.\nShe has been featured at the Limestone Comed
 y Festival\, the Milwaukee Comedy Festival and the Finger Lakes Comedy Fes
 tival. She is the co-host of the podcast Passing Notes with Ashley and Sha
 nda. Shanda’s comedy is a look into her sometimes absurd life as a mother\
 , woman and human being\, but audiences only need to be one of those 3 to 
 find her relatable and hilarious.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241220T200000
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, Corner of 4th and Walnut (upstairs)\, Bloomingt
 on
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20241221T200000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Shanda Sung
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/shanda-sung/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Shanda Sung i
 s a comedian from Bloomington\, Indiana. Her stand up has been seen by aud
 iences throughout the Midwest. Shanda was featured on the album On Tour Li
 ve from Bloomington and the premiere episode of the Vice network show Hunt
 ers.</p>\n<p>She has been featured at the Limestone Comedy Festival\, the 
 Milwaukee Comedy Festival and the Finger Lakes Comedy Festival. She is the
  co-host of the podcast Passing Notes with Ashley and Shanda. Shanda’s com
 edy is a look into her sometimes absurd life as a mother\, woman and human
  being\, but audiences only need to be one of those 3 to find her relatabl
 e and hilarious.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
