BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-129952@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:“Anyone who has seen Moth Cock perform live music can’t help bu
 t wonder at the disconnect between the physical reality of what they see b
 efore their eyes in relation to the sounds that hit their skulls.” This du
 o from Kent\, OH has been wailing away for almost 2 decades\, mixing their
  own blend of psychotic free-jazz tinged with psychedelic noise.\n Learn N
 ot to Lather: In this collaboration\, Josh Glinis and Ben Myers link their
  synthesizers together and into the visual dimension. Fusing digital circu
 its and analog tapes\, the two create slowly morphing sights and sounds th
 at will delight and mesmerize.\n Brett Alan Gershon explores sonic worlds 
 through his tinkering interests in electronic circuitry\, computer code\, 
 and electro-acoustic resonance.\n Guitars of Middle Western USA at it’s co
 re is the duo of John Dawson and Jordan Allen.These noodle-wranglers tap a
 nd strum out harmoniously to the middle western landscapes-a thickly heady
  fog settles over the cornfields as the moon disappears behind the clouds.
  You hear it everywhere you go: good times are coming and they’re sure com
 ing slow.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241228T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241228T230000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds from the Black Hole: Moth Cock / Learn Not To Lather / Brett
  Alan Gershon / Guitars of Middle Western USA
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-moth-cock-learn-not-t
 o-lather-brett-alan-gershon-gomwusa/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>“Anyone who h
 as seen Moth Cock perform live music can’t help but wonder at the disconne
 ct between the physical reality of what they see before their eyes in rela
 tion to the sounds that hit their skulls.” This duo from Kent\, OH has bee
 n wailing away for almost 2 decades\, mixing their own blend of psychotic 
 free-jazz tinged with psychedelic noise.<br />\n Learn Not to Lather: In t
 his collaboration\, Josh Glinis and Ben Myers link their synthesizers toge
 ther and into the visual dimension. Fusing digital circuits and analog tap
 es\, the two create slowly morphing sights and sounds that will delight an
 d mesmerize.<br />\n Brett Alan Gershon explores sonic worlds through his 
 tinkering interests in electronic circuitry\, computer code\, and electro-
 acoustic resonance.<br />\n Guitars of Middle Western USA at it’s core is 
 the duo of John Dawson and Jordan Allen.These noodle-wranglers tap and str
 um out harmoniously to the middle western landscapes-a thickly heady fog s
 ettles over the cornfields as the moon disappears behind the clouds. You h
 ear it everywhere you go: good times are coming and they’re sure coming sl
 ow.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
