BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130333@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Jill Vance\, Paynetown Activity Center on Monroe Lake\; 812-837-996
 7\; jvance@dnr.IN.gov\; http://bit.ly/monroefirstday
DESCRIPTION:Check-In / Same-day Registration: 2:15 p.m. to 3:15 p.m. (Fairf
 ax SRA: Bay View Shelter)\nRun / Walk Start Time: 3:30 p.m.\nThis is an un
 timed\, non-competitive run/walk. Choose from a 3.7-mile (map)\, 2.9-mile 
 (map)\, or 1.3-mile (map) course – and don’t forget to tap the bell and ri
 ng in the new year as you cross the finish line!\nAll registrations includ
 e…\n\nA food station with soup\, grilled cheese sandwiches\, hot cocoa\, a
 nd a wide variety of snacks.\nA ticket for the prize drawing\, which will 
 have TONS of great prizes!\nHundreds of free photos for you to download af
 ter the event.\nA large fire to keep you warm while waiting for the start 
 and enjoying food after you finish.\nSpecial note for leisurely walkers: P
 lease be aware that all courses close at 5 p.m. and the food station will 
 shut down shortly after that.\n\nThe FIRST 300 to register will get the 10
 0% embroidered\, collectible\, event patch!\nDogs are not encouraged but a
 re permitted. They must be on a leash of 6′ or less at all times\, and we 
 ask that you begin the run/walk at the back of the group.\nThis event is p
 resented by Monroe Lake (an Indiana State Park) and cosponsored by the Ind
 iana Trail Running Association. Proceeds support public events\, programs\
 , and interpretation at Monroe Lake.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250101T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250101T170000
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Fairfax State Recreation Area - Bay View Shelter\, 9
 301 S Fairfax Rd\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:12th Annual First Day Trail Run and Walk
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/first-day-trail-run-and-walk-2025/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Check-In / Sa
 me-day Registration: 2:15 p.m. to 3:15 p.m. (Fairfax SRA: Bay View Shelter
 )<br />\nRun / Walk Start Time: 3:30 p.m.</p>\n<p>This is an untimed\, non
 -competitive run/walk. Choose from a 3.7-mile (<a href='https://connect.ga
 rmin.com/modern/course/16519698'>map</a>)\, 2.9-mile (<a href='https://con
 nect.garmin.com/modern/course/47344648'>map</a>)\, or 1.3-mile (<a href='h
 ttps://connect.garmin.com/modern/course/16519720'>map</a>) course – and do
 n’t forget to tap the bell and ring in the new year as you cross the finis
 h line!</p>\n<p>All registrations include…</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A food station w
 ith soup\, grilled cheese sandwiches\, hot cocoa\, and a wide variety of s
 nacks.</li>\n<li>A ticket for the prize drawing\, which will have TONS of 
 great prizes!</li>\n<li>Hundreds of free photos for you to download after 
 the event.</li>\n<li>A large fire to keep you warm while waiting for the s
 tart and enjoying food after you finish.</li>\n<li>Special note for leisur
 ely walkers: Please be aware that all courses close at 5 p.m. and the food
  station will shut down shortly after that.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The FIRST 300 
 to register will get the 100% embroidered\, collectible\, event patch!</p>
 \n<p>Dogs are not encouraged but are permitted. They must be on a leash of
  6′ or less at all times\, and we ask that you begin the run/walk at the b
 ack of the group.</p>\n<p>This event is presented by Monroe Lake (an India
 na State Park) and cosponsored by the Indiana Trail Running Association. P
 roceeds support public events\, programs\, and interpretation at Monroe La
 ke.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
