BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130353@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Come one\, come all\, to another merry evening of wassailing! T
 his is the 2nd in our series of wassailing events the first having been in
  Bloomington.\nLet us drink the spiced spirits of apples\, honey\, and ber
 ries\, and go singing through the town! Let’s dress in our whimsical holid
 ay attire and bless some of our Spencer neighbors with song.\nWhat is Wass
 ailing? It’s something of a musical boozy trick or treating with origins i
 n the blessing of fruit trees\, it’s the original caroling and translates 
 to good health.\nSo let’s take this idea and make our own Yuletide Wassail
 ing Parade!\nRoute and times:\n2:00 – 2:30 Civilian Brewing (Meeting Place
  and drink)\n2:40 Main Street Coffee\n3:00 Dragonfly Gallery\n3:20 Jit’s T
 hai Bistro\n3:40 Lorelei\n4:10 Pride Center\n4:30 Civilian Brewing (Ending
  Place\, stay for dinner if you’d like)\nBusiness will be contacted ahead 
 of time and warned of our wacky plans.\nSafety and legal notes:\nNo Public
  Drinking\nNo Public Drunkenness\nThis event brought to you by Lost In The
  Woods Meadery\, and Civilian Brewing Corp\nThis event is all ages and we 
 will have some mulled cider for kids and none drinkers
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250104T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250104T164500
LOCATION:Civilian Brewing Corps\, 26 N Washington St\, Spencer
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Wassailing Part 2\, sponsored by Lost In the Woods Meadery and Civi
 lian Brewing
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/wassailing-part-2-sponsored-by-lost-in-the-woods
 -meadery-and-civilian-brewing/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Come one\, co
 me all\, to another merry evening of wassailing! This is the 2nd in our se
 ries of wassailing events the first having been in Bloomington.<br />\nLet
  us drink the spiced spirits of apples\, honey\, and berries\, and go sing
 ing through the town! Let’s dress in our whimsical holiday attire and bles
 s some of our Spencer neighbors with song.<br />\nWhat is Wassailing? It’s
  something of a musical boozy trick or treating with origins in the blessi
 ng of fruit trees\, it’s the original caroling and translates to good heal
 th.<br />\nSo let’s take this idea and make our own Yuletide Wassailing Pa
 rade!<br />\nRoute and times:<br />\n2:00 – 2:30 Civilian Brewing (Meeting
  Place and drink)<br />\n2:40 Main Street Coffee<br />\n3:00 Dragonfly Gal
 lery<br />\n3:20 Jit’s Thai Bistro<br />\n3:40 Lorelei<br />\n4:10 Pride C
 enter<br />\n4:30 Civilian Brewing (Ending Place\, stay for dinner if you’
 d like)<br />\nBusiness will be contacted ahead of time and warned of our 
 wacky plans.<br />\nSafety and legal notes:<br />\nNo Public Drinking<br /
 >\nNo Public Drunkenness<br />\nThis event brought to you by Lost In The W
 oods Meadery\, and Civilian Brewing Corp<br />\nThis event is all ages and
  we will have some mulled cider for kids and none drinkers</p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130419@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Ages: 10 – 18+ yrs\nBeginner stained-glass mosaic class\, where
  you’ll create a stunning piece of art using precut glass pieces\, ready t
 o be glued and grouted onto a red brick. In this hands-on workshop\, you’l
 l learn the fundamentals of mosaic art\, including how to design\, arrange
 \, and adhere glass pieces to create a beautiful\, colorful pattern or ima
 ge.\nOur instructor will guide you through the process\, demonstrating how
  to use adhesive to secure your glass pieces in place. Once your design is
  complete\, you’ll learn the proper techniques for grouting your mosaic\, 
 giving it a smooth and finished look. This class is perfect for beginners 
 looking to explore the world of stained-glass mosaics.\nAll materials\, in
 cluding a variety of colorful glass pieces\, adhesive\, and grout\, are pr
 ovided. Just bring your creativity and a willingness to learn! You’ll leav
 e with a gorgeous\, custom mosaic piece to proudly display or give as a gi
 ft.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250104T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250104T190000
LOCATION:Glassy Studios\, 1009 16th St\, Bedford\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Your Choice: “Snowman” or “Snowflake” Stained Glass Class
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/your-choice-snowman-or-snowflake-stained-glass-c
 lass/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Ages:
  10 – 18+ yrs</strong><br />\nBeginner stained-glass mosaic class\, where 
 you’ll create a stunning piece of art using precut glass pieces\, ready to
  be glued and grouted onto a red brick. In this hands-on workshop\, you’ll
  learn the fundamentals of mosaic art\, including how to design\, arrange\
 , and adhere glass pieces to create a beautiful\, colorful pattern or imag
 e.</p>\n<p>Our instructor will guide you through the process\, demonstrati
 ng how to use adhesive to secure your glass pieces in place. Once your des
 ign is complete\, you’ll learn the proper techniques for grouting your mos
 aic\, giving it a smooth and finished look. This class is perfect for begi
 nners looking to explore the world of stained-glass mosaics.</p>\n<p>All m
 aterials\, including a variety of colorful glass pieces\, adhesive\, and g
 rout\, are provided. Just bring your creativity and a willingness to learn
 ! You’ll leave with a gorgeous\, custom mosaic piece to proudly display or
  give as a gift.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
