BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-127984@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.mitchelloperahouse.com/event/backwoods-bluegrass/
DESCRIPTION:Doors will open at 6:15 p.m.\nComing from Southern Indiana\, Ba
 ckwoods is a traditional-style quartet bluegrass band that frequently inco
 rporates 90’s country hits and classic country into their set without stra
 ying too far away from the foundation of bluegrass music. With tight three
  part harmonies\, high energy\, and comradely between the band members\, e
 ach show is sure to be a unique and fun night for all!\nThe band has trave
 led all over Indiana and Kentucky including multiple shows at Holiday Worl
 d & Splashin’ Safari\, to Shipshewana Down Home Bluegrass Festival\, Nappa
 nee Apple Festival\, The Indiana Homesteading Conference\, to Brandenburg 
 Kentucky Homecoming Festival\, and Louisville\, Kentucky for many corporat
 e events.\n“Backwoods truly stretches the genre of bluegrass and brings to
 gether many music fans from all around!”\nBand members include Rusty Colli
 er\, Austin Harper\, Hunter Phillips\, and Sarah Stewart.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250111T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250111T210000
LOCATION:Mitchell Opera House\, 217 N 7th St\, Mitchell
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Backwoods Bluegrass
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/backwoods-bluegrass/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  will open at 6:15 p.m.</strong><br />\nComing from Southern Indiana\, Bac
 kwoods is a traditional-style quartet bluegrass band that frequently incor
 porates 90’s country hits and classic country into their set without stray
 ing too far away from the foundation of bluegrass music. With tight three 
 part harmonies\, high energy\, and comradely between the band members\, ea
 ch show is sure to be a unique and fun night for all!</p>\n<p>The band has
  traveled all over Indiana and Kentucky including multiple shows at Holida
 y World & Splashin’ Safari\, to Shipshewana Down Home Bluegrass Festival\,
  Nappanee Apple Festival\, The Indiana Homesteading Conference\, to Brande
 nburg Kentucky Homecoming Festival\, and Louisville\, Kentucky for many co
 rporate events.</p>\n<p>“Backwoods truly stretches the genre of bluegrass 
 and brings together many music fans from all around!”</p>\n<p>Band members
  include Rusty Collier\, Austin Harper\, Hunter Phillips\, and Sarah Stewa
 rt.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130637@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike around Lake Ogle
 ! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to excellent
  views of the lake. Learn about January’s full moon\, the Wolf Moon. Trail
  7 is rated moderate\, but should be considered rugged in the dark. The tr
 ail has some staircases\, uneven surfaces\, and muddy spots. It is 1.2 mil
 es and will take about an hour and a half to complete. Please do not bring
  pets on night hikes.   Red flashlights are preferred for night vision and
  can be loaned to hikers on request.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250111T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250111T203000
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Lake Ogle parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\,
  Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/full-moon-hike-brown-county-state-park-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join a park n
 aturalist for a guided night hike around Lake Ogle! The Full Moon is the b
 rightest night of the month\, leading to excellent views of the lake. Lear
 n about January’s full moon\, the Wolf Moon. <strong>Trail 7 is rated mode
 rate\, but should be considered rugged in the dark. The trail has some sta
 ircases\, uneven surfaces\, and muddy spots. It is 1.2 miles and will take
  about an hour and a half to complete. Please do not bring pets on night h
 ikes.   Red flashlights are preferred for night vision and can be loaned t
 o hikers on request.</strong>  </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
