BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130982@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A Silent Disco is an event where people dance to music heard th
 rough wireless headphones. The music is transmitted directly to each perso
 n’s headphones – on three separate channels – rather than played through s
 peakers. Those without headphones hear no music (other than people who sin
 g along to what they are hearing). The three channels of music can be sele
 cted using a simple switch on each person’s headphones\, and headphones li
 ght up blue\, red or green to show visually what channel you are listening
  to. People can dance to the same tune as others with them\, or to their o
 wn selection. If you hear a song you don’t like\, or get tired of a partic
 ular style of music\, just switch channels.\nProceeds will benefit Morgan 
 County Public Library Foundation\, a 501(c)3 organization that provides th
 e incredible Dolly Parton’s Imagination Library to children in Morgan Coun
 ty.\nPlaylists?\nBlue – a mix of 70’s and 80’s dance hits and 80’s and 90’
 s alternative rock (eg Rick James\, Devo\, B52’s)\nRed – current dance hit
 s & 90’s and 00’s hip hop (eg Dua Lipa\, Jack Harlow\, Taylor Swift)\nGree
 n – classic rock and danceable country tunes (Bon Jovi\, AC/DC\, Kenny Che
 sney)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250117T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250117T220000
LOCATION:Cedar Creek Winery\, Brewery and Distillery\, 3820 Leonard Road\, 
 Martinsville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Silent Disco
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/silent-disco/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>A Sil
 ent Disco is an event where people dance to music heard through wireless h
 eadphones.</strong> The music is transmitted directly to each person’s hea
 dphones – on three separate channels – rather than played through speakers
 . Those without headphones hear no music (other than people who sing along
  to what they are hearing). The three channels of music can be selected us
 ing a simple switch on each person’s headphones\, and headphones light up 
 blue\, red or green to show visually what channel you are listening to. Pe
 ople can dance to the same tune as others with them\, or to their own sele
 ction. If you hear a song you don’t like\, or get tired of a particular st
 yle of music\, just switch channels.<br />\nProceeds will benefit Morgan C
 ounty Public Library Foundation\, a 501(c)3 organization that provides the
  incredible Dolly Parton’s Imagination Library to children in Morgan Count
 y.<br />\nPlaylists?<br />\nBlue – a mix of 70’s and 80’s dance hits and 8
 0’s and 90’s alternative rock (eg Rick James\, Devo\, B52’s)<br />\nRed – 
 current dance hits & 90’s and 00’s hip hop (eg Dua Lipa\, Jack Harlow\, Ta
 ylor Swift)<br />\nGreen – classic rock and danceable country tunes (Bon J
 ovi\, AC/DC\, Kenny Chesney)</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
