BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130979@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:That’s right\, you read the title of this hike correctly\, The 
 Boulder in the Tree Hike. This hike is 2 miles round trip\, is quite rugge
 d and will take us about 1.5 hours to complete! The Boulder in the Tree ph
 enomenon is something we’ve seen in several places around Brown County inc
 luding here at the park and in Yellowwood State Forest. This is your chanc
 e to get out and see one of these boulders stuck in in a tree. The questio
 n is\, how did it get there? Come see it for yourself and make your most e
 ducated guess! This hike will be mostly off trail so please dress for the 
 weather and know there may be a couple creek crossings depending on how hi
 gh the water is. Boots are essential. Be prepared!\nPlease do not bring pe
 ts on off trail hikes.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250118T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250118T130000
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvil
 le
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Brown County State Park Winter Hike Series: Boulder in the Tree (se
 e notes for hike description)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/brown-county-state-park-winter-hike-series-bould
 er-in-the-tree-see-notes-for-hike-description/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>That’
 s right\, you read the title of this hike correctly\, The Boulder in the T
 ree Hike. This hike is 2 miles round trip\, is quite rugged and will take 
 us about 1.5 hours to complete! The Boulder in the Tree phenomenon is some
 thing we’ve seen in several places around Brown County including here at t
 he park and in Yellowwood State Forest. This is your chance to get out and
  see one of these boulders stuck in in a tree. The question is\, how did i
 t get there? Come see it for yourself and make your most educated guess! T
 his hike will be mostly off trail so please dress for the weather and know
  there may be a couple creek crossings depending on how high the water is.
  Boots are essential. Be prepared!</p>\n<p>Please do not bring pets on off
  trail hikes.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
