BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130152@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:DOOR TIME 5:30 pm\nThe City of Bloomington Dr. Martin Luther Ki
 ng Jr. Birthday Celebration Commission is excited to commemorate this year
 ’s event with the theme “A Necessary Renaissance in Social Justice: Tellin
 g the Stories to Ignite Change.”\nWe are thrilled to announce that Keith A
 . Beauchamp\, an acclaimed investigative journalist\, documentarian\, acti
 vist\, and filmmaker\, will be our keynote speaker for this significant oc
 casion. Beauchamp’s groundbreaking investigative reporting and his 2005 do
 cumentary were instrumental in prompting the State of Mississippi to reope
 n the murder case of Emmett Till. His long-term collaboration with Emmett’
 s mother culminated in the powerful feature film\, TILL\, which has receiv
 ed numerous nominations from the Screen Actors Guild Awards\, BAFTAs\, and
  Critics’ Choice Awards and is currently streaming on major platforms.\nTh
 e Birthday Celebration will also feature inspirational messages from local
  government and community leaders\, musical performances\, the Legacy Awar
 d presentation\, and more. \nLearn more at the Annual Dr. Martin Luther Ki
 ng Jr. Birthday Celebration page.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250120T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250120T203000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:2025 Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday Celebration: “A Necessary 
 Renaissance in Social Justice: Telling the Stories to Ignite Change.”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/2025-dr-martin-luther-king-jr-birthday-celebrati
 on-a-necessary-renaissance-in-social-justice-telling-the-stories-to-ignite
 -change/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>DOOR 
 TIME 5:30 pm</strong><br />\nThe City of Bloomington Dr. Martin Luther Kin
 g Jr. Birthday Celebration Commission is excited to commemorate this year’
 s event with the theme “A Necessary Renaissance in Social Justice: Telling
  the Stories to Ignite Change.”</p>\n<p>We are thrilled to announce that <
 strong>Keith A. Beauchamp</strong>\, an acclaimed investigative journalist
 \, documentarian\, activist\, and filmmaker\, will be our keynote speaker 
 for this significant occasion. Beauchamp’s groundbreaking investigative re
 porting and his 2005 documentary were instrumental in prompting the State 
 of Mississippi to reopen the murder case of Emmett Till. His long-term col
 laboration with Emmett’s mother culminated in the powerful feature film\, 
 TILL\, which has received numerous nominations from the Screen Actors Guil
 d Awards\, BAFTAs\, and Critics’ Choice Awards and is currently streaming 
 on major platforms.</p>\n<p>The Birthday Celebration will also feature ins
 pirational messages from local government and community leaders\, musical 
 performances\, the Legacy Award presentation\, and more. </p>\n<p>Learn mo
 re at the <a href='https://bloomington.in.gov/mlk-day/birthday-celebration
 '>Annual Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday Celebration</a> page.</p>\n</
 BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
