BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130158@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Film | Ages 21+\nSynopsis: A raucous work of queer fantasy and 
 history\, PLAYLAND conjures a time-bending night in Boston’s oldest and mo
 st notorious gay bar. \nWith an eclectic ensemble of queer performers\, in
 cluding drag icon Lady Bunny and Pose’s Danielle Cooper\, Playland is tran
 sdisciplinary in every sense of the word: music\, dance\, archival footage
 \, tableaux\, opera\, and performance art are layered into an ethereal pie
 ce subverting all boundaries. Artist-flmmaker Georden West’s debut feature
  is an expressionist and very queer bricolage\, focusing on an atemporal n
 ight in the renowned Playland Café. Following its employees and others who
  have haunted the space\, weaving together a tapestry of personal and comm
 unity anecdotes across the bar’s existence.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250123T200000
LOCATION:The Back Door\, in the alley at 207 S College Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents: PLAYLAND (2024\, NR)\, including video Q+A 
 with filmmaker
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-playland-2024-including-v
 ideo-qa-with-filmmaker/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Film 
 | Ages 21+</strong><br />\n<strong>Synopsis: </strong>A raucous work of qu
 eer fantasy and history\, <strong>PLAYLAND</strong> conjures a time-bendin
 g night in Boston’s oldest and most notorious gay bar. </p>\n<p>With an ec
 lectic ensemble of queer performers\, including drag icon Lady Bunny and P
 ose’s Danielle Cooper\, Playland is transdisciplinary in every sense of th
 e word: music\, dance\, archival footage\, tableaux\, opera\, and performa
 nce art are layered into an ethereal piece subverting all boundaries. Arti
 st-flmmaker Georden West’s debut feature is an expressionist and very quee
 r bricolage\, focusing on an atemporal night in the renowned Playland Café
 . Following its employees and others who have haunted the space\, weaving 
 together a tapestry of personal and community anecdotes across the bar’s e
 xistence.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
