BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130643@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:812-233-3286
DESCRIPTION:“Self Portrait” Linda Meyer-Wright\nLinda was an original BWS S
 ignature Member and a popular teacher who influenced a long list of studen
 t artists. She was extremely creative and prolific in many mediums\, but t
 his exhibit features primarily watercolors! Her art is reflective of her h
 umor and wit and her very vivid imagination\, making it a fun and happy sh
 ow.\nHosted by her sister Joanie Meyer\, it will feature 32 large\, profes
 sionally framed works of art. These paintings have not been recently displ
 ayed\, prior to this exhibit.  You will also have the opportunity to purch
 ase smaller\, unframed paintings from her studio.  All artwork is offered 
 at very reasonable prices.\nPlease join Joanie and friends at the receptio
 n on Friday\, January 24 – Linda’s birthday.  There will be cake!!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250124T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250124T190000
LOCATION:Bloomington Watercolor Society Gallery\, Cancer Support Community\
 , 1719 W 3rd St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Opening Reception: Linda Meyer-Wright\, 1946-2023 – In Retrospect
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/opening-reception-linda-meyer-wright-1946-2023-i
 n-retrospect/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>“Self Portrai
 t” Linda Meyer-Wright</p>\n<p>Linda was an original BWS Signature Member a
 nd a popular teacher who influenced a long list of student artists. She wa
 s extremely creative and prolific in many mediums\, but this exhibit featu
 res primarily watercolors! Her art is reflective of her humor and wit and 
 her very vivid imagination\, making it a fun and happy show.</p>\n<p>Hoste
 d by her sister Joanie Meyer\, it will feature 32 large\, professionally f
 ramed works of art. These paintings have not been recently displayed\, pri
 or to this exhibit.  You will also have the opportunity to purchase smalle
 r\, unframed paintings from her studio.  All artwork is offered at very re
 asonable prices.</p>\n<p>Please join Joanie and friends at the reception o
 n Friday\, January 24 – Linda’s birthday.  There will be cake!!</p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
END:VEVENT
