BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131032@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.orbitbtown.com/events/sftbh-bronze-giant-day-geodize
DESCRIPTION:6PM DOORS /// 7PM SHOW /// ALL-AGES\nBRONZE–\nThe seeds of Bron
 ze were planted\, curiously enough\, at an avant-garde Japanese noise show
 . Dylan Ryan and Scott McGaughey first met as teenagers at DePaul Universi
 ty in Chicago\, recognizing each other as having attended the same Ruins s
 how\, kindred spirits converging in the Chicago indie rock underground. Th
 ey played in various rock bands in the 90s\, but they found they had a par
 ticular itch that was not scratched by the various projects they were invo
 lved in\; a shared love for the likes of Robin Gibb\, Roxy Music and the s
 oundtracks of Tangerine Dream\, the kind of shimmering studio productions 
 that sound luxurious but still push the envelope.\nBronze on Bandcamp\nBro
 nze – Mezzanine on YouTube\n________________________\nGIANT DAY–\nGiant Da
 y is the new project of Elephant 6 Collective veterans Derek Almstead and 
 Emily Growden. Both longtime partners and established musicians\, they’ve 
 worked\, recorded and performed in Athens\, Georgia for many years with mu
 ltiple groups\, including The Olivia Tremor Control\, Circulatory System\,
  Elf Power\, The Glands\, of Montreal\, Faster Circuits and Marshmallow Co
 ast to name a few. This latest musical iteration combines psych\, art rock
 \, post-punk and dream pop influences into a distinctive new sound.\nGiant
  Day on Bandcamp\nGiant Day – Ignore the Flood on YouTube\n_______________
 _________\nGEODIZE–\nGeodize is Chris Barth’s current solo project.\nChris
  has also played in The Impossible Shapes\, Normanoak\, and Glitter Brains
 \, and lives and records in a holler in Brown County\, Indiana.\nGeodize o
 n Bandcamp
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250125T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250125T220000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, underground at 107 N College Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds From the Black Hole: Bronze // Giant Day // Geodize
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-bronze-giant-day-geod
 ize/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>6PM DOORS ///
  7PM SHOW /// ALL-AGES</p>\n<p><b>BRONZE</b>–<br />\nThe seeds of Bronze w
 ere planted\, curiously enough\, at an avant-garde Japanese noise show. Dy
 lan Ryan and Scott McGaughey first met as teenagers at DePaul University i
 n Chicago\, recognizing each other as having attended the same Ruins show\
 , kindred spirits converging in the Chicago indie rock underground. They p
 layed in various rock bands in the 90s\, but they found they had a particu
 lar itch that was not scratched by the various projects they were involved
  in\; a shared love for the likes of Robin Gibb\, Roxy Music and the sound
 tracks of Tangerine Dream\, the kind of shimmering studio productions that
  sound luxurious but still push the envelope.<br />\n<a href='https://bron
 zetheband.bandcamp.com/album/bronze' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-s
 aferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?q=https://bronzetheband.bandcam
 p.com/album/bronze&source=gmail&ust=1737388271347000&usg=AOvVaw3p_kZ-v3HkT
 kT4gHsYDCfn'>Bronze on Bandcamp</a><br />\n<a href='https://youtu.be/78oRL
 uVumFc?si=hk9u3SAMO1nKXigr' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-saferedire
 cturl='https://www.google.com/url?q=https://youtu.be/78oRLuVumFc?si%3Dhk9u
 3SAMO1nKXigr&source=gmail&ust=1737388271347000&usg=AOvVaw0XUEx9ovurkTI_GHM
 kw9pJ'>Bronze – Mezzanine on YouTube</a><br />\n________________________</
 p>\n<p><b>GIANT DAY</b>–<br />\nGiant Day is the new project of Elephant 6
  Collective veterans Derek Almstead and Emily Growden. Both longtime partn
 ers and established musicians\, they’ve worked\, recorded and performed in
  Athens\, Georgia for many years with multiple groups\, including The Oliv
 ia Tremor Control\, Circulatory System\, Elf Power\, The Glands\, of Montr
 eal\, Faster Circuits and Marshmallow Coast to name a few. This latest mus
 ical iteration combines psych\, art rock\, post-punk and dream pop influen
 ces into a distinctive new sound.<br />\n<a href='https://giantday.bandcam
 p.com/' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.g
 oogle.com/url?q=https://giantday.bandcamp.com/&source=gmail&ust=1737388271
 347000&usg=AOvVaw2xQYZcBUKnfyHIrrgHLr7y'>Giant Day on Bandcamp</a><br />\n
 <a href='https://youtu.be/rrWn7qiOmvc?si=B_X23vtFDeHxBiJh' target='_blank'
  rel='noopener' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?q=https:/
 /youtu.be/rrWn7qiOmvc?si%3DB_X23vtFDeHxBiJh&source=gmail&ust=1737388271347
 000&usg=AOvVaw3gMUiS_dcCQfVdNy3BKryR'>Giant Day – Ignore the Flood on YouT
 ube</a><br />\n________________________</p>\n<p><b>GEODIZE</b>–<br />\nGeo
 dize is Chris Barth’s current solo project.<br />\nChris has also played i
 n The Impossible Shapes\, Normanoak\, and Glitter Brains\, and lives and r
 ecords in a holler in Brown County\, Indiana.<br />\n<a href='https://geod
 ize.bandcamp.com/' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-saferedirecturl='ht
 tps://www.google.com/url?q=https://geodize.bandcamp.com/&source=gmail&ust=
 1737388271347000&usg=AOvVaw18rLaTYUQUtOb0-FraHAil'>Geodize on Bandcamp</a>
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
