BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131055@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Marion Mason\, Public Affairs Specialist\; (812) 277-6877\; Marion.
 Mason@usda.gov\; https://www.facebook.com/SCINWINGS
DESCRIPTION:Anyone is welcome to attend\, although programs are geared towa
 rd women age 16+.\nSeveral local natural resource and recreation organizat
 ions and agencies work together to offer outdoor recreation skills and nat
 ure knowledge programs\, with a model of women teaching women. To kick off
  the fifth season\, the organizers are hosting a Mini-Expo to offer a snea
 k peek at what’s in store for 2025\, reach new participants and give the o
 pportunity to meet and interact with the instructors.\nParticipants can dr
 op in to sample some past and future WINGS activities such as wild edibles
  foraging\, basket weaving\, outdoor cooking\, shooting\, fishing\, winter
  tree identification and stand-up paddleboarding. The event will also offe
 r themed snacks (while supplies last) and 2025 activity schedules.  \nThe 
 goal of Women in Nature Gaining Skills (WINGS) is to encourage and empower
  women with the skills and confidence they need to participate in outdoor 
 recreation activities in the south-central Indiana area. Each WINGS event 
 features women-led hands-on training\, with the goal of building a communi
 ty of women interested in outdoor recreation.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250126T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250126T130000
LOCATION:Karst Farm Park - Commons Building\, 5200 W Airport Rd\, Bloomingt
 on
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Women in Nature Gaining Skills (WINGS) Mini-Expo
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/women-in-nature-gaining-skills-wings-mini-expo/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Anyon
 e is welcome to attend\, although programs are geared toward women age 16+
 .</strong><br />\nSeveral local natural resource and recreation organizati
 ons and agencies work together to offer outdoor recreation skills and natu
 re knowledge programs\, with a model of women teaching women. To kick off 
 the fifth season\, the organizers are hosting a Mini-Expo to offer a sneak
  peek at what’s in store for 2025\, reach new participants and give the op
 portunity to meet and interact with the instructors.</p>\n<p>Participants 
 can drop in to sample some past and future WINGS activities such as wild e
 dibles foraging\, basket weaving\, outdoor cooking\, shooting\, fishing\, 
 winter tree identification and stand-up paddleboarding. The event will als
 o offer themed snacks (while supplies last) and 2025 activity schedules.  
 </p>\n<p>The goal of Women in Nature Gaining Skills (WINGS) is to encourag
 e and empower women with the skills and confidence they need to participat
 e in outdoor recreation activities in the south-central Indiana area. Each
  WINGS event features women-led hands-on training\, with the goal of build
 ing a community of women interested in outdoor recreation.</p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
END:VEVENT
