BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131297@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:About Flowers of Ukraine\nA strong\, independent\, and anarchis
 t woman full of humor sets out to protect her piece of land against all od
 ds. Initially fighting off developers\, Natalia’s struggle becomes even mo
 re existential with Russia’s attack on Ukraine. The film is a portrait of 
 a woman who never gives up and brings to viewers a sense of hope. [70 min\
 ; documentary\; Ukrainian with English subtitles]\nA Q&A with director Ade
 lina Borets will follow the screening.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250127T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: FLOWERS OF UKRAINE (Q&A with the filmmaker to follow)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-flowers-of-ukraine-qa-with-the-filmmaker-to
 -follow/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>About Flowers
  of Ukraine</p>\n<p>A strong\, independent\, and anarchist woman full of h
 umor sets out to protect her piece of land against all odds. Initially fig
 hting off developers\, Natalia’s struggle becomes even more existential wi
 th Russia’s attack on Ukraine. The film is a portrait of a woman who never
  gives up and brings to viewers a sense of hope. [70 min\; documentary\; U
 krainian with English subtitles]</p>\n<p>A Q&A with director Adelina Boret
 s will follow the screening.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131305@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:An exciting series of workshops\, readings\, and creative discu
 ssions. Join us for this early look at these works in development\, so one
  day you can say “I saw that play At First Sight”.  \nNow in its thirteent
 h year\, the At First Sight New Works Festival will feature the always pop
 ular At First Shorts evening of new short plays\, a series of panels hoste
 d by M.F.A. Dramaturgy students featuring theatre makers from the Indiana 
 community\, and playwriting workshops with special guests. Students are jo
 ined by industry professionals who provide their insight and expertise thr
 oughout the weekend.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250127T193000
LOCATION:Studio Theatre\, second floor of the Lee Norvelle Theatre and Dram
 a Center\, 275 N. Eagleson Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:At First Sight New Works Festival 2025\, Workshop reading the play 
 “Bite-sized” by Wren Latham
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/at-first-sight-new-works-festival-2025-workshop-
 reading-the-play-bite-sized-by-wren-latham/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>An exciting s
 eries of workshops\, readings\, and creative discussions. Join us for this
  early look at these works in development\, so one day you can say “I saw 
 that play At First Sight”.  </p>\n<p>Now in its thirteenth year\, the At F
 irst Sight New Works Festival will feature the always popular At First Sho
 rts evening of new short plays\, a series of panels hosted by M.F.A. Drama
 turgy students featuring theatre makers from the Indiana community\, and p
 laywriting workshops with special guests. Students are joined by industry 
 professionals who provide their insight and expertise throughout the weeke
 nd.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
