CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Kinsey (2004) is a look at the life of Alfred Kinsey\, a pionee
 r in the area of human sexuality research\, whose 1948 publication “Sexual
  Behavior in the Human Male” was one of the first recorded works that saw 
 science address sexual behavior.\nDirected by Bill Condon\, and starring L
 iam Neeson as Alfred Kinsey\, along with Laura Linney and Chris O’Donnell.
 \nPre-Film Speaker: Jessica Hille\, J.D.\, Ph.D. Assistant Director for Ed
 ucation / Clinical Assistant Professor at The Kinsey Institute
