UID:ai1ec-131464@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Flesh for Frankenstein\, aka Andy Warhol’s Frankenstein (despit
 e having at best a tenuous relationship to Warhol)\, is a delectably gory 
 and cynical social satire from acclaimed filmmaker Paul Morrissey\, who cr
 itiques gratuitous sexuality by those very same means. With an exceptional
  cast\, led by Udo Kier\, Joe Dallesandro\, Monique van Vooren\, and Itali
 an child star Nicoletta Elmi\, and featuring a lush soundtrack by Claudio 
 Gizzi\, Flesh for Frankenstein became an immediate midnight and cult movie
  sensation.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250131T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Underground Film Series: Flesh for Frankenstein
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/underground-film-series-flesh-for-frankenstein/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Flesh for Fra
 nkenstein\, aka Andy Warhol’s Frankenstein (despite having at best a tenuo
 us relationship to Warhol)\, is a delectably gory and cynical social satir
 e from acclaimed filmmaker Paul Morrissey\, who critiques gratuitous sexua
 lity by those very same means. With an exceptional cast\, led by Udo Kier\
 , Joe Dallesandro\, Monique van Vooren\, and Italian child star Nicoletta 
 Elmi\, and featuring a lush soundtrack by Claudio Gizzi\, Flesh for Franke
 nstein became an immediate midnight and cult movie sensation.</p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
