BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131288@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Sixteen years ago\, a group of IU students founded Raas Royalty
 \, one of the most prestigious Indian dance competitions. Raas Royalty sho
 wcases eight collegiate Raas dance teams from across the country and allow
 s them to compete for the crown! For the 16th year running\, Raas Royalty 
 is free of charge and continues to be the only free collegiate garba-raas 
 competition in the United States. Raas Royalty invites you to learn more a
 bout Indian culture and to watch creative and energetic performances from 
 the best teams across the country.\nWhat is Garba-Raas?\nGarba and Raas ar
 e traditional forms of dance originating in Gujarat\, a region in India. B
 oth dance forms are performed during Navratri\, a nine-day celebration tha
 t celebrates the victory of good over evil. This form of devotional dance 
 (Raas) uses sticks called ‘dandiya’ and is a partner-oriented dance done t
 o the beat of the dhol drum. In recent years\, choreographed garba-raas ha
 s become increasingly popular at universities nationwide as competitions p
 rovide the outlet to showcase the talent and creative spin put on a timele
 ss tradition.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T170000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Raas Royalty
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/raas-royalty-4/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Sixteen years
  ago\, a group of IU students founded Raas Royalty\, one of the most prest
 igious Indian dance competitions. Raas Royalty showcases eight collegiate 
 Raas dance teams from across the country and allows them to compete for th
 e crown! For the 16th year running\, Raas Royalty is free of charge and co
 ntinues to be the only free collegiate garba-raas competition in the Unite
 d States. Raas Royalty invites you to learn more about Indian culture and 
 to watch creative and energetic performances from the best teams across th
 e country.<br />\nWhat is Garba-Raas?<br />\nGarba and Raas are traditiona
 l forms of dance originating in Gujarat\, a region in India. Both dance fo
 rms are performed during Navratri\, a nine-day celebration that celebrates
  the victory of good over evil. This form of devotional dance (Raas) uses 
 sticks called ‘dandiya’ and is a partner-oriented dance done to the beat o
 f the dhol drum. In recent years\, choreographed garba-raas has become inc
 reasingly popular at universities nationwide as competitions provide the o
 utlet to showcase the talent and creative spin put on a timeless tradition
 .</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
