BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130343@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to relive the ultimate ’80s Prom Night!\nTravel back 
 to the most iconic era of big hair\, neon vibes\, and tunes at our unforge
 ttable ’80s Prom! Whether you’re reliving your glory days or discovering i
 t for the first time\, this night is all about celebrating the best of the
  decade.\nWhat’s in store for you:\n\nRetro Appetizers & Small Bites: Enjo
 y bite-sized classics that will take you back in time.\nDJ Spinning ’80s H
 its: Dance the night away to the best of ’80s pop\, rock\, and new wave. T
 hink Madonna\, Michael Jackson\, and Guns N’ Roses!\nPhotobooth Fun: Strik
 e a pose with vintage props to capture the best of your ‘80s style.\nPunch
  Bowl Cocktails: Sip on delicious\, retro-inspired cocktails or head to th
 e cash bar for a refreshing drink that takes you back to the glory days. T
 he party never stops with a fully stocked bar featuring your favorite clas
 sic drinks.\nBest Dressed Contest: Channel your inner prom queen or king —
  the most stylish will win a prize worthy of their iconic ’80s look.\n\nDu
 st off those neon leg warmers\, tease your hair\, and get ready for the mo
 st epic ’80s prom party ever. Grab your tickets now and join us as we step
  back in time for an unforgettable night.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T220000
LOCATION:Hard Truth Distilling Co\, 418 Old State Rd 46\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:’80s Prom Night (21+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/80s-prom-night-21/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Get ready to 
 relive the ultimate ’80s Prom Night!</p>\n<p>Travel back to the most iconi
 c era of big hair\, neon vibes\, and tunes at our unforgettable ’80s Prom!
  Whether you’re reliving your glory days or discovering it for the first t
 ime\, this night is all about celebrating the best of the decade.</p>\n<p>
 What’s in store for you:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Retro Appetizers & Small B
 ites:</strong> Enjoy bite-sized classics that will take you back in time.<
 /li>\n<li><strong>DJ Spinning ’80s Hits:</strong> Dance the night away to 
 the best of ’80s pop\, rock\, and new wave. Think Madonna\, Michael Jackso
 n\, and Guns N’ Roses!</li>\n<li><strong>Photobooth Fun:</strong> Strike a
  pose with vintage props to capture the best of your ‘80s style.</li>\n<li
 ><strong>Punch Bowl Cocktails:</strong> Sip on delicious\, retro-inspired 
 cocktails or head to the cash bar for a refreshing drink that takes you ba
 ck to the glory days. The party never stops with a fully stocked bar featu
 ring your favorite classic drinks.</li>\n<li><strong>Best Dressed Contest:
 </strong> Channel your inner prom queen or king — the most stylish will wi
 n a prize worthy of their iconic ’80s look.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Dust off those
  neon leg warmers\, tease your hair\, and get ready for the most epic ’80s
  prom party ever. Grab your tickets now and join us as we step back in tim
 e for an unforgettable night.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130159@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Synopsis: Werner Herzog’s only horror film is as rich with arti
 stry and tragedy as his most grounded\, human work. It is 1850 in the beau
 tiful\, perfectly-kept town of Wismar. Jonathan Harker (Bruno Ganz) is lea
 ving on a long journey over the Carpathian Mountains to finalize real esta
 te arrangements with a wealthy nobleman. His wife Lucy (POSSESSION’s Isabe
 lle Adjani) begs him not to go and is troubled by a strong premonition of 
 danger. Despite her warnings\, Jonathan arrives four weeks later at a larg
 e\, gloomy castle. Out of the mist appears a pale\, wraith-like figure wit
 h deep-sunken eyes who identifies himself as Count Dracula (Klaus Kinski).
  The events that transpire slowly convince Harker that he is in the presen
 ce of a vampire. Even still\, he doesn’t realize the magnitude of danger h
 e\, his wife and his town are about to experience.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T204500
LOCATION:Upland Wood Shop\, 354 W 11th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents: Nosferatu the Vampyre (1979\, PG)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-nosferatu-the-vampyre-197
 9/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Synop
 sis:</strong> Werner Herzog’s only horror film is as rich with artistry an
 d tragedy as his most grounded\, human work. It is 1850 in the beautiful\,
  perfectly-kept town of Wismar. Jonathan Harker (Bruno Ganz) is leaving on
  a long journey over the Carpathian Mountains to finalize real estate arra
 ngements with a wealthy nobleman. His wife Lucy (POSSESSION’s Isabelle Adj
 ani) begs him not to go and is troubled by a strong premonition of danger.
  Despite her warnings\, Jonathan arrives four weeks later at a large\, glo
 omy castle. Out of the mist appears a pale\, wraith-like figure with deep-
 sunken eyes who identifies himself as Count Dracula (Klaus Kinski). The ev
 ents that transpire slowly convince Harker that he is in the presence of a
  vampire. Even still\, he doesn’t realize the magnitude of danger he\, his
  wife and his town are about to experience.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131417@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Ani DiFranco crashed onto the music scene in the early ‘90s\, a
  thundering new voice in the cultural wilderness\, unapologetically bisexu
 al\, political and feminist. She toured relentlessly\, thrashing out hundr
 eds of frenzied shows that were part mosh pit\, part hootenanny and part f
 ull-on tent revival\, then selling cassette tapes from the trunk of her ca
 r to make it to the next gig.\nAni became a worldwide phenomenon when she 
 beat the male-dominated music industry at its own game by founding Righteo
 us Babe Records\, the first “woman-run non-corporate queer-happy” label\, 
 still going strong after nearly 35 years. The press called her “an entrepr
 eneurial wonder” and “the industry’s worst nightmare.” Prince called her “
 my hero.” Ani simply called herself a folk singer\, dedicated to art\, act
 ivism and staying true to herself\, no matter the cost.\n1-800-ON-HER-OWN 
 takes us on a wild cinematic road trip\, from DiFranco’s punk-folk past to
  her life today as she reinvents herself as a passionate activist and reve
 red rock star. Throughout the ride\, she’s brutally honest\, famously foul
 -mouthed and totally hilarious. Her daily challenges resonate as we reveal
  both an enduring\, inspiring musical icon and a very relatable contempora
 ry “everywoman” with her own epic fails and hard-won victories.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T201500
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: 1-800-ON-HER-OWN (an Ani DiFranco Documentary)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-1-800-on-her-own-an-ani-difranco-documentar
 y/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Ani DiFranco 
 crashed onto the music scene in the early ‘90s\, a thundering new voice in
  the cultural wilderness\, unapologetically bisexual\, political and femin
 ist. She toured relentlessly\, thrashing out hundreds of frenzied shows th
 at were part mosh pit\, part hootenanny and part full-on tent revival\, th
 en selling cassette tapes from the trunk of her car to make it to the next
  gig.<br />\nAni became a worldwide phenomenon when she beat the male-domi
 nated music industry at its own game by founding Righteous Babe Records\, 
 the first “woman-run non-corporate queer-happy” label\, still going strong
  after nearly 35 years. The press called her “an entrepreneurial wonder” a
 nd “the industry’s worst nightmare.” Prince called her “my hero.” Ani simp
 ly called herself a folk singer\, dedicated to art\, activism and staying 
 true to herself\, no matter the cost.<br />\n1-800-ON-HER-OWN takes us on 
 a wild cinematic road trip\, from DiFranco’s punk-folk past to her life to
 day as she reinvents herself as a passionate activist and revered rock sta
 r. Throughout the ride\, she’s brutally honest\, famously foul-mouthed and
  totally hilarious. Her daily challenges resonate as we reveal both an end
 uring\, inspiring musical icon and a very relatable contemporary “everywom
 an” with her own epic fails and hard-won victories.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
