BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131596@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:When the harmony in a village is threatened by outside elements
 \, two sisters must fight to save their people and restore the glory of a 
 mermaid goddess to the land. This screening will be followed by a Q&A with
  Prof. Maria E. Hamilton Abegunde (IU African American and African Diaspor
 a Studies) on the integration of Yoruba folklore into visual culture.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250204T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: ‘MAMI WATA’ – Part of the series\, AfroFutures: Black Women a
 nd Cinematic Storytelling
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-mami-wata-part-of-the-series-afrofutures-bl
 ack-women-and-cinematic-storytelling/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>When the harm
 ony in a village is threatened by outside elements\, two sisters must figh
 t to save their people and restore the glory of a mermaid goddess to the l
 and. This screening will be followed by a Q&A with Prof. Maria E. Hamilton
  Abegunde (IU African American and African Diaspora Studies) on the integr
 ation of Yoruba folklore into visual culture.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
