BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130147@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:DOOR TIME 7:00 pm\nWarm those winter blues with some of Indiana
 ’s finest!\nKing Bee & The Stingers is a six-piece blues\, soul and funk b
 and from Bloomington\, Indiana. Formed in 2006 under the leadership of har
 monica player and vocalist Mark “King Bee” Menefee\, the band attracted a 
 strong following across Indiana and the Midwest\, playing classic\, gritty
  roadhouse blues. In 2015\, Mark’s daughter Sarah Menefee took over as lea
 d vocalist and has been a rising star ever since. King Bee & The Stingers 
 are 2018\, 2019\, and 2023 semifinalists in The Blues Foundation’s Interna
 tional Blues Challenge in Memphis\, TN.\nMike Milligan and Steam Shovel is
  an Original\, Powerful\, Soulful group from Kokomo\, Indiana\, United Sta
 tes\, formed in 1993\, comprised of brothers\, Mike Milligan (guitar/vocal
 s) and Shaun Milligan (bass)\, and Robert “Tiny” Cook (drums/vocals).\nThe
 y Celebrate 30… THIRTY Years! of touring and recording in 2023 with their 
 NEW Album on Mojo Hut Records\,… KOKOMO HONEY!\nThey were recently honored
  with an award for a Lifetime of Keeping the Blues alive by the Fishers Bl
 ues Festival (Indy) and performed for 5000 of their biggest fans w Robert 
 Cray Band (5th time!) And received an achievement award from the Mayor Of 
 Muncie Indiana for the 30th anniversary! They also performed a sold out sh
 ow w BB KING on his final Indiana show\, and recently with BUDDY GUY (for 
 the 4th time)\, Los Lonely Boys (2nd x)\, Jimmie Vaughan\, and Robert Cray
  (again! for the SIXTH time!) !\nWith 7 CD releases on Mojo Hut Records\, 
 100’s of Thousands of touring miles\, and several Thousands of performance
 s under their belts…. it’s always Full Steam ahead.\nGordon Bonham grew up
  in Hammond\, IN and brings together a mix of styles from the Mississippi 
 Delta to the back alleys of Chicago\, from big Texas shuffles to jumpin’ W
 est Coast swing. After several years of tearing up the road\, Bonham bring
 s it all together in Indiana\, the Crossroads of America. Bonham has perfo
 rmed several times with the legendary Pinetop Perkins\, most notably in Cl
 eveland along with Robert Lockwood\, Jr. as part of the grand opening of t
 he Rock and Roll Hall of Fame. He played off and on for ten years with the
  late Indianapolis blues mandolin man\, “Yank” Rachell\, as well as Chicag
 o piano man Jimmy Walker.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250215T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250215T230000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:BCT presents: Bloomington Winter Blues Fest\, feat. King Bee and Th
 e Stingers / Mike Milligan and Steam Shovel // Gordon Bonham
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bct-presents-bloomington-winter-blues-fest-2025/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>DOOR 
 TIME 7:00 pm</strong><br />\nWarm those winter blues with some of Indiana’
 s finest!</p>\n<p><strong>King Bee & The Stingers</strong> is a six-piece 
 blues\, soul and funk band from Bloomington\, Indiana. Formed in 2006 unde
 r the leadership of harmonica player and vocalist Mark “King Bee” Menefee\
 , the band attracted a strong following across Indiana and the Midwest\, p
 laying classic\, gritty roadhouse blues. In 2015\, Mark’s daughter Sarah M
 enefee took over as lead vocalist and has been a rising star ever since. K
 ing Bee & The Stingers are 2018\, 2019\, and 2023 semifinalists in The Blu
 es Foundation’s International Blues Challenge in Memphis\, TN.</p>\n<p><st
 rong>Mike Milligan and Steam Shovel</strong> is an Original\, Powerful\, S
 oulful group from Kokomo\, Indiana\, United States\, formed in 1993\, comp
 rised of brothers\, Mike Milligan (guitar/vocals) and Shaun Milligan (bass
 )\, and Robert “Tiny” Cook (drums/vocals).</p>\n<p>They Celebrate 30… THIR
 TY Years! of touring and recording in 2023 with their NEW Album on Mojo Hu
 t Records\,… KOKOMO HONEY!</p>\n<p>They were recently honored with an awar
 d for a Lifetime of Keeping the Blues alive by the Fishers Blues Festival 
 (Indy) and performed for 5000 of their biggest fans w Robert Cray Band (5t
 h time!) And received an achievement award from the Mayor Of Muncie Indian
 a for the 30th anniversary! They also performed a sold out show w BB KING 
 on his final Indiana show\, and recently with BUDDY GUY (for the 4th time)
 \, Los Lonely Boys (2nd x)\, Jimmie Vaughan\, and Robert Cray (again! for 
 the SIXTH time!) !</p>\n<p>With 7 CD releases on Mojo Hut Records\, 100’s 
 of Thousands of touring miles\, and several Thousands of performances unde
 r their belts…. it’s always Full Steam ahead.</p>\n<p><strong>Gordon Bonha
 m</strong> grew up in Hammond\, IN and brings together a mix of styles fro
 m the Mississippi Delta to the back alleys of Chicago\, from big Texas shu
 ffles to jumpin’ West Coast swing. After several years of tearing up the r
 oad\, Bonham brings it all together in Indiana\, the Crossroads of America
 . Bonham has performed several times with the legendary Pinetop Perkins\, 
 most notably in Cleveland along with Robert Lockwood\, Jr. as part of the 
 grand opening of the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame. He played off and on for 
 ten years with the late Indianapolis blues mandolin man\, “Yank” Rachell\,
  as well as Chicago piano man Jimmy Walker.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
