BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131924@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:About 2025 Oscar-Nominated Shorts: Documentary\nFor the first t
 ime since 2012\, IU Cinema is happy to present a big-screen experience for
  the Oscar-nominated short films. Traditionally\, these shorts program hav
 e been offered to our community by the Ryder Film Series. We are honored t
 o be a part of Peter LoPilato’s Bloomington legacy of connecting our commu
 nity with global cinematic treasure through our International Arthouse Ser
 ies and dedicate our first Oscar Shorts screenings in over a decade to his
  memory.\nThe documentary line-up will include:\nDeath by Numbers – Kim A.
  Snyder\, 33 min\, USA (in English)\nI Am Ready\, Warden – Smriti Mundhra\
 , 37 min\, USA (in English)\nIncident – Bill Morrison\, 30 min\, USA (in E
 nglish)\nInstruments of a Beating Heart – Ema Ryan Yamazaki\, 23 min\, Jap
 an (in Japanese)\nThe Only Girl in the Orchestra – Molly O’Brien\, 34 min\
 , USA (in English)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250216T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:International Art House Series: 2025 OSCAR-NOMINATED SHORTS: DOCUME
 NTARY ( 2025 | Various Countries | Not Rated)
