 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong><br /
 >\nAbout 2025 Oscar-Nominated Shorts: Documentary</p>\n<p>For the first ti
 me since 2012\, IU Cinema is happy to present a big-screen experience for 
 the Oscar-nominated short films. Traditionally\, these shorts program have
  been offered to our community by the Ryder Film Series. We are honored to
  be a part of Peter LoPilato’s Bloomington legacy of connecting our commun
 ity with global cinematic treasure through our International Arthouse Seri
 es and dedicate our first Oscar Shorts screenings in over a decade to his 
 memory.</strong><br />\nThe documentary line-up will include:</p>\n<p>Deat
 h by Numbers – Kim A. Snyder\, 33 min\, USA (in English)</p>\n<p>I Am Read
 y\, Warden – Smriti Mundhra\, 37 min\, USA (in English)</p>\n<p>Incident –
  Bill Morrison\, 30 min\, USA (in English)</p>\n<p>Instruments of a Beatin
 g Heart – Ema Ryan Yamazaki\, 23 min\, Japan (in Japanese)</p>\n<p>The Onl
 y Girl in the Orchestra – Molly O’Brien\, 34 min\, USA (in English)</p>\n<
 /BODY></HTML>
