UID:ai1ec-132168@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:For the first time since 2012\, IU Cinema is happy to present a
  big-screen experience for the Oscar-nominated short films. Traditionally\
 , these shorts program have been offered to our community by the Ryder Fil
 m Series. We are honored to be a part of Peter LoPilato’s Bloomington lega
 cy of connecting our community with global cinematic treasure through our 
 International Arthouse Series and dedicate our first Oscar Shorts screenin
 gs in over a decade to his memory.\nThe animated line-up will include:\nBe
 autiful Men – Nicolas Keppens\, 18 min\, Belgium/France/Netherlands (in Fl
 emish\, Dutch\, Turkish\, and English)\nIn the Shadow of the Cypress – Hos
 sein Molayemi and Shirin Sohani\, 20 min\, Iran (no dialogue)\nMagic Candi
 es – Daisuke Nishio\, 21 min\, Japan (in Japanese)\nWander to Wonder – Nin
 a Gantz\, 14 min\, Netherlands/Belgium/France/UK (in English)\nYuck! – Loï
 c Espuche\, 13 min\, France (in French)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250223T130000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:2025 OSCAR-NOMINATED SHORTS: ANIMATED
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/2025-oscar-nominated-shorts-animated/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>For the first
  time since 2012\, IU Cinema is happy to present a big-screen experience f
 or the Oscar-nominated short films. Traditionally\, these shorts program h
 ave been offered to our community by the Ryder Film Series. We are honored
  to be a part of Peter LoPilato’s Bloomington legacy of connecting our com
 munity with global cinematic treasure through our International Arthouse S
 eries and dedicate our first Oscar Shorts screenings in over a decade to h
 is memory.</p>\n<p>The animated line-up will include:</p>\n<p>Beautiful Me
 n – Nicolas Keppens\, 18 min\, Belgium/France/Netherlands (in Flemish\, Du
 tch\, Turkish\, and English)</p>\n<p>In the Shadow of the Cypress – Hossei
 n Molayemi and Shirin Sohani\, 20 min\, Iran (no dialogue)</p>\n<p>Magic C
 andies – Daisuke Nishio\, 21 min\, Japan (in Japanese)</p>\n<p>Wander to W
 onder – Nina Gantz\, 14 min\, Netherlands/Belgium/France/UK (in English)</
 p>\n<p>Yuck! – Loïc Espuche\, 13 min\, France (in French)</p>\n</BODY></HT
 ML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-132169@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:For the first time since 2012\, IU Cinema is happy to present a
  big-screen experience for the Oscar-nominated short films. Traditionally\
 , these shorts program have been offered to our community by the Ryder Fil
 m Series. We are honored to be a part of Peter LoPilato’s Bloomington lega
 cy of connecting our community with global cinematic treasure through our 
 International Arthouse Series and dedicate our first Oscar Shorts screenin
 gs in over a decade to his memory.\nThe live-action line-up will include:
 \nA Lien – Sam Cutler-Kreutz and David Cutler-Kreutz\, 15 min\, USA (in En
 glish)\nAnuja – Adam J. Graves\, 22 min\, USA (in Hindi)\nI’m Not a Robot 
 – Victoria Warmerdam\, 22 min\, Belgium/Netherlands (in Dutch)\nThe Last R
 anger – Cindy Lee\, 28 min\, South Africa (in Xhosa)\nThe Man Who Could No
 t Remain Silent – Nebojsa Slijepcevic\, 13 min\, Croatia (in Croatian)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250223T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:2025 OSCAR-NOMINATED SHORTS: LIVE ACTION
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/2025-oscar-nominated-shorts-live-action/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>For the first
  time since 2012\, IU Cinema is happy to present a big-screen experience f
 or the Oscar-nominated short films. Traditionally\, these shorts program h
 ave been offered to our community by the Ryder Film Series. We are honored
  to be a part of Peter LoPilato’s Bloomington legacy of connecting our com
 munity with global cinematic treasure through our International Arthouse S
 eries and dedicate our first Oscar Shorts screenings in over a decade to h
 is memory.</p>\n<p>The live-action line-up will include:</p>\n<p>A Lien – 
 Sam Cutler-Kreutz and David Cutler-Kreutz\, 15 min\, USA (in English)</p>
 \n<p>Anuja – Adam J. Graves\, 22 min\, USA (in Hindi)</p>\n<p>I’m Not a Ro
 bot – Victoria Warmerdam\, 22 min\, Belgium/Netherlands (in Dutch)</p>\n<p
 >The Last Ranger – Cindy Lee\, 28 min\, South Africa (in Xhosa)</p>\n<p>Th
 e Man Who Could Not Remain Silent – Nebojsa Slijepcevic\, 13 min\, Croatia
  (in Croatian)</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
