BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-132455@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:About The African American Dance Company Presents: HIStory\, HE
 Rstory\, Our Story\nThe final installment of “HIStory\, HERstory\, Our Sto
 ry” shows the evolution of the African American Dance Company since its in
 ception in 1974. Through captivating dance and documentary\, we better und
 erstand how dance is used through resistance\, celebration\, and transitio
 n. Paired with archival footage is a panel discussion consisting of the in
 augural director\, Professor Iris Rosa\; current director Baba Stafford C.
  Berry Jr.\; and AADC alum. Audience members are encouraged to participate
  in the Q&A after the screening.\nAADC Dance Excerpts (2024\, 60 min): Fol
 lowing Because We Are\, enjoy this collection of four dances from througho
 ut the African American Dance Company’s history.\nBecause We Are (Dir. Ash
 ley Hayes\, 2024\, 19 min): Because We Are follows the story of the Africa
 n American Dance Company during their 50th season at their annual Kukusany
 a intensive workshop\, a time of gathering together in community as the te
 rm kukusanya evokes. It also invites viewers into the world of the Dance C
 ompany\, its members\, and their practice of ubuntu\, the essence of the A
 fricanist principle that “I am\, because we are.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250227T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:THE AFRICAN AMERICAN DANCE COMPANY PRESENTS: HISTORY\, HERSTORY\, O
 UR STORY\, Q and A to follow.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-african-american-dance-company-presents-hist
 ory-herstory-our-story-q-and-a-to-follow/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>About The Afr
 ican American Dance Company Presents: HIStory\, HERstory\, Our Story</p>\n
 <p>The final installment of “HIStory\, HERstory\, Our Story” shows the evo
 lution of the African American Dance Company since its inception in 1974. 
 Through captivating dance and documentary\, we better understand how dance
  is used through resistance\, celebration\, and transition. Paired with ar
 chival footage is a panel discussion consisting of the inaugural director\
 , Professor Iris Rosa\; current director Baba Stafford C. Berry Jr.\; and 
 AADC alum. Audience members are encouraged to participate in the Q&A after
  the screening.</p>\n<p>AADC Dance Excerpts (2024\, 60 min): Following Bec
 ause We Are\, enjoy this collection of four dances from throughout the Afr
 ican American Dance Company’s history.</p>\n<p>Because We Are (Dir. Ashley
  Hayes\, 2024\, 19 min): Because We Are follows the story of the African A
 merican Dance Company during their 50th season at their annual Kukusanya i
 ntensive workshop\, a time of gathering together in community as the term 
 kukusanya evokes. It also invites viewers into the world of the Dance Comp
 any\, its members\, and their practice of ubuntu\, the essence of the Afri
 canist principle that “I am\, because we are.”</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
