UID:ai1ec-132436@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Monthly improv comedy in Bloomington\, IN! Three teams perform\
 , the audience votes for their favorite\, and last month’s winner closes t
 he night with a headlining set.\nJoin us for the launch of Improv Showdown
 \, Bloomington’s newest monthly improv comedy show\, where quick wit meets
  audience votes in an unforgettable night of laughs.\nHere’s how it works:
 \nThree teams will perform side-splitting 10-minute improv sets.\nThe audi
 ence votes for their favorite team.\nThe winning team returns next month a
 s the headliner for a 25-minute set.\nFor this debut event\, we’re thrille
 d to welcome the incredible Fabuloso as our headliner. Don’t miss their up
 roarious performance to kick off this exciting new series.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250228T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250228T204500
LOCATION:Constellation Studios\, 411 East 7th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Improv Showdown: Live Improv Comedy\, featuring FABULOSO as the hea
 dliner
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/improv-showdown-live-improv-comedy-featuring-fab
 uloso-as-the-headliner/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Monthly impro
 v comedy in Bloomington\, IN! Three teams perform\, the audience votes for
  their favorite\, and last month’s winner closes the night with a headlini
 ng set.<br />\nJoin us for the launch of Improv Showdown\, Bloomington’s n
 ewest monthly improv comedy show\, where quick wit meets audience votes in
  an unforgettable night of laughs.</p>\n<p>Here’s how it works:<br />\nThr
 ee teams will perform side-splitting 10-minute improv sets.<br />\nThe aud
 ience votes for their favorite team.<br />\nThe winning team returns next 
 month as the headliner for a 25-minute set.</p>\n<p>For this debut event\,
  we’re thrilled to welcome the incredible Fabuloso as our headliner. Don’t
  miss their uproarious performance to kick off this exciting new series.</
 p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-131101@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:All Ages\nSynopsis: In this surreal vision of the not-too-dista
 nt-future\, the official language of Canada is now Farsi. Against this odd
 ball background\, three slice-of-life stories emerge: Two young friends ve
 nture to retrieve money found frozen in a block of winter ice. A man quits
  his painfully bureaucratic government job and returns home. And a peculia
 r tour guide shows off some of Winnipeg’s dullest attractions to a group o
 f discombobulated tourists. Taken together\, these deadpan stories create 
 a picture of life in the “heart of Canada” that’s both hilarious and heart
 warming.\nFeaturing masterful production design with an eye toward the abs
 urd\, director Matthew Rankin (The Twentieth Century) describes his second
  feature as “a love letter to Iranian cinema\,” combining the soulfulness 
 of Abbas Kiarostami with the visual whimsy of Wes Anderson to create an ap
 pealingly unusual odyssey.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250228T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250228T213000
LOCATION:Hopscotch Coffee + Kitchen\, 235 W Dodds St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema presents: Universal Language (2024)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-universal-language-2024/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>All Ages<br /
 >\nSynopsis: In this surreal vision of the not-too-distant-future\, the of
 ficial language of Canada is now Farsi. Against this oddball background\, 
 three slice-of-life stories emerge: Two young friends venture to retrieve 
 money found frozen in a block of winter ice. A man quits his painfully bur
 eaucratic government job and returns home. And a peculiar tour guide shows
  off some of Winnipeg’s dullest attractions to a group of discombobulated 
 tourists. Taken together\, these deadpan stories create a picture of life 
 in the “heart of Canada” that’s both hilarious and heartwarming.</p>\n<p>F
 eaturing masterful production design with an eye toward the absurd\, direc
 tor Matthew Rankin (The Twentieth Century) describes his second feature as
  “a love letter to Iranian cinema\,” combining the soulfulness of Abbas Ki
 arostami with the visual whimsy of Wes Anderson to create an appealingly u
 nusual odyssey.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
