BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-132443@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This expansive documentary released in 2024 vividly captures th
 e Los Angeles music scene starting from the late-1980s to today\, centerin
 g around a band that was hailed as the “next big thing” and you may have n
 ever heard of — Redd Kross.\nThe film gets into the mythology that grew ar
 ound the band – their brushes with success\, their giving the finger to th
 e establishment\, etc. In doing so\, it explores what defines success. Whi
 le they might not have become zillionaires or household names\, they’ve do
 ne all right on their own terms.\nYou don’t need to know Redd Kross’ music
  to appreciate this movie. It’s funny\, accessible\, candid\, and visually
  rich.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250302T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250302T203000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Born Innocent: The Redd Kross Story
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/born-innocent-the-redd-kross-story/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>This expansiv
 e documentary released in 2024 vividly captures the Los Angeles music scen
 e starting from the late-1980s to today\, centering around a band that was
  hailed as the “next big thing” and you may have never heard of — Redd Kro
 ss.</p>\n<p>The film gets into the mythology that grew around the band – t
 heir brushes with success\, their giving the finger to the establishment\,
  etc. In doing so\, it explores what defines success. While they might not
  have become zillionaires or household names\, they’ve done all right on t
 heir own terms.</p>\n<p>You don’t need to know Redd Kross’ music to apprec
 iate this movie. It’s funny\, accessible\, candid\, and visually rich.</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
