BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-132699@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Our Choice Coalition\, Inc. invites you to a special fundraisin
 g event featuring a screening of Zurawski v. Texas—a gripping documentary 
 that tells the stories of women\, like Amanda Zurawski\, who were denied a
 bortions despite facing serious health complications under Texas’ restrict
 ive abortion laws. Their experiences expose the devastating real-world con
 sequences of these bans and the urgent need for change. Amanda’s story is 
 one of resilience\, advocacy\, and an unrelenting fight for reproductive f
 reedom—a fight that impacts us all.\nIU Alumna Amanda Zurawski will be in 
 attendance and will take part in an exclusive Q&A panel following the scre
 ening\, where she will share her firsthand perspective and discuss what’s 
 at stake for reproductive rights.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250307T190000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:An Evening with Amanda Zurawski\, featuring a screening of Zurawski
  v. Texas plus a Q and A with Zurawski afterward
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/an-evening-with-amanda-zurawski-featuring-a-scre
 ening-of-zurawski-v-texas-plus-a-q-and-a-with-iu-alumna-amanda-zurawski-af
 terward/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Our C
 hoice Coalition\, Inc.</strong> invites you to a special fundraising event
  featuring a screening of Zurawski v. Texas—a gripping documentary that te
 lls the stories of women\, like Amanda Zurawski\, who were denied abortion
 s despite facing serious health complications under Texas’ restrictive abo
 rtion laws. Their experiences expose the devastating real-world consequenc
 es of these bans and the urgent need for change. Amanda’s story is one of 
 resilience\, advocacy\, and an unrelenting fight for reproductive freedom—
 a fight that impacts us all.</p>\n<p>IU Alumna Amanda Zurawski will be in 
 attendance and will take part in an exclusive Q&A panel following the scre
 ening\, where she will share her firsthand perspective and discuss what’s 
 at stake for reproductive rights.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
