BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-132723@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:New York City\, 1980s. A struggling\, deadbeat musician named J
 ulius has fallen on hard times. With no guitar\, band or paying gigs\, he 
 cooks up a get-rich-quick scheme – to find the legendary\, yet elusive gui
 tar-maker Elmore Silk. Considered one of the greatest luthiers in the busi
 ness\, Silk’s disappearance from the scene has only made his work more cov
 eted by musicians and executives looking to make a buck off his name. Juli
 us agrees to track the man down and sets out on the road. Meant to be a si
 mple journey upstate\, Julius stumbles down a long\, winding road full of 
 dead-ends and wrong turns towards an eventual revelatory conclusion in the
  Canadian wilderness.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250308T190000
LOCATION:Backspace Gallery\, inside Bonne Fête\, 112 West 6th Street\, on t
 he square in Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema: CANDY MOUNTAIN (1987) with post-film Q and A with Bl
 oomington musician Mark Bingham\, who was in the film and on the soundtrac
 k!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-candy-mountain-1987-with-post-film
 -q-and-a-with-bloomington-musician-mark-bingham-who-was-in-the-film-and-on
 -the-soundtrack/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>New York City
 \, 1980s. A struggling\, deadbeat musician named Julius has fallen on hard
  times. With no guitar\, band or paying gigs\, he cooks up a get-rich-quic
 k scheme – to find the legendary\, yet elusive guitar-maker Elmore Silk. C
 onsidered one of the greatest luthiers in the business\, Silk’s disappeara
 nce from the scene has only made his work more coveted by musicians and ex
 ecutives looking to make a buck off his name. Julius agrees to track the m
 an down and sets out on the road. Meant to be a simple journey upstate\, J
 ulius stumbles down a long\, winding road full of dead-ends and wrong turn
 s towards an eventual revelatory conclusion in the Canadian wilderness.</p
 >\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
