X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>This month’s 
 Folklore Night features presentations by Adriane Pontecorvo and chloē four
 te. All ages. Free\, but donations are welcome to support the Folklore and
  Ethnomusicology Student Associations. The usual “jam” will not be feature
 d this month\, though musicians are encouraged to reach out about performi
 ng at future events<br />\nLive from the Fillmore: Non-Profit Media in a T
 echnocapitalist Dystopia<br />\nAgainst forces of dramatic economic dispar
 ity and ongoing gentrification\, Poor People’s Radio aims to serve San Fra
 ncisco’s low-income populace with programming like Uplift\, a show created
  in tandem with the Church of John Coltrane.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
