CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Co-sponsored by Monroe County NOW and the League of Women Voter
 s of Bloomington-Monroe County.\nFrom the Emmy Award winners behind Boys S
 tate\, Jesse Moss and Amanda McBaine\, comes the Emmy Award-winning Girls 
 State\nSynopsis: Set against the backdrop of a nation grappling with a dee
 pening democratic crisis and heightened political polarization\, this comp
 elling documentary delves into the experiences of 500 teenage girls partic
 ipating in a week-long program where they construct their own state govern
 ment. It underscores the significance of civic engagement\, the intricacie
 s of democracy\, and the influence of female voices in political leadershi
 p.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250313T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250313T210000
LOCATION:Indiana University Cinema\, 1213 E 7th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Girls State
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/girls-state/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Co-sp
 onsored by Monroe County NOW and the League of Women Voters of Bloomington
 -Monroe County.</strong><br />\nFrom the Emmy Award winners behind Boys St
 ate\, Jesse Moss and Amanda McBaine\, comes the Emmy Award-winning Girls S
 tate<br />\n<strong>Synopsis: </strong>Set against the backdrop of a natio
 n grappling with a deepening democratic crisis and heightened political po
 larization\, this compelling documentary delves into the experiences of 50
 0 teenage girls participating in a week-long program where they construct 
 their own state government. It underscores the significance of civic engag
 ement\, the intricacies of democracy\, and the influence of female voices 
 in political leadership.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
