BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-130136@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Music | DOOR TIME 7 pm\nIn honor of Irish traditional music\, O
 n The Lash creates timeless sounds through original voices. With new takes
  on classic songs and original constructions of established standards\, OT
 L aims to explore the inherent energy and versatility of the genre.\nOn Th
 e Lash formed in early 2021\, with their very first set of shows being a t
 our through PA and since then\, OTL has been busy performing at festivals 
 and concert venues across the US\, as well as sharing their unique backgro
 und and experience in the genre through educational workshops. Some notabl
 e festivals include the KVMR Celtic Fest in Grass Valley\, CA\; the Yachat
 s Celtic Fest in Yachats\, OR\; the Longs Peak Highland Fest in Estes Park
 \, CO\; and the Celtic Classic in Bethlehem\, PA. Their recorded work incl
 udes the 2022 single Dog in the Distance\, with a five song performance EP
  to be released in 2024.\nAnd a new album is on the way in 2025!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250314T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250314T210000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:BCT presents: On The Lash – In celebration of St. Patrick’s Day
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bct-presents-on-the-lash-in-celebration-of-st-pa
 tricks-day/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Music
  | DOOR TIME 7 pm</strong><br />\nIn honor of Irish traditional music\, <s
 trong><a href='http://www.onthelashband.com'>On The Lash</a></strong> crea
 tes timeless sounds through original voices. With new takes on classic son
 gs and original constructions of established standards\, OTL aims to explo
 re the inherent energy and versatility of the genre.</p>\n<p>On The Lash f
 ormed in early 2021\, with their very first set of shows being a tour thro
 ugh PA and since then\, OTL has been busy performing at festivals and conc
 ert venues across the US\, as well as sharing their unique background and 
 experience in the genre through educational workshops. Some notable festiv
 als include the KVMR Celtic Fest in Grass Valley\, CA\; the Yachats Celtic
  Fest in Yachats\, OR\; the Longs Peak Highland Fest in Estes Park\, CO\; 
 and the Celtic Classic in Bethlehem\, PA. Their recorded work includes the
  2022 single Dog in the Distance\, with a five song performance EP to be r
 eleased in 2024.</p>\n<p>And a new album is on the way in 2025!</p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
END:VEVENT
