BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133270@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6:30pm\nClaire Pendreigh is an emerging indie-folk sin
 ger-songwriter born and raised here in Bloomington\, Indiana (locals may r
 ecognize her by her last name\, Frohman). With lyrics that are often both 
 softly poetic and deeply cutting at once\, Claire’s songs emerge from a pl
 ace of intimate self-expression\, inviting her listeners on a raw and vuln
 erable journey through the craggy and mysterious landscape of the heart. A
 ccompanied by her band\, her songs take on new form\, with Bryant Fox on b
 ass\, Mitch Marsh on drums\, and Peter Doyle on pedal steel.\nSprouted fro
 m the seeds of Memphis soil\, Alicia Gail crossed the Mississippi river ga
 thering friendly spirits and pouring them into songs. Her music explores t
 he blurring of lines between character and self\, daydreams and reality\, 
 joy and pain\, melody and story. A haunting elegance threads together infl
 uences of folk\, blues and soul. Enjoy at your own speed and thank you for
  tuning in.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250326T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:WFHB presents Claire Pendreigh & Alicia Gail: Live at Buskirk-Chuml
 ey Theater
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/wfhb-presents-claire-pendreigh-alicia-gail-live-
 at-buskirk-chumley-theater/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 6:30pm</strong><br />\nClaire Pendreigh is an emerging indie-folk sing
 er-songwriter born and raised here in Bloomington\, Indiana (locals may re
 cognize her by her last name\, Frohman). With lyrics that are often both s
 oftly poetic and deeply cutting at once\, Claire’s songs emerge from a pla
 ce of intimate self-expression\, inviting her listeners on a raw and vulne
 rable journey through the craggy and mysterious landscape of the heart. Ac
 companied by her band\, her songs take on new form\, with Bryant Fox on ba
 ss\, Mitch Marsh on drums\, and Peter Doyle on pedal steel.</p>\n<p>Sprout
 ed from the seeds of Memphis soil\, Alicia Gail crossed the Mississippi ri
 ver gathering friendly spirits and pouring them into songs. Her music expl
 ores the blurring of lines between character and self\, daydreams and real
 ity\, joy and pain\, melody and story. A haunting elegance threads togethe
 r influences of folk\, blues and soul. Enjoy at your own speed and thank y
 ou for tuning in.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
