DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Jazz at Lincoln Center (JALC) brings the soul of New Orleans an
 d the spirit of Mardi Gras to this amazing evening\, celebrating the compo
 sers and inspired songs of the Crescent City\, the historic epicenter of j
 azz. From Jelly Roll Morton and Louis Armstrong to Ellis Marsalis and Jame
 s Black\, New Orleans has long been an apex of innovation and inspiration.
  With world-class musicians and infectious energy\, New Orleans Songbook i
 mmerses audiences in the captivating and timeless spirit of this vibrant c
 ity.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250326T193000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Jazz at Lincoln Center Presents: New Orleans Songbook
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/jazz-at-lincoln-center-presents-new-orleans-song
 book/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Jazz at Linco
 ln Center (JALC) brings the soul of New Orleans and the spirit of Mardi Gr
 as to this amazing evening\, celebrating the composers and inspired songs 
 of the Crescent City\, the historic epicenter of jazz. From Jelly Roll Mor
 ton and Louis Armstrong to Ellis Marsalis and James Black\, New Orleans ha
 s long been an apex of innovation and inspiration. With world-class musici
 ans and infectious energy\, New Orleans Songbook immerses audiences in the
  captivating and timeless spirit of this vibrant city.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
