BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133137@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This fundraiser will benefit the parent organization of ‘Autism
  Rocks and Rolls\,’ a syndicated show that advocates for better awareness 
 and acceptance of autism.  ‘Autism Rocks and Rolls’ airs Tuesdays at 5:30p
 m on WFHB or wherever you listen to podcasts. The event will feature speak
 ers\, experts\, discussions\, vendors\, silent auction\, raffles and food.
  RVSP at 812-699-7811. \nAutism Rocks and Rolls will have a speaker flying
  in from Georgia\, Samuel Hutchins. Mr. Hutchins runs a nonprofit foundati
 on called Hope 4 Xavier. Xavier\, Mr. Hutchins son\, had autism and the wo
 rk that Mr. Hutchins and Xavier have done and are still doing is phenomena
 l. Unfortunately\, very recently\, Mr. Hutchins lost his 32 year old son\,
  Xavier\, after he had a seizure. We are inspired by the strength of Mr. H
 utchins to continue the nonprofit so that his son can live through the wor
 k he will continue to do.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250330T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250330T183000
LOCATION:Moose Lodge\, 840 South Cory Lane\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Fundraiser: Knowledge is Power: An Autism Gala
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/fundraiser-knowledge-is-power-an-autism-gala/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>This 
 fundraiser will benefit the parent organization of ‘Autism Rocks and Rolls
 \,’ a syndicated show that advocates for better awareness and acceptance o
 f autism.  ‘Autism Rocks and Rolls’ airs Tuesdays at 5:30pm on WFHB or whe
 rever you listen to podcasts. The event will feature speakers\, experts\, 
 discussions\, vendors\, silent auction\, raffles and food. RVSP at 812-699
 -7811. </strong></p>\n<p>Autism Rocks and Rolls will have a speaker flying
  in from Georgia\, Samuel Hutchins. Mr. Hutchins runs a nonprofit foundati
 on called Hope 4 Xavier. Xavier\, Mr. Hutchins son\, had autism and the wo
 rk that Mr. Hutchins and Xavier have done and are still doing is phenomena
 l. Unfortunately\, very recently\, Mr. Hutchins lost his 32 year old son\,
  Xavier\, after he had a seizure. We are inspired by the strength of Mr. H
 utchins to continue the nonprofit so that his son can live through the wor
 k he will continue to do.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
