BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133651@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Brian De Palma | 1981 | USA | R | DCP\nWhile recording sound ef
 fects for a slasher flick\, Jack Terry (John Travolta) stumbles upon a rea
 l-life horror: a car careening off a bridge and into a river. While he res
 cues Sally (Nancy Allen) from the car\, the other passenger is already dea
 d—a governor intending to run for president. As Jack does some investigati
 ng of his tapes\, and starts a perilous romance with Sally\, he enters a t
 angled web of conspiracy that might leave him dead.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250401T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:I Like to Watch: Voyeurism in Cinema Series: BLOW OUT
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/i-like-to-watch-voyeurism-in-cinema-series-blow-
 out/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Brian De Palm
 a | 1981 | USA | R | DCP<br />\nWhile recording sound effects for a slashe
 r flick\, Jack Terry (John Travolta) stumbles upon a real-life horror: a c
 ar careening off a bridge and into a river. While he rescues Sally (Nancy 
 Allen) from the car\, the other passenger is already dead—a governor inten
 ding to run for president. As Jack does some investigating of his tapes\, 
 and starts a perilous romance with Sally\, he enters a tangled web of cons
 piracy that might leave him dead. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133582@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Declared “one of the most remarkable shows in musical theater h
 istory” by The Washington Post\, DEAR EVAN HANSEN is the first musical to 
 take a groundbreaking look—from the point of view of both the parents and 
 young people—at our complex\, interconnected\, and social media-filled liv
 es.\nEvan Hansen is a high school student who always feels like he’s on th
 e outside looking in. Evan finally gets what so many of us are searching f
 or—the chance to finally fit in. What follows is a poignant\, funny\, and 
 powerful musical about how\, even though it can be hard\, we can find each
  other—and ourselves—along the way.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250401T193000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20250402T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Dear Evan Hansen (Six time Tony Award-Winning Play)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/six-time-tony-award-winner-dear-evan-hansen/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Declared “one
  of the most remarkable shows in musical theater history” by The Washingto
 n Post\, DEAR EVAN HANSEN is the first musical to take a groundbreaking lo
 ok—from the point of view of both the parents and young people—at our comp
 lex\, interconnected\, and social media-filled lives.</p>\n<p>Evan Hansen 
 is a high school student who always feels like he’s on the outside looking
  in. Evan finally gets what so many of us are searching for—the chance to 
 finally fit in. What follows is a poignant\, funny\, and powerful musical 
 about how\, even though it can be hard\, we can find each other—and oursel
 ves—along the way.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
