BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133557@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join the IU School of Nursing for a FREE showing of the film ‘F
 ood Insecure’ on April 4 from 3pm to 4:30 pm at the Health Sciences  Build
 ing\, 2631 East Discovery Parkway. ‘Food Insecure’ was created to spark co
 nversation and a deeper understanding about the issues surrounding food in
 security.  After the viewing\, our panel will discuss how food insecurity 
 affects the Bloomington community.  Our focus will be on the systems that 
 need to be changed\, the issues that need to be addressed\, our plans for 
 the future\, and ways in which you can help. We encourage you to join with
  us in examining these issues and how we can all work together toward effe
 ctive action.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250404T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250404T163000
LOCATION:IU Bloomington Health Sciences Building\, 2631 East Discovery Park
 way\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Free Showing of “Food Insecure” (a documentary that explores food i
 nsecurity\, particularly in Indiana) followed by a panel discussion of the
  issues
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/free-showing-of-food-insecure-a-documentary-that
 -explores-food-insecurity-particularly-in-indiana-with-a-panel-discussion-
 to-follow/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join the IU S
 chool of Nursing for a FREE showing of the film ‘Food Insecure’ on April 4
  from 3pm to 4:30 pm at the Health Sciences  Building\, 2631 East Discover
 y Parkway. ‘Food Insecure’ was created to spark conversation and a deeper 
 understanding about the issues surrounding food insecurity.  After the vie
 wing\, our panel will discuss how food insecurity affects the Bloomington 
 community.  Our focus will be on the systems that need to be changed\, the
  issues that need to be addressed\, our plans for the future\, and ways in
  which you can help. We encourage you to join with us in examining these i
 ssues and how we can all work together toward effective action.</p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133561@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Centurion refers to a fabled and exclusive credit card only
  available to a select few of the ultra wealthy. It’s also the title of Br
 ian Ulrich’s newest photographic series\, which examines the lure of exclu
 sivity in the world of extreme luxury. Ulrich has photographed the America
 n culture of commerce and consumption for over a decade. The Centurion tur
 ns to the country’s fascination with wealth and all its promises.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250404T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250404T200000
LOCATION:Pictura Gallery\, 202 South Rogers Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:April Gallery Walk Reception – Brian Ulrich  | The Centurion
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/april-gallery-walk-reception-brian-ulrich-the-ce
 nturion/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The Centurion
  refers to a fabled and exclusive credit card only available to a select f
 ew of the ultra wealthy. It’s also the title of Brian Ulrich’s newest phot
 ographic series\, which examines the lure of exclusivity in the world of e
 xtreme luxury. Ulrich has photographed the American culture of commerce an
 d consumption for over a decade. The Centurion turns to the country’s fasc
 ination with wealth and all its promises.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
