BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133815@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:At this multimedia workshop\, we will create a collaborative gr
 oup song on the subject of growing. We’ll approach this through visual ima
 gery and free writing\, as well as work together to create verses. We’ll l
 earn a bit about the process of zine making and its connection to grassroo
 ts music and the materials generated will be used in a special collaborati
 ve zine about Girls Rock Bloomington.\nLed by local musician\, arts educat
 or and GRB Founder/Director Amy O. Amy is a recipient of the 2020 Indiana 
 Governor’s Arts Emerging Artist Award and has been growing as a person thr
 ough songwriting for over 20 years.\nFor girls\, trans and non-binary yout
 h ages 8-17
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250406T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250406T160000
LOCATION:McCalla School\, 525 East 9th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Girls Rock Bloomington and University Collections Present: “Growing
  through Songwriting” Workshop
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/girls-rock-bloomington-and-university-collection
 s-present-growing-through-songwriting-workshop/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> At this mult
 imedia workshop\, we will create a collaborative group song on the subject
  of growing. We’ll approach this through visual imagery and free writing\,
  as well as work together to create verses. We’ll learn a bit about the pr
 ocess of zine making and its connection to grassroots music and the materi
 als generated will be used in a special collaborative zine about Girls Roc
 k Bloomington.</p>\n<p>Led by local musician\, arts educator and GRB Found
 er/Director Amy O. Amy is a recipient of the 2020 Indiana Governor’s Arts 
 Emerging Artist Award and has been growing as a person through songwriting
  for over 20 years.</p>\n<p>For girls\, trans and non-binary youth ages 8-
 17</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
