BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133792@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Looking for an opportunity to connect with local leaders\, ask 
 questions\, and get the scoop on city projects? Mayor Kerry Thomson is hos
 ting a Traveling Town Hall on Monday\, April 7\, at Banneker Community Cen
 ter\, 930 W 7th Street\, from 6 to 7 p.m. Joining the Mayor will be Parks 
 & Recreation Director\, Tim Street\, ready to share updates and answer you
 r burning questions. Here’s how it works:\n• The evening kicks off with Ma
 yor Thomson’s quick rundown of city initiatives.\n• Submit your questions 
 on index cards (provided at the door)\, and the team will tackle as many a
 s possible.\n• If time allows\, a live Q&A will round out the night!\nThes
 e Town Halls happen every other month in different districts\, giving resi
 dents a chance to engage directly with City Hall. Whether you live in Dist
 rict 2 or just love being in the know about Bloomington’s happenings\, thi
 s is your chance to join the conversation.\nCan’t make it? The meeting wil
 l be broadcast live on Community Access Television Services (CATS) and ava
 ilable on-demand at catstv.net.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250407T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250407T190000
LOCATION:Banneker Community Center\, 930 West 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mayor Kerry Thomson’s Traveling Town Hall
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mayor-kerry-thomsons-traveling-town-hall/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Looking for a
 n opportunity to connect with local leaders\, ask questions\, and get the 
 scoop on city projects? Mayor Kerry Thomson is hosting a Traveling Town Ha
 ll on Monday\, April 7\, at Banneker Community Center\, 930 W 7th Street\,
  from 6 to 7 p.m. Joining the Mayor will be Parks & Recreation Director\, 
 Tim Street\, ready to share updates and answer your burning questions. Her
 e’s how it works:<br />\n• The evening kicks off with Mayor Thomson’s quic
 k rundown of city initiatives.<br />\n• Submit your questions on index car
 ds (provided at the door)\, and the team will tackle as many as possible.<
 br />\n• If time allows\, a live Q&A will round out the night!<br />\nThes
 e Town Halls happen every other month in different districts\, giving resi
 dents a chance to engage directly with City Hall. Whether you live in Dist
 rict 2 or just love being in the know about Bloomington’s happenings\, thi
 s is your chance to join the conversation.<br />\nCan’t make it? The meeti
 ng will be broadcast live on Community Access Television Services (CATS) a
 nd available on-demand at catstv.net.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
