BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-133951@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 7pm\nCome celebrate 50 years of inspiring black dance 
 with the legendary African American Dance Company (AADC). This two-night c
 oncert event will showcase 50 years of dance in the African Diaspora\, fro
 m traditional Africa to American modern. Directed by Baba Stafford C. Berr
 y\, Jr.\, a United States Midwest Culture Bearer\, AADC will be joined by 
 Seda Negra/Black Silk on Friday\, April 11th and the world-class Dayton Co
 ntemporary Dance Company on Saturday\, April 12th 2025. You don’t want to 
 miss this!\nA jewel in the IU crown that is at the intersection of perform
 ance\, education and advocacy\, the AADC is a valuable cultural resource a
 nd ambassador to black dance performance\, African American and African di
 asporic aesthetics and culture\, embodied research\, Diversity\, Equity\, 
 & Inclusion\, and robust student leadership and creative scholarship.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250412T193000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:African American Dance Company 50th Anniversary Spring Concert (sec
 ond night)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/african-american-dance-company-50th-anniversary-
 spring-concert-second-night/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 7pm</strong><br />\nCome celebrate 50 years of inspiring black dance w
 ith the legendary African American Dance Company (AADC). This two-night co
 ncert event will showcase 50 years of dance in the African Diaspora\, from
  traditional Africa to American modern. Directed by Baba Stafford C. Berry
 \, Jr.\, a United States Midwest Culture Bearer\, AADC will be joined by S
 eda Negra/Black Silk on Friday\, April 11th and the world-class Dayton Con
 temporary Dance Company on Saturday\, April 12th 2025. You don’t want to m
 iss this!</p>\n<p>A jewel in the IU crown that is at the intersection of p
 erformance\, education and advocacy\, the AADC is a valuable cultural reso
 urce and ambassador to black dance performance\, African American and Afri
 can diasporic aesthetics and culture\, embodied research\, Diversity\, Equ
 ity\, & Inclusion\, and robust student leadership and creative scholarship
 .</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
