BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-134272@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In 1875\, critics panned Bizet’s now-indisputable masterpiece\,
  and audiences were shocked by its frankness.\nThough Bizet would die with
 out realizing his work would become one of the most famous and beloved ope
 ras of all time\, he was sure of its import for him. As he finished the pi
 ece\, he wrote to a friend that he had “absolute certainty of having found
  my path.”\nThe dynamic and fiercely independent Carmen has become a femin
 ist icon\; she lived a passionate and self-directed life on her own terms\
 , owing nothing to any man. But patriarchy will inevitably punish such fre
 edom\, in often extreme ways. Carmen eventually knew that—and even she cou
 ld not escape.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250418T183000
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center North Lobby\, 101 North Eagleson Ave.\, Bloomi
 ngton
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20250419T183000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Opera Insights – Pre-show talk on Georges Bizet’s “Carmen”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/opera-insights-pre-show-talk-on-georges-bizets-c
 armen/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>In 1875\, cri
 tics panned Bizet’s now-indisputable masterpiece\, and audiences were shoc
 ked by its frankness.</p>\n<p>Though Bizet would die without realizing his
  work would become one of the most famous and beloved operas of all time\,
  he was sure of its import for him. As he finished the piece\, he wrote to
  a friend that he had “absolute certainty of having found my path.”</p>\n<
 p>The dynamic and fiercely independent Carmen has become a feminist icon\;
  she lived a passionate and self-directed life on her own terms\, owing no
 thing to any man. But patriarchy will inevitably punish such freedom\, in 
 often extreme ways. Carmen eventually knew that—and even she could not esc
 ape.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
