CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Various Directors | 2025 | Various Countries | Not Rated\nThe N
 ew York Dog Film Festival pays tribute to the bond between dogs and people
  around the world\, as seen through the work of brilliant filmmakers. A me
 dley of animated\, documentary\, and narrative short films from around the
  world with a canine theme\, the festival premieres every year in New York
  City\, then travels to theaters across the United States and Canada. With
  10% of every ticket benefitting a local dog rescue\, IU Cinema’s screenin
 g will benefit the Monroe County Humane Association.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250503T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:CINEkids International Children’s Film Series: 2025 NEW YORK DOG FI
 LM FESTIVAL
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cinekids-international-childrens-film-series-202
 5-new-york-dog-film-festival/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Various Direc
 tors | 2025 | Various Countries | Not Rated</p>\n<p>The New York Dog Film 
 Festival pays tribute to the bond between dogs and people around the world
 \, as seen through the work of brilliant filmmakers. A medley of animated\
 , documentary\, and narrative short films from around the world with a can
 ine theme\, the festival premieres every year in New York City\, then trav
 els to theaters across the United States and Canada. With 10% of every tic
 ket benefitting a local dog rescue\, IU Cinema’s screening will benefit th
 e Monroe County Humane Association.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
