BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-134926@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 5pm\n“…The writing talent of Dylan or Guthrie… musical
  genius…hilarious and tragic\, kindhearted and careless\, all the complexi
 ties of a real human being.”\n“A hybrid of Dylan and McCartney” Kevin Matt
 hews\, Fufkin.com\nRoger Salloom’s voice quickly suggests a comparison to 
 early Bob Dylan\, but it’s this vet’s penchant for telling a great story t
 hat puts him in the same category. Time Out New York\nRoger was the subjec
 t of the 6 award-winning feature film documentary\, So Glad I Made It\, th
 e Saga of Roger Salloom\, America’s Best Unknown Songwriter which broadcas
 t on The Documentary Channel monthly for a year and was screened in 36 the
 aters\, and some additional broadcast tv stations.\nRoger’s hit video\, Do
 n’t Let My Country Wash Away\, on Facebook sits at over 386\,000 views and
  with all sites in consideration it is at a total of about 400\,000. The s
 ame song has another 200\,000 streams on Spotify\, iTunes\, Apple et al
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250503T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250503T200000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Roger Salloom
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/roger-salloom-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 5pm</strong><br />\n“…The writing talent of Dylan or Guthrie… musical 
 genius…hilarious and tragic\, kindhearted and careless\, all the complexit
 ies of a real human being.”<br />\n“A hybrid of Dylan and McCartney” Kevin
  Matthews\, Fufkin.com<br />\nRoger Salloom’s voice quickly suggests a com
 parison to early Bob Dylan\, but it’s this vet’s penchant for telling a gr
 eat story that puts him in the same category. Time Out New York<br />\nRog
 er was the subject of the 6 award-winning feature film documentary\, So Gl
 ad I Made It\, the Saga of Roger Salloom\, America’s Best Unknown Songwrit
 er which broadcast on The Documentary Channel monthly for a year and was s
 creened in 36 theaters\, and some additional broadcast tv stations.<br />
 \nRoger’s hit video\, Don’t Let My Country Wash Away\, on Facebook sits at
  over 386\,000 views and with all sites in consideration it is at a total 
 of about 400\,000. The same song has another 200\,000 streams on Spotify\,
  iTunes\, Apple et al</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-134967@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:As featured on Spotify’s ‘Got Blues’ and ‘Best Blues of 2022′ e
 ditorial playlists\, Andy Kahrs’ distinct blend of roots genres shines wit
 h powerful vocals and unique guitar style that bring his southern roots an
 d storytelling sensibilities to life. Included on Music Mecca’s Top 10 202
 3 Nashville Indie Releases\, his authentic tone draws equally from Randy T
 ravis and Otis Redding\, yet stands out as uniquely his own. His show ‘Alw
 ays On My Mind’ finds Andy weaving his signature sound through country\, b
 lues\, and soul classics from artists such as Johnny Cash\, Ray Charles\, 
 Alison Krauss\, and many more.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250503T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250503T210000
LOCATION:Mitchell Opera House\, 217 North 7th Street\, Mitchell
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Andy Kahrs
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/andy-kahrs/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>As featured o
 n Spotify’s ‘Got Blues’ and ‘Best Blues of 2022′ editorial playlists\, And
 y Kahrs’ distinct blend of roots genres shines with powerful vocals and un
 ique guitar style that bring his southern roots and storytelling sensibili
 ties to life. Included on Music Mecca’s Top 10 2023 Nashville Indie Releas
 es\, his authentic tone draws equally from Randy Travis and Otis Redding\,
  yet stands out as uniquely his own. His show ‘Always On My Mind’ finds An
 dy weaving his signature sound through country\, blues\, and soul classics
  from artists such as Johnny Cash\, Ray Charles\, Alison Krauss\, and many
  more.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
