BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-134961@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:PDVNCH [pee-dove-inch] is a spoken wordsmith and dramatic proph
 etic poetic storyteller\, creating vivid images\, with words\, from multip
 le perspectives\, and giving voice to the unheard\, with vocal tones\, tha
 t are rhythmic. Shayne Laughter is a Bloomerang\, who has lived in Seattle
  and New York\, and has spent time in Spain and India. She has won honors 
 for her screenplays\, short stories\, and first novel (Yü)\, and has been 
 a radio voice at WFHB and WFIURadio.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250504T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250504T173000
LOCATION:Juniper Art Gallery\, 615 West Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Writers Guild: PDVNCH! [pee-dove-inch] & Shayne Laughter
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/writers-guild-pdvnch-pee-dove-inch-shayne-laught
 er/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>PDVNCH [pee-d
 ove-inch] is a spoken wordsmith and dramatic prophetic poetic storyteller\
 , creating vivid images\, with words\, from multiple perspectives\, and gi
 ving voice to the unheard\, with vocal tones\, that are rhythmic. Shayne L
 aughter is a Bloomerang\, who has lived in Seattle and New York\, and has 
 spent time in Spain and India. She has won honors for her screenplays\, sh
 ort stories\, and first novel (Yü)\, and has been a radio voice at WFHB an
 d WFIURadio.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-134787@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Potluck at 5:30pm\, Music at 6pm\nJohn Depew Trio-is a musician
 \, songwriter\, and traveler with a knack for combining traditional sounds
  with thoughtful lyrics and intriguing musicality. He has been described a
 s a “midwestern Nick Drake” by Ted Gioia\, (musicologist.) He enjoys explo
 ring new places in both the natural world and in the wilderness within. Co
 mbining philosophy\, farming\, adventure\, and family\, John’s songs tackl
 e subjects that are often left behind by the mainstream. He is a Krutz Art
 ist\, Kansas State Mandolin Champion for 2022\, and a member of KCAIC’s Ka
 nsas Touring Artist Roster. He’ll be accompanied by Jordan Hehl and Peter 
 Oviatt.\nClaire Cartwright-\nJennie Williams- plays country music and live
 s in Charleston\, West Virginia where she works as the WV state folklorist
 . She’s coming to Bloomington to defend her PhD and graduate — but first! 
 She’ll play a show at the Switchyard!\nNick Romy-has been a pillar in the 
 music community for more than twenty years in almost every facet of the sc
 ene\, traveling musician\, house show host\, sound engineer\, band leader 
 and instrument repair pro (Ardent Instruments). They have become integral 
 to anything music related in Bloomington. Often playing with ensembles Nic
 k will be sharing with us a rare solo set.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250504T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250504T213000
LOCATION:Switchyard House Venue\, 1417 South Monon Drive\, Blomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:John Depew Trio / Claire Cartwright / Jennie Williams / Nick Romy
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/john-depew-trio-claire-cartwright-jennie-william
 s-nick-romy/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Potlu
 ck at 5:30pm\, Music at 6pm</strong><br />\nJohn Depew Trio-is a musician\
 , songwriter\, and traveler with a knack for combining traditional sounds 
 with thoughtful lyrics and intriguing musicality. He has been described as
  a “midwestern Nick Drake” by Ted Gioia\, (musicologist.) He enjoys explor
 ing new places in both the natural world and in the wilderness within. Com
 bining philosophy\, farming\, adventure\, and family\, John’s songs tackle
  subjects that are often left behind by the mainstream. He is a Krutz Arti
 st\, Kansas State Mandolin Champion for 2022\, and a member of KCAIC’s Kan
 sas Touring Artist Roster. He’ll be accompanied by Jordan Hehl and Peter O
 viatt.</p>\n<p>Claire Cartwright-<br />\nJennie Williams- plays country mu
 sic and lives in Charleston\, West Virginia where she works as the WV stat
 e folklorist. She’s coming to Bloomington to defend her PhD and graduate —
  but first! She’ll play a show at the Switchyard!<br />\nNick Romy-has bee
 n a pillar in the music community for more than twenty years in almost eve
 ry facet of the scene\, traveling musician\, house show host\, sound engin
 eer\, band leader and instrument repair pro (Ardent Instruments). They hav
 e become integral to anything music related in Bloomington. Often playing 
 with ensembles Nick will be sharing with us a rare solo set.</p>\n</BODY><
 /HTML>
END:VEVENT
