BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-134845@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Sounds From the Black Hole\; 317-313-1501\; soundsfromtheblackhole@
 gmail.com\; https://www.facebook.com/events/1409672660202384/
DESCRIPTION:Show starts when the shop closes. Music starts by 7:30PM\nKBD i
 s the improvisational electroacoustic trio comprising Michael Kimaid\, Gab
 riel Beam\, and Ryan Dohm. Forming in 2006\, they visited Bloomington earl
 y on–playing at (—- — ——) on Prospect Hill in 2007. Last year they stopped
  by the Gulch again\, playing at Backspace Gallery. Stretched between Ohio
  and Texas\, they haven’t stopped yet. Currently on tour with a new casset
 te on Eh? Audio Repository\, catch them at Walkover Sounds May 8.\nKBD web
 site with photos and music links\nKBD on Instagram\n______________________
 __\nCompletely Dead. Brand new band\, first show. Local Gorenoise ft. memb
 er(s) of Desensitize.\nListen on YouTube\nListen on Bandcamp\n____________
 ____________\nSolo sets from Lather and The City Underground\, with collab
 orative overlap. The City Underground plays guitar via synth-controlled el
 ectromagnetism\, coaxing out the incorporeal voices humming between the bo
 dy and the strings. Lather processes field recordings through discarded ge
 ar\, sifting through the refuse to locate the resonances.\nThe City Underg
 round\nLather on Bandcamp
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250508T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250508T220000
LOCATION:Walkover Sounds\, 122 N. Walnut St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds From the Black Hole featuring: KBD // Completely Dead // Lat
 her + The City Underground
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-featuring-kbd-complet
 ely-dead-lather-the-city-underground/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Show starts w
 hen the shop closes. Music starts by 7:30PM<br />\n<strong>KBD</strong> is
  the improvisational electroacoustic trio comprising Michael Kimaid\, Gabr
 iel Beam\, and Ryan Dohm. Forming in 2006\, they visited Bloomington early
  on–playing at (—- — ——) on Prospect Hill in 2007. Last year they stopped 
 by the Gulch again\, playing at Backspace Gallery. Stretched between Ohio 
 and Texas\, they haven’t stopped yet. Currently on tour with a new cassett
 e on Eh? Audio Repository\, catch them at Walkover Sounds May 8.<br />\n<a
  href='https://www.thenoisyattic.com/'>KBD website with photos and music l
 inks</a><br />\n<a href='https://www.instagram.com/thenoisyattic/'>KBD on 
 Instagram</a></p>\n<p>________________________</p>\n<p><strong>Completely 
 Dead</strong>. Brand new band\, first show. Local Gorenoise ft. member(s) 
 of Desensitize.<br />\n<a href='https://www.youtube.com/@acw3606'>Listen o
 n YouTube</a><br />\n<a href='https://completelydead.bandcamp.com/'>Listen
  on Bandcamp</a></p>\n<p>________________________</p>\n<p>Solo sets from <
 strong>Lather</strong> and <strong>The City Underground</strong>\, with co
 llaborative overlap. The City Underground plays guitar via synth-controlle
 d electromagnetism\, coaxing out the incorporeal voices humming between th
 e body and the strings. Lather processes field recordings through discarde
 d gear\, sifting through the refuse to locate the resonances.<br />\n<a hr
 ef='https://www.thecityunderground.com/'>The City Underground</a><br />\n<
 a href='https://lather.bandcamp.com/'>Lather on Bandcamp</p>\n</BODY></HTM
 L>
