BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-135212@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6:30pm\nThe Legacy of Ousmane Sembène & Paulin S. Viey
 ra is a film series which celebrates the crucial role these two pioneers p
 layed in the formation of early African cinemas. In collaboration with Blo
 omington’s Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, every Thursday in May\, the public wi
 ll be invited to view African films at the BCT and to participate in discu
 ssions with film critics\, some of the filmmakers’ collaborators\, witness
 es from the period\, and African Film specialists. This public-facing even
 t series will bring together both the Indiana University and Bloomington c
 ommunities to engage in discussions of film\, African cultures\, the Frenc
 h-speaking world\, and postcolonial history. It will also act as a kick-of
 f event for the Collections of Sembène and Vieyra Archival Workshop which 
 will bring an international cohort of scholars to the Indiana University c
 ampus in Summer 2025.\nThis series is organized by the Early African Cinem
 as Lab and sponsored by the Public Arts and Humanities Project\, IU Depart
 ment of French and Italian & the African Studies Program.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250508T190000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20250515T190000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20250522T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Legacy of Sembène & Vieyra
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-legacy-of-sembene-vieyra/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 6:30pm</strong><br />\nThe Legacy of Ousmane Sembène & Paulin S. Vieyr
 a is a film series which celebrates the crucial role these two pioneers pl
 ayed in the formation of early African cinemas. In collaboration with Bloo
 mington’s Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, every Thursday in May\, the public wil
 l be invited to view African films at the BCT and to participate in discus
 sions with film critics\, some of the filmmakers’ collaborators\, witnesse
 s from the period\, and African Film specialists. This public-facing event
  series will bring together both the Indiana University and Bloomington co
 mmunities to engage in discussions of film\, African cultures\, the French
 -speaking world\, and postcolonial history. It will also act as a kick-off
  event for the Collections of Sembène and Vieyra Archival Workshop which w
 ill bring an international cohort of scholars to the Indiana University ca
 mpus in Summer 2025.</p>\n<p>This series is organized by the Early African
  Cinemas Lab and sponsored by the Public Arts and Humanities Project\, IU 
 Department of French and Italian & the African Studies Program.</p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
