UID:ai1ec-134847@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Lake Lemon Conservancy District\; (812) 334-0233\; operations@lakel
 emon.org\; https://clearvibestickets.com/event/riddle-point-boogie/?fbclid
 =IwY2xjawIrH8NleHRuA2FlbQIxMAABHQPs9xn0B_gZDMgjxqiDAn3aJPqQ48sClJbM2iletZ0
 fX8rOP-4G8SsfcQ_aem_RNrP0gYx-tm4XTzPCQcDYg
DESCRIPTION:After an unforgettable debut in 2023\, Riddle Point Boogie is B
 ACK for 2025—bigger and better than ever! Nestled along the scenic shores 
 of Lake Lemon\, this one-day festival brings together the best of American
 a and bluegrass music for an unforgettable experience—all while supporting
  the conservation of Lake Lemon. This event helps raise funds and awarenes
 s for the conservation of Lake Lemon\, ensuring that this beautiful natura
 l space is protected and preserved for generations to come.\nCamping Avail
 able. Gate open at noon\, music 2-10pm.\nPerformers include: Armchair Boog
 ie\, Mama Said String Band\, The Matchsellers\, Them Lasses and The Old Do
 gs\, Avocado Chic
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250510T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250510T220000
LOCATION:Riddle Point Park\, 7599 N Tunnel Road\, Unionville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Riddle Point Boogie\, Performers include: Armchair Boogie\, Mama Sa
 id String Band\, The Matchsellers\, Them Lasses and The Old Dogs\, Avocado
  Chic
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/riddle-point-boogie/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>After an unfo
 rgettable debut in 2023\, Riddle Point Boogie is BACK for 2025—bigger and 
 better than ever! Nestled along the scenic shores of Lake Lemon\, this one
 -day festival brings together the best of Americana and bluegrass music fo
 r an unforgettable experience—all while supporting the conservation of Lak
 e Lemon. <strong>This event helps raise funds and awareness for the conser
 vation of Lake Lemon\, ensuring that this beautiful natural space is prote
 cted and preserved for generations to come.</strong></p>\n<p>Camping Avail
 able. Gate open at noon\, music 2-10pm.<br />\nPerformers include: Armchai
 r Boogie\, Mama Said String Band\, The Matchsellers\, Them Lasses and The 
 Old Dogs\, Avocado Chic</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
