BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-135344@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 4:30pm\nThe capstone of our 55th anniversary season be
 gins with a trip down memory lane\, as we recreate the opening of the BSO’
 s very first concert with Nicolai’s Merry Wives of Windsor Overture. Our Y
 outh Concerto Competition Winner\, Catelijne Hunt\, shows us the talent of
  future musical generations with Saint-Saëns’s Introduction and Rondo Capr
 iccioso\, and we will revel in the artistry of our musicians of today with
  Sibelius’s Symphony No. 2. We’ve been making music with our community for
  55 seasons\; we hope that our audience at this concert will continue to c
 elebrate with us the many reasons we love calling Bloomington our home.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250518T170000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Symphony Orchestra: BSO Past\, Present\, and Future
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-symphony-orchestra-bso-past-present-
 and-future/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 4:30pm</strong><br />\nThe capstone of our 55th anniversary season beg
 ins with a trip down memory lane\, as we recreate the opening of the BSO’s
  very first concert with Nicolai’s Merry Wives of Windsor Overture. Our Yo
 uth Concerto Competition Winner\, Catelijne Hunt\, shows us the talent of 
 future musical generations with Saint-Saëns’s Introduction and Rondo Capri
 ccioso\, and we will revel in the artistry of our musicians of today with 
 Sibelius’s Symphony No. 2. We’ve been making music with our community for 
 55 seasons\; we hope that our audience at this concert will continue to ce
 lebrate with us the many reasons we love calling Bloomington our home.</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
