BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-135633@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 5pm\nNashville’s Dallas Ugly (Libby Weitnauer\, Owen B
 urton\, and Eli Broxham) are a band of truly trusted friends who – after a
  decade of playing together – return with their best work yet. Sitting som
 ewhere between indie rock and Americana\, and beautifully produced in coll
 aboration with Grammy winning engineer Justin Francis\, their sophomore al
 bum See Me Now is contemporary\, crisp\, and alive\, a fiddle-filled entry
  in the current band-with-guitar renaissance that puts them in conversatio
 n with acts like MJ Lenderman\, Big Thief\, and Allegra Krieger while stil
 l channelling the sparkly sing-along heights of late 90s radio. The growth
  of heartache\, finding footing in an unstable world\, and modern anxiety 
 resonate out in soaring harmony.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250524T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250524T200000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Dallas Ugly // Pat Otto
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/dallas-ugly-pat-otto/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 5pm</strong><br />\nNashville’s Dallas Ugly (Libby Weitnauer\, Owen Bu
 rton\, and Eli Broxham) are a band of truly trusted friends who – after a 
 decade of playing together – return with their best work yet. Sitting some
 where between indie rock and Americana\, and beautifully produced in colla
 boration with Grammy winning engineer Justin Francis\, their sophomore alb
 um See Me Now is contemporary\, crisp\, and alive\, a fiddle-filled entry 
 in the current band-with-guitar renaissance that puts them in conversation
  with acts like MJ Lenderman\, Big Thief\, and Allegra Krieger while still
  channelling the sparkly sing-along heights of late 90s radio. The growth 
 of heartache\, finding footing in an unstable world\, and modern anxiety r
 esonate out in soaring harmony.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
