BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-135546@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:soundsfromtheblackhole@gmail.com\; https://link.dice.fm/G2a6c0f5857
 f
DESCRIPTION:Ambient psychedelia\, hypnotic sound collage\, and synthesized 
 worlds with Dylan Ryan\, Drekka\, and Taylor K. Sullivan-Peters.\n8PM DOOR
 S /// 830PM SHOW /// ALL-AGES\n________________________\nChicago-based Dyl
 an Ryan makes a return to Orbit Room\, this time performing material from 
 his new solo album\, In The Same Room With A Cactus\,” on eyes&ears Record
 s. Dylan’s band Bronze performed at Sounds From the Black Hole in January 
 2025. This solo album is the result of 3 years of work\, written primarily
  on synthesizer and drum machine. The results are reminiscent of komische\
 , new age\, and the softer facets of jazz. For this live presentation\, Dy
 lan will be joined by Nate Lepine on soprano saxophone.\nDylan Ryan has pl
 ayed with Bronze\, SAND\, Man Man\, Ether Feather\, The Red Krayola\, Bitc
 hen Bajas\, Icy Demons\, and has albums out on Cuneiform Records.\nDylan R
 yan – In The Same Room With A Cactus\n________________________\nWorking un
 der the name DREKKA since 1996\, American composer Michael Anderson has to
 ured\, traveled\, and collaborated extensively\; collecting memories and b
 uilding a personalized archive of sound that dates back to the mid-1980’s.
 \nAnderson’s work dwells heavily on themes of silence\, memory\, and forge
 tfulness\; functioning as a direct line to the mind and its tenuous cache 
 of memories. An unguarded freneticism is clearly on display\, rather than 
 being obscured by poetic abstractions\; seeking to occupy and confront tho
 se dark spaces which comprise the tenuous province of memory\, dreams\, an
 xiety\, and a palpable\, haunted sense of liminality.\nMichael also perfor
 ms in the groups Crisping Lover and Water Is The Sun.\nDrekka website\n___
 _____________________\nTaylor K. Sullivan-Peters is a musician\, electrica
 l engineer and instrument builder based out of Indianapolis. Using homemad
 e synthesizers and electronic circuitry\, Taylor creates dynamic fields of
  sound–power ambient that can contain gentle\, enveloping baths to swarmin
 g pricks and stabs. This is exciting\, adventurous ambient that takes you 
 on a journey through your own mind.\nBandcamp\nEyewool International (Synt
 hs & Pedals)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250524T200000
LOCATION:Orbit Room - 107 N. College Ave suite 001\, underground
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds From the Black Hole ft. Dylan Ryan\, Drekka & Taylor K. Sull
 ivan-Peters
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-ft-dylan-ryan-drekka-
 taylor-k-sullivan-peters/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div id=':1wv' c
 lass='Am aiL Al editable LW-avf tS-tW tS-tY' role='textbox' aria-label='Me
 ssage Body' aria-controls=':24s' aria-expanded='false'>\n<div>\n<div>Ambie
 nt psychedelia\, hypnotic sound collage\, and synthesized worlds with Dyla
 n Ryan\, Drekka\, and Taylor K. Sullivan-Peters.<br />\n8PM DOORS /// 830P
 M SHOW /// ALL-AGES</div>\n<div>________________________<br />\nChicago-ba
 sed Dylan Ryan makes a return to Orbit Room\, this time performing materia
 l from his new solo album\, In The Same Room With A Cactus\,” on eyes&ears
  Records. Dylan’s band Bronze performed at Sounds From the Black Hole in J
 anuary 2025. This solo album is the result of 3 years of work\, written pr
 imarily on synthesizer and drum machine. The results are reminiscent of ko
 mische\, new age\, and the softer facets of jazz. For this live presentati
 on\, Dylan will be joined by Nate Lepine on soprano saxophone.</p>\n<p>Dyl
 an Ryan has played with Bronze\, SAND\, Man Man\, Ether Feather\, The Red 
 Krayola\, Bitchen Bajas\, Icy Demons\, and has albums out on Cuneiform Rec
 ords.<br />\n<a href='https://dylanryan.bandcamp.com/album/in-the-same-roo
 m-with-a-cactus' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Dylan Ryan – In The Same R
 oom With A Cactus</a></div>\n<div>________________________<br />\nWorking 
 under the name DREKKA since 1996\, American composer Michael Anderson has 
 toured\, traveled\, and collaborated extensively\; collecting memories and
  building a personalized archive of sound that dates back to the mid-1980’
 s.</p>\n<p>Anderson’s work dwells heavily on themes of silence\, memory\, 
 and forgetfulness\; functioning as a direct line to the mind and its tenuo
 us cache of memories. An unguarded freneticism is clearly on display\, rat
 her than being obscured by poetic abstractions\; seeking to occupy and con
 front those dark spaces which comprise the tenuous province of memory\, dr
 eams\, anxiety\, and a palpable\, haunted sense of liminality.</p>\n<p>Mic
 hael also performs in the groups Crisping Lover and Water Is The Sun.<br /
 >\n<a href='https://bluesanct.com/bands/drekka/' target='_blank' rel='noop
 ener'>Drekka website</a></div>\n<div>________________________<br />\nTaylo
 r K. Sullivan-Peters is a musician\, electrical engineer and instrument bu
 ilder based out of Indianapolis. Using homemade synthesizers and electroni
 c circuitry\, Taylor creates dynamic fields of sound–power ambient that ca
 n contain gentle\, enveloping baths to swarming pricks and stabs. This is 
 exciting\, adventurous ambient that takes you on a journey through your ow
 n mind.<br />\n<a href='https://taylorksullivanpeters.bandcamp.com/' targe
 t='_blank' rel='noopener'>Bandcamp</a></div>\n<div><a href='https://eyewoo
 l.international/' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Eyewool International</a>
  (Synths & Pedals)</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
