BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136010@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Proceeds from this event are going to support Sacred Valley Pro
 ject (SVP) in Calca and Ollantaytambo\, Peru. Sacred Valley Project provid
 es a dormitory\, meals\, school fees\, uniforms\, supplies\, and tutoring 
 so that high school girls in remote areas of the Andes Mountains can compl
 ete their secondary education.\nA Silent Disco is an event where people da
 nce to music heard through wireless headphones. The music is transmitted d
 irectly to each person’s headphones – on three separate channels – rather 
 than played through speakers. Those without headphones hear no music (othe
 r than people who sing along to what they are hearing). The three channels
  of music can be selected using a simple switch on each person’s headphone
 s\, and headphones light up blue\, red or green to show visually what chan
 nel you are listening to. People can dance to the same tune as others with
  them\, or to their own selection. If you hear a song you don’t like\, or 
 get tired of a particular style of music\, just switch channels.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250530T190000
LOCATION:Cedar Creek Winery\, Brewery and Distillery\, 3820 Leonard Road\, 
 Martinsville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Silent Disco
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/silent-disco-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Proce
 eds from this event are going to support Sacred Valley Project (SVP) in Ca
 lca and Ollantaytambo\, Peru. Sacred Valley Project provides a dormitory\,
  meals\, school fees\, uniforms\, supplies\, and tutoring so that high sch
 ool girls in remote areas of the Andes Mountains can complete their second
 ary education.</strong><br />\nA Silent Disco is an event where people dan
 ce to music heard through wireless headphones. The music is transmitted di
 rectly to each person’s headphones – on three separate channels – rather t
 han played through speakers. Those without headphones hear no music (other
  than people who sing along to what they are hearing). The three channels 
 of music can be selected using a simple switch on each person’s headphones
 \, and headphones light up blue\, red or green to show visually what chann
 el you are listening to. People can dance to the same tune as others with 
 them\, or to their own selection. If you hear a song you don’t like\, or g
 et tired of a particular style of music\, just switch channels.</p>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
