BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136117@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join Mayor Kerry Thomson\, Councilmember Hopi Stosberg\, and Di
 rector of Economic and Sustainable Development Jane Kupersmith for the Dis
 trict 3 Traveling Town Hall. This event offers residents the chance to con
 nect directly with City leaders\, ask questions\, and learn more about key
  projects and city services.\nThe evening will begin with brief updates fr
 om the Mayor\, followed by a Q&A session based on submitted questions. If 
 time allows\, the event will conclude with live questions from attendees.
 \nTraveling Town Halls are held in a different district every other month 
 as part of the City’s commitment to transparent\, accessible government. R
 esidents of District 3—and anyone interested in how city services are deli
 vered—are encouraged to attend.\nThe meeting will be broadcast live on Com
 munity Access Television Services (CATS) and available for on-demand viewi
 ng at catstv.net.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250602T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250602T190000
LOCATION:1111 North Russell Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mayor Kerry Thomson’s Traveling Town Hall
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mayor-kerry-thomsons-traveling-town-hall-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join Mayor Ke
 rry Thomson\, Councilmember Hopi Stosberg\, and Director of Economic and S
 ustainable Development Jane Kupersmith for the District 3 Traveling Town H
 all. This event offers residents the chance to connect directly with City 
 leaders\, ask questions\, and learn more about key projects and city servi
 ces.<br />\nThe evening will begin with brief updates from the Mayor\, fol
 lowed by a Q&A session based on submitted questions. If time allows\, the 
 event will conclude with live questions from attendees.<br />\nTraveling T
 own Halls are held in a different district every other month as part of th
 e City’s commitment to transparent\, accessible government. Residents of D
 istrict 3—and anyone interested in how city services are delivered—are enc
 ouraged to attend.<br />\n<strong>The meeting will be broadcast live on Co
 mmunity Access Television Services (CATS) and available for on-demand view
 ing at catstv.net.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
