DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://bloomingtoncommunityorchard.org/site/
DESCRIPTION:These events are open to the public\, with no registration or e
 xperience required (though we appreciate advance notice for groups of 5+ p
 eople). We simply ask that you dress appropriately to do outdoor work\, an
 d bring plenty of water to stay hydrated. Snacks and drinks will be provid
 ed as well as any other tools you may need to help out!\nWe hope you can j
 oin us to get outside and enjoy nature\, make new friends\, and learn some
  sustainable\, organic orcharding practices. All are welcome!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250604T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250604T200000
EXDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20250709T170000
LOCATION:Bloomington Community Orchard\, 2120 S Highland Ave\, Bloomington
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;UNTIL=20250827T235959Z;BYDAY=WE;WKST=MO
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Work and Learn Days
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/work-and-learn-wednesdays-2025/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>These events 
 are open to the public\, with no registration or experience required (thou
 gh we appreciate advance notice for groups of 5+ people). We simply ask th
 at you dress appropriately to do outdoor work\, and bring plenty of water 
 to stay hydrated. Snacks and drinks will be provided as well as any other 
 tools you may need to help out!</p>\n<p>We hope you can join us to get out
 side and enjoy nature\, make new friends\, and learn some sustainable\, or
 ganic orcharding practices. All are welcome!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
