BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-135957@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Davey Osborne is an average 11-year-old boy with an overactive 
 imagination. He spends his days playing video games and pretending to be a
  spy with his imaginary father-figure\, Jack Flack – a substitute for his 
 real father\, who is struggling with the recent death of Davey’s mother. H
 owever\, fantasy becomes reality for Davey after he witnesses the murder o
 f an FBI agent\, who in his dying breath\, gives Davey a mysterious video 
 game cartridge called Cloak & Dagger\, which in actuality contains top-sec
 ret government information. With the help of his younger friend Kim\, the 
 tech savvy Morris\, and even a little help from his fictional secret agent
  mentor\, Davey must stay one step ahead of pursuers as he tries to surviv
 e a real-life game of espionage in the streets of San Antonio\, Texas.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250605T210000
LOCATION:Rev. Ernest D. Butler Park\, 812 West 9th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Parks and Recreation\, Cicada Cinema and Granfalloon pr
 esent “Cloak and Dagger” (1984\, rated PG)
