BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136632@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening with Russell S. Kitchner with a special 
 presentation about his book\, Alaska: Where There Was A Way\, featuring th
 e beauty of an untouched Alaska.\nA Common Man in an Enchanted Land\nThis 
 is the story of Will Kitchner who\, in 1937 and age 19\, traveled from his
  home in Syracuse\, NY to Seattle\, WA where he boarded a freighter bound 
 for Alaska. During the following 4 years Will worked a gold claim northeas
 t of Fairbanks and a fur-trapping line on the Salcha River before returnin
 g home to Syracuse where he passed away at age 38. His legacy was secured 
 by Kodachrome slides he took in an effort to capture the timeless beauty o
 f the largely unexplored Alaska Territory before it had been touched by th
 e modern civilization.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250612T180000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books\, 849 Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Author Presentation with Russell S. Kitchner
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/author-presentation-with-russell-s-kitchner/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us for a
 n evening with Russell S. Kitchner with a special presentation about his b
 ook\, Alaska: Where There Was A Way\, featuring the beauty of an untouched
  Alaska.<br />\nA Common Man in an Enchanted Land<br />\nThis is the story
  of Will Kitchner who\, in 1937 and age 19\, traveled from his home in Syr
 acuse\, NY to Seattle\, WA where he boarded a freighter bound for Alaska. 
 During the following 4 years Will worked a gold claim northeast of Fairban
 ks and a fur-trapping line on the Salcha River before returning home to Sy
 racuse where he passed away at age 38. His legacy was secured by Kodachrom
 e slides he took in an effort to capture the timeless beauty of the largel
 y unexplored Alaska Territory before it had been touched by the modern civ
 ilization. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
