BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136680@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Juneteenth also known as Freedom Day\, Jubilee Day\, Liberation
  Day\, and Emancipation Day\, is a holiday celebrating the emancipation of
  those who had been enslaved in the United States. Originating in Galvesto
 n\, Texas\, it is now celebrated annually on the 19th of June throughout t
 he United States\, with varying official recognition. It is commemorated o
 n the anniversary date of the June 19\, 1865 announcement by Union Army ge
 neral Gordon Granger\, proclaiming freedom from slavery in Texas.\nThank y
 ou to our Presenting Sponsor South Central Community Action Program\nJoin 
 the City of Bloomington for entertainment\, food\, fun\, music and communi
 ty as we commemorate Juneteenth. This event is free to the public and in c
 onjunction with Food Truck Fridays\, in partnership with Parks and Recreat
 ion and Community and Family Resources Department. We encourage community 
 members to bring chairs and blankets if they prefer to sit on the lawn.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250613T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250613T210000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 South Rogers St.\, Blomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:City of Bloomington Juneteenth Event (in conjunction with Food Truc
 k Friday)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/city-of-bloomington-juneteenth-event-in-conjunct
 ion-with-food-truck-friday/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Juneteenth al
 so known as Freedom Day\, Jubilee Day\, Liberation Day\, and Emancipation 
 Day\, is a holiday celebrating the emancipation of those who had been ensl
 aved in the United States. Originating in Galveston\, Texas\, it is now ce
 lebrated annually on the 19th of June throughout the United States\, with 
 varying official recognition. It is commemorated on the anniversary date o
 f the June 19\, 1865 announcement by Union Army general Gordon Granger\, p
 roclaiming freedom from slavery in Texas.</p>\n<p>Thank you to our Present
 ing Sponsor South Central Community Action Program<br />\nJoin the City of
  Bloomington for entertainment\, food\, fun\, music and community as we co
 mmemorate Juneteenth. This event is free to the public and in conjunction 
 with Food Truck Fridays\, in partnership with Parks and Recreation and Com
 munity and Family Resources Department. We encourage community members to 
 bring chairs and blankets if they prefer to sit on the lawn. </p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
END:VEVENT
