BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136841@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Info at hoosieroriginalmusic.com/farmette2025\nFARMette is a on
 e-day music networking and showcasing conference designed to elevate the v
 oices of folk and singer-songwriters in Indiana while fostering connection
 s with industry partners who hire them—festivals\, fairs\, venues\, and mo
 re. This conference celebrates the transformative power of music and commu
 nity\, inviting participants to rekindle their sense of purpose and creati
 vity.\nWith engaging panels like Care of Acoustic Instruments: Advice from
  a Master Luthier\, Best Practices for Live Sound\, and How to Create Show
  Success: Partnerships That Work\, FARMette provides invaluable resources 
 for artists and industry professionals alike. Together\, we’ll explore the
  magic of storytelling through song\, uncovering the awe and wonder that f
 uels artistic endeavors and strengthens our shared cultural fabric.\nFARMe
 tte 2025 will take place in venues throughout Nashville\, Indiana. Venue h
 ost spaces include The Nashville House\, The Ferguson House\, Country Heri
 tage Winery\, The Visitors Center\, Daily Grind\, Bartley House\, Common G
 round\, and more. Official showcases\, panels\, keynote\, and industry eve
 nts for Industry Pass holders will take place at the Brown County Playhous
 e.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250621T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250621T213000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St.\, Nashville\, IN (and 
 many other locations in that town)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:FARMette 2025\, the 2nd Annual music networking and showcasing conf
 erence of the Hoosier Original Music Association
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/farmette-2025-the-2nd-annual-music-networking-an
 d-showcasing-conference-of-the-hoosier-original-music-association/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Info 
 at hoosieroriginalmusic.com/farmette2025</strong><br />\nFARMette is a one
 -day music networking and showcasing conference designed to elevate the vo
 ices of folk and singer-songwriters in Indiana while fostering connections
  with industry partners who hire them—festivals\, fairs\, venues\, and mor
 e. This conference celebrates the transformative power of music and commun
 ity\, inviting participants to rekindle their sense of purpose and creativ
 ity.<br />\nWith engaging panels like Care of Acoustic Instruments: Advice
  from a Master Luthier\, Best Practices for Live Sound\, and How to Create
  Show Success: Partnerships That Work\, FARMette provides invaluable resou
 rces for artists and industry professionals alike. Together\, we’ll explor
 e the magic of storytelling through song\, uncovering the awe and wonder t
 hat fuels artistic endeavors and strengthens our shared cultural fabric.<b
 r />\n<strong>FARMette 2025 will take place in venues throughout Nashville
 \, Indiana. Venue host spaces include The Nashville House\, The Ferguson H
 ouse\, Country Heritage Winery\, The Visitors Center\, Daily Grind\, Bartl
 ey House\, Common Ground\, and more. Official showcases\, panels\, keynote
 \, and industry events for Industry Pass holders will take place at the Br
 own County Playhouse.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136942@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Our Lothlorien celebration of the Summer Solstice and the peak 
 of summer and thank you to our members. It’s a quieter community event\, m
 ore loosely planned than larger festivals with a seasonal ritual on Saturd
 ay evening. It’s an opportunity to wander the woods or hang out in the sha
 de of the trees. There are no festival fees (only members can stay overnig
 ht). Sign-in will be on the field or along the driveway. It’s also a great
  opportunity to introduce friends and family to Lothlorien. Saturday durin
 g the day is a sort of open house. You are welcome to arrive Friday also.
 \nThere will be a community potluck Saturday afternoon. There will be a He
 art Tree Ritual and a sand painting in Thunder Saturday evening.-usually f
 eaturing a sand mandala.-More details soon!\nI forgot to credit the artist
 -DeAnna Sampson Downey
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250621T230000
LOCATION:Lothlorien'Nature Sanctuary/Elvin Home\, 559 McFadden Ridge Rd\, B
 edford
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20250622T100000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Solstice ReUnion
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/solstice-reunion/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Our Lothlorie
 n celebration of the Summer Solstice and the peak of summer and thank you 
 to our members. It’s a quieter community event\, more loosely planned than
  larger festivals with a seasonal ritual on Saturday evening. It’s an oppo
 rtunity to wander the woods or hang out in the shade of the trees. There a
 re no festival fees (only members can stay overnight). Sign-in will be on 
 the field or along the driveway. It’s also a great opportunity to introduc
 e friends and family to Lothlorien. Saturday during the day is a sort of o
 pen house. You are welcome to arrive Friday also.<br />\nThere will be a c
 ommunity potluck Saturday afternoon. There will be a Heart Tree Ritual and
  a sand painting in Thunder Saturday evening.-usually featuring a sand man
 dala.-More details soon!<br />\nI forgot to credit the artist-DeAnna Samps
 on Downey</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136893@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Aly Elliott\, author of The Right Way to Drown\, is joining us 
 at Morgenstern Books for an exclusive book signing! Come on by to meet the
  author of this moving memoir. In this deeply moving memoir\, Aly chronicl
 es her journey through grief. She reveals how she found solace through pai
 nt and pixels. A blend of personal reflection and candid storytelling\, re
 aders will discover how she found purpose and resilience through her creat
 ive expression\, ultimately leading to her career as an award-winning Bere
 avement Artist. The Right Way to Drown is a testament to the enduring powe
 r of art and faith in navigating life’s greatest losses.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250621T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250621T150000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books\, 849 Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Author Signing: Aly Elliott
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/author-signing-aly-elliott/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Aly Elliott\,
  author of The Right Way to Drown\, is joining us at Morgenstern Books for
  an exclusive book signing! Come on by to meet the author of this moving m
 emoir. In this deeply moving memoir\, Aly chronicles her journey through g
 rief. She reveals how she found solace through paint and pixels. A blend o
 f personal reflection and candid storytelling\, readers will discover how 
 she found purpose and resilience through her creative expression\, ultimat
 ely leading to her career as an award-winning Bereavement Artist. The Righ
 t Way to Drown is a testament to the enduring power of art and faith in na
 vigating life’s greatest losses.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
