BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136900@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The term Blue Zones was first coined by Dan Buettner to describ
 e areas of the world where people not only lived longer than the rest of t
 he world\, but also enjoyed a higher quality of life. where people not onl
 y lived longer but also enjoyed a high quality of life in their old age. T
 his 45- minute documentary takes us to the villages of Sardinia to a sunny
  suburb of California\, as Dan and his team explore what has contributed t
 o these communities’ amazing lifespans. A brief discussion will follow the
  screening.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250622T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250622T170000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S Van Buren St\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:(Film) Live to 100: Secrets of the Blue Zones
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/film-live-to-100-secrets-of-the-blue-zones/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The term Blue
  Zones was first coined by Dan Buettner to describe areas of the world whe
 re people not only lived longer than the rest of the world\, but also enjo
 yed a higher quality of life. where people not only lived longer but also 
 enjoyed a high quality of life in their old age. This 45- minute documenta
 ry takes us to the villages of Sardinia to a sunny suburb of California\, 
 as Dan and his team explore what has contributed to these communities’ ama
 zing lifespans. A brief discussion will follow the screening.</p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
END:VEVENT
