BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136776@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:liblilly@iu.edu
DESCRIPTION:A family-friendly event to celebrate Pollinator Week.  Pollinat
 ors and the plants that they help sustain are crucial parts of our environ
 ment\, in Bloomington and all over the world. Learn about these amazing cr
 eatures!\nPage through historical materials from the Lilly Library’s colle
 ctions\, including sumptuously illustrated herbals and medieval books\, wa
 tercolor nature diaries\, original photographs by Frank Hohenberger\, and 
 much more! Or try your hand at some pollinator-themed puzzles with our Cur
 ator of Puzzles.\nRepresentatives from the Wylie House Museum will be on h
 and to talk about how to plant your own garden to enjoy. Take home some se
 eds for native Indiana plants and learn about the Wylie House heirloom gar
 den.\nAnd if you’re feeling creative\, learn how to make a simple nature d
 iary to document your own adventures outside.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250625T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250625T160000
LOCATION:IU Lilly Library: 1200 E. 7th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Pollinator Week pop-up exhibition
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/pollinator-week-pop-up-exhibition/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A family-frie
 ndly event to celebrate Pollinator Week.  Pollinators and the plants that 
 they help sustain are crucial parts of our environment\, in Bloomington an
 d all over the world. Learn about these amazing creatures!</p>\n<p>Page th
 rough historical materials from the Lilly Library’s collections\, includin
 g sumptuously illustrated herbals and medieval books\, watercolor nature d
 iaries\, original photographs by Frank Hohenberger\, and much more! Or try
  your hand at some pollinator-themed puzzles with our Curator of Puzzles.<
 /p>\n<p>Representatives from the Wylie House Museum will be on hand to tal
 k about how to plant your own garden to enjoy. Take home some seeds for na
 tive Indiana plants and learn about the Wylie House heirloom garden.</p>\n
 <p>And if you’re feeling creative\, learn how to make a simple nature diar
 y to document your own adventures outside.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
