BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136056@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://browncountyplayhouse.org/event/journeyman-eric-clapton-trib
 ute-2025/
DESCRIPTION:Shaun Hague\, bandleader\, has built quite the resume in the te
 n years. At just 17\, he was named “The Best Young Blues Guitarist” by The
  House of Blues\, and by 21\, the young guitarist was playing guitar for B
 lues phenom Kenny Wayne Shepherd. In his career\, he has shared the stage 
 with Amos Lee\, John Waite\, and Terra Naomi\, as well as performing on Ja
 y Leno and sitting in with John Fogerty! Together\, Hague and the band pro
 vide a powerful performance of all aspects of Clapton’s career from Bluesb
 reakers to From The Cradle!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250626T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250626T213000
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse\, 70 S. Van Buren St Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Journeyman – Eric Clapton Tribute
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/journeyman-eric-clapton-tribute/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Shaun Hague\,
  bandleader\, has built quite the resume in the ten years. At just 17\, he
  was named “The Best Young Blues Guitarist” by The House of Blues\, and by
  21\, the young guitarist was playing guitar for Blues phenom Kenny Wayne 
 Shepherd. In his career\, he has shared the stage with Amos Lee\, John Wai
 te\, and Terra Naomi\, as well as performing on Jay Leno and sitting in wi
 th John Fogerty! Together\, Hague and the band provide a powerful performa
 nce of all aspects of Clapton’s career from Bluesbreakers to From The Crad
 le!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136053@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Cicada Cinema
DESCRIPTION:An outrageous lesbian pop musical satire inspired by the pop fr
 enzy of the early 2000s\, QUEENS OF DRAMA charts the rise and fall of new 
 star Mimi Madamour and her passionate\, rage-fueled love affair with punk 
 icon Billie Kohler. Over the course of half a century we follow these dram
 a queens as they top the charts and set sail on the course of mad queer lo
 ve. Featuring an iconic cast\, including Asia Argento and Alma Jodorowsky\
 , and containing hit songs like ‘Don’t Touch’ by Yelle and ‘Fisted to the 
 Heart’\, this film vividly dissects the turbulence of toxic relationships—
 whether between fans and their idols or within passionate queer love affai
 rs. Director Alexis Langlois brings their trademark glittercore pop-punk a
 esthetic to create a vibrant\, unforgettable spectacle of music and passio
 n.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250626T200000
LOCATION:The Back Door\, 207 S. College Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema Presents ‘Queens of Drama’
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-queens-of-drama/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>\n<div>\n<d
 iv>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>An outrageous lesbian pop musical satire insp
 ired by the pop frenzy of the early 2000s\, QUEENS OF DRAMA charts the ris
 e and fall of new star Mimi Madamour and her passionate\, rage-fueled love
  affair with punk icon Billie Kohler. Over the course of half a century we
  follow these drama queens as they top the charts and set sail on the cour
 se of mad queer love. Featuring an iconic cast\, including Asia Argento an
 d Alma Jodorowsky\, and containing hit songs like ‘Don’t Touch’ by Yelle a
 nd ‘Fisted to the Heart’\, this film vividly dissects the turbulence of to
 xic relationships—whether between fans and their idols or within passionat
 e queer love affairs. Director Alexis Langlois brings their trademark glit
 tercore pop-punk aesthetic to create a vibrant\, unforgettable spectacle o
 f music and passion.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n
 </BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
