BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136968@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Bodies\, limestone\, satin\, green sun\, resonances\, and langu
 age.\nA unique improvised performance unfolding in the spaces we move by e
 very day. You’ll encounter dance\, music and poetry—an invitation into new
  relationships with downtown’s familiar places.\nWhat becomes possible whe
 n we come together in creative space?\nWhat can be said that usually goes 
 unsaid?\nWhat does it mean to dwell in deeper dialogue—with one another\, 
 and with what is already here?\nThis meandering performance walk is about 
 being with each other—an unfolding of presence where something uncommon ma
 y emerge. How do we gather to see differently\, to be differently together
  in these uncommon times?\nCome be inspired. Be surprised. Take some time.
  Meet someone new.\nThe performance begins under the large tree on the Nor
 thwest Lawn of the Courthouse\, across from Social Cantina.\nWe’ll begin t
 here and slowly travel two blocks\, with performance surprises in local bu
 sinesses\, ending at the Monroe County History Center.\nTasty cool treats 
 will be provided during and after.\nOptional interactive prompts offered. 
 Linger\, play\, and explore after the performance.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250627T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250627T200000
LOCATION:Monroe County Courthouse\, Northwest Lawn\, 100 W Kirkwood Ave\, B
 loomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:“Ordinary Pilgrimage” improvised performance with dance\, music\, a
 nd poetry
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ordinary-pilgrimage-improvised-performance-with-
 dance-music-and-poetry/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><span style='
 color: #000000\;'>Bodies\, limestone\, satin\, green sun\, resonances\, an
 d language.</span></p>\n<p><span style='color: #000000\;'>A unique improvi
 sed performance unfolding in the spaces we move by every day. You’ll encou
 nter dance\, music and poetry—an invitation into new relationships with do
 wntown’s familiar places.</span></p>\n<p><span style='color: #000000\;'>Wh
 at becomes possible when we come together in creative space?<br />\nWhat c
 an be said that usually goes unsaid?<br />\nWhat does it mean to dwell in 
 deeper dialogue—with one another\, and with what is already here?</span></
 p>\n<p><span style='color: #000000\;'>This meandering performance walk is 
 about being with each other—an unfolding of presence where something uncom
 mon may emerge. How do we gather to see differently\, to <em>be</em> diffe
 rently together in these uncommon times?</span></p>\n<p><span style='color
 : #000000\;'>Come be inspired. Be surprised. Take some time. Meet someone 
 new.</span></p>\n<p><span style='color: #000000\;'>The performance begins 
 under the large tree on the Northwest Lawn of the Courthouse\, across from
  Social Cantina.<br />\nWe’ll begin there and slowly travel two blocks\, w
 ith performance surprises in local businesses\, ending at the Monroe Count
 y History Center.</span></p>\n<p><span style='color: #000000\;'>Tasty cool
  treats will be provided during and after.<br />\nOptional interactive pro
 mpts offered. Linger\, play\, and explore after the performance.</span></p
 >\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
