BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-137248@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Duke Energy & SCI REMC\nThe Brown County Touch-A-T
 ruck event is a free\, hands-on event that provides kids with the opportun
 ity to see\, touch and explore their favorite big trucks\, heavy equipment
  and emergency vehicles as well as interact with community support leaders
  including police officers\, firemen\, construction workers and more! Brin
 g the entire family to get up close with these vehicles\, learn about what
  they do\, how they work and how they benefit our community!\nWe suggest t
 hat you bring ear protection for babies and children to protect their ears
  from noise and to prevent them from becoming startled by the sudden and u
 nexpected sounds of horns and sirens. We have a “quiet hour” from 10 a.m. 
 to 11 a.m. where no horns are allowed. Don’t forget sunscreen and bring wa
 ter bottles to help your family stay cool and hydrated in the heat.  \nAll
  donations benefit Brown County Weekend Backpacks\, a community-led\, tota
 lly-volunteer program whose goal is keeping hungry children fed with nutri
 tious food all weekend long.\n​Parent supervision is required and cameras 
 are highly recommended.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250628T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250628T130000
LOCATION:Brown County Music Center\, 200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Brown County Touch-a-Truck\, with All donations benefit Brown Count
 y Weekend Backpacks\, a community-led\, totally-volunteer program whose go
 al is keeping hungry children fed with nutritious food all weekend long.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/brown-county-touch-a-truck-with-all-donations-be
 nefit-brown-county-weekend-backpacks-a-community-led-totally-volunteer-pro
 gram-whose-goal-is-keeping-hungry-children-fed-with-nutritious-food-all-we
 e/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Prese
 nted by Duke Energy & SCI REMC</strong></p>\n<p>The Brown County Touch-A-T
 ruck event is a free\, hands-on event that provides kids with the opportun
 ity to see\, touch and explore their favorite big trucks\, heavy equipment
  and emergency vehicles as well as interact with community support leaders
  including police officers\, firemen\, construction workers and more! Brin
 g the entire family to get up close with these vehicles\, learn about what
  they do\, how they work and how they benefit our community!</p>\n<p>We su
 ggest that you bring ear protection for babies and children to protect the
 ir ears from noise and to prevent them from becoming startled by the sudde
 n and unexpected sounds of horns and sirens. We have a “quiet hour” from 1
 0 a.m. to 11 a.m. where no horns are allowed. Don’t forget sunscreen and b
 ring water bottles to help your family stay cool and hydrated in the heat.
   </p>\n<p>All donations benefit Brown County Weekend Backpacks\, a commun
 ity-led\, totally-volunteer program whose goal is keeping hungry children 
 fed with nutritious food all weekend long.</p>\n<p>​Parent supervision is 
 required and cameras are highly recommended. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
