BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136774@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Ben Myers\; soundsfromtheblackhole@gmail.com\; https://link.dice.fm
 /D84320a06730
DESCRIPTION:Two exciting\, improvised trios featuring musicians from St. Lo
 uis\, Chicago and Bloomington.\nALL-AGES\n________________________\nAlex C
 unningham (violin\, STL) / Damon Smith (double bass\, STL) / Jerome Bryert
 on (drums\, CHI)\nWhile all of this trio has been to Bloomington\, they ha
 ve never performed here all together. Jerome and Damon performed alongside
  Ortet last fall at Russian Recording\, but Alex has not been since 2017. 
 All seasoned improvisers\, this trio will conjure wild sounds together\, c
 omposed on the fly. Damon has been a student and explorer of the upright b
 ass for decades\, also running the label Balance Point Acoustics. Jerome a
 nd Alex are both accomplished visual artists as well. Jerome is a print-ma
 ker and painter\, and Alex creates collages that are just as kinetic as hi
 s playing.\nhttps://www.alexcunninghamviolin.com/\nhttps://balancepointaco
 ustics.com/\nhttp://www.jeromebryerton.com/\n________________________\nLXQ
  trio is Lather on tapes\, electronics and strings\, Xylocept on synthesiz
 er and electronics\, and Kyle Quass on trumpet and percussion. They perfor
 med last fall at Backspace Gallery (that performance is available on Lathe
 r’s bandcamp) and are excited to come together again for a sonic adventure
 .\nhttps://lather.bandcamp.com/\nhttps://xylocept.bandcamp.com/\nhttps://k
 ylequass.bandcamp.com/
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250628T200000
LOCATION:Orbit Room - 107 N. College Ave suite 001\, underground
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds From the Black Hole ft. Alex Cunningham / Damon Smith / Jero
 me Bryerton and LXQ trio
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-ft-alex-cunningham-da
 mon-smith-jerome-bryerton-lxq-trio/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Two exciting\
 , improvised trios featuring musicians from St. Louis\, Chicago and Bloomi
 ngton.<br />\nALL-AGES<br />\n________________________<br />\nAlex Cunning
 ham (violin\, STL) / Damon Smith (double bass\, STL) / Jerome Bryerton (dr
 ums\, CHI)<br />\nWhile all of this trio has been to Bloomington\, they ha
 ve never performed here all together. Jerome and Damon performed alongside
  Ortet last fall at Russian Recording\, but Alex has not been since 2017. 
 All seasoned improvisers\, this trio will conjure wild sounds together\, c
 omposed on the fly. Damon has been a student and explorer of the upright b
 ass for decades\, also running the label Balance Point Acoustics. Jerome a
 nd Alex are both accomplished visual artists as well. Jerome is a print-ma
 ker and painter\, and Alex creates collages that are just as kinetic as hi
 s playing.<br />\nhttps://www.alexcunninghamviolin.com/<br />\nhttps://bal
 ancepointacoustics.com/<br />\nhttp://www.jeromebryerton.com/<br />\n_____
 ___________________<br />\nLXQ trio is Lather on tapes\, electronics and s
 trings\, Xylocept on synthesizer and electronics\, and Kyle Quass on trump
 et and percussion. They performed last fall at Backspace Gallery (that per
 formance is available on Lather’s bandcamp) and are excited to come togeth
 er again for a sonic adventure.<br />\nhttps://lather.bandcamp.com/<br />
 \nhttps://xylocept.bandcamp.com/<br />\nhttps://kylequass.bandcamp.com/</p
 >\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
