BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136969@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Bodies\, limestone\, satin\, green sun\, resonances\, and langu
 age.\nA unique improvised performance unfolding in the spaces we move by e
 very day. You’ll encounter dance\, music and poetry—an invitation into new
  relationships with downtown’s familiar places.\nWhat becomes possible whe
 n we come together in creative space?\nWhat can be said that usually goes 
 unsaid?\nWhat does it mean to dwell in deeper dialogue—with one another\, 
 and with what is already here?\nThis meandering performance walk is about 
 being with each other—an unfolding of presence where something uncommon ma
 y emerge. How do we gather to see differently\, to be differently together
  in these uncommon times?\nCome be inspired. Be surprised. Take some time.
  Meet someone new.\nThe performance begins under the large tree on the Nor
 thwest Lawn of the Courthouse\, across from Social Cantina.\nWe’ll begin t
 here and slowly travel two blocks\, with performance surprises in local bu
 sinesses\, ending at the Monroe County History Center.\nTasty cool treats 
 will be provided during and after.\nOptional interactive prompts offered. 
 Linger\, play\, and explore after the performance.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250629T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250629T153000
LOCATION:Monroe County Courthouse\, Northwest Lawn\, 100 W Kirkwood Ave\, B
 loomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:“Ordinary Pilgrimage” improvised performance with dance\, music\, a
 nd poetry
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ordinary-pilgrimage-improvised-performance-with-
 dance-music-and-poetry-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='ai1e
 c-event-description'>\n<p>Bodies\, limestone\, satin\, green sun\, resonan
 ces\, and language.</p>\n<p>A unique improvised performance unfolding in t
 he spaces we move by every day. You’ll encounter dance\, music and poetry—
 an invitation into new relationships with downtown’s familiar places.</p>
 \n<p>What becomes possible when we come together in creative space?<br />
 \nWhat can be said that usually goes unsaid?<br />\nWhat does it mean to d
 well in deeper dialogue—with one another\, and with what is already here?<
 /p>\n<p>This meandering performance walk is about being with each other—an
  unfolding of presence where something uncommon may emerge. How do we gath
 er to see differently\, to <em>be</em> differently together in these uncom
 mon times?</p>\n<p>Come be inspired. Be surprised. Take some time. Meet so
 meone new.</p>\n<p>The performance begins under the large tree on the Nort
 hwest Lawn of the Courthouse\, across from Social Cantina.<br />\nWe’ll be
 gin there and slowly travel two blocks\, with performance surprises in loc
 al businesses\, ending at the Monroe County History Center.</p>\n<p>Tasty 
 cool treats will be provided during and after.<br />\nOptional interactive
  prompts offered. Linger\, play\, and explore after the performance.</p>\n
 </div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
