BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-137011@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Our July Harvest Potluck theme is Ross Gay — we’re hosting a po
 etic evening\, inviting the community to engage with poet Ross Gay and exp
 lore the art of poetry. Join us for a guided poetry writing activity inspi
 red by the orchard\, an optional open sharing of poems or reflections\, an
 d a chance to hear from Ross Gay himself (details of his participation to 
 be confirmed). Whether you’re a seasoned poet or just curious\, everyone i
 s welcome!\nJULY HARVEST POTLUCK SCHEDULE\n• 5pm: Work & Learn Day begins 
 (5-6:30pm)\n• 6:30: Break for Harvest Potluck/Picnic (featuring Pizza X do
 nated pizzas!)\n• 7:00: Poetry activities begin (guided writing\, Ross Gay
 ’s engagement\, and optional open sharing)\n• 8:00: Event ends
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250709T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250709T200000
LOCATION:Bloomington Community Orchard\, 2120 South Highland Ave.\, Bloomin
 gton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:July Orchard Harvest Potluck (with live poetry from special guest R
 oss Gay)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/july-orchard-harvest-potluck-with-live-poetry-fr
 om-special-guest-ross-gay/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Our July Harv
 est Potluck theme is Ross Gay — we’re hosting a poetic evening\, inviting 
 the community to engage with poet Ross Gay and explore the art of poetry. 
 Join us for a guided poetry writing activity inspired by the orchard\, an 
 optional open sharing of poems or reflections\, and a chance to hear from 
 Ross Gay himself (details of his participation to be confirmed). Whether y
 ou’re a seasoned poet or just curious\, everyone is welcome!<br />\nJULY H
 ARVEST POTLUCK SCHEDULE<br />\n• 5pm: Work & Learn Day begins (5-6:30pm)<b
 r />\n• 6:30: Break for Harvest Potluck/Picnic (featuring Pizza X donated 
 pizzas!)<br />\n• 7:00: Poetry activities begin (guided writing\, Ross Gay
 ’s engagement\, and optional open sharing)<br />\n• 8:00: Event ends</p>\n
 </BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
