BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-137624@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 5:30pm)\nMultilingual singer-songwriter and cultural s
 toryteller Amelia Ray brings The Soulevillance Tour – a five-month journey
  through the U.S.\, Canada and Europe to spread compassion in song – to to
 wn. The San Francisco Bay Area native’s latest single\, “Pretending to Rea
 d\,” a poignant track in the style of Bossa nova\, blends observation and 
 introspection into a melody that sneaks up on you like a mysterious strang
 er on a train. Come join Ray’s network of soulful secret agents.\nhttps://
 ameliaray.net/\nIn the ’80s\, while a student at Indiana University\, CJ a
 nd her all-woman punk band climbed through the windows of a law school cla
 ssroom\, stood on desks\, and sang a tune she wrote called “I Think I’m Go
 nna Die (and I Know I’m Gonna Flunk).” Today\, CJ is still writing songs\,
  but now they might chronicle a drunken dinner party\, the tear-down of gr
 andpa’s house\, or the joy and sadness of our headfirst dive through life.
 \nhttps://www.instagram.com/cjrbloomington/
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250711T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250711T200000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Amelia Ray – The Soulveillance Tour with CJ Reichard
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/amelia-ray-the-soulveillance-tour-with-cj-reicha
 rd/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 5:30pm)</strong><br />\nMultilingual singer-songwriter and cultural st
 oryteller Amelia Ray brings The Soulevillance Tour – a five-month journey 
 through the U.S.\, Canada and Europe to spread compassion in song – to tow
 n. The San Francisco Bay Area native’s latest single\, “Pretending to Read
 \,” a poignant track in the style of Bossa nova\, blends observation and i
 ntrospection into a melody that sneaks up on you like a mysterious strange
 r on a train. Come join Ray’s network of soulful secret agents.<br />\nhtt
 ps://ameliaray.net/<br />\nIn the ’80s\, while a student at Indiana Univer
 sity\, CJ and her all-woman punk band climbed through the windows of a law
  school classroom\, stood on desks\, and sang a tune she wrote called “I T
 hink I’m Gonna Die (and I Know I’m Gonna Flunk).” Today\, CJ is still writ
 ing songs\, but now they might chronicle a drunken dinner party\, the tear
 -down of grandpa’s house\, or the joy and sadness of our headfirst dive th
 rough life.<br />\nhttps://www.instagram.com/cjrbloomington/ </p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
END:VEVENT
