CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Registration is requested\nMake your own handbound journal from
  what most people would consider junk! Perfect for use as a diary or art j
 ournal\, these books will use a variety of papers and media to create a on
 e-of-a-kind piece. Learn to sew  easy 3-hole pamphlet stitch signatures to
  insert it into a hard cover\, and explore various ways of decorating and 
 personalizing your creation.\nNo experience is required! If you are alread
 y into junk journaling feel free to bring your journals to inspire others.
 \nAll tools and materials will be supplied. For adults and teens 13 and ol
 der.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250712T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250712T150000
LOCATION:Meeting Room B\, Brown County Public Library\, 205 Locust Lane\, N
 ashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Junk Journal July
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/junk-journal-july/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Regis
 tration is requested</strong><br />\nMake your own handbound journal from 
 what most people would consider junk! Perfect for use as a diary or art jo
 urnal\, these books will use a variety of papers and media to create a one
 -of-a-kind piece. Learn to sew  easy 3-hole pamphlet stitch signatures to 
 insert it into a hard cover\, and explore various ways of decorating and p
 ersonalizing your creation.</p>\n<p>No experience is required! If you are 
 already into junk journaling feel free to bring your journals to inspire o
 thers.</p>\n<p>All tools and materials will be supplied. For adults and te
 ens 13 and older.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-137395@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we celebrate the 10th anniversary of the Mitchell Op
 era House’s renovation and re-opening! It’s going to be a fun-filled day\,
  and we’d love for YOU to be a part of it.\nDave Cottrell is a magician\, 
 comedian & banjo player from Southville\, Kentucky.  He has been entertain
 ing for most of his life.\nDavid did his first magic show for his 6th grad
 e class at Simpsonville Elementary (KY) in 1971.  Since then he has perfor
 med over much of the United States. Each stage filled show includes live a
 nimals\, lots of audience participation and blazing 5 string bluegrass ban
 jo.\n_________\n ESB takes classic to current smash hits and explodes them
  with life! They’re not just tight harmonies and killer grooves–it’s a vis
 ual feast with dazzling costume changes\, electrifying energy\, and audien
 ce participation so infectious\, you won’t be able to resist joining the f
 un! You’ll laugh out loud and spontaneously burst into dance to ESB’s Mega
  Hit Pop\, Rock ‘n Roll\, Blues\, Memphis/Detroit Soul\, Rock ‘n Country\,
  and even DooWop!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250712T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250712T210000
LOCATION:Mitchell Opera House\, 217 N 7th St\, Mitchell\, IN\,
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mitchell Opera House 10th Anniversary\, with Dave’s Magic Show (2pm
 -3pm) and Endless Summer Band (7pm-9pm)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mitchell-opera-house-10th-anniversary/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us as we
  celebrate the 10th anniversary of the Mitchell Opera House’s renovation a
 nd re-opening! It’s going to be a fun-filled day\, and we’d love for YOU t
 o be a part of it.</p>\n<p>Dave Cottrell is a magician\, comedian & banjo 
 player from Southville\, Kentucky.  He has been entertaining for most of h
 is life.</p>\n<p>David did his first magic show for his 6th grade class at
  Simpsonville Elementary (KY) in 1971.  Since then he has performed over m
 uch of the United States. Each stage filled show includes live animals\, l
 ots of audience participation and blazing 5 string bluegrass banjo.<br />
 \n_________</p>\n<p> ESB takes classic to current smash hits and explodes 
 them with life! They’re not just tight harmonies and killer grooves–it’s a
  visual feast with dazzling costume changes\, electrifying energy\, and au
 dience participation so infectious\, you won’t be able to resist joining t
 he fun! You’ll laugh out loud and spontaneously burst into dance to ESB’s 
 Mega Hit Pop\, Rock ‘n Roll\, Blues\, Memphis/Detroit Soul\, Rock ‘n Count
 ry\, and even DooWop!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
