BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-137776@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:5:30pm – Potluck\n6pm – Music\nThe Tillers – (Cincinnati Oh) Th
 e Tillers have been thumping their own distinctive sound of string band st
 yle folk music for a decade\, riding it all over the country and across th
 e sea. Four studio albums and one live record have won them praise as mode
 rn folk storytellers of the national soundscape.\nDeep Country Dream – Ano
 ther iteration of Matt Lundquist’s musical landscape this string trio will
  bring the front porch inside. Backed up by Michael Lindeau and Devin Brow
 n these timeless songs of southern Indiana effortlessly fill the air like 
 dust in a sunbeam.\nLiv La Fluv – Liv LaFluv is a midwestern cutiepie musi
 c maker. She reaches into an imperfect world and spins beautiful yarns ful
 l of adventure\, heartbreak\, humor\, and hopeful promise. Her voice draws
  you in with its effortless dynamic range. She has a fire in her belly and
  a twinkle in her eye! Watch out!\nLuke Foster- I am a young poet and film
 maker from northern indiana. I started writing consistently in early 2024\
 , and have compiled a book of poems I plan to release by the end of the su
 mmer. Ive been hosting a monthly poetry circle out of my home for about a 
 year.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250713T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250713T213000
LOCATION:Switchyard House Venue\, 1417 South Monon Drive\, Blomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Tillers // Deep Country Dream // Liv LaFluv // Luke Foster
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-tillers-deep-country-dream-liv-lafluv-luke-f
 oster/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>5:30p
 m – Potluck<br />\n6pm – Music</strong><br />\nThe Tillers – (Cincinnati O
 h) The Tillers have been thumping their own distinctive sound of string ba
 nd style folk music for a decade\, riding it all over the country and acro
 ss the sea. Four studio albums and one live record have won them praise as
  modern folk storytellers of the national soundscape.</p>\n<p>Deep Country
  Dream – Another iteration of Matt Lundquist’s musical landscape this stri
 ng trio will bring the front porch inside. Backed up by Michael Lindeau an
 d Devin Brown these timeless songs of southern Indiana effortlessly fill t
 he air like dust in a sunbeam.</p>\n<p>Liv La Fluv – Liv LaFluv is a midwe
 stern cutiepie music maker. She reaches into an imperfect world and spins 
 beautiful yarns full of adventure\, heartbreak\, humor\, and hopeful promi
 se. Her voice draws you in with its effortless dynamic range. She has a fi
 re in her belly and a twinkle in her eye! Watch out!</p>\n<p>Luke Foster- 
 I am a young poet and filmmaker from northern indiana. I started writing c
 onsistently in early 2024\, and have compiled a book of poems I plan to re
 lease by the end of the summer. Ive been hosting a monthly poetry circle o
 ut of my home for about a year.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-137768@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Post-film video Q&A with artists Michael Townsend and Leah Smit
 h!\nSynopsis: In 2003\, eight young Rhode Islanders created a secret apart
 ment in a hidden space inside the Providence Place Mall and lived in it fo
 r four years\, filming everything along the way. They snuck in furniture\,
  tapped into the mall’s electricity\, and even secretly constructed a bric
 k wall with a locking door\, smuggling in over 2 tons of cinderblock. Far 
 more than just a wild prank\, the secret apartment became a deeply meaning
 ful place for all its inhabitants – a personal expression of defiance agai
 nst local gentrification\, a boundary-pushing work of public/private art\,
  and finally\, a 750 square foot space that sticks it to the man!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250713T180000
LOCATION:FAR Center for Contemporary Arts\, 202 South Rogers St.\, Blooming
 ton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema Screening: Secret Mall Apartment
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cicada-cinema-presents-secret-mall-apartment/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Post-film vid
 eo Q&A with artists Michael Townsend and Leah Smith!<br />\nSynopsis: In 2
 003\, eight young Rhode Islanders created a secret apartment in a hidden s
 pace inside the Providence Place Mall and lived in it for four years\, fil
 ming everything along the way. They snuck in furniture\, tapped into the m
 all’s electricity\, and even secretly constructed a brick wall with a lock
 ing door\, smuggling in over 2 tons of cinderblock. Far more than just a w
 ild prank\, the secret apartment became a deeply meaningful place for all 
 its inhabitants – a personal expression of defiance against local gentrifi
 cation\, a boundary-pushing work of public/private art\, and finally\, a 7
 50 square foot space that sticks it to the man!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136791@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250713T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:We Are Guardians (2025)\, Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwo
