BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-138195@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Nicholas is a Bloomington based artist and singer-songwriter\, 
 who creates mixed-media paintings that explore themes of modern overconsum
 ption and its impact on society and the environment. His work utilizes bol
 d colors\, rich textures\, and energetic mark-making to express the tensio
 n between order and chaos.\nNicholas’s songwriting draws inspiration from 
 his own life\, tackling relatable themes like self-doubt\, love and loss\,
  the political climate\, and even the environment. His music is a heartfel
 t exploration of the human experience.\nNicholas is exhibiting throughout 
 the month of July at I Fell.\nHe will share a bit about his creative proce
 ss\, whether creating a piece of art or a song\, and will perform a few of
  his newest songs\, too.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250724T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250724T203000
LOCATION:I Fell Gallery\, 415 West 4th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Artist Talk – Nicholas Graham Hall
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/artist-talk-nicholas-graham-hall/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Nicholas is a
  Bloomington based artist and singer-songwriter\, who creates mixed-media 
 paintings that explore themes of modern overconsumption and its impact on 
 society and the environment. His work utilizes bold colors\, rich textures
 \, and energetic mark-making to express the tension between order and chao
 s.<br />\nNicholas’s songwriting draws inspiration from his own life\, tac
 kling relatable themes like self-doubt\, love and loss\, the political cli
 mate\, and even the environment. His music is a heartfelt exploration of t
 he human experience.<br />\nNicholas is exhibiting throughout the month of
  July at I Fell.<br />\nHe will share a bit about his creative process\, w
 hether creating a piece of art or a song\, and will perform a few of his n
 ewest songs\, too.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
