CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:It’s Michael’s seventeenth birthday. His friends have decided t
 o surprise him with the ultimate gift: breaking into his house and playing
  with a Ouija board! But this harmless fun quickly transforms into a super
 natural terror\, as newly-summoned demon Virgil possesses and murders Mich
 ael’s friends! Defying reality at every turn\, DON’T PANIC is an awe-inspi
 ring 1980s horror classic\, now newly restored from the original 35mm came
 ra negative.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250724T190000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Don’t Panic (a Cicada Cinema film)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/dont-panic-a-cicada-cinema-film/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>It’s Michael’
 s seventeenth birthday. His friends have decided to surprise him with the 
 ultimate gift: breaking into his house and playing with a Ouija board! But
  this harmless fun quickly transforms into a supernatural terror\, as newl
 y-summoned demon Virgil possesses and murders Michael’s friends! Defying r
 eality at every turn\, DON’T PANIC is an awe-inspiring 1980s horror classi
 c\, now newly restored from the original 35mm camera negative.</p>\n</BODY
 ></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-136790@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Includes 12 mins of additional footage only available in the Th
 eatrical Version – after the main film.\nOcean with David Attenborough tak
 es viewers on a breathtaking journey showing there is nowhere more vital f
 or our survival\, more full of life\, wonder\, or surprise\, than the ocea
 n. In the film the celebrated broadcaster and filmmaker reveals how his li
 fetime has coincided with the great age of ocean discovery. Through specta
 cular sequences featuring coral reefs\, kelp forests and the open ocean\, 
 Attenborough shares why a healthy ocean keeps the entire planet stable and
  flourishing.\nStunning\, immersive cinematography showcases the wonder of
  life under the seas and exposes the realities and challenges facing our o
 cean as never-before-seen\, from destructive fishing techniques to mass co
 ral reef bleaching. Yet the story is one of optimism\, with Attenborough p
 ointing to inspirational stories from around the world to deliver his grea
 test message: the ocean can recover to a glory beyond anything anyone aliv
 e has ever seen.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250724T190000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Film: Ocean (2025) with David Attenborough
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-buskirk-chumley-theater-presents-ocean-2025-
 with-david-attenborough-buskirk-chumley-theatre-114-east-kirkwood-blooming
 ton/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Includes 12 m
 ins of additional footage only available in the Theatrical Version – after
  the main film.</p>\n<p>Ocean with David Attenborough takes viewers on a b
 reathtaking journey showing there is nowhere more vital for our survival\,
  more full of life\, wonder\, or surprise\, than the ocean. In the film th
 e celebrated broadcaster and filmmaker reveals how his lifetime has coinci
 ded with the great age of ocean discovery. Through spectacular sequences f
 eaturing coral reefs\, kelp forests and the open ocean\, Attenborough shar
 es why a healthy ocean keeps the entire planet stable and flourishing.</p>
 \n<p>Stunning\, immersive cinematography showcases the wonder of life unde
 r the seas and exposes the realities and challenges facing our ocean as ne
 ver-before-seen\, from destructive fishing techniques to mass coral reef b
 leaching. Yet the story is one of optimism\, with Attenborough pointing to
  inspirational stories from around the world to deliver his greatest messa
 ge: the ocean can recover to a glory beyond anything anyone alive has ever
  seen.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
