BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-138144@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Sounds From the Black Hole\; 317-313-1501\; soundsfromtheblackhole@
 gmail.com\; https://www.facebook.com/soundsfromtheblackhole
DESCRIPTION:Sounds From the Black Hole presents an evening of experimental 
 sound: percussive possibilities with Rob Funkhouser\, experimental metal f
 rom Verity Pariah\, and prog music from another realm with Vaguerriffic.\n
 ALL-AGES\n________________________\nRob Funkhouser: composer\, performer a
 nd instrument builder in Indianapolis\, IN. Rob is always doing something 
 interesting\, constantly designing new tools and exploring their sonic cap
 abilities. Also an educator and collaborator\, Rob’s work explores space\,
  memory\, pattern\, and the interstitial spaces between established genres
 . Rob’s music has been released by Auris Apothecary\, Medium Sound\, El Tu
 le\, and Orphanology.\nhttps://www.robfunkhouser.com/\nhttps://robfunkhous
 er.bandcamp.com/\n________________________\nVaguerriffic: solo project of 
 Adeptive Radiation bandleader John Knight\, joined on keyboard tonight by 
 Matt Rouge of Frugal Gormets. Matt and John have been playing together for
  over 15 years\, collaging bits and pieces of ‘popular’ song into structur
 es of another music theory entirely. The resulting songs may sound alien a
 nd chaotic but come from a mash which has been slowly fermenting\, blendin
 g flavors and mixing ideas.\nhttps://adeptiveradiation.bandcamp.com/\n____
 ____________________\nVerity Pariah: a new project from Louisville\, KY ar
 tist Eric Clark. He’s described it as experimental metal and sent along a 
 video of him welding some copper lights. Hopefully these two things are in
 corporated?! Eric has been performing as ClarkSmithy and has attended many
  Black Hole shows. This will be his debut at the series\, and we are excit
 ed to give him the stage.\nhttps://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=1000634
 57300053#\nhttps://www.instagram.com/_clarksmithy_/
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250726T200000
LOCATION:Orbit Room - 107 N. College Ave suite 001\, underground
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds From the Black Hole ft. Rob Funkhouser // Vaguerriffic // Ve
 rity Pariah
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-ft-rob-funkhouser-vag
 uerriffic-verity-pariah/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Sounds From t
 he Black Hole presents an evening of experimental sound: percussive possib
 ilities with Rob Funkhouser\, experimental metal from Verity Pariah\, and 
 prog music from another realm with Vaguerriffic.<br />\nALL-AGES<br />\n__
 ______________________<br />\nRob Funkhouser: composer\, performer and ins
 trument builder in Indianapolis\, IN. Rob is always doing something intere
 sting\, constantly designing new tools and exploring their sonic capabilit
 ies. Also an educator and collaborator\, Rob’s work explores space\, memor
 y\, pattern\, and the interstitial spaces between established genres. Rob’
 s music has been released by Auris Apothecary\, Medium Sound\, El Tule\, a
 nd Orphanology.<br />\nhttps://www.robfunkhouser.com/<br />\nhttps://robfu
 nkhouser.bandcamp.com/<br />\n________________________<br />\nVaguerriffic
 : solo project of Adeptive Radiation bandleader John Knight\, joined on ke
 yboard tonight by Matt Rouge of Frugal Gormets. Matt and John have been pl
 aying together for over 15 years\, collaging bits and pieces of ‘popular’ 
 song into structures of another music theory entirely. The resulting songs
  may sound alien and chaotic but come from a mash which has been slowly fe
 rmenting\, blending flavors and mixing ideas.<br />\nhttps://adeptiveradia
 tion.bandcamp.com/<br />\n________________________<br />\nVerity Pariah: a
  new project from Louisville\, KY artist Eric Clark. He’s described it as 
 experimental metal and sent along a video of him welding some copper light
 s. Hopefully these two things are incorporated?! Eric has been performing 
 as ClarkSmithy and has attended many Black Hole shows. This will be his de
 but at the series\, and we are excited to give him the stage.<br />\nhttps
 ://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100063457300053#<br />\nhttps://www.ins
 tagram.com/_clarksmithy_/</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
