BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-138853@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is designed for dogs who have some basic training
  but struggle with leash manners and impulse control in real-world environ
 ments. In this workshop\, you’ll:\n • Learn how dogs think\, communicate\,
  and respond to stimuli\n • Explore the emotional roots of excited behavio
 r and barrier frustration\n • Receive hands-on guidance using tools such a
 s clickers\, treats\, gentle leaders\, calming touch\, leashes\, and harne
 sses\n • Discover how to manage\, modify\, and train using positive reinfo
 rcement techniques\n • Practice leash handling strategies to reduce pullin
 g and frustration on both ends of the leash\nPlease note: This workshop is
  not suitable for dogs with a history of aggression or biting.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250823T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250823T100000
LOCATION:MCHA Animal Care Campus\, 791 S Fieldstone Blvd\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Monroe County Humane Association Leash Skills & Reactivity Workshop
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mcha-leash-skills-reactivity-workshop/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p align='center
 '>This workshop is designed for dogs who have some basic training but stru
 ggle with leash manners and impulse control in real-world environments. In
  this workshop\, you’ll:</p>\n<p align='center'> • Learn how dogs think\, 
 communicate\, and respond to stimuli</p>\n<p align='center'> • Explore the
  emotional roots of excited behavior and barrier frustration</p>\n<p align
 ='center'> • Receive hands-on guidance using tools such as clickers\, trea
 ts\, gentle leaders\, calming touch\, leashes\, and harnesses</p>\n<p alig
 n='center'> • Discover how to manage\, modify\, and train using positive r
 einforcement techniques</p>\n<p align='center'> • Practice leash handling 
 strategies to reduce pulling and frustration on both ends of the leash</p>
 \n<p align='center'>Please note: This workshop is not suitable for dogs wi
 th a history of aggression or biting.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
