BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139471@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:First Thursdays showcase the diversity of arts and humanities a
 t IU Bloomington and offer a welcoming environment for students\, faculty\
 , staff\, and community members to explore new creative outlets.\nSeptembe
 r’s event will be a kick-off to the school year that is open to all with d
 ozens of arts and humanities partners hosting special activities\, demonst
 rations\, giveaways\, and more. Around the plaza\, there will be t-shirt u
 pcycling\, collaborative textile making\, soap-carving\, and computer gami
 ng among many other activities. On the stage\, we’ll have an interactive b
 irthday celebration in honor of salsa legend Celia Cruz alongside performa
 nces by the African American Choral Ensemble\, Bloomington Delta Music Clu
 b\, and IU Jacobs Opera. For more details\, visit  go.iu.edu/first-thursda
 ys.\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250904T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250904T190000
LOCATION:IU Fine Arts Plaza\, 1201 E 7th St\, Bloomington\,
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:IU First Thursdays
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/september-4-first-thursdays/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>First Thursda
 ys showcase the diversity of arts and humanities at IU Bloomington and off
 er a welcoming environment for students\, faculty\, staff\, and community 
 members to explore new creative outlets.</p>\n<p>September’s event will be
  a kick-off to the school year that is open to all with dozens of arts and
  humanities partners hosting special activities\, demonstrations\, giveawa
 ys\, and more. Around the plaza\, there will be t-shirt upcycling\, collab
 orative textile making\, soap-carving\, and computer gaming among many oth
 er activities. <strong>On the stage\, we’ll have an interactive birthday c
 elebration in honor of salsa legend Celia Cruz alongside performances by t
 he African American Choral Ensemble\, Bloomington Delta Music Club\, and I
 U Jacobs Opera.</strong> For more details\, visit <a href='https://artsand
 humanities.indiana.edu/council-programs/first-thursdays/index.html' target
 ='_blank' rel='noopener' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?
 q=https://artsandhumanities.indiana.edu/council-programs/first-thursdays/i
 ndex.html&source=gmail&ust=1756316938930000&usg=AOvVaw0KbEZVtjsZ6t1hkOlLev
 1X'> go.iu.edu/first-thursdays</a>.</p>\n<p> </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
