BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139800@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Weather or Not is a solo exhibition by local artist Bert Gilber
 t\, featuring evocative metal and mixed media sculptures that grapple with
  the tensions between permanence and impermanence\, form and formlessness.
  With a background rooted in sculpture and painting\, and a practice reign
 ited later in life\, Gilbert draws on industrial materials\, personal hist
 ory\, and found objects to create works that are both structurally bold an
 d conceptually rich.\nThrough cast iron\, salvaged steel\, and repurposed 
 everyday detritus\, Gilbert explores themes of memory\, contradiction\, an
 d cultural decay—offering viewers a space to question\, reflect\, and conn
 ect.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250905T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250905T210000
LOCATION:Gather\, 116 N Walnut Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Opening Reception for Weather or Not by Bert Gilbert
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/opening-reception-for-weather-or-not-by-bert-gil
 bert/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div><span style
 ='color: #000000'>Weather or Not is a solo exhibition by local artist Bert
  Gilbert\, featuring evocative metal and mixed media sculptures that grapp
 le with the tensions between permanence and impermanence\, form and formle
 ssness. With a background rooted in sculpture and painting\, and a practic
 e reignited later in life\, Gilbert draws on industrial materials\, person
 al history\, and found objects to create works that are both structurally 
 bold and conceptually rich.<br />\nThrough cast iron\, salvaged steel\, an
 d repurposed everyday detritus\, Gilbert explores themes of memory\, contr
 adiction\, and cultural decay—offering viewers a space to question\, refle
 ct\, and connect.</p>\n<p></span></div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
