BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139850@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 8:30pm\nIthaca\, NY via Bloomington based alt.country 
 rockers\, Freight\, are touring the midwest with their newly released albu
 m\, Old Bones\, in tow. Recorded at Grass Alley in Chicago\, IL\, Sunwood 
 Studios in Trumansburg\, NY\, and Electric Wilburland in Newfield\, NY\, t
 he album was produced by Jaime Gartelos and comprises 10 original\, roots-
 based tracks—ranging from contemplative\, downbeat meditations to full-til
 t rockabilly and Crazy Horse-style rockers.\nLed by the songwriting of Ind
 iana native\, JP Payton\, Old Bones blends East Nashville polish\, garage 
 rock grit\, and a devil-may-care attitude. Freight has long explored the u
 niversal themes of love\, longing\, and loss\, and on Old Bones\, they dou
 ble down\, delivering an album that is both timeless and refreshingly orig
 inal.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250906T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250906T230000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Freight (Old Bones Tour) with special guests\, LowLanders
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/freight-old-bones-tour-with-special-guests-lowla
 nders/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 8:30pm</strong><br />\nIthaca\, NY via Bloomington based alt.country r
 ockers\, Freight\, are touring the midwest with their newly released album
 \, Old Bones\, in tow. Recorded at Grass Alley in Chicago\, IL\, Sunwood S
 tudios in Trumansburg\, NY\, and Electric Wilburland in Newfield\, NY\, th
 e album was produced by Jaime Gartelos and comprises 10 original\, roots-b
 ased tracks—ranging from contemplative\, downbeat meditations to full-tilt
  rockabilly and Crazy Horse-style rockers.<br />\nLed by the songwriting o
 f Indiana native\, JP Payton\, Old Bones blends East Nashville polish\, ga
 rage rock grit\, and a devil-may-care attitude. Freight has long explored 
 the universal themes of love\, longing\, and loss\, and on Old Bones\, the
 y double down\, delivering an album that is both timeless and refreshingly
  original.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
