BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139851@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Ithaca\, NY via Bloomington based alt.country rockers\, Freight
 \, are touring the midwest with their newly released album\, Old Bones\, i
 n tow. Recorded at Grass Alley in Chicago\, IL\, Sunwood Studios in Truman
 sburg\, NY\, and Electric Wilburland in Newfield\, NY\, the album was prod
 uced by Jaime Gartelos and comprises 10 original\, roots-based tracks—rang
 ing from contemplative\, downbeat meditations to full-tilt rockabilly and 
 Crazy Horse-style rockers.\nLed by the songwriting of Indiana native\, JP 
 Payton\, Old Bones blends East Nashville polish\, garage rock grit\, and a
  devil-may-care attitude. Freight has long explored the universal themes o
 f love\, longing\, and loss\, and on Old Bones\, they double down\, delive
 ring an album that is both timeless and refreshingly original.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250907T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250907T190000
LOCATION:The Cabin Restaurant and Lounge\, 4015 South State Hwy 446\, Bloom
 ington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Freight (the Old Bones Tour) with special guests Rikki Jean\, LeRoy
  McQueen and Kat Kinney
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/freight-the-old-bones-tour-with-special-guests-r
 ikki-jean-leroy-mcqueen-and-kat-kinney/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Ithaca\, NY v
 ia Bloomington based alt.country rockers\, Freight\, are touring the midwe
 st with their newly released album\, Old Bones\, in tow. Recorded at Grass
  Alley in Chicago\, IL\, Sunwood Studios in Trumansburg\, NY\, and Electri
 c Wilburland in Newfield\, NY\, the album was produced by Jaime Gartelos a
 nd comprises 10 original\, roots-based tracks—ranging from contemplative\,
  downbeat meditations to full-tilt rockabilly and Crazy Horse-style rocker
 s.<br />\nLed by the songwriting of Indiana native\, JP Payton\, Old Bones
  blends East Nashville polish\, garage rock grit\, and a devil-may-care at
 titude. Freight has long explored the universal themes of love\, longing\,
  and loss\, and on Old Bones\, they double down\, delivering an album that
  is both timeless and refreshingly original.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
