BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139720@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Tonight the Bloomington Common Council\, the Planning and Trans
 portation Department\, and the Housing and Neighborhood Development Depart
 ment are collaborating to facilitate a\ncommunity conversation related to 
 housing and neighborhood typologies in Bloomington.\nThis conversation is 
 open to all community members\, including current residents and future res
 idents\, who want to live in Bloomington\, but have been unable to find at
 tainable housing\nwithin city limits. The primary purpose of this session 
 is information gathering. Please come prepared to share your experiences w
 ith housing\, bearing in mind that there are no\nright or wrong answers du
 ring this type of dialogue and all experiences are valid.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250910T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250910T200000
LOCATION:City Hall Council Chambers (Room 115)\, 401 North Morton Street\, 
 Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Common Council Housing Discussion: Bloomington Housing Experiences
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/common-council-housing-discussion/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Tonight the B
 loomington Common Council\, the Planning and Transportation Department\, a
 nd the Housing and Neighborhood Development Department are collaborating t
 o facilitate a<br />\ncommunity conversation related to housing and neighb
 orhood typologies in Bloomington.<br />\n<strong>This conversation is open
  to all community members\, including current residents and future residen
 ts\, who want to live in Bloomington\, but have been unable to find attain
 able housing<br />\nwithin city limits. The primary purpose of this sessio
 n is information gathering. Please come prepared to share your experiences
  with housing\, bearing in mind that there are no<br />\nright or wrong an
 swers during this type of dialogue and all experiences are valid.</strong>
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
