BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140100@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Part of the Brown County Art Colony Weekend.\nInfo at: browncou
 ntyartguild.org\nMarie Goth and V.J. Cariani\, along with Genevieve Goth G
 raf and Carl Graf\, were immeasurably connected as they journeyed through 
 life. All four encouraged one another in their painting pursuits\, particu
 larly en plein air. Each couple was aligned in their commitment to the gro
 wing arts movement in Brown County\, and their individual successes were u
 ndoubtedly attributed to the flourishing art colony as a whole.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250912T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250912T190000
LOCATION:Brown County Art Guild\, 48 South Van Buren St.\, Nashville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A Founders Exhibition – Painting Partners – Exhibition Opening
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/a-founders-exhibition-painting-partners-exhibiti
 on-opening/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Part of the B
 rown County Art Colony Weekend.<br />\nInfo at: browncountyartguild.org<br
  />\nMarie Goth and V.J. Cariani\, along with Genevieve Goth Graf and Carl
  Graf\, were immeasurably connected as they journeyed through life. All fo
 ur encouraged one another in their painting pursuits\, particularly en ple
 in air. Each couple was aligned in their commitment to the growing arts mo
 vement in Brown County\, and their individual successes were undoubtedly a
 ttributed to the flourishing art colony as a whole.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
