BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139195@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:For the last year\, artifacts from The Jim Irsay Collection wer
 e on display at Indiana University\nBloomington as a part of Amped at IU\,
  an exhibition that focused on the history of the modern guitar. This\ncol
 laborative exhibition with IU Collections celebrated music and shared piec
 es from Irsay’s world-renowned guitar\ncollection and instruments from aro
 und the world found at IU.\nThe exhibition will close its successful\, yea
 r-long run with a Sept. 13 event featuring:\nOne-day-only exhibition of ra
 re guitars owned and played by Jerry Garcia\, Bob Dylan\, David Gilmour\,
 \nEric Clapton\, Prince\, Kurt Cobain\, John Lennon\, George Harrison\, Pa
 ul McCartney\, Jimi Hendrix\,\nNancy Wilson\, Lou Reed\, and Eddie Van Hal
 en\,\nLectures by IU faculty about music\, culture and collections\,\nOne 
 last look at the year-long exhibit space\, and performances by students fr
 om the IU Jacobs School of Music.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250913T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250913T170000
LOCATION:University Collections at McCalla\, 525 E. 9th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Closing Event of Amped at IU
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/closing-event-of-amped-at-iu/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>For the last 
 year\, artifacts from The Jim Irsay Collection were on display at Indiana 
 University<br />\nBloomington as a part of Amped at IU\, an exhibition tha
 t focused on the history of the modern guitar. This<br />\ncollaborative e
 xhibition with IU Collections celebrated music and shared pieces from Irsa
 y’s world-renowned guitar<br />\ncollection and instruments from around th
 e world found at IU.</p>\n<p>The exhibition will close its successful\, ye
 ar-long run with a Sept. 13 event featuring:<br />\nOne-day-only exhibitio
 n of rare guitars owned and played by Jerry Garcia\, Bob Dylan\, David Gil
 mour\,<br />\nEric Clapton\, Prince\, Kurt Cobain\, John Lennon\, George H
 arrison\, Paul McCartney\, Jimi Hendrix\,<br />\nNancy Wilson\, Lou Reed\,
  and Eddie Van Halen\,</p>\n<p>Lectures by IU faculty about music\, cultur
 e and collections\,</p>\n<p>One last look at the year-long exhibit space\,
  and performances by students from the IU Jacobs School of Music.</p>\n</B
 ODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
