BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139953@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The talk and demo itself will be about an hour (2-3pm)\, and Ji
 m will take questions and be available for casual discussion for the follo
 wing hour. The artist will talk about his 3-D paintings\, plus his new scu
 lptures created from resin (or concrete) in molds\, and then presented on 
 beautiful stone or wooden bases.\nHere is Jim’s statement about his talk o
 n September 13th:\nPainter or sculptor?\n“It is impossible for me to narro
 w my love of art to just those two roles. I love color and form\, and take
  joy in a well-crafted design. Artfulness is not limited to painting and s
 culpture but is inherent to music\, dance\, literature\, architecture and 
 even the design of a toaster. There is a beauty to the precision of comput
 er code or the curve of a road.  No\, I cannot deprive myself of any oppor
 tunity to take time to appreciate the artfulness that is all around us. I 
 am a painter and a sculptor\, I am neither and both.” ~ James B. Campbell
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250913T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250913T160000
LOCATION:Juniper Art Gallery\, 615 West Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Artist Talk & Demo – James B. Campbell
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/artist-talk-demo-james-b-campbell/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The talk and 
 demo itself will be about an hour (2-3pm)\, and Jim will take questions an
 d be available for casual discussion for the following hour. The artist wi
 ll talk about his 3-D paintings\, plus his new sculptures created from res
 in (or concrete) in molds\, and then presented on beautiful stone or woode
 n bases.</p>\n<p>Here is Jim’s statement about his talk on September 13th:
 </p>\n<p>Painter or sculptor?<br />\n“It is impossible for me to narrow my
  love of art to just those two roles. I love color and form\, and take joy
  in a well-crafted design. Artfulness is not limited to painting and sculp
 ture but is inherent to music\, dance\, literature\, architecture and even
  the design of a toaster. There is a beauty to the precision of computer c
 ode or the curve of a road.  No\, I cannot deprive myself of any opportuni
 ty to take time to appreciate the artfulness that is all around us. I am a
  painter and a sculptor\, I am neither and both.” ~ James B. Campbell</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
