BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140069@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:What a Way to Go! is a visual and aural delight of lavish costu
 mes\, comedic zingers\, and dazzling choreography\, all wrapped in a Nelso
 n Riddle score. Louisa May Foster (Shirley MacLaine) is convinced her love
  life is jinxed as she recounts to her psychiatrist (Robert Cummings) how 
 her four marriages spiraled into tragedy\, leaving her feeling cursed—and 
 extraordinarily rich. Featuring a jaw-dropping wardrobe from the Oscar-win
 ning legend Edith Head and an all-star cast of Paul Newman\, Gene Kelly\, 
 Dean Martin\, Dick Van Dyke\, Robert Mitchum\, and more\, What a Way to Go
 ! is a cinematic experience like no other. [111 min\; comedy\, musical\; E
 nglish]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250913T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Three Cheers for 100 Years film series: What a Way to Go!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/three-cheers-for-100-years-film-series-what-a-wa
 y-to-go/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>What a Way to
  Go! is a visual and aural delight of lavish costumes\, comedic zingers\, 
 and dazzling choreography\, all wrapped in a Nelson Riddle score. Louisa M
 ay Foster (Shirley MacLaine) is convinced her love life is jinxed as she r
 ecounts to her psychiatrist (Robert Cummings) how her four marriages spira
 led into tragedy\, leaving her feeling cursed—and extraordinarily rich. Fe
 aturing a jaw-dropping wardrobe from the Oscar-winning legend Edith Head a
 nd an all-star cast of Paul Newman\, Gene Kelly\, Dean Martin\, Dick Van D
 yke\, Robert Mitchum\, and more\, What a Way to Go! is a cinematic experie
 nce like no other. [111 min\; comedy\, musical\; English] </p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140057@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Hsiao-Feng Lin\, an internationally acclaimed world flute virtu
 oso\, fuses traditional Chinese music with contemporary performance. Guide
 d by visionary foresight and deep dedication\, Lin reshapes how the bamboo
  flute resonates on the world stage. \nThe IU-Taiwan Collaborations in Mus
 ic project\, housed under the Taiwan Studies Initiative and East Asia Stud
 ies Center (EASC)\, fosters cultural and academic exchanges between Indian
 a University and Taiwan. This project\, organized and produced by Hsuan Ch
 ang Kitano\, unites student composers\, musicians\, and scholars to explor
 e Taiwan’s rich cultural and musical traditions. Through workshops\, lectu
 res\, and collaborative performances\, participants create innovative work
 s inspired by Taiwanese cultural insights.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250913T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250913T190000
LOCATION:IU Museum of Archaeology & Anthropology\, 416 N. Indiana Ave.\, Bl
 oomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:IU-Taiwan Music Project: Resonant Island\, featuring Hsiao-Feng Lin
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/iu-taiwan-music-project-resonant-island-featurin
 g-hsiao-feng-lin/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Hsiao-Feng Li
 n\, an internationally acclaimed world flute virtuoso\, fuses traditional 
 Chinese music with contemporary performance. Guided by visionary foresight
  and deep dedication\, Lin reshapes how the bamboo flute resonates on the 
 world stage. </p>\n<p>The IU-Taiwan Collaborations in Music project\, hous
 ed under the Taiwan Studies Initiative and East Asia Studies Center (EASC)
 \, fosters cultural and academic exchanges between Indiana University and 
 Taiwan. This project\, organized and produced by Hsuan Chang Kitano\, unit
 es student composers\, musicians\, and scholars to explore Taiwan’s rich c
 ultural and musical traditions. Through workshops\, lectures\, and collabo
 rative performances\, participants create innovative works inspired by Tai
 wanese cultural insights.  </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
