BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140239@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Inheritance explores the underlying causes of the opioid epidem
 ic in America through the life of one boy and five generations of his exte
 nded family over 11 years.\nAn unflinching documentary a decade in the mak
 ing\, Inheritance follows Curtis as he grows up in rural Appalachia in a f
 amily and community surrounded by substance use disorder and poverty.\nA Q
 &A will follow the screening with filmmaker Amy Toensing\; Jon Agley\, Cri
 s Henderson\, and Angela Campbell from IU’s School of Public Health\; and 
 Kathy Hewett of the Monroe County Health Department.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250916T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Inheritance w/Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/inheritance-w-qa-additional-films-and-guests/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Inher
 itance explores the underlying causes of the opioid epidemic in America th
 rough the life of one boy and five generations of his extended family over
  11 years.</strong><br />\nAn unflinching documentary a decade in the maki
 ng\, Inheritance follows Curtis as he grows up in rural Appalachia in a fa
 mily and community surrounded by substance use disorder and poverty.<br />
 \n<strong>A Q&A will follow the screening with filmmaker Amy Toensing\; Jo
 n Agley\, Cris Henderson\, and Angela Campbell from IU’s School of Public 
 Health\; and Kathy Hewett of the Monroe County Health Department.</strong>
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
