BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140340@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:What happens when a 30-something gay actor\, stuck in the audit
 ion grind\, gets one more shot at his biggest dream—the Jimmy Awards?\nIn 
 this one-person tour de force\, the audience takes a riotous and heartfelt
  journey through Broadway dreams\, hook-up mishaps\, and the existential c
 rises that lie in between. With biting wit\, showbiz satire\, and a whole 
 lot of belting\, Ryan Wants a Jimmy Award is a love letter to theatre\, to
  queer resilience\, and to the beautiful art of never letting go.\nThis pr
 oject is subsidized in part by an open stages grant from Constellation Sta
 ge & Screen and the city of Bloomington
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250919T190000
LOCATION:John Waldron Arts Center Firebay\, 122 South Walnut St.\, Blooming
 ton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryan Wants A Jimmy Award
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryan-wants-a-jimmy-award/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>What happens 
 when a 30-something gay actor\, stuck in the audition grind\, gets one mor
 e shot at his biggest dream—the Jimmy Awards?</p>\n<p>In this one-person t
 our de force\, the audience takes a riotous and heartfelt journey through 
 Broadway dreams\, hook-up mishaps\, and the existential crises that lie in
  between. With biting wit\, showbiz satire\, and a whole lot of belting\, 
 Ryan Wants a Jimmy Award is a love letter to theatre\, to queer resilience
 \, and to the beautiful art of never letting go.</p>\n<p>This project is s
 ubsidized in part by an open stages grant from Constellation Stage & Scree
 n and the city of Bloomington</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140285@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The inaugural show in a new monthly/bi-monthly creative worksho
 p series named the secret sessions @Pillar Arts.  The intention is to crea
 te a forum to present new material or to bring together new configurations
  of people and workshop music in an informal interactive environment.  Thi
 s Friday they will be workshopping a piece of Norbert Herber’s which focus
 es on evolving rhythmic cycles.  The ensemble will be Norbert\, Kyle Quass
  and Brendan Keller-Tuberg.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250919T190000
LOCATION:Pillar Arts Alliance Center - College Mall\, 2894 E 3rd St
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Secret Sessions@Pillar Arts: A Creative Workshop Series led by 
 Kyle Quass
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-secret-sessions-a-creative-workshop-series/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>The inaugur
 al show in a new monthly/bi-monthly creative workshop series named the sec
 ret sessions @Pillar Arts.  The intention is to create a forum to present 
 new material or to bring together new configurations of people and worksho
 p music in an informal interactive environment.  <strong>This Friday they 
 will be workshopping a piece of Norbert Herber’s which focuses on evolving
  rhythmic cycles.  The ensemble will be Norbert\, Kyle Quass and Brendan K
 eller-Tuberg.</strong></div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
