BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140341@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015806Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:What happens when a 30-something gay actor\, stuck in the audit
 ion grind\, gets one more shot at his biggest dream—the Jimmy Awards?\nIn 
 this one-person tour de force\, the audience takes a riotous and heartfelt
  journey through Broadway dreams\, hook-up mishaps\, and the existential c
 rises that lie in between. With biting wit\, showbiz satire\, and a whole 
 lot of belting\, Ryan Wants a Jimmy Award is a love letter to theatre\, to
  queer resilience\, and to the beautiful art of never letting go.\nThis pr
 oject is subsidized in part by an open stages grant from Constellation Sta
 ge & Screen and the city of Bloomington
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250920T150000
LOCATION:John Waldron Arts Center Firebay\, 122 South Walnut St.\, Blooming
 ton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ryan Wants a Jimmy Award
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/ryan-wants-a-jimmy-award-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>What happens 
 when a 30-something gay actor\, stuck in the audition grind\, gets one mor
 e shot at his biggest dream—the Jimmy Awards?</p>\n<p>In this one-person t
 our de force\, the audience takes a riotous and heartfelt journey through 
 Broadway dreams\, hook-up mishaps\, and the existential crises that lie in
  between. With biting wit\, showbiz satire\, and a whole lot of belting\, 
 Ryan Wants a Jimmy Award is a love letter to theatre\, to queer resilience
 \, and to the beautiful art of never letting go.</p>\n<p>This project is s
 ubsidized in part by an open stages grant from Constellation Stage & Scree
 n and the city of Bloomington</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
