 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The October F
 irst Thursdays will be a festival of art\, ideas\, and community featuring
  2 performance stages\, 70+ activity booths\, 20+ arts vendors\, food truc
 ks\, giveaways\, and more. Around the IU Fine Arts Plaza\, there will be a
  zine-making station\, an “ask a philosopher” booth\, a/v technology and f
 abrication demos\, and henna tattooing among many other activities. On the
  main stage\, we’ll have country line dancing with Wall to Wall Line Dance
  Club along with performances by the African American Dance Company\, NOTU
 S (IU Jacobs)\, IU Musical Theatre\, and IU Contemporary Dance. For more d
 etails\, visit <a href='https://artsandhumanities.indiana.edu/council-prog
