BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-139812@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Fifty-seven years ago\, Elliott conducted her now-legendary Blu
 e-Eyed/Brown-Eyed Exercise that exposed children to the harsh realities of
  discrimination based solely on eye color—a condition over which they had 
 no control. A Contrast in Color is a powerful exploration of race\, identi
 ty\, and the human condition.\nA reception and talkback will follow each p
 erformance. There will be a Special Talkback on Friday\, October 3rd\, fea
 turing Jane and Sarah Elliott.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251002T180000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center 202 E 6th St\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20251003T180000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Jane Elliott — A Contrast in Color\, presented by Resilience Produc
 tions
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/jane-elliott-a-contrast-in-color-presented-by-re
 silience-productions/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Fifty-seven y
 ears ago\, Elliott conducted her now-legendary Blue-Eyed/Brown-Eyed Exerci
 se that exposed children to the harsh realities of discrimination based so
 lely on eye color—a condition over which they had no control. A Contrast i
 n Color is a powerful exploration of race\, identity\, and the human condi
 tion.</p>\n<p>A reception and talkback will follow each performance. There
  will be a Special Talkback on Friday\, October 3rd\, featuring Jane and S
 arah Elliott.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
