 ows-at-7pm-930pm/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Jiaoying Summ
 ers is a comedy powerhouse on a rapid rise blending fearless\, dark humor 
 with a deeply personal and refreshingly global perspective. Born in China 
 and now based in Los Angeles\, she turns cultural clashes\, immigrant iden
 tity\, and motherhood into razor-sharp comedy that resonates across contin
 ents.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140908@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Gaucho Gaucho paints an Argentinian Western with image and soun
 d that reach an operatic beauty. Acclaimed photographers and now three-tim
 e Sundance-fêted filmmakers Gregory Kershaw and Michael Dweck (The Truffle
  Hunters\, The Last Race) return to the screen\, this time focusing on the
  vast mountains of Argentina\, expressed in stunning black-and-white photo
 graphy\, and a small community of gauchos who hold profound connections to
  the surrounding nature and their own traditions. As older generations dis
 pense their wisdom\, the film keeps its eye toward a new generation who co
 ntinue to fight for their families’ legacy in a modern world. [85 min\; do
 cumentary\; Spanish with English subtitles]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251003T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20251004T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:New Americas Cinema Series: GAUCHO GAUCHO
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/new-americas-cinema-series-gaucho-gaucho/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Gaucho Gaucho
  paints an Argentinian Western with image and sound that reach an operatic
  beauty. Acclaimed photographers and now three-time Sundance-fêted filmmak
 ers Gregory Kershaw and Michael Dweck (The Truffle Hunters\, The Last Race
 ) return to the screen\, this time focusing on the vast mountains of Argen
 tina\, expressed in stunning black-and-white photography\, and a small com
 munity of gauchos who hold profound connections to the surrounding nature 
 and their own traditions. As older generations dispense their wisdom\, the
  film keeps its eye toward a new generation who continue to fight for thei
 r families’ legacy in a modern world. [85 min\; documentary\; Spanish with
  English subtitles] </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
