BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140519@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:It starts with the sound of a spoon scraping against glass and 
 the wet noise of lips smacking together. June and Lurie have a haunting ne
 w houseguest – and she’s ravenously hungry. They do their best to keep her
  fed and happy\, but Beatrice always demands more. As she burrows deeper a
 nd deeper into their lives\, the couple faces a horrific question: What wi
 ll it cost to exorcise Beatrice forever?\nKirsten Greenidge’s spine-chilli
 ng gothic tale\, about a contemporary Black couple haunted by the ghost of
  a young white girl\, deftly explores questions of race\, class and the Am
 erican Dream.\nCW: racism\, child sexual abuse\, child death\, racist slur
 s\nThe Redbud Community Play Reading Series is a free monthly reading seri
 es in which community members and theatre professionals share in the joy o
 f reading plays aloud together. These unrehearsed readings offer opportuni
 ties to appreciate plays written by local playwrights and IU alums\, and e
 stablished plays we may not otherwise be exposed to.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251008T190000
LOCATION:Redbud Books\, 408 West Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Community Play Reading: “Feeding Beatrice: A Gothic Tale” by Kirste
 n Greenidge
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/community-play-reading-feeding-beatrice-a-gothic
 -tale-by-kirsten-greenidge/
X-COST-TYPE:free
