CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This free\, community-centered event is dedicated to connecting
  older adults and their families with\nessential resources that promote he
 althy\, active\, and independent living. Attendees can explore\nover 40 lo
 cal vendors\, enjoy engagement activities and healthy snacks at each table
 \, and\nparticipate in wellness offerings such as chair yoga\, bingo\, and
  a Medicare 101 session.\nThe Expo will also feature free hearing screenin
 gs and will host the annual Community Dementia\nAlliance Caregiver Awards\
 , recognizing outstanding caregivers in the Bloomington community.\nThe ev
 ent is proudly presented by Elara Caring and Bell Trace Senior Living\, wi
 th premier sponsors\nComfort Keepers\, Home Instead\, and Elder’s Journey 
 Home Care\, and supporting sponsors\nincluding McCormick’s Creek Rehabilit
 ation and Healthcare Center\, Owen Valley Rehabilitation\nand Healthcare C
 enter\, Brickyard Healthcare- Bloomington\, Stonecroft Health Campus\, Dyn
 asty\nHaven\, and Jones Music Therapy.\nFor more information about the eve
 nt\, visit our Facebook Page (Bloomington Healthy Aging Expo) or\ncontact 
 Sandra McGow at smcgow@cardon.us/812-961-0446
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251009T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251009T140000
LOCATION:1375 North Wellness Way\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Healthy Aging Expo
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-healthy-aging-expo/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>This free\, c
 ommunity-centered event is dedicated to connecting older adults and their 
 families with<br />\nessential resources that promote healthy\, active\, a
 nd independent living. Attendees can explore<br />\nover 40 local vendors\
 , enjoy engagement activities and healthy snacks at each table\, and<br />
 \nparticipate in wellness offerings such as chair yoga\, bingo\, and a Med
 icare 101 session.<br />\nThe Expo will also feature free hearing screenin
 gs and will host the annual Community Dementia<br />\nAlliance Caregiver A
 wards\, recognizing outstanding caregivers in the Bloomington community.<b
 r />\nThe event is proudly presented by Elara Caring and Bell Trace Senior
  Living\, with premier sponsors<br />\nComfort Keepers\, Home Instead\, an
 d Elder’s Journey Home Care\, and supporting sponsors<br />\nincluding McC
 ormick’s Creek Rehabilitation and Healthcare Center\, Owen Valley Rehabili
 tation<br />\nand Healthcare Center\, Brickyard Healthcare- Bloomington\, 
 Stonecroft Health Campus\, Dynasty<br />\nHaven\, and Jones Music Therapy.
 </p>\n<p>For more information about the event\, visit our Facebook Page (B
 loomington Healthy Aging Expo) or<br />\ncontact Sandra McGow at smcgow@ca
 rdon.us/812-961-0446</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
