CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION: MCHA’s dedicated veterinary team of volunteers and staff will 
 be available from 1–3 p.m. with no appointment needed\; all are welcome!\n
 \nMobile Clinics offer a range of services\, including legally mandated ra
 bies vaccines for pets aged 12 weeks (about 3 months) and older. Additiona
 lly\, clinics provide nail trims\, anal gland expressions\, microchips\, a
 nd preventive measures for flea\, tick\, and heartworm.\n\nProtect Your Do
 g and Save Money at the October Mobile Vaccine Clinic:\nLeptospirosis is a
  serious\, life-threatening disease that can spread to humans\, so keeping
  your dog protected is essential. Ask about a special we will offer for va
 ccination to prevent this disease. \n\nSubsidized rates are available to r
 esidents experiencing financial hardship. To qualify for these rates\, res
 idents should bring valid documentation with them to the Mobile Vaccine Cl
 inic. Safety is paramount. Cats must be in carriers\, and dogs must be lea
 shed (no retractable leashes). It’s essential for pet owners to understand
  that pets showing signs of illness or aggression might be turned away.\n
 \nLearn more about Mobile Vaccine Clinics\, including future dates and loc
 ations\, at monroehumane.org.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251012T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251012T150000
LOCATION:Cambridge Square Apartments\, 307 N Pete Ellis Drive\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Monroe County Humane Association sponsored Low-Cost Vaccine Clinic 
 for Dogs and Cats
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/monroe-county-humane-association-to-offer-low-co
 st-appointment-free-vaccine-clinic-for-dogs-and-cats/
