BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141163@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Freedoms under Assault is a powerful full-length documentary th
 at chronicles the systematic destruction of a world-class university and t
 he politically motivated culture war against its faculty over a two-year p
 eriod. A perfect storm of an autocratic university president collaborating
  with a supermajority reactionary state legislature following the ideologi
 cal agenda of the White House has effectively curtailed the institutional 
 autonomy of Indiana University as well as shared governance structures\, a
 cademic freedom\, free speech and assembly rights\, tenure\, and the viabi
 lity of arts and humanities programs. The documentary shows the lengths to
  which a university administration is willing to silence\, intimidate\, pe
 rsecute and even exile faculty members in accord with arbitrary policies a
 nd “financial exigencies.” The film is co-directed/produced by Robert Arno
 ve\, IU Chancellor’s Professor Emeritus of Education\, and award-winning d
 ocumentarian\, Jacky Comforty.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251012T140000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theatre\, 114 East Kirkwood\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Freedoms under Assault\, a documentary
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/freedoms-under-assault-a-documentary/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Freedoms unde
 r Assault is a powerful full-length documentary that chronicles the system
 atic destruction of a world-class university and the politically motivated
  culture war against its faculty over a two-year period. A perfect storm o
 f an autocratic university president collaborating with a supermajority re
 actionary state legislature following the ideological agenda of the White 
 House has effectively curtailed the institutional autonomy of Indiana Univ
 ersity as well as shared governance structures\, academic freedom\, free s
 peech and assembly rights\, tenure\, and the viability of arts and humanit
 ies programs. The documentary shows the lengths to which a university admi
 nistration is willing to silence\, intimidate\, persecute and even exile f
 aculty members in accord with arbitrary policies and “financial exigencies
 .” The film is co-directed/produced by Robert Arnove\, IU Chancellor’s Pro
 fessor Emeritus of Education\, and award-winning documentarian\, Jacky Com
 forty.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
