UID:ai1ec-141402@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Can AI enable us to live forever? Filmmaker Ann Shin sets out o
 n a journey\, exploring the latest AI and biotech with scientists and visi
 onaries who foresee a “post-biological” world where humans and AI merge. W
 ill AI be the best\, or the last thing we ever do? [74 min\; documentary\;
  English]\nA panel discussion and Q&A will follow the screening with Selma
  Šabanović (IU Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing\, and Engineering)\
 ; Amy Kinney (IU Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing\, and Engineering
 )\; Eliza Frenkel (IU Department of Anthropology)\; Nathan Ensmenger (IU L
 uddy School of Informatics\, Computing\, and Engineering)\; and Katy Abram
 son (IU Department of Philosophy).
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251014T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Additional Films & Guests Series: A.rtificial I.mmortality w/Q&A
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/additional-films-guests-series-a-rtificial-i-mmo
 rtality-w-qa/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> Can AI enabl
 e us to live forever? Filmmaker Ann Shin sets out on a journey\, exploring
  the latest AI and biotech with scientists and visionaries who foresee a “
 post-biological” world where humans and AI merge. Will AI be the best\, or
  the last thing we ever do? [74 min\; documentary\; English]</p>\n<p><stro
 ng>A panel discussion and Q&A will follow the screening with Selma Šabanov
 ić (IU Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing\, and Engineering)\; Amy Ki
 nney (IU Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing\, and Engineering)\; Eliz
 a Frenkel (IU Department of Anthropology)\; Nathan Ensmenger (IU Luddy Sch
 ool of Informatics\, Computing\, and Engineering)\; and Katy Abramson (IU 
 Department of Philosophy).</strong> </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
