CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This talk\, presented by the Department of Middle Eastern Langu
 ages and Cultures\, launches from the murdered Gazan poet Hiba Abu Nada’s 
 work to present a reading of the Arabic poetic tradition through the lens 
 of Gaza\, highlighting a long Arabic legacy of confronting time and its ca
 lamities with defiant “alone-ness.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251015T193000
LOCATION:Shreve Auditorium (GA0001) in the Global Studies Building on the I
 U Campus\, 355 Eagleson Avenue\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:“Not Just Passing: Hiba Abu Nada\, A Gazan Poet in Context\,” a pre
 sentation by Dr. Huda Fakhreddine
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/not-just-passing-hiba-abu-nada-a-gazan-poet-in-c
 ontext-a-presentation-by-dr-huda-fakhreddine/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>This talk\, p
 resented by the Department of Middle Eastern Languages and Cultures\, laun
 ches from the murdered Gazan poet Hiba Abu Nada’s work to present a readin
 g of the Arabic poetic tradition through the lens of Gaza\, highlighting a
  long Arabic legacy of confronting time and its calamities with defiant “a
 lone-ness.”</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
