BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141586@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Featuring songs composed in collaboration with others over the 
 course of the artist’s career\nA specialist in the fields of higher educat
 ion and popular music studies\, West’s Ph.D. focuses on the teaching and l
 earning of songwriting\, and he has an M.A. in Professional Learning. In 2
 006\, he designed and course-directed the world’s first master’s degree in
  songwriting.\nHis first book\, The Art of Songwriting\, was published by 
 Bloomsbury in 2016 and is now in its fifth edition. A second book\, Higher
  Music Education: 21 Questions for the 21st Century\, was published by Lee
 ds Conservatoire in 2020\, and his third book\, Paul Weller and Popular Mu
 sic\, was published by Routledge in 2022.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251017T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251017T180000
LOCATION:Ford-Crawford Hall\, located on the second floor of the Simon Musi
 c Center\, 200 S. Eagleson Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Faculty Recital: Andy West\, voice/guitar/songwriter
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/faculty-recital-andy-west-voice-guitar-songwrite
 r/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Featu
 ring songs composed in collaboration with others over the course of the ar
 tist’s career</strong><br />\nA specialist in the fields of higher educati
 on and popular music studies\, West’s Ph.D. focuses on the teaching and le
 arning of songwriting\, and he has an M.A. in Professional Learning. In 20
 06\, he designed and course-directed the world’s first master’s degree in 
 songwriting.</p>\n<p>His first book\, The Art of Songwriting\, was publish
 ed by Bloomsbury in 2016 and is now in its fifth edition. A second book\, 
 Higher Music Education: 21 Questions for the 21st Century\, was published 
 by Leeds Conservatoire in 2020\, and his third book\, Paul Weller and Popu
 lar Music\, was published by Routledge in 2022.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
