UID:ai1ec-141592@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Renowned shaman Lee Haw-rim and her protégé are hired by a weal
 thy\, enigmatic family to investigate a disturbing supernatural illness th
 at affects only the first-born children of each generation. Drawing on the
  help of a knowledgeable mortician and the country’s most revered geomance
 r\, the quartet soon trace the affliction’s origin to a long-hidden family
  grave located on sacred ground. But as something much darker emerges\, th
 ey soon discover what befalls those who dare to mess with the wrong grave.
  [134 min\; horror\; Korean and Japanese with English subtitles]\n“Exhuma 
 is a masterpiece of art-horror and South Korean filmmaking\, ensured to en
 thrall viewers into repeated viewings and deep dives into each chapter.” —
  Josiah Teal\, Film Threat
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251017T220000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Friday Night Frights Series: Exhuma/Pamyo
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/friday-night-frights-series-exhuma-pamyo/
