BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141593@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:L’Argent\, the final film by French auteur Robert Bresson\, ada
 pts Tolstoy’s The Forged Coupon into a stripped-down meditation on moral c
 ausality. A counterfeit bill sets off a chain of escalating consequences\,
  revealing how minor acts of deceit spiral into irreversible violence. Kno
 wn for his minimalist style and use of non-professional actors\, Bresson d
 elivers a haunting portrait of systemic indifference. The film won Best Di
 rector at Cannes\, capping Bresson’s career with one of his starkest visio
 ns. [125 min\; drama\; French with English subtitles]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251018T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:City Lights Film Series: L’Argent
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/city-lights-film-series-largent/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>L’Argent\, th
 e final film by French auteur Robert Bresson\, adapts Tolstoy’s The Forged
  Coupon into a stripped-down meditation on moral causality. A counterfeit 
 bill sets off a chain of escalating consequences\, revealing how minor act
 s of deceit spiral into irreversible violence. Known for his minimalist st
 yle and use of non-professional actors\, Bresson delivers a haunting portr
 ait of systemic indifference. The film won Best Director at Cannes\, cappi
 ng Bresson’s career with one of his starkest visions. [125 min\; drama\; F
 rench with English subtitles] </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
