DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy acclaimed artists at Bloomington Boogies: The Bloomington
  Blues & Boogie Woogie Piano Festival.  Featuring musicians who perform bo
 ogie-woogie\, blues\, and related styles in free and ticketed performances
 \, the festival strives to introduce young people to artists and various s
 tyles through public concerts and free educational activities\, including 
 school performances\, workshops\, and master classes.\nThe festival begins
  at 1:30 p.m.\, Oct. 19th with a performance/piano workshop presented by G
 reenville\, MS pianist\, vocalist\, and composer Eden Brent at Monroe Coun
 ty History Center\, 202 E 6th St.  Youth and aspiring pianists are invited
 . Pre-register at the festival website Education page.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251019T133000
LOCATION:Monroe County History Center\, 202 E 6th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Blues & Boogie Woogie Piano Festival Piano Workshop\, f
 eaturing pianist\, vocalist\, and composer Eden Brent
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-blues-boogie-woogie-piano-festival-p
 iano-workshop/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Enjoy acclaim
 ed artists at Bloomington Boogies: The Bloomington Blues & Boogie Woogie P
 iano Festival.  Featuring musicians who perform boogie-woogie\, blues\, an
 d related styles in free and ticketed performances\, the festival strives 
 to introduce young people to artists and various styles through public con
 certs and free educational activities\, including school performances\, wo
 rkshops\, and master classes.</p>\n<p>The festival begins at 1:30 p.m.\, O
 ct. 19th with a performance/piano workshop presented by Greenville\, MS pi
 anist\, vocalist\, and composer Eden Brent at Monroe County History Center
 \, 202 E 6th St.  Youth and aspiring pianists are invited. Pre-register at
  the festival website Education page.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
