BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141595@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:“Diane… 6:18 am\, room 315\, Great Northern Hotel up here in Tw
 in Peaks. Slept pretty well.” That might have been the last good sleep Age
 nt Dale Cooper ever had in Twin Peaks…\nEpisode 1 (pilot\, “Northwest Pass
 age”): The small northwest town of Twin Peaks\, Washington is shaken up wh
 en the body of the homecoming queen\, Laura Palmer\, is discovered washed 
 up on a riverbank\, wrapped in plastic.\nEpisode 2 (“Traces to Nowhere”): 
 Agent Cooper enjoys the comforts of the Great Northern Hotel. Bobby Briggs
  and Mike Nelson are released from jail. Doctor Hayward hands over the aut
 opsy report on Laura Palmer. [150 min total\; drama\, mystery\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251019T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Twin Peaks Season 1\, Episodes 1 and 2
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/twin-peaks-season-1-episodes-1-and-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>“Diane… 6:18 
 am\, room 315\, Great Northern Hotel up here in Twin Peaks. Slept pretty w
 ell.” That might have been the last good sleep Agent Dale Cooper ever had 
 in Twin Peaks…</p>\n<p>Episode 1 (pilot\, “Northwest Passage”): The small 
 northwest town of Twin Peaks\, Washington is shaken up when the body of th
 e homecoming queen\, Laura Palmer\, is discovered washed up on a riverbank
 \, wrapped in plastic.</p>\n<p>Episode 2 (“Traces to Nowhere”): Agent Coop
 er enjoys the comforts of the Great Northern Hotel. Bobby Briggs and Mike 
 Nelson are released from jail. Doctor Hayward hands over the autopsy repor
 t on Laura Palmer. [150 min total\; drama\, mystery\; English]</p>\n</BODY
 ></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141401@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 3:30pm\n4pm Pre-concert talk with our friends from My 
 Sister’s Closet \, included with ticket. 5pm Concert with the Bloomington 
 Symphony Orchestra\nMusic opens up new horizons – to places we’ve always l
 onged to see\, or maybe even places we’ve only imagined. This October\, pl
 ease join us and our friends from My Sister’s Closet as we explore the bou
 ndaries of imagination in Otherwhere.\nOn the program:\n● Gabriela Ortiz d
 escribed her work Antrópolis “as the sonorous reflection of a city through
  its experiences…in this very complex but fascinating Mexico City.”\n● Fel
 ix Mendelssohn’s Piano Concerto No. 1 in G minor\, Opus 25 (1st movement) 
 featuring BSO Youth Concerto Competition winner Solar Manley .\n● Amy Beac
 h’s Gaelic Symphony pays tribute\, in her own words\, to the “simple\, rug
 ged\, and unpretentious beauty” of traditional Irish folksongs.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251019T170000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Symphony Orchestra presents: Otherwhere
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-symphony-orchestra-presents-otherwhe
 re/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 3:30pm</strong><br />\n4pm Pre-concert talk with our friends from My S
 ister’s Closet \, included with ticket. 5pm Concert with the Bloomington S
 ymphony Orchestra</p>\n<p>Music opens up new horizons – to places we’ve al
 ways longed to see\, or maybe even places we’ve only imagined. This Octobe
 r\, please join us and our friends from My Sister’s Closet as we explore t
 he boundaries of imagination in Otherwhere.</p>\n<p>On the program:</p>\n<
 p>● Gabriela Ortiz described her work Antrópolis “as the sonorous reflecti
 on of a city through its experiences…in this very complex but fascinating 
 Mexico City.”</p>\n<p>● Felix Mendelssohn’s Piano Concerto No. 1 in G mino
 r\, Opus 25 (1st movement) featuring BSO Youth Concerto Competition winner
  Solar Manley .</p>\n<p>● Amy Beach’s Gaelic Symphony pays tribute\, in he
 r own words\, to the “simple\, rugged\, and unpretentious beauty” of tradi
 tional Irish folksongs.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
