BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141525@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Green Drinks Bloomington is a lively\, informal social networki
 ng event for people from all walks of life who are interested in making a 
 greener world. We gather monthly to\nshare libations and dialogue\, explor
 e ideas and make new friends and business connections.\nDid you know that 
 water shortages plagued our community before Lake Monroe was constructed? 
 Reliable drinking water is an essential part of modern life for everything
  from\ndrinking to bathing to agriculture to manufacturing. Our lake is al
 so a huge destination for boating\, fishing and swimming which generates a
  significant boost to our economy. Last but\nnot least\, Lake Monroe is an
  important destination for wildlife\, particularly migrating waterfowl. Le
 arn how Friends of Lake Monroe is working to protect and improve this\nval
 uable resource that supports us all.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251022T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251022T193000
LOCATION:UplandBrewing Wood Shop\, 354 West 11th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:“We All Need Water: How Friends of Lake Monroe is Protecting Our Mo
 st Important (and Popular) Water Source\,” presented by Green Drinks Bloom
 ington
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/we-all-need-water-how-friends-of-lake-monroe-is-
 protecting-our-most-important-and-popular-water-source-presented-by-green-
 drinks-bloomington/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Green Drinks 
 Bloomington is a lively\, informal social networking event for people from
  all walks of life who are interested in making a greener world. We gather
  monthly to<br />\nshare libations and dialogue\, explore ideas and make n
 ew friends and business connections.</p>\n<p>Did you know that water short
 ages plagued our community before Lake Monroe was constructed? Reliable dr
 inking water is an essential part of modern life for everything from<br />
 \ndrinking to bathing to agriculture to manufacturing. Our lake is also a 
 huge destination for boating\, fishing and swimming which generates a sign
 ificant boost to our economy. Last but<br />\nnot least\, Lake Monroe is a
 n important destination for wildlife\, particularly migrating waterfowl. L
 earn how Friends of Lake Monroe is working to protect and improve this<br 
 />\nvaluable resource that supports us all.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141693@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 5:30pm\nJoin us for Astronomy on Tap Bloomington’s upc
 oming spooky event on October 22nd featuring amazing talks by IU astronomy
  graduate students!  Speakers: Tash Sandford and Lexi Gault\nCome explore 
 the wonders of the Universe! Dive into fascinating astronomy topics\, enjo
 y interactive games\, and compete for exciting prizes. Our events are open
  to all ages—so bring the whole family\, and don’t forget to dress the kid
 s and yourselves in the spookiest costumes!
