CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The bedtime singing of monks and nuns\, Compline (pronounced “K
 OMP-lin”) consists of Gregorian Chant and choral music lasting approximate
 ly twenty minutes. Its repertoire includes masterworks by Tallis\, Victori
 a\, Byrd and Palestrina\, together with compositions of later ages. While 
 the music sung is from the Christian tradition\, there is no church affili
 ation\, nor are clergy present.\n\nCompline is sung in a darkened space\, 
 lit only by candles. The organ is used only sparingly and there is an over
 all quietness and peace which invites contemplation.  Because the music is
  ‘otherworldly’ and the physical setting arranged to facilitate meditation
 \, Compline offers space for mindfulness and contemplation— to be ‘alone t
 ogether.’\nAlumni Hall\, at the crossroads of our campus\, is architectura
 lly distinguished and boasts a fine organ. It is an ideal Bloomington loca
 tion for choral Compline.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251026T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251026T213000
LOCATION:Alumni Hall\, Indiana Memorial Union\, 900 E 7th Street\, Blooming
 ton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Choral Compline by Candlelight – Jeffrey Smith\, director
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/choral-compline-by-candlelight-jeffrey-smith-dir
 ector-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>The bedtime
  singing of monks and nuns\, Compline (pronounced “KOMP-lin”) consists of 
 Gregorian Chant and choral music lasting approximately twenty minutes. Its
  repertoire includes masterworks by Tallis\, Victoria\, Byrd and Palestrin
 a\, together with compositions of later ages. While the music sung is from
  the Christian tradition\, there is no church affiliation\, nor are clergy
  present.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Compline is sung in a darkened space\, 
 lit only by candles. The organ is used only sparingly and there is an over
 all quietness and peace which invites contemplation.  Because the music is
  ‘otherworldly’ and the physical setting arranged to facilitate meditation
 \, Compline offers space for mindfulness and contemplation— to be ‘alone t
 ogether.’</div>\n<div>Alumni Hall\, at the crossroads of our campus\, is a
 rchitecturally distinguished and boasts a fine organ. It is an ideal Bloom
 ington location for choral Compline.</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
