BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141997@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Seed ticks? Alpha-gal? Dogs and Lonestars? What’s it all mean? 
 This year’s tick season has been extremely active\, but there are many way
 s you can protect yourself. Join us for a “Tick Talk” with Kenny Holsclaw\
 , naturalist\, invasive species remover\, and tick enthusiast\, to explore
  the fascinating and sometimes unsettling world of ticks. You’ll learn how
  to identify common species\, understand their life cycles and habitats\, 
 and discover practical tips for staying safe while enjoying the outdoors. 
 Sign up at sycamorelandtrust.org/events.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251029T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251029T193000
LOCATION:4898 E Heritage Woods Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Tick Talk with Kenny Holsclaw\, naturalist\, invasive species remov
 er\, and tick enthusiast
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/tick-talk-with-kenny-holsclaw-naturalist-invasiv
 e-species-remover-and-tick-enthusiast/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Seed ticks? A
 lpha-gal? Dogs and Lonestars? What’s it all mean? This year’s tick season 
 has been extremely active\, but there are many ways you can protect yourse
 lf. Join us for a “Tick Talk” with Kenny Holsclaw\, naturalist\, invasive 
 species remover\, and tick enthusiast\, to explore the fascinating and som
 etimes unsettling world of ticks. <strong>You’ll learn how to identify com
 mon species\, understand their life cycles and habitats\, and discover pra
 ctical tips for staying safe while enjoying the outdoors. Sign up at sycam
 orelandtrust.org/events.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
