BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142023@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The altar celebrates the ancestors\, both distant and near\, re
 cent and ancient. We invite visitors to contribute to the altar in honor o
 f their deceased loved ones. There are pens and paper available to write n
 otes to the departed and place them on or attach them to the altar. Visito
 rs are also invited to leave a gift to their ancestors on the altar.\nOffe
 rings and notes left on the altar are collected each year and incorporated
  into future altars. Each year the Community Altar is built upon the found
 ation of the previous years’ offerings. Many of the items on the altar hav
 e been there for years.\nWe encourage visitors to spend some time with the
  book on the altar that contains all of the notes left during previous alt
 ars. We collect these each year and read them after the altar is taken dow
 n and then put them in this book so visitors can read them. Some are so po
 ignant they literally bring tears.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251031T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251031T200000
LOCATION:Backspace Gallery\, inside Bonne Fête\, 112 West 6th Street\, on t
 he square in Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Closing Gathering for the 18th Annual Bloomington Community Altar C
 elebrating The Dead
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/closing-gathering-for-the-18th-annual-bloomingto
 n-community-altar-celebrating-the-dead/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>The a
 ltar celebrates the ancestors\, both distant and near\, recent and ancient
 . We invite visitors to contribute to the altar in honor of their deceased
  loved ones. There are pens and paper available to write notes to the depa
 rted and place them on or attach them to the altar. Visitors are also invi
 ted to leave a gift to their ancestors on the altar.<br />\nOfferings and 
 notes left on the altar are collected each year and incorporated into futu
 re altars. Each year the Community Altar is built upon the foundation of t
 he previous years’ offerings. Many of the items on the altar have been the
 re for years.<br />\nWe encourage visitors to spend some time with the boo
 k on the altar that contains all of the notes left during previous altars.
  We collect these each year and read them after the altar is taken down an
 d then put them in this book so visitors can read them. Some are so poigna
 nt they literally bring tears.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
