BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142200@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:https://sciencefest.indiana.edu/\nhttps://sciencefest.indiana.e
 du/map/index.html\nWhat else is new at Science Fest this year?\n– a ROCKET
  SCIENCE with Physics!\n– COLORFUL CORAL – Science Under the Sea with Biol
 ogy!\n– MOLECULAR EXPRESSIONS – with Hoosier Henna in Chemistry!\n– The Be
 autiful and Hidden World of CRYSTAL STRUCTURE in Chemistry\n– CUNEIFORM TA
 BLETS and the Mathematics of Ancient Babylonians with the History and Phil
 osophy of Science and Mathematics Dept!\n– LUNGevity with the IU Simon Com
 prehensive Cancer Center!\n– STAR POLYDEDRA with Mathematics!\n– MATH BALL
 OONS!\nIt’s easy to explore your options and plan your visit by taking a l
 ook here at the Science Fest website\, where you’ll find many resources fo
 r ongoing science education\, too. Parking is free for Science Fest! There
  will be plenty of volunteers on hand to help you find your way from place
  to place as you take in the fun\, at your own pace and according to what 
 interests you most.\nScience Fest is an extraordinary community festival\,
  focused on giving children\, families\, educators\, caregivers\, and scho
 ol groups the chance to experiment with and experience many facets of scie
 ntific exploration. And new this year is a scavenger hunt!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251101T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251101T160000
LOCATION:790 E Kirkwood\, Bloomington (but check the website for other info
 )
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Science Fest 2025 at IU’s College of Arts and Sciences
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/science-fest-2025-at-ius-college-of-arts-and-sci
 ences/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>https
 ://sciencefest.indiana.edu/</strong><br />\n<strong>https://sciencefest.in
 diana.edu/map/index.html</strong><br />\nWhat else is new at Science Fest 
 this year?<br />\n– a ROCKET SCIENCE with Physics!<br />\n– COLORFUL CORAL
  – Science Under the Sea with Biology!<br />\n– MOLECULAR EXPRESSIONS – wi
 th Hoosier Henna in Chemistry!<br />\n– The Beautiful and Hidden World of 
 CRYSTAL STRUCTURE in Chemistry<br />\n– CUNEIFORM TABLETS and the Mathemat
 ics of Ancient Babylonians with the History and Philosophy of Science and 
 Mathematics Dept!<br />\n– LUNGevity with the IU Simon Comprehensive Cance
 r Center!<br />\n– STAR POLYDEDRA with Mathematics!<br />\n– MATH BALLOONS
 !<br />\nIt’s easy to explore your options and plan your visit by taking a
  look here at the Science Fest website\, where you’ll find many resources 
 for ongoing science education\, too. Parking is free for Science Fest! The
 re will be plenty of volunteers on hand to help you find your way from pla
 ce to place as you take in the fun\, at your own pace and according to wha
 t interests you most.</p>\n<p>Science Fest is an extraordinary community f
 estival\, focused on giving children\, families\, educators\, caregivers\,
  and school groups the chance to experiment with and experience many facet
 s of scientific exploration. And new this year is a scavenger hunt!</p>\n<
 /BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
