BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142115@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A true delight for the eyes\, this vibrant animated feature tel
 ls the story of a strong-willed young girl and her burgeoning curiosity\, 
 creativity\, and zest for life\, a young girl who will one day become a le
 gendary artist and activist. Surrounded by the visceral and dazzling sight
 s and sounds of her hometown of Coyoacán\, Mexico\, young Frida’s daily ad
 ventures are punctuated with drawing\, tree climbing\, playing with her si
 ster\, and adventures with the neighborhood dog. But her childhood is put 
 on hold following a devastating polio diagnosis\, and Frida must spend her
  days in her bedroom. Forced to live a spell indoors\, she turns to her im
 agination and creates a world filled with endless possibilities\, supporte
 d by her loving family and friends\, and develops an ironclad inner spirit
  that will guide her through life’s hardships. [82 min\; animation\; Spani
 sh with English subtitles]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251101T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:CINEkids International Children’s Film Series: Hola Frida!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cinekids-international-childrens-film-series-hol
 a-frida/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A true deligh
 t for the eyes\, this vibrant animated feature tells the story of a strong
 -willed young girl and her burgeoning curiosity\, creativity\, and zest fo
 r life\, a young girl who will one day become a legendary artist and activ
 ist. Surrounded by the visceral and dazzling sights and sounds of her home
 town of Coyoacán\, Mexico\, young Frida’s daily adventures are punctuated 
 with drawing\, tree climbing\, playing with her sister\, and adventures wi
 th the neighborhood dog. But her childhood is put on hold following a deva
 stating polio diagnosis\, and Frida must spend her days in her bedroom. Fo
 rced to live a spell indoors\, she turns to her imagination and creates a 
 world filled with endless possibilities\, supported by her loving family a
 nd friends\, and develops an ironclad inner spirit that will guide her thr
 ough life’s hardships. [82 min\; animation\; Spanish with English subtitle
 s] </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
