UID:ai1ec-142096@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Registration secures you a spot. Walk-ins accepted before class
  if capacity allows. Info: https://www.inthekitchen-bloomington.com/classe
 s\nThe best soups are made at home. There\, we said it. Is there a time an
 d place for canned tomato or restaurant bisque? You bet. But when the weat
 her turns chilly and you want something bright\, cheery and warm\, a from-
 scratch soup triumphs over just about any other meal. In this class\, we’l
 l embark on a hearty recipe that riffs on traditional Italian pasta-and-sa
 usage soup. With a simplified chicken brodo base\, layers of herbs and smo
 key fattiness from the sausage\, this soup basically builds its own flavor
 . Come learn a recipe you’ll be cooking all winter long!\nDemonstration-st
 yle class with Ava. You’ll leave with soup starter to finish at home.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251102T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251102T143000
LOCATION:In the Kitchen\, 115 N College Ave\, Suite 014\, Bloomington. Use 
 the Uptown Plaza alley entrance between JL Waters and Peach Cobbler Factor
 y.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cooking Class: Weeknight’s Inspired: Sausage\, Orecchiette & Kale S
 oup
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cooking-class-weeknights-inspired-sausage-orecch
 iette-kale-soup/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Regis
 tration secures you a spot. Walk-ins accepted before class if capacity all
 ows. Info: https://www.inthekitchen-bloomington.com/classes</strong><br />
 \nThe best soups are made at home. There\, we said it. Is there a time and
  place for canned tomato or restaurant bisque? You bet. But when the weath
 er turns chilly and you want something bright\, cheery and warm\, a from-s
 cratch soup triumphs over just about any other meal. In this class\, we’ll
  embark on a hearty recipe that riffs on traditional Italian pasta-and-sau
 sage soup. With a simplified chicken brodo base\, layers of herbs and smok
 ey fattiness from the sausage\, this soup basically builds its own flavor.
  Come learn a recipe you’ll be cooking all winter long!</p>\n<p>Demonstrat
 ion-style class with Ava. You’ll leave with soup starter to finish at home
 .</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
