CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Each month\, this class provides nutrition education and teache
 s culinary skills to enhance your cooking experience. There is a cost for 
 all classes\, with different skill levels for each class.\nRegistration is
  required. Find the link to sign up in our Linktree\, found in our Instagr
 am and Facebook bios.\nNov.- Kitchen Explorers: Family meals\, made easier
 : A fun\, interactive cooking class where kids and adults team up to creat
 e healthy\, hands-on meals together. Recipes are easy to follow\, low in a
 dded sugar\, and packed with fruits\, veggies\, and whole grains. Skill Le
 vel: All levels Audience: Families with children ages 5–16
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251104T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251104T110000
LOCATION:Banneker Community Center\, 930 West 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Cooking Classroom
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-cooking-classroom/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Each 
 month\, this class provides nutrition education and teaches culinary skill
 s to enhance your cooking experience. There is a cost for all classes\, wi
 th different skill levels for each class.<br />\nRegistration is required.
  Find the link to sign up in our Linktree\, found in our Instagram and Fac
 ebook bios.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Nov.- Kitchen Explorers: Family meals
 \, made easier: A fun\, interactive cooking class where kids and adults te
 am up to create healthy\, hands-on meals together. Recipes are easy to fol
 low\, low in added sugar\, and packed with fruits\, veggies\, and whole gr
 ains. Skill Level: All levels Audience: Families with children ages 5–16</
 strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141785@wfhb.org
