BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142256@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the year\, ZTA keeps the IU campus engaged through t
 ournaments\, exciting social events\, merchandise sales\, and countless ot
 her activities that make fundraising both fun and impactful. ZTA’s hard wo
 rk is celebrated when the grand total is announced at the end of this annu
 al talent show. As IU’s largest Greek organization focused on philanthropy
 \, ZTA is committed to positively impacting the Indiana University campus 
 and beyond. \nBMOC continues ZTA’s longstanding commitment to the fight ag
 ainst breast cancer. ZTA donates funds to local research with the IU Simon
  Cancer Center and Dr. Hari’s groundbreaking breast cancer research\, dire
 ctly fueling education\, awareness\, and advancements in treatment. Additi
 onally\, ZTA partners with the Breast Cancer Research Foundation\, America
 n Cancer Society\, and the NFL. One in eight women are diagnosed with brea
 st cancer. The goal is to help make pink just a color again!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251104T190000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Big Man on Campus – an all-male talent show where participants from
  across campus compete for the title of Big Man on Campus.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/big-man-on-campus-an-all-male-talent-show-where-
 participants-from-across-campus-compete-for-the-title-of-big-man-on-campus
 /
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Throughout th
 e year\, ZTA keeps the IU campus engaged through tournaments\, exciting so
 cial events\, merchandise sales\, and countless other activities that make
  fundraising both fun and impactful. ZTA’s hard work is celebrated when th
 e grand total is announced at the end of this annual talent show. As IU’s 
 largest Greek organization focused on philanthropy\, ZTA is committed to p
 ositively impacting the Indiana University campus and beyond. </p>\n<p>BMO
 C continues ZTA’s longstanding commitment to the fight against breast canc
 er. ZTA donates funds to local research with the IU Simon Cancer Center an
 d Dr. Hari’s groundbreaking breast cancer research\, directly fueling educ
 ation\, awareness\, and advancements in treatment. Additionally\, ZTA part
 ners with the Breast Cancer Research Foundation\, American Cancer Society\
 , and the NFL. One in eight women are diagnosed with breast cancer. The go
 al is to help make pink just a color again!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142262@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This insightful documentary asks how we have come to imagine wh
 at life is like for LGBTQ people in rural places—and provides an opportuni
 ty to imagine it otherwise.\nIn Plain Sight challenges “metronormativity” 
 by exploring the lives of LGBTQ+ women in the rural Upper Midwest. This do
 cumentary uncovers a surprising reality: contrary to popular stereotypes o
 f rural conservatism\, many of these women find safety\, support\, and hap
 piness in their communities. The film prompts viewers to reconsider precon
 ceived notions about LGBTQ+ experiences outside of urban centers\, offerin
 g a fresh and uplifting perspective on rural inclusivity. [35 min\; docume
 ntary\; English]\nPresented in partnership with Spencer Pride.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251104T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Queer in the Heartland Series: IN PLAIN SIGHT (2019)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/queer-in-the-heartland-series-in-plain-sight-201
 9/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>This 
 insightful documentary asks how we have come to imagine what life is like 
 for LGBTQ people in rural places—and provides an opportunity to imagine it
  otherwise.</strong></p>\n<p>In Plain Sight challenges “metronormativity” 
 by exploring the lives of LGBTQ+ women in the rural Upper Midwest. This do
 cumentary uncovers a surprising reality: contrary to popular stereotypes o
 f rural conservatism\, many of these women find safety\, support\, and hap
 piness in their communities. The film prompts viewers to reconsider precon
 ceived notions about LGBTQ+ experiences outside of urban centers\, offerin
 g a fresh and uplifting perspective on rural inclusivity. [35 min\; docume
 ntary\; English]</p>\n<p>Presented in partnership with Spencer Pride. </p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141205@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:THE HUNGER GAMES (2012)\nBased on the novel by author Suzanne C
 ollins –\nIn a dystopian future\, the totalitarian nation of Panem is divi
 ded into 12 districts and the Capitol. Each year two young representatives
  from each district are selected by lottery to participate in The Hunger G
 ames. Part entertainment\, part brutal retribution for a past rebellion\, 
 the televised games are broadcast throughout Panem. The 24 participants ar
 e forced to eliminate their competitors while the citizens of Panem are re
 quired to watch. When 16-year-old Katniss’ young sister\, Prim\, is select
 ed as District 12’s female representative\, Katniss volunteers to take her
  place. She and her male counterpart\, Peeta\, are pitted against bigger\,
  stronger representatives\, some of whom have trained for this their whole
  lives.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251104T190000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The BCT presents The Hunger Games (2012)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-buskirk-chumley-theater-presents-the-hunger-
 games-2012/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>THE HUNGER GA
 MES (2012)<br />\nBased on the novel by author Suzanne Collins –</p>\n<p>I
 n a dystopian future\, the totalitarian nation of Panem is divided into 12
  districts and the Capitol. Each year two young representatives from each 
 district are selected by lottery to participate in The Hunger Games. Part 
 entertainment\, part brutal retribution for a past rebellion\, the televis
 ed games are broadcast throughout Panem. The 24 participants are forced to
  eliminate their competitors while the citizens of Panem are required to w
 atch. When 16-year-old Katniss’ young sister\, Prim\, is selected as Distr
 ict 12’s female representative\, Katniss volunteers to take her place. She
  and her male counterpart\, Peeta\, are pitted against bigger\, stronger r
 epresentatives\, some of whom have trained for this their whole lives.</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
