BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142231@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Caroline Davis’s Portals project is an immersive sound and hapt
 ic experience\, drawing upon the idea of mourning and ancestral communicat
 ions as textural entities. The music has been mindfully written to offer c
 onnections to Caroline’s ancestors who have transitioned and elements they
  would have liked to explore through the life-cycle portal. Through the co
 mpositions\, the ensemble engages in the improvisatory tissue between dual
  and non-dual realms of existence. The core quartet features Julian Shore\
 , Chris Tordini\, and Timothy Angulo\, and invited guests on her two Porta
 ls albums: Volume 1: Mourning (2021) and Volume 2: Returning (2024).
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251104T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251104T220000
LOCATION:Ford-Crawford Hall\, located on the second floor of the Simon Musi
 c Center\, 200 S. Eagleson Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Guest Recital: Caroline Davis Quartet – “Portals”\, Presented by th
 e IU Jazz Studies Department
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/guest-recital-caroline-davis-quartet-portals-pre
 sented-by-the-jazz-studies-departmentcaroline-davis-quartet/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Caroline Davi
 s’s Portals project is an immersive sound and haptic experience\, drawing 
 upon the idea of mourning and ancestral communications as textural entitie
 s. The music has been mindfully written to offer connections to Caroline’s
  ancestors who have transitioned and elements they would have liked to exp
 lore through the life-cycle portal. Through the compositions\, the ensembl
 e engages in the improvisatory tissue between dual and non-dual realms of 
 existence. The core quartet features Julian Shore\, Chris Tordini\, and Ti
 mothy Angulo\, and invited guests on her two Portals albums: Volume 1: Mou
 rning (2021) and Volume 2: Returning (2024).</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
