BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141514@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION: \nThe African Children’s Choir is marking over four decades of
  transforming lives through the power of music\, education and hope. As th
 ey embark on a tour of more than 100 cities\, the Choir will continue to c
 aptivate audiences with their heartwarming performances with a show that b
 lends traditional hymns and African cultural sounds.\nComprised of childre
 n ages 8 to 10\, all from vulnerable backgrounds across Africa\, the Choir
  serves as a powerful testament to the resilience and potential of Africa’
 s future leaders. Each child in the Choir has faced significant hardship\,
  often with limited access to education. Yet\, through the Choir\, these c
 hildren gain life-changing opportunities for education and personal growth
 \, becoming beacons of hope for their communities.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251105T190000
LOCATION:Mt Gilead Church\, 6019 East SR 144\, Mooresville\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:African Children’s Choir
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/african-childrens-choir/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><span style='
 color: #000000'> </span></p>\n<p dir='ltr'><span style='font-size: large'>
 <a href='https://africanchildrenschoir.com/' target='_blank' rel='noopener
 ' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?q=https://africanchildr
 enschoir.com/&source=gmail&ust=1760638266785000&usg=AOvVaw1ih90im6uyudk6uR
 oEh39a'>The African Children’s Choir</a> is marking over four decades of t
 ransforming lives through the power of music\, education and hope. As they
  embark on a tour of more than 100 cities\, the Choir will continue to cap
 tivate audiences with their heartwarming performances with a show that ble
 nds traditional hymns and African cultural sounds.</span></p>\n<p dir='ltr
 '><span style='font-size: large'>Comprised of children ages 8 to 10\, all 
 from vulnerable backgrounds across Africa\, the Choir serves as a powerful
  testament to the resilience and potential of Africa’s future leaders. Eac
 h child in the Choir has faced significant hardship\, often with limited a
 ccess to education. Yet\, through the Choir\, these children gain life-cha
 nging opportunities for education and personal growth\, becoming beacons o
 f hope for their communities.</span></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
