BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-141134@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Award-winning violinist Robin Scott has built a varied career a
 s a soloist\, chamber musician\, and concertmaster. He has competed intern
 ationally\, winning first prizes in the California International Young Art
 ists Competition and the WAMSO Young Artist Competition in Minnesota\, and
  second prizes in the Yehudi Menuhin International Violin Competition\, th
 e Irving M. Klein International String Competition\, and the Stulberg Inte
 rnational String Competition.\n\nPianist Chih-Yi Chen’s versatile qualitie
 s as a collaborative partner\, chamber musician\, and teacher have contrib
 uted to a distinguished international career. Chen has been on the faculty
  of the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music since 2003 and is the as
 sociate chair of the Chamber and Collaborative Music Department. She was a
  recipient of the 2023 IU Trustees Teaching Award.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251105T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251105T213000
LOCATION:Auer Hall\, located on the second floor of the Simon Music Center\
 , 200 South Eagleson Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Faculty/Guest Recital – Robin Scott\, violin\; Chih-Yi Chen\, piano
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/faculty-guest-recital-robin-scott-violin-chih-yi
 -chen-piano/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div>Award-winni
 ng violinist Robin Scott has built a varied career as a soloist\, chamber 
 musician\, and concertmaster. He has competed internationally\, winning fi
 rst prizes in the California International Young Artists Competition and t
 he WAMSO Young Artist Competition in Minnesota\, and second prizes in the 
 Yehudi Menuhin International Violin Competition\, the Irving M. Klein Inte
 rnational String Competition\, and the Stulberg International String Compe
 tition.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Pianist Chih-Yi Chen’s versatile qualitie
 s as a collaborative partner\, chamber musician\, and teacher have contrib
 uted to a distinguished international career. Chen has been on the faculty
  of the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music since 2003 and is the as
 sociate chair of the Chamber and Collaborative Music Department. She was a
  recipient of the 2023 IU Trustees Teaching Award.</div>\n<div></div>\n</B
 ODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
