BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142402@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Before Western science accepted the existence of meteorites\, m
 any cultures formed their own beliefs about them. Encounters with the cele
 stial rocks have long inspired fear and reverence. Photographer Emilia Mar
 tin is fascinated by the stones\, but also by the people who study and ado
 re them. With whimsy and extensive research\, Martin presents a series of 
 photographs that playfully investigate the old stories and the collective 
 memory surrounding meteorites.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251107T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251107T200000
LOCATION:FAR Center for Contemporary Arts\, 202 South Rogers St.\, Blooming
 ton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:November Gallery Walk Opening Reception: Emilia Martin\, “I saw a t
 ree bearing stones in the place of apples and pears”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/november-gallery-walk-opening-reception-emilia-m
 artin-i-saw-a-tree-bearing-stones-in-the-place-of-apples-and-pears/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Before Wester
 n science accepted the existence of meteorites\, many cultures formed thei
 r own beliefs about them. Encounters with the celestial rocks have long in
 spired fear and reverence. Photographer Emilia Martin is fascinated by the
  stones\, but also by the people who study and adore them. With whimsy and
  extensive research\, Martin presents a series of photographs that playful
 ly investigate the old stories and the collective memory surrounding meteo
 rites.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142049@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This captivating collection showcases imagery from Sara’s recen
 tly released oracle deck — a body of work inspired by dreams\, myths\, and
  archetypes that emerged through an intuitive creative process.\nEach piec
 e invites viewers to look inward\, exploring the symbolic and spiritual co
 nnections that guide the artist’s vision. Merging storytelling and mystici
 sm\, McQueen’s work bridges the seen and unseen worlds with color\, form\,
  and imagination.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251107T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251107T200000
LOCATION:Pillar Arts By Hand \,101 W Kirkwood Ave\, Ste 109\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Opening Reception for “Intuitive Inquiry” by Sara Steffey McQueen
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/opening-reception-for-intuitive-inquiry-by-sara-
 steffey-mcqueen/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>This captivat
 ing collection showcases imagery from Sara’s recently released oracle deck
  — a body of work inspired by dreams\, myths\, and archetypes that emerged
  through an intuitive creative process.</p>\n<p>Each piece invites viewers
  to look inward\, exploring the symbolic and spiritual connections that gu
 ide the artist’s vision. Merging storytelling and mysticism\, McQueen’s wo
 rk bridges the seen and unseen worlds with color\, form\, and imagination.
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
