BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142396@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Why New Farmer U?\n https://www.eventbrite.com/e/new-farmer-u-i
 ndiana-tickets-1657041197829\nFarming means wearing many hats—including th
 at of an entrepreneur and business owner. Understanding the ins and outs o
 f financial planning\, marketing\, and business management is key to makin
 g your farm thrive.\nNew Farmer U is a two-day training and gathering desi
 gned to help small and mid-scale farmers with 2–6 years of experience deve
 lop these skills while connecting with peers and exploring creative ways t
 o manage their operations.\nThis event is all about practical learning and
  real-world strategies. Expect farmer-to-farmer conversations\, interactiv
 e workshops\, small group discussions\, and plenty of time to connect over
  shared meals and campfires.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251108T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251108T170000
LOCATION:611 W 12th St\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20251109T080000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:New Farmer University
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/new-farmer-university/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Why New Farme
 r U?</p>\n<p><strong> https://www.eventbrite.com/e/new-farmer-u-indiana-ti
 ckets-1657041197829</strong><br />\nFarming means wearing many hats—includ
 ing that of an entrepreneur and business owner. Understanding the ins and 
 outs of financial planning\, marketing\, and business management is key to
  making your farm thrive.</p>\n<p><strong>New Farmer U is a two-day traini
 ng and gathering designed to help small and mid-scale farmers with 2–6 yea
 rs of experience develop these skills while connecting with peers and expl
 oring creative ways to manage their operations.</strong></p>\n<p>This even
 t is all about practical learning and real-world strategies. Expect farmer
 -to-farmer conversations\, interactive workshops\, small group discussions
 \, and plenty of time to connect over shared meals and campfires.</p>\n</B
 ODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
