BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142444@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Author and wildlife rehabber Terry Masear has an ambitious goal
 : to save every injured hummingbird in Los Angeles. But the path to surviv
 al is fraught with danger. This heart-expanding Sundance hit introduces au
 diences to Terry’s diminutive patients through breathtaking slow-motion ph
 otography and emotional storytelling. Over the course of director Sally Ai
 tken’s moving documentary\, we become deeply invested in baby hummingbirds
  like Cactus and Wasabi\, celebrating their tiny victories and lamenting t
 heir tragedies. Through Terry’s eyes\, each bird becomes memorable\, might
 y and heroic. Her compassion and empathy serves as a reminder that grace c
 an be found in the smallest of acts and the tiniest of creatures. Previous
 ly shown on PBS Nature in a shortened version under the title Hummingbirds
  of Hollywood. [93 min\; documentary\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251108T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:New Americas Cinema Series: EVERY LITTLE THING
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/new-americas-cinema-series-every-little-thing/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Author and wi
 ldlife rehabber Terry Masear has an ambitious goal: to save every injured 
 hummingbird in Los Angeles. But the path to survival is fraught with dange
 r. This heart-expanding Sundance hit introduces audiences to Terry’s dimin
 utive patients through breathtaking slow-motion photography and emotional 
 storytelling. Over the course of director Sally Aitken’s moving documentar
 y\, we become deeply invested in baby hummingbirds like Cactus and Wasabi\
 , celebrating their tiny victories and lamenting their tragedies. Through 
 Terry’s eyes\, each bird becomes memorable\, mighty and heroic. Her compas
 sion and empathy serves as a reminder that grace can be found in the small
 est of acts and the tiniest of creatures. Previously shown on PBS Nature i
 n a shortened version under the title Hummingbirds of Hollywood. [93 min\;
  documentary\; English] </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
