CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Soul on Fire is based on the true story of John O’Leary\, who a
 t age nine suffered burns on 100% of his body. The movie chronicles his mi
 raculous survival and his journey of healing\, relying on family\, faith\,
  and community. It highlights his decision to live with purpose after the 
 accident.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251109T140000
LOCATION:The Historic Tivoli Theatre\, 24 North Washington St.\, Spencer
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:‘Soul on Fire’ (open caption)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/soul-on-fire-open-caption/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Soul on Fire 
 is based on the true story of John O’Leary\, who at age nine suffered burn
 s on 100% of his body. The movie chronicles his miraculous survival and hi
 s journey of healing\, relying on family\, faith\, and community. It highl
 ights his decision to live with purpose after the accident.</p>\n</BODY></
 HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-140587@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:This live storytelling event features a series of true stories 
 about the experiences of immigrants\, refugees\, and asylum seekers. From 
 choosing to pursue your dreams in a new country\, to fleeing violence in a
  home you never thought you’d leave\, the stories in this production showc
 ase the diverse experiences of Bloomington’s immigrant community. Join us 
 for this celebration of tenacity\, resilience\, and joy.\nEste evento de n
 arración en vivo presenta una serie de historias reales sobre las experien
 cias de inmigrantes\, refugiados y solicitantes de asilo. Desde la decisió
 n de perseguir tus sueños en un nuevo país hasta huir de la violencia en u
 n hogar que nunca pensaste que dejarías\, las historias de esta producción
  muestran las diversas experiencias de la comunidad inmigrante de Blooming
 ton. Acompáñanos en esta celebración de la tenacidad\, la resiliencia y la
  alegría.\nSpanish show free with advance sign-up via El Centro Comunal La
 tino. Call 812-355-7513 or email elcentrocomunal@gmail.com.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251109T140000
LOCATION:Constellation Playhouse\,107 W 9th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Off Night Stories: Immigrants\, Refugees\, and Asylum Seekers prese
 nted by Off Night Productions (English-language Show at 2:00\; Spanish-lan
 guage show at 7:00)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/off-night-stories-immigrants-refugees-and-asylum
 -seekers-english-show/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p dir='ltr'>Thi
 s live storytelling event features a series of true stories about the expe
 riences of immigrants\, refugees\, and asylum seekers. From choosing to pu
 rsue your dreams in a new country\, to fleeing violence in a home you neve
 r thought you’d leave\, the stories in this production showcase the divers
 e experiences of Bloomington’s immigrant community. Join us for this celeb
 ration of tenacity\, resilience\, and joy.</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>Este evento d
 e narración en vivo presenta una serie de historias reales sobre las exper
 iencias de inmigrantes\, refugiados y solicitantes de asilo. Desde la deci
 sión de perseguir tus sueños en un nuevo país hasta huir de la violencia e
 n un hogar que nunca pensaste que dejarías\, las historias de esta producc
 ión muestran las diversas experiencias de la comunidad inmigrante de Bloom
 ington. Acompáñanos en esta celebración de la tenacidad\, la resiliencia y
  la alegría.</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>Spanish show free with advance sign-up via 
 El Centro Comunal Latino. Call 812-355-7513 or email <a href='mailto:elcen
 trocomunal@gmail.com' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>elcentrocomunal@gmail
 .com</a>.</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
