BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142594@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A virtual Q&A with Chad Beguelin\, co-writer and lyricist of th
 e Broadway version of The Prom\, and Spencer Pride President Jonathan Bala
 sh will follow the screening.\nWhen an Indiana high school student is deni
 ed bringing her girlfriend to prom\, her story grabs the attention of self
 -centered Broadway stars (Meryl Streep\, Nicole Kidman\, and James Corden)
  looking for a cause. This star-studded musical comedy\, based on the Tony
 -nominated Broadway hit\, follows their hilarious and heartwarming attempt
 s to advocate for inclusivity in a small\, conservative town\, ultimately 
 uniting a community in celebration of love and acceptance. [130 min\; musi
 cal\, comedy\, drama\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251111T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Queer in the Heartland Film Series: THE PROM
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/queer-in-the-heartland-film-series-the-prom/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong> A vi
 rtual Q&A with Chad Beguelin\, co-writer and lyricist of the Broadway vers
 ion of The Prom\, and Spencer Pride President Jonathan Balash will follow 
 the screening.</strong><br />\nWhen an Indiana high school student is deni
 ed bringing her girlfriend to prom\, her story grabs the attention of self
 -centered Broadway stars (Meryl Streep\, Nicole Kidman\, and James Corden)
  looking for a cause. This star-studded musical comedy\, based on the Tony
 -nominated Broadway hit\, follows their hilarious and heartwarming attempt
 s to advocate for inclusivity in a small\, conservative town\, ultimately 
 uniting a community in celebration of love and acceptance. [130 min\; musi
 cal\, comedy\, drama\; English] </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
