BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142033@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Indiana University Athletics Sports Mem
 orabilia Collection\, University Collections at McCalla is proud to presen
 t its newest exhibit\, Outfitting IU\nAthletics: Hoosier Champions. This s
 howcase highlights individual and team champions throughout IU’s rich athl
 etics heritage. Featuring uniforms\, gear\, and trophies\, Outfitting IU A
 thletics traces IU’s athletic accomplishments from the founding of the fir
 st sport at IU (baseball)\, through 2025 individual national champions in 
 women’s and men’s swimming and diving. Objects in the exhibit include the 
 1938 men’s cross country national championship trophy\, Lilly King’s signe
 d Olympic swimming cap\, Kyle Schwarber’s 2013 College World Series bat\, 
 basketball objects\,\nand tennis shoes worn by Heather Crowe during her ru
 n to an individual and team national championship in women’s tennis in 198
 2.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251114T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251114T180000
LOCATION:University Collections at McCalla\, 525 E 9th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Outfitting IU Athletics: Hoosier Champions
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/outfitting-iu-athletics-hoosier-champions/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>In partnershi
 p with the Indiana University Athletics Sports Memorabilia Collection\, Un
 iversity Collections at McCalla is proud to present its newest exhibit\, O
 utfitting IU<br />\nAthletics: Hoosier Champions. This showcase highlights
  individual and team champions throughout IU’s rich athletics heritage. Fe
 aturing uniforms\, gear\, and trophies\, Outfitting IU Athletics traces IU
 ’s athletic accomplishments from the founding of the first sport at IU (ba
 seball)\, through 2025 individual national champions in women’s and men’s 
 swimming and diving. Objects in the exhibit include the 1938 men’s cross c
 ountry national championship trophy\, Lilly King’s signed Olympic swimming
  cap\, Kyle Schwarber’s 2013 College World Series bat\, basketball objects
 \,<br />\nand tennis shoes worn by Heather Crowe during her run to an indi
 vidual and team national championship in women’s tennis in 1982.</p>\n</BO
 DY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
