CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Step back in time this weekend! Join the Monroe County History 
 Center for a free walking tour of Bloomington’s beloved Near West Side nei
 ghborhood on Saturday\, November 15 at 1 p.m. The program begins at City o
 f Bloomington\, IN – Banneker Community Center with a presentation on the 
 history of the “Bucktown” district before heading out for the tour. All ar
 e welcome—come learn more about the stories\, landmarks\, and people who s
 haped this vibrant part of Bloomington.\nRSVP at education@monroehistory.o
 rg.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251115T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251115T150000
LOCATION:Banneker Community Center Gymnasium\, 930 West 7th Street\, Bloomi
 ngton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Near West Side Historical Walking Tour
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/near-west-side-historical-walking-tour/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Step back in 
 time this weekend! Join the Monroe County History Center for a free walkin
 g tour of Bloomington’s beloved Near West Side neighborhood on Saturday\, 
 November 15 at 1 p.m. The program begins at City of Bloomington\, IN – Ban
 neker Community Center with a presentation on the history of the “Bucktown
 ” district before heading out for the tour. All are welcome—come learn mor
 e about the stories\, landmarks\, and people who shaped this vibrant part 
 of Bloomington.<br />\n<strong>RSVP at education@monroehistory.org.</stron
 g></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142065@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Freedoms under Assault is a powerful full-length documentary th
 at chronicles the systematic destruction of a world-class university and t
 he politically motivated culture war against its faculty over a two-year p
 eriod. A perfect storm of an autocratic university president collaborating
  with a supermajority reactionary state legislature following the ideologi
 cal agenda of the White House has effectively curtailed the institutional 
 autonomy of Indiana University as well as shared governance structures\, a
 cademic freedom\, free speech and assembly rights\, tenure\, and the viabi
 lity of arts and humanities programs.\nThe documentary shows the lengths t
 o which a university administration is willing to silence\, intimidate\, p
 ersecute\, and even exile faculty members in accord with arbitrary policie
 s and “financial exigencies.” The film is co-directed/produced by Robert A
 rnove\, IU Chancellor’s Professor Emeritus of Education\, and award-winnin
 g documentarian\, Jacky Comforty.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251115T140000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Freedoms Under Assault presented by The Learning Project
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/freedoms-under-assault-presented-by-the-learning
 -project/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><span style='
 font-size: small'><em><strong>Freedoms under Assault</strong></em><strong>
  </strong>is a powerful full-length documentary that chronicles the system
 atic destruction of a world-class university and the politically motivated
  culture war against its faculty over a two-year period. A perfect storm o
 f an autocratic university president collaborating with a supermajority re
 actionary state legislature following the ideological agenda of the White 
 House has effectively curtailed the institutional autonomy of Indiana Univ
 ersity as well as shared governance structures\, academic freedom\, free s
 peech and assembly rights\, tenure\, and the viability of arts and humanit
 ies programs.</span></p>\n<p><span style='font-size: small'>The documentar
 y shows the lengths to which a university administration is willing to sil
 ence\, intimidate\, persecute\, and even exile faculty members in accord w
 ith arbitrary policies and “financial exigencies.” The film is co-directed
 /produced by Robert Arnove\, IU Chancellor’s Professor Emeritus of Educati
 on\, and award-winning documentarian\, Jacky Comforty.</span></p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
