BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142333@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION: In a world where geographical boundaries increasingly blur\, t
 he concept of Pangaea—a supercontinent that once connected disparate lands
 —serves as a fitting metaphor for the music of Pangaea Sky.\nThrough perfo
 rmances of highly arranged traditional tunes\, coupled with original compo
 sitions that draw from both folkloric & modern sources\, the quartet explo
 res the traditional and contemporary global music scene and emphasizes how
  global influences and technology are shaping soundscapes and influencing 
 music. Pangaea Sky draws from a global palette\, creating hybrid genres th
 at reflect a more interconnected world.\nTom Clark: saxophones\, flutes\, 
 keys\, electronics\nPeter Kienle (KEEN-lee): guitars\, guitar synth\nJulia
 n Douglas: percussion\nRon Kadish (KAY-dish): bass\, electronics
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251118T190000
LOCATION:The Lotus Firebay\, 105 S. Rogers Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Pangaea Sky
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/pangaea-sky/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='gmai
 l_default'> In a world where geographical boundaries increasingly blur\, t
 he concept of Pangaea—a supercontinent that once connected disparate lands
 —serves as a fitting metaphor for the music of Pangaea Sky.</p>\n<p>Throug
 h performances of highly arranged traditional tunes\, coupled with origina
 l compositions that draw from both folkloric & modern sources\, the quarte
 t explores the traditional and contemporary global music scene and emphasi
 zes how global influences and technology are shaping soundscapes and influ
 encing music. Pangaea Sky draws from a global palette\, creating hybrid ge
 nres that reflect a more interconnected world.</p>\n<p>Tom Clark: saxophon
 es\, flutes\, keys\, electronics<br />\nPeter Kienle (KEEN-lee): guitars\,
  guitar synth<br />\nJulian Douglas: percussion<br />\nRon Kadish (KAY-dis
 h): bass\, electronics</p></div>\n<div class='gmail_default'></div>\n</BOD
 Y></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
