BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143244@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Though she may not exactly be putting brush to canvas\, Delaney
  Bailey imprints heavy feelings of heartbreak\, betrayal\, isolation\, and
  uncertainty onto her music with alternately ethereal and expressive vocal
 s. Her dynamic voice feels right at home layered into the fabric of otherw
 orldly beat-craft\, expansive sonic vistas\, and living and breathing soun
 dscapes.\nAmassing hundreds of millions of streams and earning critical ac
 claim\, she paints a portrait of who she is.\nGrowing up in Indiana\, Dela
 ney uncovered her passion for music early on. Given that she was named aft
 er Jimmy Buffet’s daughter\, it’s perhaps no surprise. She went from liste
 ning to Norah Jones and Adele to My Chemical Romance\, Pierce The Veil\, N
 ick Drake\, Lorde\, and Grizzly Bear. Simultaneously\, she honed her voice
  by singing in theater and choir throughout high school. With seven siblin
 gs\, she had an unpredictable and interesting childhood\, to say the least
 . As such\, she developed keen empathy and a heightened sense of understan
 ding.\n“Since I grew up around so many different individuals\, it became a
 n important skill to learn why others were feeling the way they were and\,
  in turn\, why I was feeling how I was\,” she goes on. “I knew what mood e
 verybody would be in based on what was going and how to navigate it. I’ve 
 always had an ability to look internally\, and I don’t take it for granted
 . Maybe it contributed to me growing up a little too fast\, but it makes f
 or good songwriting.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251202T200000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 South Walnut St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Delaney Bailey\, with This House is Creaking (18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/delaney-bailey-with-this-house-is-creaking-18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Though she ma
 y not exactly be putting brush to canvas\, Delaney Bailey imprints heavy f
 eelings of heartbreak\, betrayal\, isolation\, and uncertainty onto her mu
 sic with alternately ethereal and expressive vocals. Her dynamic voice fee
 ls right at home layered into the fabric of otherworldly beat-craft\, expa
 nsive sonic vistas\, and living and breathing soundscapes.</p>\n<p>Amassin
 g hundreds of millions of streams and earning critical acclaim\, she paint
 s a portrait of who she is.</p>\n<p>Growing up in Indiana\, Delaney uncove
 red her passion for music early on. Given that she was named after Jimmy B
 uffet’s daughter\, it’s perhaps no surprise. She went from listening to No
 rah Jones and Adele to My Chemical Romance\, Pierce The Veil\, Nick Drake\
 , Lorde\, and Grizzly Bear. Simultaneously\, she honed her voice by singin
 g in theater and choir throughout high school. With seven siblings\, she h
 ad an unpredictable and interesting childhood\, to say the least. As such\
 , she developed keen empathy and a heightened sense of understanding.</p>
 \n<p>“Since I grew up around so many different individuals\, it became an 
 important skill to learn why others were feeling the way they were and\, i
 n turn\, why I was feeling how I was\,” she goes on. “I knew what mood eve
 rybody would be in based on what was going and how to navigate it. I’ve al
 ways had an ability to look internally\, and I don’t take it for granted. 
 Maybe it contributed to me growing up a little too fast\, but it makes for
  good songwriting.”</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
