BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143245@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Mini Trees is the solo project of LA-based songwriter Lexi Vega
 \, whose intimate blend of indie and alt pop explores the tension between 
 self-doubt and persistence. Her recent singles unravel cycles of disappoin
 tment and growth\, emotional loops that echo in both personal relationship
 s and her journey through the music industry.\nOn “Spinning\,” Vega captur
 es the quiet dread of chasing something uncertain\, singing\,“still gettin
 g older while I’m going nowhere”\, a line that distills the fear of runnin
 g out of time without anything to show for it. “Close” flips the lens outw
 ard\, turning frustration into clarity as she confronts an industry that r
 epeatedly says\, “you almost would’ve made it. ” And on “Hollow\,” she ref
 lects on being the one who pulls away\, tracing the aftermath of emotional
  unavailability with unflinching honesty.\nNow working toward her first in
 dependently released full-length album\, Mini Trees continues to carve out
  space on her own terms\, creating music that lives in the in-between\, wh
 ere doubt and devotion quietly coexist.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251204T210000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 South Walnut St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mini Trees with Just Penelope and Kay Krull (18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mini-trees-with-just-penelope-and-kay-krull-18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Mini Trees is
  the solo project of LA-based songwriter Lexi Vega\, whose intimate blend 
 of indie and alt pop explores the tension between self-doubt and persisten
 ce. Her recent singles unravel cycles of disappointment and growth\, emoti
 onal loops that echo in both personal relationships and her journey throug
 h the music industry.</p>\n<p>On “Spinning\,” Vega captures the quiet drea
 d of chasing something uncertain\, singing\,“still getting older while I’m
  going nowhere”\, a line that distills the fear of running out of time wit
 hout anything to show for it. “Close” flips the lens outward\, turning fru
 stration into clarity as she confronts an industry that repeatedly says\, 
 “you almost would’ve made it. ” And on “Hollow\,” she reflects on being th
 e one who pulls away\, tracing the aftermath of emotional unavailability w
 ith unflinching honesty.</p>\n<p>Now working toward her first independentl
 y released full-length album\, Mini Trees continues to carve out space on 
 her own terms\, creating music that lives in the in-between\, where doubt 
 and devotion quietly coexist.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
