BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143547@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Before Western science accepted the existence of meteorites\, m
 any cultures formed their own beliefs about them. Encounters with the cele
 stial rocks have long inspired fear and reverence. Photographer Emilia Mar
 tin is fascinated by the stones\, but also by the people who study and ado
 re them. With whimsy and extensive research\, Martin presents a series of 
 photographs that playfully investigate the old stories and the collective 
 memory surrounding meteorites.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251205T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251205T200000
LOCATION:Pictura Gallery\, 202 South Rogers St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:December Gallery Walk: Emilia Martin  “I saw a tree bearing stones 
 in the place of apples and pears”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/december-gallery-walk-emilia-martin-i-saw-a-tree
 -bearing-stones-in-the-place-of-apples-and-pears/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Before Wester
 n science accepted the existence of meteorites\, many cultures formed thei
 r own beliefs about them. Encounters with the celestial rocks have long in
 spired fear and reverence. Photographer Emilia Martin is fascinated by the
  stones\, but also by the people who study and adore them. With whimsy and
  extensive research\, Martin presents a series of photographs that playful
 ly investigate the old stories and the collective memory surrounding meteo
 rites.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
