BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-126643@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:https://www.bloomingtonwinterfarmersmarket.com/winter-farmers-marke
 t-1
DESCRIPTION:Come for a celebration of harvest\, local food\, crafts\, and c
 ommunity. We can’t wait to see everyone there!\nThe BWFM is the oldest win
 ter market in Indiana as it enters its 20th year serving the community of 
 Bloomington.\nThe Bloomington Winter Farmers’ Market has a diversity of ve
 ndors and products including fresh produce\, local meat and poultry\, dair
 y products\, eggs\, maple syrup\, honey products\, breads\, baked goods\, 
 jams and sauces\, prepared foods\, locally roasted coffee\, cut flowers\, 
 seeds and plants\, artisanal crafts and many other items. You can find eve
 rything you need for nourishing winter meals along with local crafts\, sea
 sonal gifts and shareable treats!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251206T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251206T123000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park pavilion\, 1601 S. Rogers St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Winter Farmers’ Market with entertainment from Taylor W
 oodward (9-10:30am) and Ditch Tea Steepers (11am-12:30pm)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-winter-farmers-market-2025-2026/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Come for a ce
 lebration of harvest\, local food\, crafts\, and community. We can’t wait 
 to see everyone there!<br />\nThe BWFM is the oldest winter market in Indi
 ana as it enters its 20th year serving the community of Bloomington.</p>\n
 <p>The Bloomington Winter Farmers’ Market has a diversity of vendors and p
 roducts including fresh produce\, local meat and poultry\, dairy products\
 , eggs\, maple syrup\, honey products\, breads\, baked goods\, jams and sa
 uces\, prepared foods\, locally roasted coffee\, cut flowers\, seeds and p
 lants\, artisanal crafts and many other items. You can find everything you
  need for nourishing winter meals along with local crafts\, seasonal gifts
  and shareable treats!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143328@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Tulip Trestle Community Restoration\, Inc\; ttcrinc@gmail.com\; Fac
 ebook.com/GreeneCountyViaductProject
DESCRIPTION:Santa Claus is coming to town for the 35th year! Climb aboard t
 he stationary\, vintage passenger car to visit with Santa and Mrs. Claus\,
  and more. Mail a letter to Santa. Treats for all and gifts for kids (whil
 e supplies last/weather permitting)\nWarm coats\, hats\, and gloves are av
 ailable to children in need this holiday season.\nWatch the Indiana Rail R
 oad Company Santa Train cross the Trestle\, 10a -11. The Indiana Rail Road
 ’s 35th annual Santa Train will visit 11 communities over three days as pa
 rt of its annual trip across the railroad\, set for Dec. 5-7\, 2025.\nTTCR
 \, Inc. is a community nonprofit dedicated to providing a welcoming space 
 for people to explore habitat & area history.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251206T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251206T120000
LOCATION:Tulip Trestle Observation Deck 2615 N. Viaduct Road\, Bloomfield\,
  IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Christmas at The Deck
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/christmas-at-the-deck/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Santa Claus i
 s coming to town for the 35th year! Climb aboard the stationary\, vintage 
 passenger car to visit with Santa and Mrs. Claus\, and more. Mail a letter
  to Santa. Treats for all and gifts for kids (while supplies last/weather 
 permitting)</p>\n<p>Warm coats\, hats\, and gloves are available to childr
 en in need this holiday season.</p>\n<p>Watch the Indiana Rail Road Compan
 y Santa Train cross the Trestle\, 10a -11. The Indiana Rail Road’s 35th an
 nual Santa Train will visit 11 communities over three days as part of its 
 annual trip across the railroad\, set for Dec. 5-7\, 2025.</p>\n<p>TTCR\, 
 Inc. is a community nonprofit dedicated to providing a welcoming space for
  people to explore habitat & area history.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
