BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143246@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A singer-songwriter known for his lyrical acumen and plaintive 
 harmonica style\, Joe Pug dropped out of college and moved to Chicago wher
 e he worked as a carpenter before breaking into the city’s music scene. Si
 nce 2008 he has released a string of critically-acclaimed albums and toure
 d heavily in the U.S. and abroad. Paste Magazine wrote of his music: “Unle
 ss your surname is Dylan\, Waits\, Ritter or Prine\, you could face-palm y
 ourself to death trying to pen songs half as inspired.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251206T200000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 South Walnut St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Joe Pug  (18+)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/joe-pug-18/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A singer-song
 writer known for his lyrical acumen and plaintive harmonica style\, Joe Pu
 g dropped out of college and moved to Chicago where he worked as a carpent
 er before breaking into the city’s music scene. Since 2008 he has released
  a string of critically-acclaimed albums and toured heavily in the U.S. an
 d abroad. Paste Magazine wrote of his music: “Unless your surname is Dylan
 \, Waits\, Ritter or Prine\, you could face-palm yourself to death trying 
 to pen songs half as inspired.”</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143266@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 8pm\nPlummer Jazz Sextet with Lenard Simpson\n++Late S
 how after the The Splattertones++\nLenard Simpson- Alto\nZoey Thornburg\, 
 trumpet\nPeter Goggin\, alto saxophone\nTakoda Collins\, tenor saxophone\n
 Alayna Ringsby\, piano\nNolan Phillips\, bass\nJackson Foerster\, drums\nL
 enard Simpson is a saxophonist\, composer and educator from Milwaukee\, Wi
 sconsin. Lenard was mostly self-taught through high school\, but his natur
 al ability and musicianship earned him accolades such as membership in the
  esteemed Grammy Camp Jazz Session\, and an outstanding soloist award at t
 he Mingus Jazz Competition in New York City. Lenard has had the opportunit
 y to play and travel with artists such as pianist and composer-Billy Child
 s\, Kurt Elling\, Marquis Hill\, and Clayton Cameron. Lenard received a B.
 M in Jazz performance at Northern Illinois University. While studying at N
 IU\, Lenard was awarded first place in Chicago’s esteemed Luminarts Jazz C
 ompetition.\nUpon graduation\, Lenard moved to Chicago and soon became one
  of the city’s top call saxophonists playing sideman to legendary local dr
 ummers\, George Fludas and Charles Heath. Lenard’s trio has appeared at pr
 emier clubs and jazz festivals throughout the Chicago and Milwaukee area. 
 Lenard recently graduated from the Thelonious Monk Institute Fellowship\, 
 which has since been renamed to the Herbie Hancock Institut where he was s
 elected by a panel of Wayne Shorter\, Herbie Hancock\, James Newton and Am
 brose Akinmusire.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251206T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251206T220000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Lenard Simpson with the Plummer Jazz Sextet
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/lenard-simpson-with-the-plummer-jazz-sextet/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 8pm</strong><br />\nPlummer Jazz Sextet with Lenard Simpson<br />\n++L
 ate Show after the The Splattertones++<br />\nLenard Simpson- Alto<br />\n
 Zoey Thornburg\, trumpet<br />\nPeter Goggin\, alto saxophone<br />\nTakod
 a Collins\, tenor saxophone<br />\nAlayna Ringsby\, piano<br />\nNolan Phi
 llips\, bass<br />\nJackson Foerster\, drums<br />\nLenard Simpson is a sa
 xophonist\, composer and educator from Milwaukee\, Wisconsin. Lenard was m
 ostly self-taught through high school\, but his natural ability and musici
 anship earned him accolades such as membership in the esteemed Grammy Camp
  Jazz Session\, and an outstanding soloist award at the Mingus Jazz Compet
 ition in New York City. Lenard has had the opportunity to play and travel 
 with artists such as pianist and composer-Billy Childs\, Kurt Elling\, Mar
 quis Hill\, and Clayton Cameron. Lenard received a B.M in Jazz performance
  at Northern Illinois University. While studying at NIU\, Lenard was award
 ed first place in Chicago’s esteemed Luminarts Jazz Competition.<br />\nUp
 on graduation\, Lenard moved to Chicago and soon became one of the city’s 
 top call saxophonists playing sideman to legendary local drummers\, George
  Fludas and Charles Heath. Lenard’s trio has appeared at premier clubs and
  jazz festivals throughout the Chicago and Milwaukee area. Lenard recently
  graduated from the Thelonious Monk Institute Fellowship\, which has since
  been renamed to the Herbie Hancock Institut where he was selected by a pa
 nel of Wayne Shorter\, Herbie Hancock\, James Newton and Ambrose Akinmusir
 e.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
