BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143799@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Faculty Dance: Body to Body\, an investigation into the power o
 f dance passed through humanity\, body to body. Dancers learning from thei
 r elders are the lineage holders and carriers of embodied wisdom and unmed
 iated somatic knowledge. Featuring guest artists Maxine Montilus\, Afro-Ha
 itian contemporary dance maker based in NYC\, and Ishmael Konney\, Ghanaia
 n Folklore and contemporary dance maker at the University of Wisconsin-Mil
 waukee. Both guests will collaborate with composers to create original sco
 res for their dances. Also featuring new dances by department dance facult
 y and performed by IU Contemporary Dance Theatre members\, the BFA dance m
 ajors.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251213T140000
LOCATION:Ruth N. Halls Theatre\, 275 N. Eagleson Ave.\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20251213T140000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Body To Body Faculty Winter Dance Concert (performances at 2pm & 7:
 30pm)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/body-to-body-faculty-winter-dance-concert-perfor
 mances-at-2pm-730pm/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Faculty Dance
 : Body to Body\, an investigation into the power of dance passed through h
 umanity\, body to body. Dancers learning from their elders are the lineage
  holders and carriers of embodied wisdom and unmediated somatic knowledge.
  Featuring guest artists Maxine Montilus\, Afro-Haitian contemporary dance
  maker based in NYC\, and Ishmael Konney\, Ghanaian Folklore and contempor
 ary dance maker at the University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee. Both guests will
  collaborate with composers to create original scores for their dances. Al
 so featuring new dances by department dance faculty and performed by IU Co
 ntemporary Dance Theatre members\, the BFA dance majors.</p>\n</BODY></HTM
 L>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-142906@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Jacobs faculty choreographer Sasha Janes shatters stereotypes i
 n his reimagined version of this classic ballet\, telling the story from t
 he perspective of curious young Marie.\nWith assistance from her Aunt Dros
 selmeier\, Marie learns to unlock the power of her creativity to take the 
 audience with her on an incredible adventure.\nThis contemporary take on a
  fantastical story still features the iconic score by Peter Ilyich Tchaiko
 vsky—and leaves audiences wondering where reality stops\, and imagination 
 begins.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251213T140000
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 101 North Eagleson Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Nutcracker by Peter Ilyich Tchaikovsky\, performances at 2:00 a
 nd 7:30
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-nutcracker-by-peter-ilyich-tchaikovsky-4/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Jacobs facult
 y choreographer Sasha Janes shatters stereotypes in his reimagined version
  of this classic ballet\, telling the story from the perspective of curiou
 s young Marie.<br />\nWith assistance from her Aunt Drosselmeier\, Marie l
 earns to unlock the power of her creativity to take the audience with her 
 on an incredible adventure.<br />\nThis contemporary take on a fantastical
  story still features the iconic score by Peter Ilyich Tchaikovsky—and lea
 ves audiences wondering where reality stops\, and imagination begins.</p>
 \n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
