BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-143922@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Oscar-nominated writer-director Rian Johnson and Daniel Craig a
 re back\, bringing their version of Hercule Poirot to the screen for the t
 hird time with Craig’s Benoit Blanc in Wake Up Dead Man. Taking inspiratio
 n from Edgar Allan Poe and the classic locked-room mysteries of Sherlock H
 olmes\, this installment of the enormously entertaining series finds Blanc
  in a small\, upstate New York town\, embroiled in an impossible murder fo
 cused around the town’s local church and its small but devoted congregatio
 n. Led by Craig and Josh O’Connor\, the stellar ensemble cast includes Jos
 h Brolin\, Glenn Close\, Kerry Washington\, Andrew Scott\, Cailee Spaeny\,
  Jeremy Renner\, Mila Kunis\, and Thomas Haden Church. [144 min\; comedy\,
  mystery\; English]\nThis screening will be followed by a Q&A with Nathan 
 Johnson\, the film’s composer. Johnson is an award-winning composer whose 
 work has been featured in films like Brick\, Nightmare Alley\, Looper\, Th
 e Brothers Bloom\, and Knives Out\, among others.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251219T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:New Americas Cinema Series: Wake Up Dead Man: A Knives Out Mystery 
 w/composer
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/new-americas-cinema-series-wake-up-dead-man-a-kn
 ives-out-mystery-w-composer/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> Oscar-nomina
 ted writer-director Rian Johnson and Daniel Craig are back\, bringing thei
 r version of Hercule Poirot to the screen for the third time with Craig’s 
 Benoit Blanc in Wake Up Dead Man. Taking inspiration from Edgar Allan Poe 
 and the classic locked-room mysteries of Sherlock Holmes\, this installmen
 t of the enormously entertaining series finds Blanc in a small\, upstate N
 ew York town\, embroiled in an impossible murder focused around the town’s
  local church and its small but devoted congregation. Led by Craig and Jos
 h O’Connor\, the stellar ensemble cast includes Josh Brolin\, Glenn Close\
 , Kerry Washington\, Andrew Scott\, Cailee Spaeny\, Jeremy Renner\, Mila K
 unis\, and Thomas Haden Church. [144 min\; comedy\, mystery\; English]</p>
 \n<p><strong>This screening will be followed by a Q&A with Nathan Johnson\
 , the film’s composer.</strong> Johnson is an award-winning composer whose
  work has been featured in films like Brick\, Nightmare Alley\, Looper\, T
 he Brothers Bloom\, and Knives Out\, among others. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
