BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144350@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:You know those adorable seashell shaped cookies? That’s a madel
 eine! Technically a tiny sponge cake\, these treats originated from Northe
 rn France in the 18th century. Soft\, buttery\, spongey and versatile\, ma
 deleines are a great dessert all year round. Calling all bakers! Today Sha
 ne O’Bannon will walk you through how he does madeleines from start to fin
 ish\, and also show you how to create a version that’s dipped in chocolate
 . \nWe encourage you to sign up for classes online. When you register onli
 ne\, you’ll also pay online. While we will accept walk-ins before class if
  capacity allows\, registering ahead of time secures your spot and creates
  a more seamless class experience.\nhttps://www.inthekitchen-bloomington.c
 om/classes
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260104T150000
LOCATION:In the Kitchen\, 115 N College Ave\, Suite 014\, Bloomington. Use 
 the Uptown Plaza alley entrance between JL Waters and Peach Cobbler Factor
 y.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Madeleines 101: The Ultimate French Cookie with Shane from Kirkwood
  Sweet Shop
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/madeleines-101-the-ultimate-french-cookie-with-s
 hane-from-kirkwood-sweet-shop/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>You know thos
 e adorable seashell shaped cookies? That’s a madeleine! Technically a tiny
  sponge cake\, these treats originated from Northern France in the 18th ce
 ntury. Soft\, buttery\, spongey and versatile\, madeleines are a great des
 sert all year round. Calling all bakers! Today Shane O’Bannon will walk yo
 u through how he does madeleines from start to finish\, and also show you 
 how to create a version that’s dipped in chocolate. </p>\n<p><strong>We en
 courage you to sign up for classes online. When you register online\, you’
 ll also pay online. While we will accept walk-ins before class if capacity
  allows\, registering ahead of time secures your spot and creates a more s
 eamless class experience.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>https://www.inthekitche
 n-bloomington.com/classes</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
