BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144441@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Cozy up\, pick up a needle\, and let’s make something. Knit Nig
 ht happens every second Friday and it’s all about stitches\, snacks\, and 
 laughs. Beginners\, pros\, or people who just want to watch yarn do its th
 ing . All welcome. Bring your project\, start a new one\, or just sit at t
 he table and soak in the cozy vibes. Tips\, tricks\, and yarn jokes includ
 ed.\nEvery week we’re offering a new craft night\, so boredom is not invit
 ed. This is your ticket to slow down\, make something with your hands\, an
 d maybe accidentally meet your new craft buddy. Quiet concentration option
 al. Giggles and “oops I dropped a stitch” moments encouraged. You might le
 ave with a scarf\, a tiny triumph\, or just the satisfaction of having mad
 e something with your own two hands and shared it with a table full of hum
 ans who get it.\nWinter is long. Knit Night is shorter than the nights fee
 l. Come warm your hands\, your brain\, and your soul.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260109T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260109T210000
LOCATION:Gather : handmade shoppe & Co\, 116 N Walnut\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260213T180000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260313T180000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Knit Night
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/knit-night/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Cozy up\, pic
 k up a needle\, and let’s make something. Knit Night happens every second 
 Friday and it’s all about stitches\, snacks\, and laughs. Beginners\, pros
 \, or people who just want to watch yarn do its thing . All welcome. Bring
  your project\, start a new one\, or just sit at the table and soak in the
  cozy vibes. Tips\, tricks\, and yarn jokes included.<br />\nEvery week we
 ’re offering a new craft night\, so boredom is not invited. This is your t
 icket to slow down\, make something with your hands\, and maybe accidental
 ly meet your new craft buddy. Quiet concentration optional. Giggles and “o
 ops I dropped a stitch” moments encouraged. You might leave with a scarf\,
  a tiny triumph\, or just the satisfaction of having made something with y
 our own two hands and shared it with a table full of humans who get it.<br
  />\nWinter is long. Knit Night is shorter than the nights feel. Come warm
  your hands\, your brain\, and your soul. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
