BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144444@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Plant 101: Getting Rooted is a cozy\, beginner-friendly introdu
 ction to plant care\, designed to help you build confidence from the groun
 d up.\nWe’ll break down the essentials — light\, water\, soil\, and enviro
 nment — using real plants\, real examples\, and zero judgment. You’ll lear
 n how to read what your plant is telling you\, what’s normal vs. what need
 s attention\, and how to choose plants that actually fit your space and li
 festyle.\nExpect a relaxed\, conversational class with hands-on demonstrat
 ions\, plenty of time for questions\, and optional guided shopping afterwa
 rd if you’d like help selecting your next plant.\nYou don’t need a green t
 humb — just curiosity and a willingness to start where you are.\nWhat you 
 get:\nA beginner-friendly plant care workshop\nHands-on demos with real pl
 ants\nGuidance on light\, watering\, soil\, and environment\nHelp choosing
  plants that fit your space and lifestyle\nTime for Q&A and personalized a
 dvice\nOne drink included from Café Thistle\n20% off any plants purchased 
 during the workshop\nLeave feeling calmer\, more grounded\, and confident 
 caring for your plants.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260111T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260111T133000
LOCATION:oak.Bloomington\, 116 W 6th St. Suite 101\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Houseplant 101 – Getting Rooted
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/houseplant-101-getting-rooted/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Plant 101: Ge
 tting Rooted is a cozy\, beginner-friendly introduction to plant care\, de
 signed to help you build confidence from the ground up.<br />\nWe’ll break
  down the essentials — light\, water\, soil\, and environment — using real
  plants\, real examples\, and zero judgment. You’ll learn how to read what
  your plant is telling you\, what’s normal vs. what needs attention\, and 
 how to choose plants that actually fit your space and lifestyle.<br />\nEx
 pect a relaxed\, conversational class with hands-on demonstrations\, plent
 y of time for questions\, and optional guided shopping afterward if you’d 
 like help selecting your next plant.<br />\nYou don’t need a green thumb —
  just curiosity and a willingness to start where you are.<br />\n<strong>W
 hat you get:</strong><br />\nA beginner-friendly plant care workshop<br />
 \nHands-on demos with real plants<br />\nGuidance on light\, watering\, so
 il\, and environment<br />\nHelp choosing plants that fit your space and l
 ifestyle<br />\nTime for Q&A and personalized advice<br />\nOne drink incl
 uded from Café Thistle<br />\n20% off any plants purchased during the work
 shop<br />\nLeave feeling calmer\, more grounded\, and confident caring fo
 r your plants.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
