BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144438@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Juniper Art Gallery is excited to kick off our New Year with Th
 e Monon Troubadours for January’s Third Thursday Monthly Music Night! (6-7
 :30pm)! We will reopen that morning after our Winter Break at 11:00am and 
 have a celebratory day and evening as we look towards Juniper’s 2026 creat
 ive offerings!\nThe Monon Troubadours explore timeless themes with guitar 
 grooves and vocal harmonies. Shaun McDermott and Jim Stowers have been pla
 ying and writing songs together for more than 15 years. They’ll be joined 
 by drummer Pat Petro. Don’t miss this super fun evening of original music 
 and art! Please join us!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260115T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260115T193000
LOCATION:Juniper Art Gallery\, 615 West Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Monthly Music Night: The Monon Troubadours
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/monthly-music-night-the-monon-troubadours-2/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Juniper Art G
 allery is excited to kick off our New Year with The Monon Troubadours for 
 January’s Third Thursday Monthly Music Night! (6-7:30pm)! We will reopen t
 hat morning after our Winter Break at 11:00am and have a celebratory day a
 nd evening as we look towards Juniper’s 2026 creative offerings!<br />\nTh
 e Monon Troubadours explore timeless themes with guitar grooves and vocal 
 harmonies. Shaun McDermott and Jim Stowers have been playing and writing s
 ongs together for more than 15 years. They’ll be joined by drummer Pat Pet
 ro. Don’t miss this super fun evening of original music and art! Please jo
 in us! </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144871@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Presented By: Pam Hurst Designs & Studio PH.D  (317) 459-3581\n
 pamalahurst@yahoo.com Contact to ask about the cost.\nStudio PH.D is a ser
 ies of jewelry classes offered by artist Pam Hurst at The Sterling Butterf
 ly in downtown Martinsville. Some classes may have prerequisites. \nJanuar
 y will kick off Charm School – a monthly Charm Making Session! Each month 
 will feature a different type of charm\, and if you attend at least four s
 essions\, you will be able to make a charm holder pendant (this will be a 
 separate session you can attend for free!). If you attend eight sessions\,
  you can create a charm bracelet (also a separate session.) Participants i
 n each charm school session will create a specific type of charm. \nThis s
 ession has no prerequisites and no experience is necessary. All materials\
 , necessary tools and instruction is included in the class fee. Class size
  is limited. Please bring reading glasses or your preferred magnification 
 device.\nCharm School classes in January will be at 6 pm on Jan. 15 and Ja
 n. 20 and at Noon on Jan. 22\, and will last approximately 2 hours.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260115T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260115T200000
LOCATION:The Sterling Butterfly\, 96 E. Morgan Street\, Martinsville
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260120T180000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Studio PH.D Class: Charm School
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/studio-ph-d-class-charm-school/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Presented By:
  Pam Hurst Designs & Studio PH.D  (317) 459-3581<br />\npamalahurst@yahoo.
 com <strong>Contact to ask about the cost.</strong></p>\n<p>Studio PH.D is
  a series of jewelry classes offered by artist Pam Hurst at The Sterling B
 utterfly in downtown Martinsville. Some classes may have prerequisites. </
 p>\n<p>January will kick off Charm School – a monthly Charm Making Session
 ! Each month will feature a different type of charm\, and if you attend at
  least four sessions\, you will be able to make a charm holder pendant (th
 is will be a separate session you can attend for free!). If you attend eig
 ht sessions\, you can create a charm bracelet (also a separate session.) P
 articipants in each charm school session will create a specific type of ch
 arm. </p>\n<p>This session has no prerequisites and no experience is neces
 sary. All materials\, necessary tools and instruction is included in the c
 lass fee. Class size is limited. Please bring reading glasses or your pref
 erred magnification device.</p>\n<p><strong>Charm School classes in Januar
 y will be at 6 pm on Jan. 15 and Jan. 20 and at Noon on Jan. 22\, and will
  last approximately 2 hours.</strong> </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
