BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144840@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Cold temperatures are very important for some of our native pla
 nt species. They need something called “cold stratification” to root and b
 loom in the spring. Join us to make native seed paper you can plant now (o
 r give to a friend!) to prep for spring and summer flowers.\nWebsite:  htt
 ps://events.iu.edu/libraries/all/tags/Crafternoons
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260117T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260117T140000
LOCATION:Wylie House Museum\, Morton C. Bradley Jr. Education Center\, 317 
 E 2nd Street\, Bloomington.
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260124T110000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260131T110000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Saturday Crafternoon at the Wylie House Museum
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/saturday-crafternoon-at-the-wylie-house-museum/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Cold temperat
 ures are very important for some of our native plant species. They need so
 mething called “cold stratification” to root and bloom in the spring. Join
  us to make native seed paper you can plant now (or give to a friend!) to 
 prep for spring and summer flowers.</p>\n<p>Website: <a href='https://even
 ts.iu.edu/libraries/all/tags/Crafternoons' data-saferedirecturl='https://w
 ww.google.com/url?q=https://events.iu.edu/libraries/all/tags/Crafternoons&
 source=gmail&ust=1768417383436000&usg=AOvVaw3G4HhOgj1OOk5tP-T57Hvy'> https
 ://events.iu.edu/libraries/all/tags/Crafternoons</a></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144888@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:3+ miles\, rating: very rugged\, 3 hours long\nJoin us to see t
 he 3rd lake in Brown County State Park – the one that was started but neve
 r finished by the name of Taylor Hollow Lake. This hike is about 3.5 miles
  long and is very rugged\, with a fairly steep climb with ruts and several
  creek crossings! This hike will take us about 3 hours to complete and is 
 worth every minute! Come see this amazing site complete with spillway\, da
 m\, and almost totally complete lake structure which has been reclaimed by
  the forest! This hike is what started this Winter Hike Series and is a fa
 n favorite. Please make sure to dress for the weather. Muck style boots or
  rain boots will be very helpful to cross the creeks.  Meet at the Nature 
 Center\; then we’ll carpool to the destination.\nPlease note this hike is 
 longer than usual due to a road closure.\nPlease do not bring pets on off 
 trail hikes.\nhttps://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260117T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260117T140000
LOCATION:Nature Center\, Brown County State Park\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvil
 le
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Winter Hike Series: The Lake That Never Was
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/winter-hike-series-the-lake-that-never-was/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>3+ mi
 les\, rating: very rugged\, 3 hours long</strong></p>\n<p>Join us to see t
 he 3rd lake in Brown County State Park – the one that was started but neve
 r finished by the name of Taylor Hollow Lake. <strong>This hike is about 3
 .5 miles long and is very rugged\, with a fairly steep climb with ruts and
  several creek crossings! This hike will take us about 3 hours to complete
  and is worth every minute!</strong> Come see this amazing site complete w
 ith spillway\, dam\, and almost totally complete lake structure which has 
 been reclaimed by the forest! This hike is what started this Winter Hike S
 eries and is a fan favorite. Please make sure to dress for the weather. Mu
 ck style boots or rain boots will be very helpful to cross the creeks.  Me
 et at the Nature Center\; then we’ll carpool to the destination.</p>\n<p>P
 lease note this hike is longer than usual due to a road closure.</p>\n<p>P
 lease do not bring pets on off trail hikes.<br />\nhttps://on.in.gov/Brown
 CountySP</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
