UID:ai1ec-143731@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:You’re invited to join the City of Bloomington for the 2026 Dr.
  Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday Celebration event. This year’s theme Soul
 \, Spirit\, and Sacrifice: Honoring the Legacy of Coretta Scott King and t
 he Women Who Faced America to Save U.S.\, will feature community leaders\,
  a performance by world-renowned mezzo-soprano Marietta Simpson\, and an i
 nspiring keynote speech from Dr. Traci Parker.\n \nThis event will also in
 clude the presentation of the 2026 Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Legacy Award
 . The award recognizes individuals\, businesses\, or organizations whose w
 ork reflects the values exemplified by Dr. King. \nDoors at 5:30.\nEvent L
 ink: bton.in/MLK26 \nContact: Aubrey Seader (MLK Commission Liaison)\, mlk
 @bloomington.in.gov\, 812-349-3433
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260119T180000
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday Celebration Event
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/dr-martin-luther-king-jr-birthday-celebration-ev
 ent/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div><span style
 ='color: #000000'><span style='font-family: arial\, sans-serif'>You’re inv
 ited to join the City of Bloomington for the 2026 Dr. Martin Luther King J
 r. Birthday Celebration event. This year’s theme Soul\, Spirit\, and Sacri
 fice: Honoring the Legacy of Coretta Scott King and the Women Who Faced Am
 erica to Save U.S.\, will feature community leaders\, a performance by wor
 ld-renowned mezzo-soprano Marietta Simpson\, and an inspiring keynote spee
 ch from Dr. Traci Parker.</span></span></div>\n<div><span style='color: #0
 00000\;font-family: arial\, sans-serif'> </span></div>\n<div><span style='
 color: #000000'>This event will also include the presentation of the 2026 
 Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Legacy Award. The award recognizes individuals\
 , businesses\, or organizations whose work reflects the values exemplified
  by Dr. King. </span></div>\n<p>Doors at 5:30.</p>\n<div><span style='colo
 r: #000000'><b>Event Link: </b><a href='http://bton.in/MLK26' target='_bla
 nk' rel='noopener' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?q=http
 ://bton.in/MLK26&source=gmail&ust=1765392646439000&usg=AOvVaw2lPDWz9szfiNy
 vbFcY6RoF'>bton.in/MLK26</a> </span></div>\n<div><span style='color: #0000
 00'><b>Contact:</b> Aubrey Seader (MLK Commission Liaison)\, <a href='mail
 to:mlk@bloomington.in.gov' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>mlk@bloomington.
 in.gov</a>\, 812-349-3433</span></div>\n<div></div>\n</BODY></HTML>
