BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-145240@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Kon Ichikawa’s Tokyo Olympiad paints a stunning picture of emot
 ion and spectacle in capturing the 1964 Olympic Games\, held in Tokyo. A f
 eat of cutting-edge technology and cinematography\, the film engages with 
 the drama already inherent to sport\, offering a vision of triumph and gri
 ef—in short\, what makes the Games human—instead of results. Ichikawa’s in
 sistence on the human\, the poetic\, and the aesthetic makes this a landma
 rk film in documentary filmmaking. [169 min\; documentary\; Japanese with 
 English subtitles]\nA Q&A with Dr. Hannah Airriess (IU Department of East 
 Asian Languages and Cultures) and Dr. Brandon Wallace (IU Media School) wi
 ll follow the screening.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260127T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Tokyo Olympiad w/Q&A | Cinematic Sports Documentary: History\, Poli
 tics\, Aesthetics
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/tokyo-olympiad-w-qa-cinematic-sports-documentary
 -history-politics-aesthetics/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Kon Ichikawa’
 s Tokyo Olympiad paints a stunning picture of emotion and spectacle in cap
 turing the 1964 Olympic Games\, held in Tokyo. A feat of cutting-edge tech
 nology and cinematography\, the film engages with the drama already inhere
 nt to sport\, offering a vision of triumph and grief—in short\, what makes
  the Games human—instead of results. Ichikawa’s insistence on the human\, 
 the poetic\, and the aesthetic makes this a landmark film in documentary f
 ilmmaking. [169 min\; documentary\; Japanese with English subtitles]</p>\n
 <p><strong>A Q&A with Dr. Hannah Airriess (IU Department of East Asian Lan
 guages and Cultures) and Dr. Brandon Wallace (IU Media School) will follow
  the screening.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
