 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 7pm</strong><br />\nTransparent\, an audible family portrait\, introdu
 ces a suite of compositions created and recorded with the support of the J
 azz Road Creative Residency program in collaboration with the Hundredth Hi
 ll under the direction of Monika Herzig. Modern\, sophisticated jazz instr
 umentals evoke the stories and concerns of parents and caregivers of trans
 gender children through intricate melodies and improvisations. Performers 
 for the event are internationally renowned jazz musicians Tom Clark (saxop
 hone)\, Peter Kienle (guitar)\, Monika Herzig (piano)\, Jeremy Allen (bass
 )\, Karina Colis (drums) with Cyr Wheel and Aerial Choreography by Zackary
  Herzig.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
