CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Hidden Fortress stars the inimitable Toshiro Mifune as a ge
 neral charged with guarding his defeated clan’s princess (a fierce Misa Ue
 hara) as the two smuggle royal treasure across hostile territory. Accompan
 ying them are a pair of bumbling\, conniving peasants who may or may not b
 e their friends. This rip-roaring ride is among the director’s most belove
 d films and was a primary influence on George Lucas’s Star Wars. The Hidde
 n Fortress delivers Kurosawa’s trademark deft blend of wry humor\, breatht
 aking action\, and compassionate humanity. [139 min\; action\, adventure\,
  drama\; Japanese with English subtitles]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260131T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
