BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-145707@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Join us in an exploration of traditional Puerto Rican music as 
 expressed through Bad Bunny and his collaborators.\nFrom Vega Baja\, Puert
 o Rico\, to the global stage\, Benito Antonio Martínez Ocasio grew up imme
 rsed in the rich musical heritage of his beloved island\, which he highlig
 hts in his music. Bad Bunny has also been vocal about issues affecting Pue
 rto Rico\, including Hurricane Maria\, gentrification\, and the destructio
 n and privatization of nature. This exhibit presents moments from Bad Bunn
 y’s career\, with an emphasis on his use of bomba\, plena\, and jíbaro mus
 ic on the 2025 album DeBÍ TiRAR MáS FOToS.\nCome together to celebrate thi
 s historic moment as Bad Bunny provides the soundtrack to the Super Bowl. 
 Already being dubbed the “Benito Bowl\,” Bad Bunny has created a unique pl
 atform for Puerto Ricans around the world to share their culture and ident
 ity with a global audience.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260206T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260206T140000
LOCATION:William & Gayle Cook Music Library\,within the Simon Music Library
  and Recital Center building\, 200 S. Eagleson Avenue\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:BadBunnyNation: “Tell your ABuELA\, we’re the halftime show!” DJ Ar
 acena is in the house!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/badbunnynation-tell-your-abuela-were-the-halftim
 e-show-dj-aracena-is-in-the-house/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Join us in an
  exploration of traditional Puerto Rican music as expressed through Bad Bu
 nny and his collaborators.</p>\n<p>From Vega Baja\, Puerto Rico\, to the g
 lobal stage\, Benito Antonio Martínez Ocasio grew up immersed in the rich 
 musical heritage of his beloved island\, which he highlights in his music.
  Bad Bunny has also been vocal about issues affecting Puerto Rico\, includ
 ing Hurricane Maria\, gentrification\, and the destruction and privatizati
 on of nature. This exhibit presents moments from Bad Bunny’s career\, with
  an emphasis on his use of bomba\, plena\, and jíbaro music on the 2025 al
 bum DeBÍ TiRAR MáS FOToS.</p>\n<p>Come together to celebrate this historic
  moment as Bad Bunny provides the soundtrack to the Super Bowl. Already be
 ing dubbed the “Benito Bowl\,” Bad Bunny has created a unique platform for
  Puerto Ricans around the world to share their culture and identity with a
  global audience. </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
