BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-145716@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:the soft work of staying\nPhotography and words by Talia Hallid
 ay\nJoin us for a multi-tiered evening of art\, words\, and making—an imme
 rsive experience unfolding throughout Gather.\nIn the Gallery\, The Soft A
 ct of Staying opens as a photography exhibition paired with intimate\, pow
 erful writing by Talia Halliday\, tracing the quiet ways plants have held 
 space through grief. The work explores staying—staying present\, staying t
 ender\, staying alive—when loss reshapes everything.\nIn the back of Gathe
 r\, a small stage comes to life with spoken word from local poets\, offeri
 ng voices that echo\, expand\, and respond to the themes of grief\, resili
 ence\, and becoming.\nAt the heart of the store\, the DIY Bar invites you 
 into the circle: paint a planter as an act of joy. Because joy and grief a
 re not opposites—they arrive together\, each giving shape to the other. Cr
 eate something bright. Sit with something heavy. Let both be true.\nCome w
 ander\, listen\, make\, and stay awhile.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260206T170000
LOCATION:Gather : handmade shoppe & Co\, 116 N Walnut\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The soft work of staying – a Gather After Hours event
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-soft-work-of-staying-a-gather-after-hours-ev
 ent/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>the soft work
  of staying<br />\nPhotography and words by Talia Halliday<br />\nJoin us 
 for a multi-tiered evening of art\, words\, and making—an immersive experi
 ence unfolding throughout Gather.<br />\nIn the Gallery\, The Soft Act of 
 Staying opens as a photography exhibition paired with intimate\, powerful 
 writing by Talia Halliday\, tracing the quiet ways plants have held space 
 through grief. The work explores staying—staying present\, staying tender\
 , staying alive—when loss reshapes everything.<br />\nIn the back of Gathe
 r\, a small stage comes to life with spoken word from local poets\, offeri
 ng voices that echo\, expand\, and respond to the themes of grief\, resili
 ence\, and becoming.<br />\nAt the heart of the store\, the DIY Bar invite
 s you into the circle: paint a planter as an act of joy. Because joy and g
 rief are not opposites—they arrive together\, each giving shape to the oth
 er. Create something bright. Sit with something heavy. Let both be true.<b
 r />\nCome wander\, listen\, make\, and stay awhile.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
