BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144509@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Almost since its inception\, PBS has been a political football.
  Even so it continues to be one of the most trusted institutions in Americ
 a. But even many of PBS’ champions do not know where PBS came from\, how i
 t is structured or how it is funded. Steve Krahnke\, former Senior Lecture
 r at the Indiana University Media School\, a 30 year veteran of PBS statio
 ns and program production\, and executive producer of the award-winning Cu
 ba: The Forgotten Revolution\, provides some clarity.\nA brief reception w
 ill follow the lecture.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260207T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260207T153000
LOCATION:Brown County Library\, 205 Locust Lane\, Nashville\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Traveling University presents: PBS: A Legacy of Service
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/pbs-a-legacy-of-service/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div class='even
 tlist-excerpt'>\n<p data-rte-preserve-empty='true'>Almost since its incept
 ion\, PBS has been a political football. Even so it continues to be one of
  the most trusted institutions in America. But even many of PBS’ champions
  do not know where PBS came from\, how it is structured or how it is funde
 d. Steve Krahnke\, former Senior Lecturer at the Indiana University Media 
 School\, a 30 year veteran of PBS stations and program production\, and ex
 ecutive producer of the award-winning <em>Cuba: The Forgotten Revolution</
 em>\, provides some clarity.</p>\n<p data-rte-preserve-empty='true'>A brie
 f reception will follow the lecture.</p>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
