BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-145561@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Tai Chi drop-in fitness class held inside Switchyard Park Pavil
 ion. 1601 S. Rogers Street\, Bloomington. No pre-registration required. Sl
 ight charge per person.\nTai chi is a practice that involves a series of s
 low gentle movements and physical postures\, a meditative state of mind\, 
 and controlled breathing. Participants can engage in movements sitting or 
 standing. Class will last 60 minutes.\nFollow City of Bloomington\, IN – P
 arks and Recreation on Facebook or visit bloomington.in.gov/recreation/fit
 ness/exercise for more information.\nIn order for individuals with disabil
 ities to participate as fully as possible\, reasonable accommodations are 
 provided. Reasonable accommodations are individualized techniques and reso
 urces used to enhance program participation without fundamentally altering
  a program. For more information or to request assistance\, contact Amy Sh
 rake\, Certified Therapeutic Recreation Specialist\, at 349-3747
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260209T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260209T220000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park Pavillion\, 1601 South Rogers St.\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260216T190000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260223T190000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260302T190000
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260309T190000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Winter Fitness in the Park – Tai Chi
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/winter-fitness-in-the-park-tai-chi/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Tai Chi drop-
 in fitness class held inside Switchyard Park Pavilion. 1601 S. Rogers Stre
 et\, Bloomington. No pre-registration required. Slight charge per person.<
 /p>\n<p>Tai chi is a practice that involves a series of slow gentle moveme
 nts and physical postures\, a meditative state of mind\, and controlled br
 eathing. Participants can engage in movements sitting or standing. Class w
 ill last 60 minutes.</p>\n<p>Follow City of Bloomington\, IN – Parks and R
 ecreation on Facebook or visit bloomington.in.gov/recreation/fitness/exerc
 ise for more information.<br />\nIn order for individuals with disabilitie
 s to participate as fully as possible\, reasonable accommodations are prov
 ided. Reasonable accommodations are individualized techniques and resource
 s used to enhance program participation without fundamentally altering a p
 rogram. For more information or to request assistance\, contact Amy Shrake
 \, Certified Therapeutic Recreation Specialist\, at 349-3747</p>\n</BODY><
 /HTML>
END:VEVENT
