CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Brett Kashmere’s 2014 film From Deep is an essay-style document
 ary that interrogates the game of basketball and its place in American cul
 ture. Offering both critical sports history and experimental filmmaking\, 
 Kashmere blends archival footage\, mixtape aesthetics\, and social comment
 ary to trace basketball’s evolution in U.S. culture\, specifically in Afri
 can American communities. This inventive blend of experimental form and so
 cial consciousness of sport marks a significant intervention in the contem
 porary sport documentary landscape. [88 min\; documentary\, experimental\;
  English]\nA Q&A with filmmaker Brett Kashmere will follow the screening.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260210T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Cinematic Sports Documentary Series: From Deep w/filmmaker
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/cinematic-sports-documentary-series-from-deep-w-
 filmmaker/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Brett Kashmer
 e’s 2014 film From Deep is an essay-style documentary that interrogates th
 e game of basketball and its place in American culture. Offering both crit
 ical sports history and experimental filmmaking\, Kashmere blends archival
  footage\, mixtape aesthetics\, and social commentary to trace basketball’
 s evolution in U.S. culture\, specifically in African American communities
 . This inventive blend of experimental form and social consciousness of sp
 ort marks a significant intervention in the contemporary sport documentary
  landscape. [88 min\; documentary\, experimental\; English]</p>\n<p>A Q&A 
 with filmmaker Brett Kashmere will follow the screening.</p>\n</BODY></HTM
 L>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
