 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>You’re invite
 d to join Janet Eger from the White River Forestry Committee to hone your 
 skills in identifying trees in winter. <strong>Participants are encouraged
  to attend both the classroom (Thursday\, 2/12) and outdoor (Saturday\, 2/
 14) sessions of the workshop\, but those who are able to attend only one s
 ession will still get value from the class.</strong></p>\n<p>In this first
  session session\, Eger will describe ways to distinguish different specie
 s of trees without their leaves. Participants will compare the bark\, buds
 \, nuts\, and seeds of common trees to compare different species.</p>\n</B
 ODY></HTML>
