BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146066@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Punch-Drunk Love crawled so Uncut Gems could walk! Paul Thomas 
 Anderson’s foray into a romantic (and still dark!) comedy is about as chao
 tic and off-kilter as one might expect. Barry Egan (Adam Sandler\, in his 
 first dramatic starring role) is a small business owner with seven sisters
  whose abuse has kept him alone and unable to fall in love. When a harmoni
 um and a mysterious woman enters his life (Emily Watson)\, his romantic jo
 urney begins\, but not without an extortion side quest for the ages—enter 
 Philip Seymour Hoffman in yet another small\, but wildly impactful\, role.
  Jon Brion (Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind\, Magnolia) helps fuel t
 he narrative with a baroque\, futurist score that helps Punch-Drunk Love c
 hannel “the spirit of classic Hollywood musicals and the whimsy of Jacques
  Tati into an idiosyncratic ode to the delirium of new romance” (Criterion
  Collection). [95 min\; drama\, comedy\, romance\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260214T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Punch Drunk Love
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/punch-drunk-love/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Punch-Drunk L
 ove crawled so Uncut Gems could walk! Paul Thomas Anderson’s foray into a 
 romantic (and still dark!) comedy is about as chaotic and off-kilter as on
 e might expect. Barry Egan (Adam Sandler\, in his first dramatic starring 
 role) is a small business owner with seven sisters whose abuse has kept hi
 m alone and unable to fall in love. When a harmonium and a mysterious woma
 n enters his life (Emily Watson)\, his romantic journey begins\, but not w
 ithout an extortion side quest for the ages—enter Philip Seymour Hoffman i
 n yet another small\, but wildly impactful\, role. Jon Brion (Eternal Suns
 hine of the Spotless Mind\, Magnolia) helps fuel the narrative with a baro
 que\, futurist score that helps Punch-Drunk Love channel “the spirit of cl
 assic Hollywood musicals and the whimsy of Jacques Tati into an idiosyncra
 tic ode to the delirium of new romance” (Criterion Collection). [95 min\; 
 drama\, comedy\, romance\; English] </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
