BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146068@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Episode 14 (“Double Play”): Windom Earle has taken his first vi
 ctim in the deadly chess game. Audrey tells Bobby they have to save Ben fr
 om his Civil War fantasy. Leo escapes.\nEpisode 15 (“Slaves and Masters”):
  The police look for James in the Marsh murder. Bobby and Shelly tell Trum
 an that Leo is gone and also reveal that Hank shot Leo the night the mill 
 burned. Albert returns to Twin Peaks with information on Windom Earle.\nEp
 isode 16 (“The Condemned Woman”): Truman puts Hank in prison for the attem
 pted murder of Leo\, while Hank points the finger at Josie for the murder 
 of Andrew Packard. Albert reveals who shot Cooper. Ben enlists the help of
  John Justice Wheeler.\nEpisode 17 (“Wounds and Scars”): Harry sinks into 
 a deep depression after a tragedy. Norma’s troubled sister\, Annie\, arriv
 es in Twin Peaks. Wheeler and Audrey hit it off. Cooper’s stalemate angers
  Earle.\n[185 min total\; drama\, mystery\; English]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260215T160000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Twin Peaks Season 2\, Episodes 14-17
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/twin-peaks-season-2-episodes-14-17/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Episode 14 (“
 Double Play”): Windom Earle has taken his first victim in the deadly chess
  game. Audrey tells Bobby they have to save Ben from his Civil War fantasy
 . Leo escapes.</p>\n<p>Episode 15 (“Slaves and Masters”): The police look 
 for James in the Marsh murder. Bobby and Shelly tell Truman that Leo is go
 ne and also reveal that Hank shot Leo the night the mill burned. Albert re
 turns to Twin Peaks with information on Windom Earle.</p>\n<p>Episode 16 (
 “The Condemned Woman”): Truman puts Hank in prison for the attempted murde
 r of Leo\, while Hank points the finger at Josie for the murder of Andrew 
 Packard. Albert reveals who shot Cooper. Ben enlists the help of John Just
 ice Wheeler.</p>\n<p>Episode 17 (“Wounds and Scars”): Harry sinks into a d
 eep depression after a tragedy. Norma’s troubled sister\, Annie\, arrives 
 in Twin Peaks. Wheeler and Audrey hit it off. Cooper’s stalemate angers Ea
 rle.</p>\n<p>[185 min total\; drama\, mystery\; English]</p>\n</BODY></HTM
 L>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
