BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-145659@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:About the book: Torn from his father\, siblings\, and all that 
 he knew and loved in Provence\, François Hugon spent years in the City of 
 Light virtually alone. Then one fateful afternoon\, his life changed when 
 he caught his first glimpse of New York City in the latest issue of Paris 
 Match\, a peek into the promise of a better life.\n\nOver the next decade\
 , he would find his way back to his family in Provence\, learn the value o
 f hard work\, and feel the thrill of taking chances.\nThis Book Share will
  be facilitated by Linda Whikehart
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260218T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260218T170000
LOCATION:Juniper Art Gallery\, 615 West Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Juniper Book Share–“Made in France” by François Hugon and Aimee Ada
 ms
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/juniper-book-share-made-in-france-by-francois-hu
 gon-and-aimee-adams/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><div dir='auto'>
 About the book: Torn from his father\, siblings\, and all that he knew and
  loved in Provence\, François Hugon spent years in the City of Light virtu
 ally alone. Then one fateful afternoon\, his life changed when he caught h
 is first glimpse of New York City in the latest issue of <em>Paris Match</
 em>\, a peek into the promise of a better life.</div>\n<div dir='auto'><sp
 an><br />\n</span>Over the next decade\, he would find his way back to his
  family in Provence\, learn the value of hard work\, and feel the thrill o
 f taking chances.</p>\n<p>This Book Share will be facilitated by Linda Whi
 kehart</p></div>\n<div class='yj6qo'></div>\n<div class='adL'></div>\n</BO
 DY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
