BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146188@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Weaving a compelling historical and cultural tapestry\, The Bes
 t of the Best: Jazz from Detroit chronicles the defining influence of Detr
 oit’s innovative jazz musicians while tracing the city’s dramatic rise and
  fall as an industrial power\, the struggles and triumphs of its creative 
 and resilient African American community\, and the profound tradition of m
 entorship nurturing Detroit jazz since the 1950s. [90 min\; documentary\; 
 English]\nA Q&A with producer/writer Mark Stryker and Natalie Boeyink from
  the Jacobs School of Music will follow the screening.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260221T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:New Americas Cinema Series: The Best of the Best: Jazz from Detroit
  w/producer
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/new-americas-cinema-series-the-best-of-the-best-
 jazz-from-detroit-w-producer/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Weaving a com
 pelling historical and cultural tapestry\, The Best of the Best: Jazz from
  Detroit chronicles the defining influence of Detroit’s innovative jazz mu
 sicians while tracing the city’s dramatic rise and fall as an industrial p
 ower\, the struggles and triumphs of its creative and resilient African Am
 erican community\, and the profound tradition of mentorship nurturing Detr
 oit jazz since the 1950s. [90 min\; documentary\; English]</p>\n<p><strong
 >A Q&A with producer/writer Mark Stryker and Natalie Boeyink from the Jaco
 bs School of Music will follow the screening.</strong></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146160@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6pm\, Music at 7pm\nThe Spine Stealers make spooky fol
 k inspired by dark lakes\, brain-burned nostalgia and a melancholic hue. T
 he band grew from the duo of Kate Ruland and Emma O’Shea\, who learned gui
 tar together during the pandemic and started frequenting open mics in the 
 end of 2022.\nTheir first year in 2023 they opened for Dead Horses at the 
 Majestic Theater Folk Fest in Madison\, WI\, won the Blue Ox Music Festiva
 l Virtual Band Competition and played the festival that June. They release
 d their first EP\, River Teeth Tapes\, in July of 2023.\nIn 2024\, they hi
 t the highways\, concretizing their place in the folk scene of the Midwest
 . The duo were featured on the lineups of Madison\, WI Waterfront Festival
  and Atwood Fest\, Rhinelander\, WI Project North Music Festival\, Grand R
 apid\, MN Festival Rialto. They played the Lounge at Stoughton Opera house
  for Haley Heyndrickx\, and opened for Arcadian Wild at Stoughton Opera Ho
 use. They released their debut album\, If the Sky Falls\, Beyond the Sidew
 alks\, in October of 2024. The band was featured on Gems on VHS playlist i
 n October.\n2025 they supported Basia Bulat at the Majestic Theater in Mad
 ison\, WI and played at Blue Ox Music Festival followed by their first nat
 ional tour thru the Pacific Northwest and Western United States. Their sec
 ond EP Yellow Feather was released in August of 2025.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260221T190000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Spine Stealers/Rianna Marie/Ditch Tea Steepers
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-spine-stealers-rianna-marie-ditch-tea-steepe
 rs/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 6pm\, Music at 7pm</strong><br />\nThe Spine Stealers make spooky folk
  inspired by dark lakes\, brain-burned nostalgia and a melancholic hue. Th
 e band grew from the duo of Kate Ruland and Emma O’Shea\, who learned guit
 ar together during the pandemic and started frequenting open mics in the e
 nd of 2022.<br />\nTheir first year in 2023 they opened for Dead Horses at
  the Majestic Theater Folk Fest in Madison\, WI\, won the Blue Ox Music Fe
 stival Virtual Band Competition and played the festival that June. They re
 leased their first EP\, River Teeth Tapes\, in July of 2023.<br />\nIn 202
 4\, they hit the highways\, concretizing their place in the folk scene of 
 the Midwest. The duo were featured on the lineups of Madison\, WI Waterfro
 nt Festival and Atwood Fest\, Rhinelander\, WI Project North Music Festiva
 l\, Grand Rapid\, MN Festival Rialto. They played the Lounge at Stoughton 
 Opera house for Haley Heyndrickx\, and opened for Arcadian Wild at Stought
 on Opera House. They released their debut album\, If the Sky Falls\, Beyon
 d the Sidewalks\, in October of 2024. The band was featured on Gems on VHS
  playlist in October.<br />\n2025 they supported Basia Bulat at the Majest
 ic Theater in Madison\, WI and played at Blue Ox Music Festival followed b
 y their first national tour thru the Pacific Northwest and Western United 
 States. Their second EP Yellow Feather was released in August of 2025. </p
 >\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
