BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146421@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Julien Faraut’s John McEnroe: In the Realm of Perfection explor
 es the tennis legend’s psyche and emotion on the court of the 1984 French 
 Open. Through 16mm film\, Faraut reimagines athletic performance as cinema
 tic and aesthetic performance\, blurring the boundaries between these two 
 seemingly separate categories. McEnroe’s obsession and volatility are tran
 sformed into an aesthetic consideration of performance and emotion in one 
 of the contemporary period’s most inventive sport documentaries. [95 min\;
  documentary\; English and French with English subtitles]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260224T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:John McEnroe: In the Realm of Perfection\, with a Q&A to follow the
  screening.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/john-mcenroe-in-the-realm-of-perfection-with-a-q
 a-to-follow-the-screening/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Julien Faraut
 ’s John McEnroe: In the Realm of Perfection explores the tennis legend’s p
 syche and emotion on the court of the 1984 French Open. Through 16mm film\
 , Faraut reimagines athletic performance as cinematic and aesthetic perfor
 mance\, blurring the boundaries between these two seemingly separate categ
 ories. McEnroe’s obsession and volatility are transformed into an aestheti
 c consideration of performance and emotion in one of the contemporary peri
 od’s most inventive sport documentaries. [95 min\; documentary\; English a
 nd French with English subtitles] </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
