BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146435@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Overtuned Fest is a community-driven festival uniting experimen
 tal rock and contemporary classical music. Dedicated to redefining the con
 cert experience\, it blends genre fusion\, visual art\, and education to f
 oster collaboration and inclusivity. By commissioning new works for electr
 ic guitar\, drumset\, sinfonietta\, and multimedia ensembles—and reimagini
 ng classics like Schubert’s Winterreise—the festival supports emerging art
 ists and celebrates music as a living art form. Through workshops with MCC
 SC High School orchestras\, Overtuned Fest nurtures creativity\, curiosity
 \, and connection\, empowering the next generation to shape the future of 
 concert art and build bridges across musical communities.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260225T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260225T193000
LOCATION:Pillar Arts Performance Space\, Arts Alliance Center\, inside Coll
 ege Mall\, 2894 E 3rd St Suite L-10D\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Overtuned Festival: Featured Artist Recital: JIJI
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/overtuned-festival-featured-artist-recital-jiji/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Overtuned Fes
 t is a community-driven festival uniting experimental rock and contemporar
 y classical music. Dedicated to redefining the concert experience\, it ble
 nds genre fusion\, visual art\, and education to foster collaboration and 
 inclusivity. By commissioning new works for electric guitar\, drumset\, si
 nfonietta\, and multimedia ensembles—and reimagining classics like Schuber
 t’s Winterreise—the festival supports emerging artists and celebrates musi
 c as a living art form. Through workshops with MCCSC High School orchestra
 s\, Overtuned Fest nurtures creativity\, curiosity\, and connection\, empo
 wering the next generation to shape the future of concert art and build br
 idges across musical communities.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146235@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Green Drinks Bloomington partnering with the Sassa
 fras Audubon Society.\nIn March 2025\, the Southern Indiana Cerulean Warbl
 er BirdScape\n(SICWB) was launched as a collaborative effort with experts 
 from more than two\ndozen organizations across The Americas to help protec
 t and manage cerulean\nwarbler habitats. As the BirdScape Coordinator\, Oe
 hlman will be presenting on all the\nways this partnership is having direc
 t impacts to help curb the rapid decline of\ncerulean warblers\, and how t
 here might be ways for you\, a community member\, to get\ninvolved.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260225T180000
LOCATION:Upland Woodshop\, 354 W 11th Street\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:“The Indiana Cerulean Warbler Birdscape: An international conservat
 ion mission in our own backyard”.
