BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146436@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Overtuned Fest is a community-driven festival uniting experimen
 tal rock and contemporary classical music. Dedicated to redefining the con
 cert experience\, it blends genre fusion\, visual art\, and education to f
 oster collaboration and inclusivity. By commissioning new works for electr
 ic guitar\, drumset\, sinfonietta\, and multimedia ensembles—and reimagini
 ng classics like Schubert’s Winterreise—the festival supports emerging art
 ists and celebrates music as a living art form. Through workshops with MCC
 SC High School orchestras\, Overtuned Fest nurtures creativity\, curiosity
 \, and connection\, empowering the next generation to shape the future of 
 concert art and build bridges across musical communities.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260226T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260226T203000
LOCATION:Switchyard Park Pavillion\, 1601 South Rogers St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Overtuned Festival:  Rock Sinfonia\, featuring Chamber Orchestra wi
 th Visual Media\, Featuring world premieres by Miggy Torres\, Timothy Rein
 holz\, Eli Hocking\, and Jee Won Kim in collaboration with visual artists 
 Gulli Björnsson\, Wyatt Cannon\, Courage Barda and Elina Zazulia
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/overtuned-festival-rock-sinfonia-featuring-chamb
 er-orchestra-with-visual-media-featuring-world-premieres-by-miggy-torres-t
 imothy-reinholz-eli-hocking-and-jee-won-kim-in-collaboration-with-visua/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Overtuned Fes
 t is a community-driven festival uniting experimental rock and contemporar
 y classical music. Dedicated to redefining the concert experience\, it ble
 nds genre fusion\, visual art\, and education to foster collaboration and 
 inclusivity. By commissioning new works for electric guitar\, drumset\, si
 nfonietta\, and multimedia ensembles—and reimagining classics like Schuber
 t’s Winterreise—the festival supports emerging artists and celebrates musi
 c as a living art form. Through workshops with MCCSC High School orchestra
 s\, Overtuned Fest nurtures creativity\, curiosity\, and connection\, empo
 wering the next generation to shape the future of concert art and build br
 idges across musical communities.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146410@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Q&A with Filmaker Michael Husain and former Pacers Darnell “Dr.
  Dunk” HIllman and Dave Robisch after the film!\nAn incredible story of th
 e ABA – a flamboyant rival league to the NBA – and its players. They creat
 ed much of what the billion dollar NBA is today–the 3-point shot\, slam du
 nk contest\, fashion and culture innovators–but then are forgotten in a bu
 siness deal gone bad.\nThe Waiting Game is a powerful documentary that rev
 eals an incredible battle between the NBA and a tiny not-for-profit workin
 g to gain full recognition for the men of the ABA. It’s a fight for benefi
 ts the players of the ABA felt were promised\, but never delivered. While 
 following an investigation of the legal trail of the ABA-NBA merger\, key 
 impact journalism and the advocacy for justice\, the film reveals the line
 s that can stand between raw corporate interest and basic human dignity.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260226T190000
LOCATION:Buskirk Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Waiting Game (2024) w/filmmaker Q & A
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-waiting-game-2024-w-filmmaker-q-a/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Q&A with Film
 aker Michael Husain and former Pacers Darnell “Dr. Dunk” HIllman and Dave 
 Robisch after the film!</p>\n<p>An incredible story of the ABA – a flamboy
 ant rival league to the NBA – and its players. They created much of what t
 he billion dollar NBA is today–the 3-point shot\, slam dunk contest\, fash
 ion and culture innovators–but then are forgotten in a business deal gone 
 bad.</p>\n<p>The Waiting Game is a powerful documentary that reveals an in
 credible battle between the NBA and a tiny not-for-profit working to gain 
 full recognition for the men of the ABA. It’s a fight for benefits the pla
 yers of the ABA felt were promised\, but never delivered. While following 
 an investigation of the legal trail of the ABA-NBA merger\, key impact jou
 rnalism and the advocacy for justice\, the film reveals the lines that can
  stand between raw corporate interest and basic human dignity.</p>\n</BODY
 ></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
