BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146780@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Deaf President Now! recounts the eight days of historic protest
 s held at Gallaudet University in 1988 after the school’s board of trustee
 s appointed a hearing president over several very qualified Deaf candidate
 s. After a week of rallies\, boycotts\, and protests\, the students of Gal
 laudet University triumph over an uncaring board and administration as the
  hearing president resigns and beloved dean Dr. I. King Jordan becomes the
  university’s first Deaf president. The protests marked a pivotal moment i
 n civil rights history\, with an impact that extended well beyond the Gall
 audet campus\, and paved the way for the Americans with Disabilities Act (
 ADA). [100 min\; documentary\; American Sign Language and English with Eng
 lish subtitles]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260307T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:New Americas Cinema: Deaf President Now!
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/new-americas-cinema-deaf-president-now/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Deaf Presiden
 t Now! recounts the eight days of historic protests held at Gallaudet Univ
 ersity in 1988 after the school’s board of trustees appointed a hearing pr
 esident over several very qualified Deaf candidates. After a week of ralli
 es\, boycotts\, and protests\, the students of Gallaudet University triump
 h over an uncaring board and administration as the hearing president resig
 ns and beloved dean Dr. I. King Jordan becomes the university’s first Deaf
  president. The protests marked a pivotal moment in civil rights history\,
  with an impact that extended well beyond the Gallaudet campus\, and paved
  the way for the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). [100 min\; documen
 tary\; American Sign Language and English with English subtitles] </p>\n</
 BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146812@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 6:15.\nBilly Joel and Elton John are two of the most h
 ighly acclaimed artists and respected\nentertainers in the world. Their mu
 sic has acted as cultural touchstones for millions of\npeople. Their music
  is celebrated all in one night in a spectacular two part performance\napp
 ropriately titled “Still Rock n’ Roll” and “Madmen Across the Water” Back 
 to Back\ntribute show.\nJoe D’Amato\, nicknamed Elton Joe\, launches the s
 how as Billy Joel and creates an\nimpressive live Billy Joel celebration i
 ncluding all of the favorites. At the peak of the\nperformance and after a
  quick break\, D’Amato disappears\, and after only a quick change of\nclot
 hes\, reappears as Elton John to electrify the audience with all of the gr
 eats of Elton\nJohn. Supported by Brad Canaday on Drums\, Butch Ellis on B
 ass\, and Larry Bourne on\nGuitar and Keys\, “Still Rock n’\; Roll” and “M
 admen Across the Water” brings a two part\nshow into one amazing rock fest
  performance.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260307T190000
LOCATION:Mitchell Opera House\, 217 North 7th Street\, Mitchell. IN
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:“Still Rock n’ Roll” and “Madmen Across the Water” – A Back-to-Back
  Tribute to Elton John and Billy Joel
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/still-rock-n-roll-and-madmen-across-the-water-a-
 back-to-back-tribute-to-elton-john-and-billy-joel/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Doors at 6:15
 .</p>\n<p>Billy Joel and Elton John are two of the most highly acclaimed a
 rtists and respected<br />\nentertainers in the world. Their music has act
 ed as cultural touchstones for millions of<br />\npeople. Their music is c
 elebrated all in one night in a spectacular two part performance<br />\nap
 propriately titled “Still Rock n’ Roll” and “Madmen Across the Water” Back
  to Back<br />\ntribute show.<br />\nJoe D’Amato\, nicknamed Elton Joe\, l
 aunches the show as Billy Joel and creates an<br />\nimpressive live Billy
  Joel celebration including all of the favorites. At the peak of the<br />
 \nperformance and after a quick break\, D’Amato disappears\, and after onl
 y a quick change of<br />\nclothes\, reappears as Elton John to electrify 
 the audience with all of the greats of Elton<br />\nJohn. Supported by Bra
 d Canaday on Drums\, Butch Ellis on Bass\, and Larry Bourne on<br />\nGuit
 ar and Keys\, “Still Rock n’\; Roll” and “Madmen Across the Water” brings 
 a two part<br />\nshow into one amazing rock fest performance.</p>\n</BODY
 ></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
