BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146937@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Andy Cohen\, in town from his Memphis\, TN home for a HOOMAC (H
 oosier Original Music Association) show the night before\, also at Sleeper
 ’s Bar\, has graciously agreed to have a workshop on the Piedmont style of
  guitar playing for anyone interested (all ages). There’s no advance regis
 tration or payment\, participants should count on paying $25 cash (or chec
 k) to Cohen at the workshop. All proceeds go to the artist. andycohenmusic
 .com or https://www.facebook.com/AndyCohenBlues for info on Andy.\nFrom Co
 hen:\n“What I usually do is walk through the mechanics of Piedmont style p
 laying\, which involves coaching people to alternate their thumb over two 
 or more strings while they use their fingers to play a melody. I have a wa
 y of forcing it\, such that the students get the idea in a practical way\,
  while I also teach them how to count and what to listen for in this kind 
 of music. Depending on the initial skill level of the students\, I can tak
 e it to any of several levels and leave them with homework. Participants s
 hould bring their phones or a camera\, and a notebook to take notes.”
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260311T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260311T200000
LOCATION:Sleeper's Bar (back room)\, 2601 N. Walnut St. (Cascades Inn)\, Bl
 oomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Piedmont Guitar Style Workshop with Andy Cohen
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/piedmont-guitar-style-workshop-with-andy-cohen/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Andy Cohen\, 
 in town from his Memphis\, TN home for a HOOMAC (Hoosier Original Music As
 sociation) show the night before\, also at Sleeper’s Bar\, has graciously 
 agreed to have a workshop on the Piedmont style of guitar playing for anyo
 ne interested (all ages). There’s no advance registration or payment\, par
 ticipants should count on paying $25 cash (or check) to Cohen at the works
 hop. All proceeds go to the artist. andycohenmusic.com or https://www.face
 book.com/AndyCohenBlues for info on Andy.</p>\n<p>From Cohen:<br />\n“What
  I usually do is walk through the mechanics of Piedmont style playing\, wh
 ich involves coaching people to alternate their thumb over two or more str
 ings while they use their fingers to play a melody. I have a way of forcin
 g it\, such that the students get the idea in a practical way\, while I al
 so teach them how to count and what to listen for in this kind of music. D
 epending on the initial skill level of the students\, I can take it to any
  of several levels and leave them with homework. Participants should bring
  their phones or a camera\, and a notebook to take notes.”</p>\n</BODY></H
 TML>
END:VEVENT
