BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-147049@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Kuriki-Olivo is known for her conceptual works of sculpture\, i
 nstallation\, and performance that combine readymade objects\, popular cul
 ture\, and autobiography to address themes of transgender identity\, race\
 , and power in contemporary society. Her work is currently featured on the
  cover of Art in America\, and two of her sculptures were featured in the 
 2024 Venice Biennial. Her 2017 work Liberté (Liberty)\, was the first and 
 only work of performance art to be acquired by the Whitney Museum of Ameri
 can Art for its permanent collection.\n\nRSVP at https://events.iu.edu/blo
 omington/event/2223729-visiting-artist-jade-guanaro-kuriki-olivo-puppies
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260312T170000
LOCATION:Martin Commons\, Eskenazi Museum of Art\, 1133 E 7th St\, Blooming
 ton
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Performance by visiting multidisciplinary artist Jade Guanaro Kurik
 i-Olivo (Puppies Puppies)
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/performance-by-visiting-multidisciplinary-artist
 -jade-guanaro-kuriki-olivo-puppies-puppies/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Kuriki-Olivo 
 is known for her conceptual works of sculpture\, installation\, and perfor
 mance that combine readymade objects\, popular culture\, and autobiography
  to address themes of transgender identity\, race\, and power in contempor
 ary society. Her work is currently featured on the <a href='https://www.ar
 tnews.com/art-in-america/interviews/puppies-puppies-jade-guanaro-kuriki-ol
 ivo-cover-dead-liberty-skeleton-1234774239/' target='_blank' rel='noopener
 ' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.artnews.c
 om/art-in-america/interviews/puppies-puppies-jade-guanaro-kuriki-olivo-cov
 er-dead-liberty-skeleton-1234774239/&source=gmail&ust=1773251271643000&usg
 =AOvVaw3fvFdsny-pgr_PFcY1IeuW'>cover of Art in America</a>\, and two of he
 r sculptures were featured in the <a href='https://www.labiennale.org/en/a
 rt/2024/nucleo-contemporaneo/puppies-puppies-jade-guanaro-kuriki-olivo' ta
 rget='_blank' rel='noopener' data-saferedirecturl='https://www.google.com/
 url?q=https://www.labiennale.org/en/art/2024/nucleo-contemporaneo/puppies-
 puppies-jade-guanaro-kuriki-olivo&source=gmail&ust=1773251271643000&usg=AO
 vVaw3HfbKFMPwH133N92v07ZN5'>2024 Venice Biennial</a>. Her 2017 work Libert
 é (Liberty)\, was the first and only work of performance art to be acquire
 d by the Whitney Museum of American Art for its permanent collection.</p>
 \n<div></div>\n<div>RSVP at <a href='https://events.iu.edu/bloomington/eve
 nt/2223729-visiting-artist-jade-guanaro-kuriki-olivo-puppies' target='_bla
