BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-147010@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Girls to the Front! The Cinema of Jennifer Reeder\, Jorgensen G
 uest Filmmaker Series\nWriter\, director\, and producer Jennifer Reeder ha
 s earned comparisons to other filmmakers: the surrealism of Lynch\, the ca
 mp of Waters\, the pop-culture sensibility of Spheeris\, the stylistic exp
 erimentation of Deren. While her influences are varied\, Reeder is a singu
 lar filmmaker all her own. Reeder’s films have premiered and screened at p
 restigious global festivals including Sundance\, Berlin\, Rotterdam\, SXSW
 \, Tribeca\, BFI-London Film Festival\, the Whitney Biennial\, and the Ven
 ice Biennale. She received the 2024 Tour De Force Award from the Chicago I
 nternational Film Festival and in 2020 was named by Oscar-winner Bong Joon
 -ho as a filmmaker pivotal to the future of cinema. [60 min]
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260312T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A Conversation with Jennifer Reeder
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/a-conversation-with-jennifer-reeder/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> <strong>Girl
 s to the Front! The Cinema of Jennifer Reeder\, Jorgensen Guest Filmmaker 
 Series</strong></p>\n<p>Writer\, director\, and producer Jennifer Reeder h
 as earned comparisons to other filmmakers: the surrealism of Lynch\, the c
 amp of Waters\, the pop-culture sensibility of Spheeris\, the stylistic ex
 perimentation of Deren. While her influences are varied\, Reeder is a sing
 ular filmmaker all her own. Reeder’s films have premiered and screened at 
 prestigious global festivals including Sundance\, Berlin\, Rotterdam\, SXS
 W\, Tribeca\, BFI-London Film Festival\, the Whitney Biennial\, and the Ve
 nice Biennale. She received the 2024 Tour De Force Award from the Chicago 
 International Film Festival and in 2020 was named by Oscar-winner Bong Joo
 n-ho as a filmmaker pivotal to the future of cinema. [60 min]</p>\n</BODY>
 </HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
