BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146544@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:The Silkroad Ensemble’s latest flagship program with Artistic D
 irector Rhiannon Giddens is Sanctuary: The Power of Resonance and Ritual. 
 In this program\, Giddens and the ensemble explore how to experience music
  to better understand the world\, find comfort\, process loss in a changin
 g environment\, and rebuild community based on humanity. Historically\, wh
 en people have found themselves in a time of conflict or stress\, they hav
 e always turned to music.\nThe idea of trance\, something that can bring a
  deep peace that is hard to find in modern society\, is profoundly tied to
  the communal music-making traditions found in many different cultures\, f
 rom Morocco to India to Ireland\, and is a way to build a stronger human c
 onnection amidst all the noise. In Sanctuary: The Power of Resonance and R
 itual\, the musicians will delve deeply into one another’s music and tradi
 tions\, such as Sicilian tarantella with Mauro Durante and Francesco Turri
 si\, Moroccan gnawa with Mehdi Nassouli\, Indian classical music with Sand
 eep Das\, American old-time with Giddens on banjo\, and more\, and invite 
 audiences to join them as partners and participants in the performance\, i
 nstead of solely as passive bystanders.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260312T193000
LOCATION:Indiana University Auditorium\, 1211 E 7th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Harmony and Power | Silkroad Ensemble with Rhiannon Giddens
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/harmony-and-power-silkroad-ensemble-with-rhianno
 n-giddens/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>The Silkroad 
 Ensemble’s latest flagship program with Artistic Director Rhiannon Giddens
  is Sanctuary: The Power of Resonance and Ritual. In this program\, Gidden
 s and the ensemble explore how to experience music to better understand th
 e world\, find comfort\, process loss in a changing environment\, and rebu
 ild community based on humanity. Historically\, when people have found the
 mselves in a time of conflict or stress\, they have always turned to music
 .</p>\n<p>The idea of trance\, something that can bring a deep peace that 
 is hard to find in modern society\, is profoundly tied to the communal mus
 ic-making traditions found in many different cultures\, from Morocco to In
 dia to Ireland\, and is a way to build a stronger human connection amidst 
 all the noise. In Sanctuary: The Power of Resonance and Ritual\, the music
 ians will delve deeply into one another’s music and traditions\, such as S
 icilian tarantella with Mauro Durante and Francesco Turrisi\, Moroccan gna
 wa with Mehdi Nassouli\, Indian classical music with Sandeep Das\, America
 n old-time with Giddens on banjo\, and more\, and invite audiences to join
  them as partners and participants in the performance\, instead of solely 
 as passive bystanders.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
