UID:ai1ec-147011@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Anxious shut-in Ken is divorced\, unemployed\, and growing more
  and more estranged from his children. In a bid to form connection—and gen
 erate a little cash—he tries his hand at a series of YouTube personas and 
 unwittingly captures his new apartment’s ghosts in the process. Stumbling 
 down a rabbit hole of murderous lore and home exercises with catastrophic 
 unintended consequences\, Ken may just end up changing the world forever. 
 [81 min\; thriller\; English]\nPreceded by an introduction from director J
 ennifer Reeder.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260312T220000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Girls to the Front! The Cinema of Jennifer Reeder: Night’s End w/fi
 lmmaker
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/girls-to-the-front-the-cinema-of-jennifer-reeder
 -nights-end-w-filmmaker/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> Anxious shut
 -in Ken is divorced\, unemployed\, and growing more and more estranged fro
 m his children. In a bid to form connection—and generate a little cash—he 
 tries his hand at a series of YouTube personas and unwittingly captures hi
 s new apartment’s ghosts in the process. Stumbling down a rabbit hole of m
 urderous lore and home exercises with catastrophic unintended consequences
 \, Ken may just end up changing the world forever. [81 min\; thriller\; En
 glish]</p>\n<p>Preceded by an introduction from director Jennifer Reeder. 
 </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
