BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-145035@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A Grand Night for Singing offers a collection of the greatest l
 ove songs in music theatre history given to us by the incomparable writing
  duo\, Richard Rodgers and Oscar Hammerstein II. Featuring songs from the 
 musicals Oklahoma!\, The Sound of Music\, Carousel\, The King and I\, Sout
 h Pacific\, Cinderella and many more! With a modern setting and perspectiv
 e\, MCCT’s production will reveal how relevant Oscar Hammerstein II’s word
 s still are and how Richard Rodger’s music will always make audiences’ ima
 ginations soar.\nTickets @ mcct@ludus.com\n 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260313T193000
LOCATION:Waldron Firebay\, 122 South Walnut\, Bloomington
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260314T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A Grand Night for Singing
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/a-grand-night-for-singing/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>A Grand Night
  for Singing offers a collection of the greatest love songs in music theat
 re history given to us by the incomparable writing duo\, Richard Rodgers a
 nd Oscar Hammerstein II. Featuring songs from the musicals Oklahoma!\, The
  Sound of Music\, Carousel\, The King and I\, South Pacific\, Cinderella a
 nd many more! With a modern setting and perspective\, MCCT’s production wi
 ll reveal how relevant Oscar Hammerstein II’s words still are and how Rich
 ard Rodger’s music will always make audiences’ imaginations soar.</p>\n<p>
 Tickets @ mcct@ludus.com</p>\n<p> </p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146834@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Chris Collins and Boulder Canyon are a John Denver Tribute that
  will take you back to the days reminiscent of the concerts from one of th
 e greatest artists of our time.\nSince forming in Aspen\, Colorado\, Chris
  and Boulder Canyon have gone on to tour from coast-to-coast to pay tribut
 e to the music of John Denver. With similarities between Chris’s and John’
 s voices\, award-winning singer\, songwriter Chris Collins brings amazing 
 energy and the unmistakable enthusiasm to the stage that was a hallmark of
  a John Denver performance. From sold-out shows to breaking a theater reco
 rd for the largest audience ever to attend an event\, Chris Collins and Bo
 ulder Canyon have emerged as top performers of John Denver’s music.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260313T193000
LOCATION:Historic Brown County Playhouse\, 70 South Van Buren Street\, Nash
 ville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Chris Collins & Boulder Canyon: John Denver Tribute Band
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/chris-collins-boulder-canyon-john-denver-tribute
 -band/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Chris Collins
  and Boulder Canyon are a John Denver Tribute that will take you back to t
 he days reminiscent of the concerts from one of the greatest artists of ou
 r time.</p>\n<p>Since forming in Aspen\, Colorado\, Chris and Boulder Cany
 on have gone on to tour from coast-to-coast to pay tribute to the music of
  John Denver. With similarities between Chris’s and John’s voices\, award-
 winning singer\, songwriter Chris Collins brings amazing energy and the un
 mistakable enthusiasm to the stage that was a hallmark of a John Denver pe
 rformance. From sold-out shows to breaking a theater record for the larges
 t audience ever to attend an event\, Chris Collins and Boulder Canyon have
  emerged as top performers of John Denver’s music.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
