BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146805@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION: \nhttps://www.eventbrite.com/e/dr-jennifer-vencill-on-desire-t
 ickets-1983916713295\nIn partnership with the Kinsey Institute\, we presen
 t a conversation with Jennifer Vencill\, PhD\, one of the co-authors of De
 sire: An Inclusive Guide to Navigating Libido Differences in Relationships
 . For this event\, Jennifer will be joined in conversation by Jessica Hill
 e\, JD\, PhD\, Assistant Director of Education for the Kinsey Institute.\n
 ABOUT THE BOOK:\nDesire invites readers of all ages\, genders\, sexual ori
 entations\, and relationship structures to shed the shame and misinformati
 on that surround the topic of sex and instead learn from 2 certified sex t
 herapists about how libido really works. Desire differences are one of the
  most common relationship issues\, yet\, with fewer than 1\,100 certified 
 sex therapists in the country\, it can be difficult to find help. This ess
 ential book breaks the mold of the sex self-help genre\, which typically f
 ocuses only on cisgender women.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260323T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260323T190000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books & Cafe\, 849 South Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Author Event with Jennifer Vencill
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/author-event-with-jennifer-vencill/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> </p>\n<p dir
 ='ltr'><a href='https://www.eventbrite.com/e/dr-jennifer-vencill-on-desire
 -tickets-1983916713295' target='_blank' rel='noopener' data-saferedirectur
 l='https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.eventbrite.com/e/dr-jennifer-v
 encill-on-desire-tickets-1983916713295&source=gmail&ust=1772653348160000&u
 sg=AOvVaw2fH_EwBxxk_dzPANXrW13J'>https://www.eventbrite.com/e/<wbr />dr-je
 nnifer-vencill-on-desire-<wbr />tickets-1983916713295</a></p>\n<p dir='ltr
 '>In partnership with the Kinsey Institute\, we present a conversation wit
 h Jennifer Vencill\, PhD\, one of the co-authors of <em>Desire: An Inclusi
 ve Guide to Navigating Libido Differences in Relationship</em>s. For this 
 event\, Jennifer will be joined in conversation by Jessica Hille\, JD\, Ph
 D\, Assistant Director of Education for the Kinsey Institute.</p>\n<p dir=
 'ltr'>ABOUT THE BOOK:</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>Desire invites readers of all ages
 \, genders\, sexual orientations\, and relationship structures to shed the
  shame and misinformation that surround the topic of sex and instead learn
  from 2 certified sex therapists about how libido really works. Desire dif
 ferences are one of the most common relationship issues\, yet\, with fewer
  than 1\,100 certified sex therapists in the country\, it can be difficult
  to find help. This essential book breaks the mold of the sex self-help ge
 nre\, which typically focuses only on cisgender women.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
