BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-147530@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Doors at 8pm\nThe Obertones\, Oberlin’s only men’s and nonbinar
 y a cappella group\, have been bringing their energetic and unique sound t
 o performances all over the country since 1984. The Obertones’ mission\, o
 ver forty years later\, remains the same: to deliver their signature sound
  to audiences far and wide in fun-filled performances overflowing with con
 tagious energy.\nEver a campus favorite at Oberlin and a fixture in northe
 ast Ohio’s Lorain County\, the Obertones are also frequently on the road\,
  including an annual tour during the last week of March. Their quest to sh
 are their love of singing has taken them from coast to coast\, south and n
 orth\; from busking on the streets of New York\, to major festival stages 
 in Washington\, DC\, to a livestream of over 100\,000 viewers\, and everyw
 here in between. They have been featured on HBO’s Girls and Netflix’s Boja
 ck Horseman. And they would love to bring their music to you.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260324T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260324T220000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Obertones\, OBERLIN COLLEGE’S MEN’S + NON-BINARY A CAPPELLA GRO
 UP
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-obertones-oberlin-colleges-mens-non-binary-a
 -cappella-group/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><strong>Doors
  at 8pm</strong><br />\nThe Obertones\, Oberlin’s only men’s and nonbinary
  a cappella group\, have been bringing their energetic and unique sound to
  performances all over the country since 1984. The Obertones’ mission\, ov
 er forty years later\, remains the same: to deliver their signature sound 
 to audiences far and wide in fun-filled performances overflowing with cont
 agious energy.<br />\nEver a campus favorite at Oberlin and a fixture in n
 ortheast Ohio’s Lorain County\, the Obertones are also frequently on the r
 oad\, including an annual tour during the last week of March. Their quest 
 to share their love of singing has taken them from coast to coast\, south 
 and north\; from busking on the streets of New York\, to major festival st
 ages in Washington\, DC\, to a livestream of over 100\,000 viewers\, and e
 verywhere in between. They have been featured on HBO’s Girls and Netflix’s
  Bojack Horseman. And they would love to bring their music to you.</p>\n</
 BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
