UID:ai1ec-147507@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Science ambassador Neil deGrasse Tyson returns to Bloomington f
 or the first time since 2017 and will present a lecture titled “An Astroph
 ysicist Goes to the Movies – Part II.”\nFrom the Wizard of Oz to Mary Popp
 ins to 2001: A Space Odyssey to Harry Potter to A Bug’s Life\, it will be 
 an entertaining and enlightening review of all the science that our favori
 te movies got wrong\, combined with some of the stuff they got right. The 
 discussion will incorporate the latest films as well as some classics that
  you may not have known had any science in them at all.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260326T193000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:A Lecture by Neil deGrasse Tyson: “An Astrophysicist Goes to the Mo
 vies – Part II”
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/neil-degrasse-tyson-an-astrophysicist-goes-to-th
 e-movies-part-ii/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Science ambas
 sador Neil deGrasse Tyson returns to Bloomington for the first time since 
 2017 and will present a lecture titled “An Astrophysicist Goes to the Movi
 es – Part II.”</p>\n<p>From the Wizard of Oz to Mary Poppins to 2001: A Sp
 ace Odyssey to Harry Potter to A Bug’s Life\, it will be an entertaining a
 nd enlightening review of all the science that our favorite movies got wro
 ng\, combined with some of the stuff they got right. The discussion will i
 ncorporate the latest films as well as some classics that you may not have
  known had any science in them at all.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
