UID:ai1ec-147605@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to join us and your local wordsmiths for a nigh
 t of poetry\, libations\, and passion! The night begins with an open mic f
 eaturing local artists\, singers\, musicians\, and writers then ends with 
 a poetry slam.\nFeatured Poet for March is Hílda Davis!\nHílda Davis is a 
 first-generation Black Costa Rican American from Staten Island\, NY. A gra
 duate of the University at Albany and Indiana University – Bloomington\, s
 he has an MFA in Creative Writing from NYU and an MSW in Clinical Social W
 ork from the University of Washington. As a birth and postpartum doula and
  social worker\, she serves community members in Seattle\, where she lives
  with her family. As an artist\, her work focuses on girlhood\, survival\,
  and those she loves\, living and dead.\nDoors 8:30pm | Show 9pm | 18+\nHo
 sted by Andrea M. Sterling & Dan “Sully” Sullivan\nGrooves brought to you 
 by DJ Good Peoples\nVenue is wheelchair accessible.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260327T210000
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 South Walnut St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bloomington Poetry Slam Featuring Hilda Davis
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-poetry-slam-featuring-hilda-davis/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>You are invit
 ed to join us and your local wordsmiths for a night of poetry\, libations\
 , and passion! The night begins with an open mic featuring local artists\,
  singers\, musicians\, and writers then ends with a poetry slam.</p>\n<p><
 strong>Featured Poet for March is Hílda Davis!</strong></p>\n<p>Hílda Davi
 s is a first-generation Black Costa Rican American from Staten Island\, NY
 . A graduate of the University at Albany and Indiana University – Blooming
 ton\, she has an MFA in Creative Writing from NYU and an MSW in Clinical S
 ocial Work from the University of Washington. As a birth and postpartum do
 ula and social worker\, she serves community members in Seattle\, where sh
 e lives with her family. As an artist\, her work focuses on girlhood\, sur
 vival\, and those she loves\, living and dead.</p>\n<p>Doors 8:30pm | Show
  9pm | 18+</p>\n<p>Hosted by Andrea M. Sterling & Dan “Sully” Sullivan<br 
 />\nGrooves brought to you by DJ Good Peoples</p>\n<p>Venue is wheelchair 
 accessible.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
