BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-147534@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Cuzn Eddy – A man of many names and projects\, connected by a s
 ingle thread and vision. Eddy/Joshua came to the Black Hole last year with
  his project Thee Maji\, which built guitar\, voice and synthesizer to cre
 ate sacred monuments of sound. When the Cuzn is out\, the rhythm picks up 
 and the toe starts tapping. These cosmic gospel freakouts hearken back to 
 the Eddy Price cassingles on Auris Apothecary or Eddy’s old psycho-billy b
 and Th’Empires. Cuzn Eddy will be performing songs from his new cassette\,
  titled Cornbread.\nhttps://cuzneddy.bandcamp.com/\nhttps://www.yesuelhu.c
 om/\n________________________\nPSK – free improvisation ensemble led by Al
 ex Wray. Membership for 3/28 likely still to be determined\, likely drawin
 g players from Bloomington and beyond. Good cacophonous fun.\nhttps://sacr
 edvibrations.bandcamp.com/album/psk-9-20-25\nhttps://sacredvibrations.band
 camp.com/album/pandemonium-4\n________________________\nLather – Host and 
 curator of SFTBH. Cassette tapes\, loops\, circuitry\, sounds both collect
 ed and created then collaged together live.\nhttps://lather.bandcamp.com/
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260328T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260328T230000
LOCATION:Orbit Room\, 107 North College Ave.\, Suite 001 (downstairs)\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Sounds From The Black Hole: PSK // Cuzn Eddy // Lather
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/sounds-from-the-black-hole-psk-cuzn-eddy-lather/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Cuzn Eddy – A
  man of many names and projects\, connected by a single thread and vision.
  Eddy/Joshua came to the Black Hole last year with his project Thee Maji\,
  which built guitar\, voice and synthesizer to create sacred monuments of 
 sound. When the Cuzn is out\, the rhythm picks up and the toe starts tappi
 ng. These cosmic gospel freakouts hearken back to the Eddy Price cassingle
 s on Auris Apothecary or Eddy’s old psycho-billy band Th’Empires. Cuzn Edd
 y will be performing songs from his new cassette\, titled Cornbread.<br />
 \nhttps://cuzneddy.bandcamp.com/<br />\nhttps://www.yesuelhu.com/<br />\n_
 _______________________<br />\nPSK – free improvisation ensemble led by Al
 ex Wray. Membership for 3/28 likely still to be determined\, likely drawin
 g players from Bloomington and beyond. Good cacophonous fun.<br />\nhttps:
 //sacredvibrations.bandcamp.com/album/psk-9-20-25<br />\nhttps://sacredvib
 rations.bandcamp.com/album/pandemonium-4<br />\n________________________<b
 r />\nLather – Host and curator of SFTBH. Cassette tapes\, loops\, circuit
 ry\, sounds both collected and created then collaged together live.<br />
 \nhttps://lather.bandcamp.com/</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
