BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-147642@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:We encourage you to sign up for classes online. When you regist
 er online\, you’ll also pay online. While we will accept walk-ins before c
 lass if capacity allows\, registering ahead of time secures your spot and 
 creates a more seamless class experience.\nhttps://www.inthekitchen-bloomi
 ngton.com/classes\nSpring has returned and patio brunch season is just aro
 und the corner. Whether it’s for Easter\, Mother’s day\, girl’s afternoon\
 , whatever— a good quiche is the cornerstone of a lovely\, expansive break
 fast. The trick is developing a flaky crust that doesn’t soak up your egg 
 mixture and turn soggy. Quiche lorraine is a famous French preparation wit
 h crispy bacon\, but a veggie-forward blend with greens and herbs can be a
  crowd-pleasing delight. We’ll practice both! Come learn how to nail this 
 staple recipe anytime at home.\nActive participant style class with Ava. Y
 ou’ll leave with your own quiche!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260331T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260331T193000
LOCATION:In the Kitchen\, 115 N College Ave\, Suite 014\, Bloomington. Use 
 the Uptown Plaza alley entrance between JL Waters and Peach Cobbler Factor
 y.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Quiche Two-Way
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/quiche-two-way/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>We encourage 
 you to sign up for classes online. When you register online\, you’ll also 
 pay online. While we will accept walk-ins before class if capacity allows\
 , registering ahead of time secures your spot and creates a more seamless 
 class experience.<br />\nhttps://www.inthekitchen-bloomington.com/classes<
 br />\nSpring has returned and patio brunch season is just around the corn
 er. Whether it’s for Easter\, Mother’s day\, girl’s afternoon\, whatever— 
 a good quiche is the cornerstone of a lovely\, expansive breakfast. The tr
 ick is developing a flaky crust that doesn’t soak up your egg mixture and 
 turn soggy. Quiche lorraine is a famous French preparation with crispy bac
 on\, but a veggie-forward blend with greens and herbs can be a crowd-pleas
 ing delight. We’ll practice both! Come learn how to nail this staple recip
 e anytime at home.</p>\n<p>Active participant style class with Ava. You’ll
  leave with your own quiche!</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-147678@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Un/Filmed is an international documentary film development proj
 ect and a regular partner with the Byrnes Institute at IU focused on prese
 rving the tradition of independent\, Russian-language documentary filmmaki
 ng\, providing competitive workshops for participants with the opportunity
  to create films reflecting on pressing social issues. This program is sho
 wcasing the top six films of the 2024-2025 cohort with subtitles presented
  in English.\nA Q&A with Un/Filmed organizer and founder Victor Ilyukhin w
 ill follow the screening. \nLike Mother\, Like Daughter (dir. Sofia Sedlov
 a\, 2025\, Russia and France): \nWe’re Fine (dir. Daria Yurishcheva\, 2025
 \, Russia and France): \nShe Became a Pillar of Salt (dir. Xenia Vasilkova
 \, 2025\, Russia)\nUneasy Living (dir. Nikita Nadezhdin\, 2025\, Russia)\n
 Kozlov Mitya\, 81+ (dir. Yulia Ruzmanova\, 2025\, Russia)\nMemory is Me? (
 dir. Vlada Lodesk\, 2025\, Russia)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260331T190000
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East Seventh St. (on the North side of the IU Aud
 itorium)\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Best of Un/Filmed: Short Documentaries from Russian-Speaking Filmma
 kers w/Q&A
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/best-of-un-filmed-short-documentaries-from-russi
 an-speaking-filmmakers-w-qa/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p> Un/Filmed is
  an international documentary film development project and a regular partn
 er with the Byrnes Institute at IU focused on preserving the tradition of 
 independent\, Russian-language documentary filmmaking\, providing competit
 ive workshops for participants with the opportunity to create films reflec
 ting on pressing social issues. This program is showcasing the top six fil
 ms of the 2024-2025 cohort with subtitles presented in English.</p>\n<p>A 
 Q&A with Un/Filmed organizer and founder Victor Ilyukhin will follow the s
 creening. </p>\n<p>Like Mother\, Like Daughter (dir. Sofia Sedlova\, 2025\
 , Russia and France): </p>\n<p>We’re Fine (dir. Daria Yurishcheva\, 2025\,
  Russia and France): </p>\n<p>She Became a Pillar of Salt (dir. Xenia Vasi
 lkova\, 2025\, Russia)</p>\n<p>Uneasy Living (dir. Nikita Nadezhdin\, 2025
 \, Russia)</p>\n<p>Kozlov Mitya\, 81+ (dir. Yulia Ruzmanova\, 2025\, Russi
 a)</p>\n<p>Memory is Me? (dir. Vlada Lodesk\, 2025\, Russia)</p>\n</BODY><
 /HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-147753@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Daniel is widely known for hosting and creating TOSH.0 on Comed
 y Central. The show showcased internet clips with the addition of Daniel’s
  comedic perspective and was one of the longest-running comedy series for 
 Comedy Central.\nHe can currently be heard and seen hosting his video podc
 ast\, TOSH SHOW. The show premiered garnering millions of watches and list
 ens in the first weeks.\nDaniel has performed live stand-up comedy to sold
  out venues all over the world including New Zealand\, Australia\, Montrea
 l\, and Ireland. Following his 2025 US Daniel Tosh Live tour\, he just ann
 ounced his new 2026 North America stand-up tour\, Daniel Tosh: My First Fa
 rewell Tour.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260331T190000
LOCATION:IU Auditorium\, 1211 East 7th St.\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Daniel Tosh: My First Farewell Tour
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/daniel-tosh-my-first-farewell-tour/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>Daniel is wid
 ely known for hosting and creating TOSH.0 on Comedy Central. The show show
 cased internet clips with the addition of Daniel’s comedic perspective and
  was one of the longest-running comedy series for Comedy Central.</p>\n<p>
 He can currently be heard and seen hosting his video podcast\, TOSH SHOW. 
 The show premiered garnering millions of watches and listens in the first 
 weeks.</p>\n<p>Daniel has performed live stand-up comedy to sold out venue
 s all over the world including New Zealand\, Australia\, Montreal\, and Ir
 eland. Following his 2025 US Daniel Tosh Live tour\, he just announced his
  new 2026 North America stand-up tour\, Daniel Tosh: My First Farewell Tou
 r.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146809@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A Death Cafe is a group-directed discussion of death with no ag
 enda\, ideology\, objectives\, or themes. It is a discussion group rather 
 than grief support or counseling session. Death Cafes have spread quickly 
 around the world. Over 16\,500 Death Cafes are held in 85 countries. It is
  all volunteer-run.\nThe monthly Death Cafe at Morgenstern Books is run by
  co-hosts Rick Clayton and Casey Stover. Rick Clayton is a hospice chaplai
 n\, end-of life doula\, and musician who enjoys playing harp\, cello\, and
  guitar for his clients. Casey Stover is a Certified Family Life Educator 
 whose professional work often exists adjacent to death and grief\, shaping
  her belief in the importance of accessible spaces to normalize honest con
 versation and community care.\nYou can find our Death Cafe at the back cor
 ner of the bookstore\, near the restrooms\, on the last Tuesday of every m
 onth at 7 pm.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260331T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260331T210000
LOCATION:Morgenstern Books & Cafe\, 849 South Auto Mall Road\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Death Cafe
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/death-cafe-7/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p dir='ltr'>A D
 eath Cafe is a group-directed discussion of death with no agenda\, ideolog
 y\, objectives\, or themes. It is a discussion group rather than grief sup
 port or counseling session. Death Cafes have spread quickly around the wor
 ld. Over 16\,500 Death Cafes are held in 85 countries. It is all volunteer
 -run.</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>The monthly Death Cafe at Morgenstern Books is run
  by co-hosts Rick Clayton and Casey Stover. Rick Clayton is a hospice chap
 lain\, end-of life doula\, and musician who enjoys playing harp\, cello\, 
 and guitar for his clients. Casey Stover is a Certified Family Life Educat
 or whose professional work often exists adjacent to death and grief\, shap
 ing her belief in the importance of accessible spaces to normalize honest 
 conversation and community care.</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>You can find our Death 
 Cafe at the back corner of the bookstore\, near the restrooms\, on the las
 t Tuesday of every month at 7 pm.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
