CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to experience 1984 – Radio Play\, a haunting ad
 aptation of George Orwell’s classic dystopian novel brought to life on sta
 ge.\nIn a world where every thought is monitored and the Party controls tr
 uth itself\, Winston Smith dares to question the system. When forbidden lo
 ve awakens him to the possibility of freedom\, he risks everything in a ch
 illing battle against a regime where even thinking differently is a crime.
 \n// What is a radio play? //\nA radio play is performed live on stage usi
 ng voice actors\, vintage-style microphones\, live sound effects\, and mus
 ic to create the entire world through sound. You’ll see the actors and Fol
 ey artists at work as they transport you into Orwell’s dystopian future — 
 just like the golden age of radio.\n* Disclaimer: This is a fictional stor
 y about control and freedom\, meant to entertain and provoke thought. It’s
  not intended as commentary on current events\, political parties\, or tod
 ay’s social climate.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260410T193000
LOCATION:Historic Brown County Playhouse\, 70 South Van Buren Street\, Nash
 ville
RDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20260411T193000
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:1984 – Radio Play
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/1984-radio-play/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p>You are invit
 ed to experience <em>1984 – Radio Play\,</em> a haunting adaptation of Geo
 rge Orwell’s classic dystopian novel brought to life on stage.</p>\n<p>In 
 a world where every thought is monitored and the Party controls truth itse
 lf\, Winston Smith dares to question the system. When forbidden love awake
 ns him to the possibility of freedom\, he risks everything in a chilling b
 attle against a regime where even thinking differently is a crime.</p>\n<p
 >// What is a radio play? //</p>\n<p>A radio play is performed live on sta
 ge using voice actors\, vintage-style microphones\, live sound effects\, a
 nd music to create the entire world through sound. You’ll see the actors a
 nd Foley artists at work as they transport you into Orwell’s dystopian fut
 ure — just like the golden age of radio.</p>\n<p>* Disclaimer: This is a f
 ictional story about control and freedom\, meant to entertain and provoke 
 thought. It’s not intended as commentary on current events\, political par
 ties\, or today’s social climate.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
