BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-146551@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Crankies were created in Japan as 11th-century scroll paintings
 . As this art form spread across the world\, its form and name changed man
 y times. In the 1960s\, Peter Schumann invented the term “cranky”. This le
 d to the current name of cranky/ crankie.\nA crankie is a form of storytel
 ling\, using a box with dowel rods to attach and crank (turn) a scroll. A 
 crankie is usually accompanied by music or poetry\, with the imagery on th
 e scroll. A scroll can be as long as the artist wants. The box of a cranki
 e can range in size from a matchbox to as large as you can imagine. There 
 are crankie festivals all across the world\, and in the US\, and we hope t
 o bring the joy of this art form to Bloomington. 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260418T150000
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library Auditorium\, 303 E Kirkwood Ave\, Blo
 omington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:We’re Crankie: Crankie Festival
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/were-crankie-crankie-festival/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p><span style='
 font-family: arial\, sans-serif'>Crankies were created in Japan as 11th-ce
 ntury scroll paintings. As this art form spread across the world\, its for
 m and name changed many times. In the 1960s\, Peter Schumann invented the 
 term “cranky”. This led to the current name of cranky/ crankie.</p>\n<p>A 
 crankie is a form of storytelling\, using a box with dowel rods to attach 
 and crank (turn) a scroll. A crankie is usually accompanied by music or po
 etry\, with the imagery on the scroll. A scroll can be as long as the arti
 st wants. The box of a crankie can range in size from a matchbox to as lar
 ge as you can imagine. There are crankie festivals all across the world\, 
 and in the US\, and we hope to bring the joy of this art form to Bloomingt
 on. </span></p>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
