BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai1ec-144514@wfhb.org
DTSTAMP:20260331T015807Z
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:How do museums differ from classrooms\, publications\, and othe
 r learning media? What do museum people want their visitors to learn and f
 eel—and what preconceptions help or hinder visitors from meeting those exp
 ectations? Eric Sandweiss\, Thomas and Kathryn Miller Professor of History
 \, offers an insider’s look at two exciting new IU exhibitions that allows
  us to hear how museum people think—and to respond for ourselves. We’ll ta
 ke a historical tour of campus on our way between the museums\, and we’ll 
 wind up our afternoon with an informal chat at the McCalla School—home to 
 IU’s wonderful University Collections.\nThe structure of this event is unu
 sual (and exciting) for the Traveling University.\nParticipants will meet 
 at the IU Art Museum atrium at 1 pm on Apr. 24 where they will be greeted 
 by curators and shown the new Mulyana: Vital Ecosystems show.\nThat visit 
 to the IU Art Museum will be followed by a short historical campus tour (c
 . 2-230 pm) en route to the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology. Par
 ticipants will meet with curators before viewing their new Shipwrecks: Liv
 ing Museums show.\nThe event will finish up (c. 3:30) at the McCalla Schoo
 l where participants will learn more about University Collections and spen
 d half hour or so debriefing on the day. Estimated finish: 4 or 4:30.\nWe 
 will ask participants to preregister as this event is limited to 25 partic
 ipants.\n\n\n\n\nContact\ntravelinguniv@gmail.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T163000
LOCATION:Indiana University Art Museum\, 1133 E 7th St\, Bloomington
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Museum in Question: An Inside Look at Two New IU Exhibitions
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-museum-in-question-an-inside-look-at-two-new
 -iu-exhibitions/
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//E
 N'>\\n<HTML>\\n<HEAD>\\n<TITLE></TITLE>\\n</HEAD>\\n<BODY><p data-rte-pres
 erve-empty='true'>How do museums differ from classrooms\, publications\, a
 nd other learning media? What do museum people want their visitors to lear
 n and feel—and what preconceptions help or hinder visitors from meeting th
 ose expectations? Eric Sandweiss\, Thomas and Kathryn Miller Professor of 
 History\, offers an insider’s look at two exciting new IU exhibitions that
  allows us to hear how museum people think—and to respond for ourselves. W
 e’ll take a historical tour of campus on our way between the museums\, and
  we’ll wind up our afternoon with an informal chat at the McCalla School—h
 ome to IU’s wonderful University Collections.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-pr
 eserve-empty='true'>The structure of this event is unusual (and exciting) 
 for the Traveling University.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-preserve-empty='tr
 ue'>Participants will meet at the IU Art Museum atrium at 1 pm on Apr. 24 
 where they will be greeted by curators and shown the new <a href='https://
 artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/upcoming/_feature-exhibitions/2026-02-07
 -mulyana-vital-ecosystems.html'><em>Mulyana: Vital Ecosystems</em></a> sho
 w.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-preserve-empty='true'>That visit to the IU Ar
 t Museum will be followed by a short historical campus tour (c. 2-230 pm) 
 en route to the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology. Participants wi
 ll meet with curators before viewing their new <a href='https://iumaa.iu.e
 du/exhibits/upcoming-exhibitions/index.html'><em>Shipwrecks: Living Museum
 s</em></a> show.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-preserve-empty='true'>The event
  will finish up (c. 3:30) at the McCalla School where participants will le
 arn more about University Collections and spend half hour or so debriefing
  on the day. Estimated finish: 4 or 4:30.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-preser
 ve-empty='true'>We will ask participants to preregister as this event is l
 imited to 25 participants.</p>\n<div class='fe-block fe-block-61395d3b5325
 8d7a9c4b'>\n<div id='block-61395d3b53258d7a9c4b' class='sqs-block html-blo
 ck sqs-block-html' data-blend-mode='NORMAL' data-block-type='2' data-borde
 r-radii='{'topLeft':{'unit':'px'\,'value':0.0}\,'topRight':{'unit':'px'\,'
 value':0.0}\,'bottomLeft':{'unit':'px'\,'value':0.0}\,'bottomRight':{'unit
 ':'px'\,'value':0.0}}' data-sqsp-block='text'>\n<div class='sqs-block-cont
 ent'>\n<div class='sqs-html-content' data-sqsp-text-block-content=''>\n<h4
 >Contact</h4>\n<p class=''>travelinguniv@gmail.com</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</
 div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
END:VEVENT
